window.DOSSIER_LEVELS = {"e001":[{"level":1,"title":"Kaichi","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Summon Kaichi, a yellow drill horn (a manifestation, not a separate creature; lasts until dismissed or resummoned) · When you take the Attack action, make one extra melee CE attack with it, 10-ft reach. · Passive · Kaichi's melee attack damage scales with level: 1d6 (1st), 1d8 (3rd), 1d10 (6th), 1d12 (11th), 3d6 (18th)."},{"level":3,"title":"Reiki","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Double your walking speed until the end of your next turn · Alternatively, Reaction · 2 CE · +5 AC against the triggering attack (after the roll, before the result)."},{"level":6,"title":"Kirin","rules":"Bonus action · Spend 1 to PB CE · Gain 5 temp HP per CE spent; your speed becomes 0 until the start of your next turn · Existing exhaustion effects are suppressed while these temp HP remain."},{"level":11,"title":"Ryu","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Summon Ryu in an open space within 30 ft · Lasts 1 hour, until dismissed, or until reduced to 0 HP. · Passive · Ryu: Large dragon shikigami · AC 13 + PB · HP 10 x character level · Speed 30 ft, fly 60 ft · Uses your CE attack modifier and CE save DC · No independent CE, Multiattack, Domain Expansion, or Maximum Technique. · Bonus action · Command Ryu's action (it acts immediately after you; otherwise it Dodges). · Ryu's attack · Melee CE attack, 10-ft reach · On hit: 2d10 + CE modifier piercing damage. · Ryu's action · 30-ft cone · Dexterity save · 5d8 lightning damage, half on success · Recharge 5-6. · Passive · If reduced to 0 HP, Ryu vanishes and cannot be summoned again until you complete a long rest."}],"e002":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Crows","rules":"Passive · Begin with three cursed crows (charmed, obey your orders; Raven stat block, Cursed Spirit type) · Direct up to PB + CE modifier at once (minimum 3) · Action + 1 CE to bond a restrained, grappled, or incapacitated raven. · Action · Close your eyes to see through one crow (same plane, no range limit; you are blinded; deafened if you also listen; no reactions depending on your body's senses) · Switch crow: action · End link: bonus action."},{"level":3,"title":"Omen of Death","rules":"Bonus action · Each creature of your choice you can see within 30 ft makes a Wisdom save · Fail: frightened of you for 1 minute (repeats the save at the end of each of its turns) · Success: immune until next dawn."},{"level":6,"title":"Raven’s Eye","rules":"Passive · +1 passive Perception for every active crow within 1 mile, capped at +PB. · Passive · Switching the crow you view through is now a bonus action; ending the link costs no action."},{"level":11,"title":"Bird Strike","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Order one active crow to attack a target it can reach · Dexterity save - fail: 10d10 force damage + one revised limb-injury result; success: half damage, no limb result · The crow is destroyed, hit or miss."}],"e003":[{"level":1,"title":"Blood Constructs / Battle Blood","rules":"Action · 1 CE + 1 HP per 5-ft segment · Pull blood from an available source to create a connected semi-solid construct in an open space within reach (wall, bridge, simple tool, or weapon shape; no moving machinery) · AC 13, HP equal to your level per CE spent, lasts 1 hour · An external blood source waives only the HP cost. · Action · 4 CE · One creature within 30 ft · Strength save or restrained (repeats the save at the end of each turn, up to 1 minute with Technique Focus) · The binding is an object: AC 13, HP 2 x your level · One binding at a time. · Action · 1 CE · Ranged CE attack, 60/120 ft · On hit: 1d10 necrotic damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Flowing Red Scale","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE (requires Technique Focus) · For 1 minute: speed doubled, +2 AC, advantage on Dexterity saves and Strength checks, one extra action per turn (one weapon attack, Dash, Disengage, Hide, or Use an Object; does not stack with another extra-action source)."},{"level":6,"title":"Convergence","rules":"Passive (before you use a cursed technique) · Spend additional CE up to your CE modifier and pay an equal amount of HP · Each extra CE adds one damage die (matching the feature's base die) or one round of duration · External blood waives only the HP cost."},{"level":11,"title":"Piercing Blood","rules":"Action · 10 CE + 10 HP · 100-ft-long, 5-ft-wide line of supersonic blood · Dexterity save: 10d8 piercing damage, half on success · Convergence may replace the save with one CE attack against each target's AC (roll once); missed targets take nothing."}],"e004":[{"level":1,"title":"Graverobber","rules":"Long rest · 1 CE · Transfer your brain into an intact, dead Humanoid whose body can physically contain it · The prior body dies · Unsuitable vessel: the CE is not spent and the transfer fails safely. · Passive · Replace Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution with the vessel's printed values; retain Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma · Gain its ancestry traits, mundane proficiencies, movement, senses, size, and languages · No class levels, feats, spellcasting, CE, legendary/lair/mythic actions, or Innate Technique (except via Skill Theft) · Class Hit Dice and CE Reserve never change. · Passive · The forehead scar is visible · DC 30 Insight to notice behavioral inconsistency (advantage for creatures who knew the vessel) · DC 20 Medicine to find the surgical anomaly on close inspection."},{"level":3,"title":"Skill Theft","rules":"Long rest (after a successful transplant) · Store one eligible feature the body possessed, including an Innate Technique's base feature · Slots: 1 at level 3, 2 at 6, 3 at 11, 4 at 18 · A copied technique uses your CE attack, save DC, CE pool, and Output Rank · Multiattack, regeneration, legendary resistance, boss phases, and monster-CR-only features are ineligible."},{"level":18,"title":"Immortality","rules":"Passive · Biological age becomes that of each new vessel; death from old age is prevented · Does not prevent death, soul damage, brain destruction, or a failed transfer."}],"e005":[{"level":1,"title":"Boogie","rules":"Action, bonus action, or reaction (+2 CE for reaction) · 1 CE · Clap to exchange exactly two targets you can perceive within 30 ft: yourself with a willing creature or an eligible object · Teleportation (no opportunity attacks; preserves facing, conditions, momentum, altitude) · Each destination must fit the arriving target; worn or carried objects cannot be selected separately. · Action · 1 CE · Imbue an ordinary Small-or-larger object so it counts as eligible for Boogie Woogie for 1 minute (does not make it a reusable magic item)."},{"level":3,"title":"Woogie","rules":"Passive · You may now move hostile creatures and swap two creatures other than yourself · Each unwilling creature makes a Charisma save: if either member of a pair succeeds, that pair does not move (CE still spent) · Success grants immunity to unwilling swaps until the start of your next turn · A swapped unwilling creature loses its reaction until the start of its next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Clapping With Soul","rules":"Passive · Range extends to 45 ft · Every Boogie Woogie use costs 1 less CE · Once per turn, use Boogie Woogie with no action · No creature can be moved by your Boogie Woogie more than twice in one turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Round of Applause","rules":"Passive · Range extends to 60 ft · When you use your reaction to clap, resolve two disjoint pairs among up to four targets at no added CE cost · If the swap changes ally/enemy adjacency (yourself or a target), your next attack roll has advantage."}],"e006":[{"level":1,"title":"Construct","rules":"Bonus action · Spend 1 to PB CE · Create a nonmagical object you understand in an open space within 10 ft: up to 10 lb and 1 cubic ft per CE, real and permanent · Complex objects require a blueprint, tool proficiency, or studied example · Cannot contain energy, active chemicals, information, or living tissue you do not understand. · Passive (on creation) · Combine two understood mundane item designs into one object at double total CE and mass · Choose one base damage die and combine compatible weapon properties; conflicting properties (e.g. light and heavy) choose one · Created currency and valuables read as constructed under CE detection but remain physically real."},{"level":3,"title":"Cursed Creation","rules":"Bonus action (with creation) · Create a named cursed or magic item (name the exact item; GM confirms its grade and lore fit) · Cost: 3 CE + 1 per grade above common (up to Grade 1) · Lasts CE modifier hours; requires normal attunement; cannot supply wishes or permanent ability increases; vanishes without leaving saleable components. · Passive · Voluntarily constructing a Special Grade cursed tool kills you immediately after the item is completed · That death cannot be undone by ordinary Reverse Cursed Technique or any revival effect."},{"level":6,"title":"Liquid Metal","rules":"Passive (at creation) · Spend up to an additional 4 CE to make a created weapon fluid: each CE adds +10 ft melee reach and raises its damage die one tier (1d8 to 1d10 to 1d12 to 2d6 to 2d8) · Lasts 1 minute (Technique Focus); dismiss with no action."},{"level":11,"title":"Insectoid Armor","rules":"Bonus action · 10 CE (Technique Focus) · Surround yourself in insectoid armor for 1 minute: +4 Strength, Dexterity, and AC; resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing (immunity at level 20); fly speed equal to walking speed; once per turn Dash with no action; unarmed strikes deal two additional damage dice (+1 more on crit) · Ends if incapacitated."}],"e007":[{"level":1,"title":"Granite Blast","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Ranged CE attack, 150/600 ft · On hit: force damage = 3d8 (1st), 6d8 (3rd), 8d8 (6th), 10d8 (11th), 12d8 (15th), 12d10 (18th)."},{"level":3,"title":"Grape Shot","rules":"Passive (+1 CE on Granite Blast) · Split the blast among 2 up to PB targets (maximum = the number of damage dice), at least one die each · Separate CE attack per target; a creature can receive only one portion."},{"level":6,"title":"Guided Shell","rules":"Free action · After the roll but before the result: spend 1-5 CE and add that amount to the attack roll · Explicit exception to the shared +2 accuracy ceiling; affects one attack roll only; cannot also raise that use's save DC."},{"level":11,"title":"Nuclear Shell","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Create an obvious, audible charge (held until the end of your next turn; lost if incapacitated or you begin another Maximum) · Release with an action, no added base cost: 150-ft cone, damage rolled once (current Granite Blast dice + CE modifier dice of the same die); each creature makes the printed Dexterity save."}],"e008":[{"level":1,"title":"Power of Words","rules":"Passive · You speak ten cursed words - Sleep, Return, Run Away, Blast Away, Plummet, Get Twisted, Get Crushed, Don't Move, Explode, Die - each with its own CE cost and effect (see the Word Binding procedure reference) · Outside them you can speak only a meaningless concept (e.g. sushi ingredients). · Passive · Vocal-cord HP pool = one third of your maximum HP (rounded up) · Each CE spent on a word deals that much vocal damage after it resolves · Regain 1 vocal HP at the start of each turn while above 0; a short or long rest restores the pool · At 0 vocal HP you cannot use words."},{"level":3,"title":"Interjection","rules":"Passive · Choose one word after a long rest: it may fire as a bonus action, or as a reaction when a legal target begins movement, starts an action, summons a creature, or targets you · You still pay all CE and vocal strain. · Passive · Unlock +1 CE of enhancement per word at levels 3, 6, 11, and 18 (maximum four) · A listed +1 DC per CE is an explicit technique exception · \"X\" in base damage means CE modifier; \"additional Xd10\" means one d10 per added CE."},{"level":6,"title":"Iron Chords","rules":"Passive · The vocal-HP pool doubles to one half of your maximum HP (rounded up)."},{"level":11,"title":"Resounding Voice","rules":"Passive · Pay 5 extra CE to replace a word's normal target area with a 35-ft cone from you: every creature that can hear you is affected (including allies); roll damage once · Unlocks your third CE of word enhancement (the fourth unlocks at 18)."}],"e009":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Spirit Absorption","rules":"Action or reaction (after a non-Humanoid within 120 ft reaches 0 HP) · 1 CE · Turn it into an orb and eat it (automatic) · A living creature with CR lower than your PB instead makes a Wisdom save (must have the Cursed Spirit type); failure turns it into an orb · Legendary resistance can prevent this. · Passive (part of absorption) · Safely consume orbs of CR equal to or lower than your level · Higher-CR orb: Constitution save (DC 5 + the creature's CR) - success: absorb it (usable after a short or long rest); failure: 2 levels of exhaustion + necrotic damage equal to the creature's CR in d12s. · Passive · When the number stored first crosses a multiple of 10: DC 10 Wisdom save - fail: exhaustion (fail by 5 or less: 1 level; by more than 5: 2 levels; by 10 or more: 3 levels) · A lost spirit does not let the same threshold trigger again. · Passive · Stored spirits unlimited, recorded by exact stat block and CR · Summoning costs CE = CR rounded up (minimum 1) · Active spirits up to your CE modifier (minimum 1); they act immediately after you; one bonus action gives all the same simple order, an action gives distinct or complex orders; otherwise they Dodge. · Passive · Spirits cannot use legendary, lair, or mythic actions · Spellcasting and Innate Techniques are allowed, CE costs paid from your pool · A spirit reduced to 0 HP is permanently exorcised."},{"level":3,"title":"Curse-Infused Spirits","rules":"Passive · Spirits' Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution each gain your CE modifier (maximum 22); recalculate attacks, damage, AC, HP, and save DCs · Sacrificial defense (requires an active spirit): X = its CR rounded up (minimum 1); spend X CE to reduce one damage instance by Xd20, destroying the spirit. · Passive · Spirits regain all HP at the end of a short rest; immune to frightened and charmed; you know when one is exorcised, even at a distance."},{"level":6,"title":"Perfect Control","rules":"Passive · Collection strain is now checked at multiples of 20 instead of 10 · Summoning cursed spirits becomes a bonus action."}],"e010":[{"level":1,"title":"Judge’s Gavel","rules":"Bonus action · Summon your gavel (your CE focus; counts as magical): light hammer (1d4, light, thrown 20/60), maul (2d6, heavy, two-handed), or pole hammer (1d10, heavy, reach, two-handed) · Change form as a bonus action · First summon after each long rest is free; later summons cost 1 CE."},{"level":3,"title":"Deadly Sentencing","rules":"Domain action · Choose one creature caught inside the Domain · While court is in session: no creature can make attacks, deal damage, force movement, or activate an effect intended to harm another; attempted offensive actions simply fail · The trial resolves immediately, then the barrier ends. · Passive · The GM names one meaningful act the defendant actually committed as the charge; if none exists, the verdict is innocent · Judgeman produces evidence (roll on the table): the caster sees the evidence, the defendant hears only the charge. · Passive · The defendant chooses silence, denial, confession, or explanation and states a brief case · Trial contest: your CE ability check with PB vs the defendant's Charisma (Deception or Persuasion) or Intelligence (Investigation), matching its argument; the evidence modifies the contest · Ties favor the defendant. · Passive · Acquittal: nothing confiscated · Guilty, nonlethal offense: Confiscation · Deliberate killing, attempted mass killing, or comparably grave offense: Confiscation + Death Penalty if you win the contest by 5 or more, else Confiscation. · Passive · Confiscation priority: Innate Technique, then CE use, then one attuned magic item, then one class feature chosen by Judgeman · The confiscated source cannot be used until you dismiss the sentence, die, or a later trial acquits it · An item becomes mundane but remains physically present. · Passive · Your gavel becomes the Executioner's Sword: a hit against the convicted creature kills it; against any other target it is a mundane longsword · Vanishes when the sentence ends or the convicted creature dies."},{"level":6,"title":"Gavel Improvements","rules":"Passive · Summoning the gavel costs no action · Large form doubles the weapon's base dice; Huge triples them · Once per turn, a Huge gavel attack can instead target a 10-ft square: creatures there make a Dexterity save, taking the weapon's damage on failure or half on success."},{"level":11,"title":"Better Evidence","rules":"Passive · Evidence: roll one die; at level 11 roll two dice and choose the result; at level 18 roll three dice and choose."},{"level":18,"title":"Unstopping Justice","rules":"Passive · Your first CE modifier uses per long rest (minimum one) require no CE; further uses pay the normal Domain cost · Does not bypass Domain Burnout."}],"e011":[{"level":1,"title":"Flames of Disaster","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · 15-foot cone · Dexterity save: 1d8 fire damage (2d8 at 5th, 3d8 at 11th, 4d8 at 17th); half on success · Ignited unattended objects burn; creatures and worn objects are not automatically ignited."},{"level":3,"title":"Erupting Volcanoes","rules":"Action · 2 CE each · Create 1 to CE modifier (minimum 1) volcanoes in unoccupied ground spaces within 120 feet · Each is a 5-foot-diameter object, AC 14, HP 5 × level, immune to fire and poison · 1 minute, uses Technique Focus. · Bonus action · 0 CE · Command any number of your volcanoes to erupt, each targeting a different 30-by-10-foot line · Each creature in a line: Dexterity save, 5d10 fire damage + restrained by magma for 1 minute (Strength save at end of each turn to break); half damage and no restraint on success · Overlapping lines: one save, one damage roll · Lines remain difficult terrain until the volcano ends."},{"level":6,"title":"Ember Insects","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Create one ember-insect swarm (appendix profile) within 5 feet · Acts after you, lasts 1 minute · Bonus action to command it; otherwise it Dodges · Only one swarm at a time."}],"e012":[{"level":1,"title":"Tides of Disaster","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Ranged CE attack, 60/120 feet, using water the technique creates · On hit: 1d8 cold damage (2d8 at 5th, 3d8 at 11th, 4d8 at 17th) · You know the Shape Water cantrip."},{"level":3,"title":"Horizon of Captivating Skandha / Death Swarm","rules":"Passive · Your Domain opens at 3rd level · Two free uses per long rest, then 20 CE per use · Full Domain rules in the Pinnacle expression section. · Action · Only while the Domain is open · Choose any mixture of shikigami up to your CE modifier in active count, paying each printed cost (appendix profiles) · They appear in unoccupied spaces you can see and attack normally. · Passive · At initiative 20 inside the Domain, the spectral school engulfs every chosen hostile · Each automatically takes 8d10 piercing or cold damage (you choose which) and is restrained until the next initiative 20 · Protected creatures: Dexterity save, half damage and no restraint."},{"level":6,"title":"Water Defensive Ring","rules":"Action for 6 CE, or reaction to incoming damage for 8 CE · Ring of water grants temporary HP equal to CE modifier × 15; incoming damage applies to the ring first · While any temp HP remain: immunity to cold damage, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing · Ends at 0 HP, when dismissed, or after 10 minutes · No second ring while one persists."},{"level":11,"title":"Flash Flood","rules":"Action · 8 CE · CE attack against one target within 30 feet · On hit: 10d8 cold damage and the target is pushed 80 feet away (no collision damage). · Action · 10 CE · Choose a point within 30 feet · Creatures in a 10-foot-radius circle: Dexterity save, 8d12 cold damage, half on success · The water fills a physically enclosed space 10 feet deep for 1 hour, then drains · Creatures too large for the space are not crushed."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Tsunami","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Cast the 8th-level Tsunami spell with your CE save DC, no material components · Requires Technique Focus."}],"e013":[{"level":1,"title":"Forests of Disaster","rules":"Passive · You manipulate plants at will and know the Druidcraft cantrip · Grants Binding Plants, Piercing Roots, and Wall of Roots below. · Action · 1 CE · One target within 30 feet · Failed Strength save: restrained by plants for up to 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each turn · Plants have AC 13 and HP equal to twice your level. · Action · 1 CE · Roots rise in a 50-foot-long, 5-foot-wide line · Dexterity save: 1d12 piercing (2d12 at 5th, 3d12 at 11th, 4d12 at 17th); half on success. · Reaction · 1 CE · When you or an ally within 30 feet is targeted by an attack: place a 10-foot-wide, 10-foot-tall, 5-foot-thick wall between attacker and target · Recalculate cover before resolving the triggering attack · AC 13, HP equal to CE modifier × PB (minimum 1), lasts until the start of your next turn or destroyed."},{"level":3,"title":"Root Bundle","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Create exactly two wooden balls within 5 feet of you, 10 minutes · AC 10 + CE modifier, HP equal to CE modifier; at most two exist · Bonus action: launch any number at targets within 30 feet, one CE attack per ball, 2d10 piercing per hit · You may ride one: flying speed equal to walking speed while within 30 feet of you."},{"level":6,"title":"Flower Field","rules":"Action · 10 CE · 30-foot-radius circle of petals at a point within 100 feet · Wisdom save: charmed, speed 0, and cannot take an action, bonus action, or reaction intended to advance combat, for 1 minute; repeats the save at the end of each turn · A hostile attack or save targeting the creature ends the condition after it resolves · Uses Technique Focus."},{"level":11,"title":"Cursed Buds","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Launch cursed buds equal to your CE modifier at targets within 30 feet, one CE attack each · Each hit attaches a bud: at the start of the host’s turn, each bud deals necrotic damage equal to your CE modifier (minimum 1) · An action plus Strength (Athletics) against your CE DC removes one bud. · Action · 10 CE · Create a Large tree (AC 15, HP 10 × PB, 1 minute, Technique Focus) · At the start of each of your turns it fires one bud at every hostile creature within 30 feet of it: one ranged CE attack per target, 2d6 piercing per hit."}],"e014":[{"level":1,"title":"Divergent Flow","rules":"Trigger · After you hit with an attack, pay 1 CE · Record the total damage that attack would deal after resistance; deal none now · At the start of the target’s next turn, it takes the recorded amount as force damage · The delayed damage cannot critically hit, cannot trigger Black Flash, and is not changed again by resistance or vulnerability."},{"level":3,"title":"Martial Prowess","rules":"Passive · Only one Martial Prowess option may be used per turn. · Passive · Declared as part of an unarmed strike · On a hit, roll normal damage · Constitution save (DC 8 + PB + your Strength or Dexterity modifier): failure doubles that final damage and stuns the target until the end of its next turn; success deals normal damage with no stun. · Bonus action · Make two unarmed attacks · The first omits the ability modifier from damage; if it hits, the second has advantage and adds three times your Strength or Dexterity modifier to damage instead of once. · Reaction · Gain the Dodge action’s benefits until the start of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Controlled Divergent Flow","rules":"Passive · Your Divergent Flow improves: apply it to two different attacks per turn (1 CE after each hit) · Each target takes its recorded force damage at the start of its own next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Stance of the Sparks","rules":"Action · Enter a stance lasting until ended with no action, you are incapacitated, or you make more than one attack in a turn · You can make only one attack total on your turn, regardless of source · If that attack hits, it is eligible for the current Black Flash roll even without a critical hit."},{"level":18,"title":"Chosen by the Sparks","rules":"Passive · A critical hit or a qualifying stance hit automatically becomes a Black Flash · All once-per-turn and amplification rules for Black Flash still apply."}],"e015":[{"level":1,"title":"Hands of Love","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Create two Medium hands in open spaces within 15 feet; they last 10 minutes · Each: speed 30, AC equal to your CE save DC, HP equal to twice your CE save DC; magical objects, not creatures · Each must remain within 15 feet of you and snaps to the nearest legal space if the tether is exceeded. · Passive · At the start of each of your turns, move each hand up to its speed with no action · Your unarmed strikes, grapples, and shoves may originate from either hand using your own statistics · The hands grant no extra attacks · A hand has advantage on its grapple and shove checks. · Passive · When a hand takes damage, you lose one tenth of the damage actually applied to it, rounded down · This loss is not damage, cannot be reduced, and cannot reduce you below 1 HP · A destroyed hand stays gone until you summon the pair again, which dismisses any surviving hand."},{"level":3,"title":"Handy","rules":"Passive · Your hands improve: AC increases by your PB; attacks originating from a hand add your CE modifier to damage once; the tether range becomes 30 feet; a creature a hand grapples is restrained."},{"level":6,"title":"Hand Shield","rules":"Reaction · When you or an ally adjacent to a hand is targeted by an attack, spell, or effect requiring an attack roll or saving throw: place that hand between source and target · The target has three-quarters cover against the triggering effect, and until the start of your next turn while it stays adjacent · Area effects passing through the hand damage it normally."},{"level":11,"title":"Cutie Honey","rules":"Trigger · After an attack originating from a hand hits, pay 5 CE · Wisdom save: on failure the target is charmed for up to 1 minute and cannot willingly target another creature while it can perceive and legally target you · It repeats the save at the end of each turn."}],"e016":[{"level":1,"title":"Ice Creation","rules":"Action · 1 CE · 10-foot cone · Dexterity save: 1d10 cold damage and restrained as ice covers them; half damage and no restraint on success · A restrained creature may make a Strength save at the beginning of its turns to break free · Damage rises to 2d10 at 3rd, 3d10 at 6th, 4d10 at 10th, 5d10 at 14th, and 6d10 at 20th."},{"level":3,"title":"Extreme Cold","rules":"Passive · A creature restrained by your ice suffers one additional exhaustion level, which cannot stack with itself and vanishes when the restraint ends · A creature without cold resistance or immunity has halved speed while within 5 feet of any persistent technique ice."},{"level":6,"title":"Frost Calm","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Send a cloud of freezing mist to a spot within 60 feet · Every creature in a 30-foot-radius circle: Dexterity save, 7d8 cold damage and restrained by the ice layer; half damage and no restraint on success · A restrained creature may make a Strength save at the beginning of its turns to break free · The area becomes difficult terrain until all its ice is destroyed or dismissed."},{"level":11,"title":"Ice Fall","rules":"Action · 8 CE · You fall prone until the start of your next turn · One CE attack compared against every creature within 30 feet: on a hit, 1d10 cold damage and restrained (Strength save at the beginning of its turns to break free) · Hit or miss, each targeted creature also makes a Dexterity save: 6d8 cold + 6d8 piercing damage, half on success; roll the spike damage once."}],"e017":[{"level":1,"title":"Transfiguration / Transfigured Creatures","rules":"Passive · Natural weapons, unarmed strikes, and deliberate touch attacks deal +1d6 necrotic · Action · 1 CE · One creature within your reach: Constitution save, 1d10 necrotic (2d10 at 5th, 3d10 at 9th, 4d10 at 13th, 5d10 at 17th); half on success · Constructs are immune to conversion, not to the damage. · Passive · A creature reduced to 0 HP by your Idle Transfiguration becomes a Transfigured Creature instead of dying: maximum HP becomes half its former maximum (minimum 1) and it returns at full HP · Store up to your level × max(1, CE modifier); at most CE modifier (minimum 1) active at once · Bonus action: extract any number into open spaces within 10 feet, or store adjacent willing transfigured creatures. · Passive · During a rest, customize a transfigured creature: choose Tiny through Huge (size changes space and reach only); set Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma to 4, then move the removed points among Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution (maximum 22 each); remove supernatural features, spellcasting, techniques, and proficiencies · AC 10 + Dexterity; attacks use your PB + Strength or Dexterity, 1d6 + modifier · Bonus action: one simple order to all active creatures; action: distinct or complex orders."},{"level":3,"title":"Ally and Self Alterations","rules":"Passive · During a rest, a willing creature may receive permanent alterations: up to PB per creature, and Hardened Skin chooses one of bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing · They last until you reverse them, the creature dies, or Technique Extermination removes them; creature type is unchanged · Choose from the alteration list in the Appendix. · Bonus action each · Printed CE each, 1 minute · Maintain up to PB compatible alterations; ending one costs no action · No Technique Focus · Choose from the alteration list in the Appendix."},{"level":6,"title":"Body Clone","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Create a perfect copy of yourself: controlled by you, acts on your initiative, takes only the actions you grant it with your bonus action · Divide maximum HP and maximum CE evenly between bodies (odd points to the original); current pools drop to their new maxima · On recombination, restore maxima and add its remaining current HP/CE; if it dies, the reserved maxima return after your next long rest but its current resources are lost · It cannot create another clone."},{"level":11,"title":"Soul Multiplicity","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Spend 2 or more Transfigured Creatures, fusing them into one of the listed effects · Consumed creatures are permanently destroyed. · Action · A Soul Multiplicity fusion effect · One CE attack, 60/120-foot range · 5d8 necrotic damage, plus 1d8 for every creature beyond the first two, with no hidden cap. · Action · A Soul Multiplicity fusion effect · Create a Polymorphic Soul Isomer (appendix profile; counts as one active summon) · You may spend 5 additional CE to add another Transfigured Creature to the fusion (minimum 2 total); each transfigured creature counts as one soul."}],"e018":[{"level":1,"title":"Infinity","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE to encase yourself in Infinity · Pay 1 CE at the start of each later turn or it ends · Infinity is an explicit non-Focus sustained technique. · Passive · Before resolving each distinct external attack or harmful saving-throw effect against a protected creature, roll the Infinity d6: on 4 or higher that creature is not hit or affected and makes no save; on failure, resolve normally · One area effect calls for one roll per protected creature, not per damage die. · Passive · Infinity cannot stop poison already inside the body, suffocation, starvation, a condition applied before activation, soul effects with no spatial path, or a creature or effect already touching you when it activates · Before level 6 it also cannot stop a source you cannot perceive. · Passive · While you take the Dodge action: advantage on each Infinity die, and protection extends to creatures within your reach; each ally rolls separately."},{"level":3,"title":"Lapse Blue","rules":"Action · X CE (X capped at PB unless Maximum Output raises it) · Pick an unoccupied space within 30 feet you can see: create a sphere with radius 5 × X feet · Each creature in range: Strength save, (X + 2)d8 force damage and pulled to the nearest legal spaces adjacent to the sphere; half damage and no pull on success. · Passive · Maximum Output Blue lasts up to 1 minute with Technique Focus · Its center must stay within 30 feet of its original point · A creature saves at most once per turn against its movement with a Strength save; on failure it is pulled 15 feet toward the center."},{"level":6,"title":"Reversal Red","rules":"Bonus action · Spend 2X CE (X capped at PB) · One creature within 60 feet: Strength save, (X + 4)d8 force damage and pushed 20 × X feet; half damage and no push on success · If it impacts a steel-strength substance, each 10 feet of prevented movement becomes 1d6 collision damage (maximum 20d6) · With Maximum Output, the push doubles and a failed save also knocks the creature prone. · Passive · From level 6, unseen sources are eligible for Infinity (poison remains ineligible) · The Infinity d6 succeeds on 3 or higher from 6th level, and on 2 or higher from 11th."},{"level":14,"title":"Automatic Infinity","rules":"Passive · At 14th level, you may activate Infinity as a reaction after you are targeted but before the attack or save is resolved. · Passive · When activating Infinity, you may spend 6 additional CE so every Infinity die automatically succeeds · This costs 2 CE at the start of each of your turns while active."}],"e019":[{"level":1,"title":"Love Rendezvous","rules":"Free action, once per turn (no action) · 1 CE · Touch a target or hit it with an unarmed strike · One target bears one star; marks follow the sequence Imai → Acrux → Mimosa → Ginan → Gacrux · Marks last 10 minutes; their light is visible and DC 15 Perception reveals a mark’s name. · Passive · You may maintain the same star on up to CE modifier targets (minimum 1) · If a new mark would exceed the limit, choose an old mark of that star to end. · Passive · A marked mover begins immediately after its own star in the sequence · It may always move away from marks; to willingly reduce distance to a differently marked creature or object, the destination must bear its current required star, and touching that star advances the requirement to the next · After touching Gacrux, its route is complete until its mark is reapplied · If no legal course exists, the route is dormant and movement is unrestricted until one exists; check before each movement. · Passive · An illegal approach ends the movement; the mover is restrained until the start of its next turn · Every creature or object bearing the mover’s same star is pulled in a straight line toward the bearer of that star with the greatest current CE (objects have 0; ties are your choice), stopping adjacent or at the last legal space · This forced movement never recursively triggers the technique · After witnessing a violation, a creature may use an action for Insight against your CE DC to understand the route (disadvantage unless familiar with CE tracking or the Southern Cross). · Passive · For each pulled target that travels at least 5 feet and collides: roll one size die (Tiny d4, Small d6, Medium d8, Large d10, Huge d12, Gargantuan 2d12) for every 5 feet actually traveled before the collision · The anchor takes the full roll; the moving target takes half · Resolve each target separately; see the collision-die reference · Immunity remains immunity."},{"level":3,"title":"Effective Marking","rules":"Passive · You gain one additional reaction per round, usable only to mark a target you touch or hit during the triggering event · This is the global maximum of two reactions."},{"level":6,"title":"Gravity","rules":"Passive · Your collision damage ignores resistance."},{"level":11,"title":"Shining Stars","rules":"Passive · You may maintain the same star on up to twice your CE modifier targets (minimum 2)."},{"level":18,"title":"Universal Force","rules":"Passive · Your collision damage becomes force damage and still ignores resistance."}],"e020":[{"level":1,"title":"Electric Energy","rules":"Trigger · After you hit with a melee weapon attack, spend 1 CE to deal extra lightning damage · 1d10 at level 1, usable once per turn · Damage grows as you level: 2d10 at 3rd, 3d10 at 6th, 4d10 at 11th, 5d10 at 14th, 6d10 at 18th."},{"level":3,"title":"Lightning Body","rules":"Passive · Your Electric Energy extra damage becomes 2d10, and you may use Electric Energy twice per turn · Add your Cursed Energy modifier to your initiative rolls · Whenever you deal lightning damage, add one additional d10 to each separate lightning damage roll."},{"level":6,"title":"Lightning Discharge","rules":"Passive · After hitting a creature with Electric Energy, you may mark it with a positive charge; a target can hold up to twice your CE modifier (minimum 2), and charges last 1 minute · Action: consume every charge on one target you can perceive within 300 feet; the bolt automatically reaches it and deals 1d12 lightning damage per charge."},{"level":11,"title":"Mythical Beast Amber Release","rules":"Action · 20 CE · Your body fills with electric cursed energy and constantly grows in power · Usable only once in your character’s existence: mark it permanently, even if deactivated immediately or suppressed; RCT cannot restore it · Lasts until you deactivate it with a bonus action or 5 minutes elapse. · Passive · Release minutes table: each elapsed minute increases Str, Dex, and Con (+2 at 0 minutes up to +6 at 4 minutes, ignoring limits), lightning immunity, speed (+20 to +100 feet), and extra attacks or actions · Bonuses replace earlier rows rather than stacking · Deactivating: Constitution save, DC 10 at minute 0 rising by 5 per minute; failure gains exhaustion levels, success gains fewer · At 5 minutes you die; only a campaign-level effect such as Wish can reverse it. · Passive · Minute 1: +1 extra attack; minute 2: +1 bonus action · Minute 3: +1 extra action that can Attack (one attack), Dash, Disengage, or use a Release feature · Minute 4: two extra actions with that same restriction; an explicit calamity exception to the normal extra-action cap. · Passive · When this form is active, your unarmed strikes change their whole damage roll to one chosen type (Thunder, Lightning, Fire, Force, or Cold) and deal one additional weapon die + 1d10 lightning. · Action and passive · Loud Blast (1 minute): uses an action; make a cursed energy attack roll against a creature within 30 feet — on a hit 6d10 lightning damage; all creatures within 15 feet of the aimed creature make a Constitution save: 6d6 thunder damage and deafened until the beginning of your next turn, half damage and no deafening on success · Lightning Armor (2 minutes): damage reduction equal to your Cursed Energy modifier, reducing each damage instance once (minimum 0) · X-Ray Vision (3 minutes): 120 feet of truesight. · Action · 10 CE · Huge cursed energy beam in a 30-foot line: every creature in the line makes a Dexterity save; on failure 10d10 force damage and blinded until the beginning of your next turn; half damage and no blinding on success · You may add up to your PB in CE, each adding 1d10 force damage and +1 to its DC (calamity exception)."},{"level":18,"title":"Lightning God’s Realm","rules":"Passive · Domain Expansion: Lightning God’s Realm · At initiative 20, every other creature gains three of your charge markers with no charge cap; only you can discharge them."}],"e021":[{"level":1,"title":"True New Shadow Style: Simple Domain","rules":"Passive · Gain the New Shadow Style: Simple Domain feat without its normal prerequisite · 20-ft radius · PB times per long rest: activate without CE as a bonus action or as a reaction to a Domain or sure-hit effect · Further uses pay the feat’s normal cost."},{"level":3,"title":"Batto Sword Draw","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Choose a continuous path up to half your speed and up to your Dexterity modifier of creatures (minimum one) within weapon reach of it · One weapon attack with advantage, compared against each chosen AC; roll damage once for those hit · Teleport along the path, provoking no opportunity attacks, finishing just beyond the farthest target."},{"level":6,"title":"Evening Moon Sword Drawing","rules":"Passive · While your Simple Domain is active and you wield a melee weapon: once per round when hostile creatures enter its radius, use a reaction to attack each entering creature once · On a hit, choose: spend 1 to PB CE to make it a critical and add that many weapon dice; or gain +5 AC and +5 on saves against CE effects until the start of your next turn (no CE required)."},{"level":11,"title":"Moonlight Veil","rules":"Bonus action · Technique Focus · Imbue one wielded melee weapon for 1 minute · Add your CE modifier to its attack and damage rolls · With only a broken weapon or unarmed: a spectral weapon uses the original weapon’s base die, or 1d6 unarmed, with no magic-item properties."},{"level":18,"title":"Perfect Shadow Style","rules":"Passive · Simple Domain no longer costs CE, has no use limit, and movement no longer ends it · Bonus action: add 60 feet to the range of one New Shadow Style technique used before the end of the current turn; for Simple Domain this increases its radius by 60 feet until the start of your next turn."}],"e022":[{"level":1,"title":"Great Luck","rules":"Free action · Once per long rest · Before making one attack roll: treat the d20 as a natural 20 · It is a critical hit if the attack lands, but it cannot trigger Black Flash."},{"level":3,"title":"Idle Death Gamble","rules":"Action · Free once per long rest, then 25 CE · Expand your Domain using the source’s chosen-creature rule · Lasts 1 minute unless a pending event needs longer, then only until that event resolves. · Passive · Inside the Domain the three attacks are bonus actions; hits bank expectation (Green +10%, Red +25%, Gold +50%) into one shared total capped at 190% · Bonus action to bet: consume all expectation, roll d20 + floor(expectation/10) (over 20 counts as 20) to select an event and jackpot die (d12/d10/d8/d6); the event lasts 1d4 rounds and only one event runs at a time · At the event’s end roll another d20 with the same bonus for the multiplier (1–12: 3, 13–15: 4, 16–17: 5, 18–19: 10, 20+: Rainbow), then roll three jackpot dice, rerolling any or all up to the multiplier and keeping dice between rerolls · Three matching values, or Rainbow, wins; failure resets expectation to 0 and a new cycle may begin while the Domain remains · Jackpot: the Domain ends and four rounds begin — CE refills to maximum each turn, automatic healing may spend up to your CE modifier, damage cannot drop you below 1 HP — but destruction of brain or body, or any death that never touches hit points, is still death."},{"level":6,"title":"On a Roll","rules":"Passive · After completing one Jackpot: advantage on event and multiplier d20 rolls until the next long rest."},{"level":11,"title":"The Fever","rules":"Passive · After entering your Jackpot: each time the Jackpot prevents you dropping below 1 HP, gain one Fever point (maximum PB), lost when the Jackpot ends · Spend one Fever point for a critical hit, +10 to one save or check, or one restricted extra action; only one Fever action per turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Luckiest Sorcerer Alive","rules":"Passive · Roll three d20s for the multiplier and choose one · Automatic RCT may spend twice your CE modifier · Jackpot lasts your CE modifier in minutes (minimum one), and you may initiate that RCT with no action when damage is received."}],"e023":[{"level":1,"title":"Prayer","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Choose one opponent you can perceive within 60 feet and begin Prayer for up to 1 minute using Technique Focus · At the start of each of your turns increase turns active by one before acting; effects are cumulative · Prayer ends if the target remains beyond 60 feet or imperceptible at the end of your turn · AC reductions apply against all attacks; saving-throw penalties apply only against your effects; your bonuses apply against every source · Starting Prayer again replaces the target and resets the count to 1. · Passive · Prayer progression (levels 1–10), cumulative by turns active: 1: +2 AC and +2 Dexterity saves; 2: chosen opponent’s AC decreases by 2; 3: add your CE modifier to your attack damage; 4: the opponent has disadvantage on attacks, you have advantage on saving throws; 5: your attacks deal additional damage equal to your proficiency bonus."},{"level":3,"title":"Marcado","rules":"Passive · Once per turn after an attack hits: pay 2 CE to add one of that attack’s base damage dice · Counts as one damage amplifier."},{"level":6,"title":"Caesura","rules":"Reaction · Once per round, 2 CE · When a creature you can perceive within 60 feet rolls an attack, save, or damage: force the entire roll to be rerolled and use the new result."},{"level":11,"title":"Crescendo","rules":"Passive · Replaces the five-beat track with the complete ten-beat progression, cumulative by turns active: 1: +3 AC and +3 Dexterity saves; 2: target AC −3; 3: add CE modifier to unarmed/natural damage; 4: add CE modifier to all attack damage; 5: add proficiency bonus damage; 6: reduce the target’s damage by your proficiency bonus; 7: one additional attack during the Attack action; 8: target’s totals −5 AC and −5 on saves against you; 9: critical range +1; 10: the turn-10 restriction below. · Passive · At turn 10 of Prayer and beyond: at the start of each target turn it makes a Wisdom save · On failure, during that turn it may choose only one — take an action, take a bonus action, or move up to its speed — and it cannot use reactions · On success it ignores the restriction for that turn."}],"e024":[{"level":1,"title":"Projection","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE to activate, plus 1 CE at the start of each turn to maintain · While active: walking speed +10 feet; the Attack action contains one additional attack (cannot stack with another extra-attack source beyond the core limit) · At activation and at the end of every turn thereafter, declare a legal route for your next turn as a sequence of spaces up to your current speed · On that turn you may stop early but cannot leave the route, reverse, add a new turn, or pass through an unknown obstruction; forced movement and teleportation are not part of the route · If you willingly break the route, strike an unexpected obstruction, or cannot enter the next declared space, movement ends and Projection ends after the current action."},{"level":3,"title":"Acceleration","rules":"Passive · After each consecutive turn in which you move at least half your speed on-route: add 10 feet to speed, up to 10 × PB additional feet · Once per turn after moving at least 10 feet in one straight, uninterrupted segment: a melee hit can add 1d6 per 10 feet of that segment."},{"level":6,"title":"24 Frame Rule","rules":"After an unarmed hit · 3 CE · Deal no damage; the target makes an Intelligence save · On failure it is stunned until the start of your next turn; the first attack that hits before then is automatically critical and applies one penetration step, then the stun ends · On a successful save no CE is refunded."},{"level":11,"title":"Fastest Sorcerer Alive","rules":"Passive · Activation immediately adds 30 feet to speed · At the start of each paid turn add 20 feet, capped at 20 × PB additional feet from this feature; losing Projection clears both acceleration pools · Dexterity +2 and maximum Dexterity +2 apply only while active."}],"e025":[{"level":1,"title":"Basic Puppet","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Summon the Basic Puppet chassis into an open space within 30 feet · It may carry two Minor traits · All puppets use the base profile, command, and trait rules above."},{"level":3,"title":"Lesser Puppet","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Summon the Lesser Puppet chassis into an open space within 30 feet · It may carry two Minor traits and two Lesser traits · All puppets use the base profile, command, and trait rules above."},{"level":6,"title":"Advanced Puppet","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Summon the Advanced Puppet chassis into an open space within 30 feet · It may carry two Minor traits, two Lesser traits, and two Advanced traits · All puppets use the base profile, command, and trait rules above."},{"level":11,"title":"Absolute Puppet","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Summon the Absolute Puppet chassis (the source’s “Master Puppet”) into an open space within 30 feet · It may carry two Minor, two Lesser, two Advanced, and two Absolute traits · All puppets use the base profile, command, and trait rules above."}],"e026":[{"level":1,"title":"Critical Focus","rules":"Passive · Your natural critical range widens by one, and every critical carries one extra base weapon/unarmed die · Combines with other wideners to a maximum natural range of 18–20 · “Damage dice” means the attack’s base weapon or unarmed die, not every rider die."},{"level":3,"title":"Ratio","rules":"After an attack hits, before damage · 1 CE: roll a d10 — a 3 or 7 makes that hit critical · Additional CE up to your CE modifier adds one d10 each, paid before rolling · Multiple qualifying dice make only one critical · From level 3 a critical adds two extra base weapon/unarmed dice."},{"level":6,"title":"Collapse","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Destroy the ground in a 30-foot circle centered on a ground point you touch (not necessarily on your body) · It becomes difficult terrain until repaired · Roll unarmed damage once plus 3d10; a failed Dexterity save takes full damage, success takes half · This is a save effect and cannot become critical through Ratio · From level 6 a critical adds three extra base weapon/unarmed dice."},{"level":11,"title":"Improved Ratio","rules":"Passive · Ratio rolls two d10 by default and the hit is critical if any die is 3 or 7 · Additional CE up to your CE modifier adds one d10 each, paid before rolling · Multiple qualifying dice make only one critical · From level 11 a critical adds four extra base weapon/unarmed dice."},{"level":18,"title":"Golden Ratio","rules":"Passive · Every attack that hits is critical, without rolling Ratio or spending its CE · Does not turn a miss into a hit and does not make a save-based feature critical · A qualifying critical may interact with Black Flash under the current Black Flash rules · A critical adds five extra base weapon/unarmed dice."}],"e027":[{"level":1,"title":"Dismantle","rules":"Attack action (replace one attack) · Spend 1 to PB CE per replaced attack · Ranged CE attack, 150/600 ft · On hit: (CE spent)d8 slashing · The cut is invisible: adjacent hostile creatures impose no disadvantage if the target cannot perceive it; long-range disadvantage still applies."},{"level":3,"title":"Cleave","rules":"Action · Spend 1 to 10 CE · Make one ranged CE attack within 150 feet · On hit: (PB + CE spent)d10 slashing, and the target’s structure is marked for 1 minute · A later Cleave hit while marked applies one penetration step: immunity becomes resistance, or resistance is ignored · Further hits add no more steps; a different target begins unadapted."},{"level":6,"title":"Divine Flame: Open","rules":"Action · Spend X CE, from 1 to twice your PB · Choose a point at 150/600 ft; radius 5 × X feet · Xd12 fire damage, Dexterity save for half · The incantation and the projectile are perceptible even when Dismantle is not."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfect Form","rules":"Passive · CE ability, Strength, and Constitution each increase by 2, and their maxima rise by 2 · You gain an extra bonus action (each bonus action must perform a different named feature unless that feature says otherwise) and an extra attack joins the Attack action · Once per turn: waive the charging action of one Maximum Output use · Never waives the CE cost, Technique Focus, level, Output Rank, Burnout, or any fatal consequence; cannot accelerate Domain Expansion."}],"e028":[{"level":1,"title":"Sky Shape","rules":"Reaction · 1 CE · Use after an attack roll targeting you or an ally within reach is seen, before its result: add +4 AC against that attack only (you still have only one reaction, even when Dodge lets you protect an ally) · If a ranged attack misses because of this bonus: make one CE attack against its source if within the original attack’s range — on hit, reroll the original attack’s base damage dice and add its ordinary damage modifier using the original damage type; do not copy a critical, limited-use rider, poison, technique, or condition · If a melee weapon attack misses because of the bonus: the striking limb is unusable until the start of that creature’s next turn (not lasting limb damage)."},{"level":3,"title":"Sky Armor","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · For 1 minute: your AC equals 11 + CE modifier + PB, and you gain flight equal to your walking speed · This is an alternative AC calculation and does not add armor or shield bonuses; you may use a higher legal calculation instead."},{"level":6,"title":"Sky Shape Improvement","rules":"Reaction · 6 CE · When you are included in a cone or line: make its save · On failure, resolve normally · On success, you and every other original target are unaffected, and the same shape is redirected from your space toward its source · The source makes its own save against the original DC and damage · A redirected effect cannot be redirected again."},{"level":11,"title":"Thin Ice Breaker","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Every creature in a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide line makes a Dexterity saving throw · Flying grants disadvantage only on the initial save · Failure: (CE modifier)d10 force damage and falls prone; success: half damage and remains standing."}],"e029":[{"level":1,"title":"Forbidden Zone","rules":"Full action · 1 CE · Create a fixed 30-foot-radius sphere centered on your space · Lasts 1 minute using Technique Focus · A creature you regard as an ally has advantage on all its d20 rolls only while inside · Changing allegiance after activation does not change who qualifies."},{"level":3,"title":"Bless","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Choose one willing creature within 60 feet · For up to 1 minute using Technique Focus: it has the Zone’s advantage while on the same plane · Because both use Technique Focus, you cannot sustain Bless and a separate Zone simultaneously."},{"level":6,"title":"Arena","rules":"Passive · Each allied damage roll made inside the Zone adds your CE modifier (minimum 0) · When a hostile creature attempts to cross the Zone boundary in either direction, willingly or through forced movement, it makes a Charisma save; on failure 5 feet of movement is spent and it remains on the original side · One creature saves at most once per turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximize Output","rules":"Passive · When the Zone begins, choose one allied creature inside · The first time on each of its turns that it rolls damage for a CE attack or CE save effect, it may treat that feature’s printed base damage dice as maximum; critical, Black Flash, item, and other added dice are still rolled · Change the chosen ally as a bonus action."}],"e030":[{"level":1,"title":"Virtual Mass Increase","rules":"Bonus action · Spend mass points in CE: up to your CE modifier (minimum 0) at activation · Lasts your CE modifier in rounds (minimum one) · Cannot be dismissed or activated again until that duration ends · Every two mass points step the unarmed die once along 1 → d4 → d6 → d8 → d10 → d12 → 2d8, which is the ceiling · Add +1 to every unarmed damage roll per mass point spent · For grapples, count one size larger per point, maximum Gargantuan; your occupied space and reach do not change · Ability checks and carrying capacity use your actual statistics; virtual size affects only grapple/shove eligibility · Extreme mass does not break floors or structures unless the GM determines the fiction calls for it. · Passive · On an unarmed critical, the struck target makes a Constitution save · At 1+ mass, failure knocks it prone · At 2+ mass, creatures of your choice in a 5-foot cone directly behind it take the same attack damage once, excluding target-only riders; the cone is oriented directly away from you through the target · At 3+ mass, failure also halves its speed until your next turn; at 4+ mass its speed becomes 0 instead · A creature takes this copied damage only once per attack, and the copied damage cannot itself critical, trigger Black Flash, or create another cone."},{"level":3,"title":"Improved Duration","rules":"Passive · Virtual mass now lasts twice your CE modifier in rounds (minimum one)."},{"level":6,"title":"Virtual Mass Improvement","rules":"Passive · You may now spend up to twice your CE modifier in mass points when activating virtual mass."},{"level":11,"title":"Virtual Mass Mastery","rules":"Passive · You may now spend up to four times your CE modifier in mass points when activating virtual mass."}],"e031":[{"level":1,"title":"Nail Projectile","rules":"Action · 1 CE + 2 nails · Two ranged CE attacks at 20/60 ft · +4 CE and 2 more nails: two more attacks."},{"level":3,"title":"Resonance","rules":"Reaction · When a creature within 30 ft takes slashing or piercing damage: Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) vs its AC · On success: pay 3 CE, bind its link into your straw doll (1 target, 1 minute) · Once per turn (action): strike the doll, auto-hit, fragment consumed — Minor: PBd6 + disadvantage on attacks to end of next turn · Medium: (CE modifier + PB)d8, no reactions to end of next turn · Major: (2× CE modifier + PB)d10 + repeating Constitution save (your CE save DC) vs stun, retried at end of each of its turns."},{"level":6,"title":"Hairpin","rules":"Bonus action · X CE (X = 1 to PB) · Plant X nails in one object within reach, 1 hour · Bonus action (or reaction when a creature comes within 5 ft): pay X CE again to detonate — 10-ft radius, Dexterity save, 6d8 + (X − 1)d8 force, half on success."},{"level":10,"title":"Nail Recovery","rules":"Bonus action · Touch an embedded nail's target: DC 10 Charisma check · On success: recover that one nail."},{"level":11,"title":"Improved Resonance","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Melee CE attack vs a creature with a listed condition (incapacitated, restrained, stunned, petrified, paralyzed) · On hit: prone, printed damage, and 1-minute CE suppression · Repeat the Charisma save (no disadvantage) at the end of each turn · On a failed activation save: CE is spent, feature fails."},{"level":18,"title":"Resonance: maximum HP reduction","rules":"Passive (level 18+) · Resonance damage also reduces the target's maximum HP by the same amount until a long rest."}],"e032":[{"level":1,"title":"Extinguishment","rules":"Action · 1 CE · One perceived creature within 60 ft: Charisma save · Failure: 2d12 radiant (levels 1–5) + cannot cast spells, spend CE, activate an Innate Technique, or maintain Technique Focus for up to 1 minute · Success: half damage, no suppression · Save repeats at end of each turn · May suppress any number of targets; same-name effects don't stack."},{"level":3,"title":"Angel’s Blessing","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Flying speed = half walking speed for 1 minute (wings of light, halo); extend 1 minute for 1 CE, no action · Resistance to radiant damage · Passing a barrier costs 5 ft of movement; works on curtains/spell barriers of PB level or lower · Barrier keyed against you: CE ability check vs its DC."},{"level":6,"title":"Improved Extinguishment","rules":"Passive · Extinguishment now deals 5d12 radiant · While suppressed, the target's worn/carried magic and cursed items are suppressed (bonuses, spells, charges, attunement off; items intact and attuned) · Artifacts suppressed 1 round at a time."},{"level":13,"title":"Maximum Output improvement","rules":"Passive · Maximum Output: Jacob's Ladder radius becomes 30 ft · Evasion-like zero-damage results denied."},{"level":18,"title":"Garden of Eden","rules":"Domain (autonomous purge) · At initiative 20: every chosen hostile automatically takes 8d10 radiant and loses its Innate Technique + CE-granted features until the next initiative 20 · Protected creature: Charisma save for half damage, no suppression."}],"e033":[{"level":1,"title":"First Core","rules":"Passive · +1 maximum HP per character level, including levels already gained · Recalculated when total level changes."},{"level":3,"title":"Second Core","rules":"Choice (remade only when you gain a level) · Bonus action: activate one form until you switch, fall unconscious, or seal the core · Unblockable Blows: after a hit, 1 CE — immunity→resistance, resistance ignored, or vulnerability · Energy Blast: action, X CE (1–PB), one ranged CE attack at 120 ft, Xd6 force on hit · Defensive Form: on activation and as a bonus action while active, X CE (1–PB), gain 5×X temporary HP."},{"level":6,"title":"Third Core","rules":"Choice (remade only when you gain a level) · Choose a different one of the three Second Core forms · Same three forms and same rules."},{"level":11,"title":"Insurance","rules":"Reaction · When reduced to 0 HP but not killed outright: seal one unsealed selected form for 7 full days and return to half maximum HP · A sealed form can't activate, insure again, or benefit from the Domain · If both cores sealed: Insurance unavailable."}],"e034":[{"level":1,"title":"Partial Manifestation","rules":"Once per turn · After you make at least one attack: pay 1 CE · The spirit makes melee CE attacks vs creatures within 10 ft of you — 1 at level 1, 2 at level 3, 3 at level 6, 4 at level 10 · 1d12 slashing each on hit · Spirit untargetable during the flash. · Passive · The bound object grants the cursed-energy-enhanced weapon benefit · If destroyed: Partial and Full Manifestation unavailable until a replacement is bound (long rest)."},{"level":3,"title":"Involuntary Full Manifestation","rules":"Trigger · After one damage instance exceeds your level + CE modifier: DC 20 Wisdom save · Failure: the spirit manifests in an open space within 10 ft and acts after you · Before level 6 it is berserk (attacks the last creature to damage you or the closest other creature) · Once per turn (no action): Persuasion check to dismiss."},{"level":6,"title":"Controlled window / Mimicry","rules":"From level 6: on a failed trigger the spirit obeys you for CE modifier rounds (min 1), then dismisses · Mimicry (while fully manifested): bonus action, command a claw attack vs a creature · On hit: DNA trace; CE ability check vs 10 + half the feature's base CE cost, rounded up (DC 10 if no cost) · Success: store that Innate Technique's base non-passive feature (max CE modifier stored, min 1; replace when over capacity) · Copied features usable only during full manifestation."},{"level":10,"title":"Voluntary Manifestation","rules":"Once per turn (no action) · Manifest the spirit for 1 minute (danger triggers no longer force a save) · Uses = half CE modifier rounded down (min 1) per long rest; one use returns on a short rest · Controlled spirit follows one simple spoken order; without orders it Dodges and protects you."},{"level":11,"title":"Stronger Bond","rules":"Passive · Choose two spirit ability scores +2 (including maxima) · While manifested: your CE ability and maximum +2; current CE +2 on entry, −2 when it leaves (no farming) · Spirit gains temporary HP = half your current HP on arrival."}],"e035":[{"level":1,"title":"Divine Dogs","rules":"Passive · Begin with the paired Divine Dogs already tamed · 1 CE each to manifest; together they count as one manifestation sharing one action and reaction · Normal capacity: one manifestation."},{"level":3,"title":"Trial Unlock & Expanded Manifestation","rules":"Passive · Taming ritual unlocks at 3rd level: challenge any untamed shadow on the full roster (no higher level gate; listed CE cost, no-outside-aid rule, and the waiting creature are the gates) · Normal manifestation capacity increases to two. · Action · Pay the shikigami's listed CE cost · It appears at full HP in an unoccupied space within 30 ft; roll initiative; it treats you as its primary enemy · Reduce it to 0 HP without outside aid to tame it permanently (an interferer becomes a participant and a valid target) · CE is spent even if the ritual fails. · Passive · Mahoraga uses its complete CR 25 stat block during and after taming — no diminished player version."},{"level":6,"title":"Shadow Storage","rules":"Object interaction: store or retrieve one object you carry (weight still counts; must fit a 5-ft opening; can't be worn/carried by an unwilling creature) · 1 CE: retrieve as a reaction, or emerge it from a visible shadow within 30 ft."},{"level":8,"title":"Shadow Wearing","rules":"Bonus action · Spend half the shikigami's normal summon cost, rounded up (min 1 CE) · Draw a tamed, available, unmanifested shikigami's shadow over your body for 1 minute (ends early: unconscious, dismissed, or another form) · One worn at a time; wearing is not a manifestation and uses no slot · Worn shadow can't be manifested or fused. · Passive · Shadow Wearing attacks use your CE attack bonus; saves use your CE save DC · Uses your action economy; an expended once-per-activation ability returns only on a new activation · Not a second creature or separate HP pool."},{"level":11,"title":"Wells Unknown Abyss","rules":"Action · Merge two manifested shikigami through one of fifteen predetermined recipes (no extra CE) · Fusion occupies one slot; components can't exist separately · Bonus action: undo (no HP regained) · If the fusion reaches 0 HP: both components die permanently and qualify for the Totality ritual · Normal capacity increases to three."},{"level":17,"title":"Wheel Wearing","rules":"Prerequisite: 17th level, Shadow Wearing, Mahoraga tamed and available · Bonus action · 10 CE · Wear Mahoraga's shadow for 1 minute, once per long rest (locks Mahoraga as source). · No action (trigger) · When you take damage or fail a save vs a phenomenon: open an adaptation track (maintain up to PB) · At end of your turn, advance one exposed track one turn (max once per round) · 1 turn: advantage on saves/checks vs that effect · 2 turns: resistance, or advantage + limited removal · 3 turns: immunity (or ignore/counter) for the rest of Wheel Wearing. · Quick Adaptation: reaction · 3 CE · Advance one existing track immediately (PB times per long rest) · General's Recovery: at start of your turn regain PB + CE modifier HP · Executioner's Edge: once per turn, +3d12 radiant on a melee hit vs a cursed spirit or undead · When the form ends: no Shadow Wearing, Mahoraga, or fusions until end of your next turn; 3+ completed tracks: 1 exhaustion."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Chimera Shadow Garden","rules":"Domain · Interior becomes a fluid-shadow garden: difficult terrain for creatures of your choice; you gain freedom of movement benefits. · Domain sure-hit · At initiative 20: chosen hostile creatures touching the Domain's surfaces are automatically restrained until the next initiative 20 · Protected creature: Strength save to avoid · Restrained creature may use its action for a Strength check vs your CE save DC to end early. · Shadow Clones: bonus action · Spend up to CE modifier CE for that many clones (your AC, 1 HP, your speed, no attacks or class features) · Reaction before damage: swap with a clone within 60 ft, making it the target · Shikigami Copies: once per round when manifesting a non-Mahoraga shikigami, create one perfect temporary copy free · In the Domain: shikigami manifest for 0 CE; free manifestations and copies vanish when the Domain ends."}],"e036":[{"level":1,"title":"Siphon","rules":"Passive · Three consecutive qualifying hits (Siphon Counter 3) steal CE · Target loses up to PB current CE (incl. Temporary CE); you gain the amount lost as Temporary CE · Temporary CE cap = 4 × character level. · Trigger · When the Siphon Counter reaches 3: target loses up to PB current CE (incl. Temporary CE); you gain the amount actually lost as Temporary CE · A target with only 1 CE supplies only 1 CE. · Passive · Temporary CE cap = 4 × character level · Multiple chains can fill it in one combat."},{"level":3,"title":"Siphon Tap","rules":"Overview · Siphon Tap: bonus action, spend Temporary CE to add force damage to your strikes until end of turn (see next card). · Bonus action · Spend up to PB Temporary CE · Until end of your turn: qualifying strikes deal +1d6 force damage per 2 Temporary CE spent."},{"level":6,"title":"Blood on the Sand","rules":"Overview · Domain: full-turn action, 10 CE (need 5 Temporary CE), 60-ft radius, 1 minute · Siphon threshold becomes 2 hits · Arena Tribute feeds the Pool. · Full-turn action · 10 CE · 60-ft radius, 1 minute · Must have 5 Temporary CE before paying (not an extra payment). · Victory · If you're the last active competitor: cash out the Colosseum Pool, gain Victor's Momentum (uncapped Cashout Score), avoid Burnout, obtain one Colosseum Spoil. · Passive · Siphon threshold becomes 2 consecutive qualifying hits. · Inside the Domain · When Siphon triggers: choose Temporary CE or Tribute · Tribute: stolen CE goes to the Pool; target loses Gladiator HP = half that amount, rounded up · If it had 0 CE before the drain: loses Gladiator HP = your PB instead. · Victory · If you're the last active competitor: cash out the Pool as an uncapped Cashout Score · Absorb Temporary CE up to cap (excess empowers Momentum, then disappears) · Gain the complete package for your Cashout Score for 1 minute. · Spoils · Roll once after a caster victory (an 18th-level option may change this) · A Spoil lasts 1 minute, until dismissed, or until you're unconscious · Weapon Spoils are cursed tools · An Arena Beast is an independent shikigami taking a turn immediately after yours · Emperor's Favor extends a Spoil (and a beast's manifestation) to 10 minutes."},{"level":11,"title":"Roar of the Crowd","rules":"Overview · Domain improves: 8 CE (4 Temporary required), 90-ft radius, 2 CE drain per pulse · During Victor's Momentum: expand as an action; an Encore starts with 5 CE in the Pool · Ovation Siphon: Arena Tribute adds Favor to the Pool. · Domain expansion · 8 CE (4 Temporary CE required) · 90-ft radius · 2 CE drain per pulse. · During Victor's Momentum · Expand as an action · An Encore begins with 5 CE already in the Pool. · Passive · Arena Tribute adds bonus CE to the Pool = current Favor (min 1, max PB)."},{"level":18,"title":"Emperor of the Living Dead","rules":"Overview · Once per turn Siphon grants an extra attack · Grand Amphitheater: 6 CE (3 Temporary), 120-ft radius, 3 CE per pulse; Encore as a bonus action · Imperial Tribute feeds the Pool; improved Spoils; two Arena Beasts. · Passive · Once per turn when Siphon triggers: make one additional weapon or unarmed attack as part of the same action. · Domain expansion · 6 CE (3 Temporary CE required) · 120-ft radius · 3 CE drain per pulse · Encore Casting becomes a bonus action. · Passive · An Encore begins with 10 CE plus the previous Domain's final Gladiator Favor. · Inside the Domain · Siphon grants Temporary CE = CE actually stolen AND adds that same amount to the Pool. · After victory · Choose any one Spoil, roll twice and gain both, or roll once and make that Spoil last 10 minutes · Maintain two Spoils (dismiss one before gaining a third). · Passive · At level 18 you may maintain two Arena Beasts at once (see Arena Bestiary)."}],"e037":[{"level":1,"title":"Wind-Up Engine","rules":"Overview · Bonus action, 1 CE: Kinetic Transmission for 1 minute · Begin at Gear = PB; +1 at turn end for moving 15 ft and +1 for hitting a hostile creature · Spend Gear on Acceleration Shift (15 ft per Gear), Impact Shift (+1 Drive Die + CE modifier, 10-ft push per Gear), or Brake Shift. · Bonus action · 1 CE · Kinetic Transmission for 1 minute · Begin at Gear = PB · At turn end gain 1 for moving 15 ft and 1 for hitting a hostile creature. · Spend Gear · Acceleration Shift: 15 ft of movement per Gear · Impact Shift: +1 Drive Die + CE modifier damage and 10 ft of push per Gear. · Passive · Your Drive Die is a d6."},{"level":3,"title":"Clutch Control","rules":"Overview · End-of-turn generation becomes 3 Gears (moved 15 ft and hit) · Impact Shift usable multiple times per turn · Inertial Footwork after Acceleration Shift · Brake Shift: reaction to reduce damage, forced movement, or falling. · Passive · If you moved at least 15 ft and hit a hostile creature: gain 3 Gears at turn end instead of 2. · Passive · You may use Impact Shift more than once per turn · Each use lowers Gear separately; Current Gear is the only limit. · Passive · After using Acceleration Shift: difficult terrain costs no extra movement, change direction freely, cross liquids and vertical surfaces, opportunity attacks against you have disadvantage. · Reaction · When you take damage or are forcibly moved: lower Gear by X · Per Gear, choose: reduce damage by 1 Drive Die + CE modifier; reduce forced movement by 15 ft; or reduce effective falling distance by 30 ft · Different Gears may choose different options."},{"level":6,"title":"Velocity Override","rules":"Overview · Mark creatures/objects on hit or touch (up to PB, 1 minute) · Bonus action (or reaction when a marked target moves, falls, or attacks): 3 CE + lower Gear; target within 120 ft · Up-Shift: move 20 ft per Gear · Down-Shift: slow, −AC/Dex saves, restrain at 0 speed. · No action · When you hit a creature, or touch a willing creature or object: mark it for 1 minute · Maintain up to PB marks (exceeding ends one of your choice). · Bonus action, or reaction when a marked target moves, falls, or attacks · 3 CE + lower Gear by X · Target within 120 ft · Unwilling creature: Constitution save. · Move the target 20 ft per Gear in any direction, no opportunity attacks · Solid collision: 2 Drive Dice per Gear, knocked prone · Creature collision: other creature makes a Dexterity save — failure: collision damage and both prone. · Speed −15 ft per Gear until the beginning of your next turn · Target can't react; AC and Dexterity saves −1 per Gear (max PB) · At speed 0: restrained for the duration. · Passive · Your Drive Die is a d8."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfect Transmission & Redline","rules":"Overview · Strength, Dexterity, and CE scores and maxima +2 · Once per turn: regain 1 Gear after a Shift · Redline: bonus action, 10 CE, set Gear to 10 for PB rounds; when it ends: 2 Drive Dice per round of force (ignores resistance/immunity/reduction), 1 exhaustion, Transmission ends, Technique Burnout. · Passive · Strength, Dexterity, and CE scores and maxima +2 · Once per turn after an ordinary Acceleration, Impact, Brake, or Override Shift lowers Gear: regain 1 of the Gears spent (not Burn Out, Dead Ignition, or Relativistic Break). · Bonus action · 10 CE · Set Current Gear to 10 · Redline lasts PB rounds; Current Gear returns to 10 at the beginning of each of your turns. · While Redline is active · Speed tripled; movement doesn't provoke · Move across vertical surfaces, liquids, and open air; stop/reverse instantly · Can't be forcibly moved unless you choose · +1 action for one attack, Dash, Disengage, or Use an Object · Once per turn: Velocity Override with no CE or action (Gear still lowers) · Once per round: Brake Shift without your reaction (Gear still lowers). · Passive · When Redline ends: take 2 Drive Dice of force per round it remained active (ignores resistance, immunity, and reduction) · Gain 1 exhaustion level · Kinetic Transmission ends; normal Technique Burnout. · Passive · Your Drive Die is a d10."},{"level":18,"title":"First Ignition","rules":"Overview · Prerequisite: personally witness or correctly diagnose an open-barrier Domain · Reaction when you perceive another creature begin Domain Expansion: pay 20 CE to answer with Zugzwang Engine; afterward you may expand it normally (full-turn action). · Prerequisite · You must personally witness or correctly diagnose an open-barrier Domain · Level 18 provides the output; the observed Domain provides the blueprint. · Reaction · When you perceive another creature begin Domain Expansion: pay 20 CE to answer with Zugzwang Engine (resolve clash normally) · Afterward, expand it normally with a full-turn action. · Passive · Your Drive Die is a d12."}],"e038":[{"level":1,"title":"Directive Arrows","rules":"Overview · Bonus action, 1 CE: create PB arrows within 60 ft (1 minute; up to 2×PB active) · Activate up to PB per turn to move 20 ft each · Vector Edge: +1d6 force per arrow activated (max PBd6) after a weapon hit. · Bonus action · 1 CE · Create PB arrows within 60 ft · Last 1 minute without Technique Focus · Maintain up to 2 × PB active arrows. · Each activation moves you 20 ft · Activate up to PB arrows during a turn · An arrow is expended when activated unless a later feature says otherwise. · Once per turn · After a weapon attack hits: add 1d6 force per arrow you activated that turn (max PBd6) · Must use a weapon attack roll."},{"level":3,"title":"Quick Inscription & Acceleration Sphere","rules":"Overview · Once per turn after a weapon hit: inscribe one free arrow (no action, no CE) · Acceleration Sphere: action — PB temporary arrows around one target within 60 ft, sequence repeated PB times. · Once per turn · Immediately after you hit with a weapon attack: create one Directive Arrow (no action, no CE) in an unoccupied space within 5 ft of you or the target. · Action (not the Attack action) · Choose one creature you can see within 60 ft and a wielded weapon · Conjure PB temporary arrows around the target (don't count against capacity; only you activate them) · Repeat the printed sequence PB times; each leg = one arrow activation for Vector Edge · Temporary arrows vanish when the action finishes; you remain in the final space."},{"level":6,"title":"Living Directives","rules":"Overview · Allies may activate your arrows (up to PB, no Vector Edge unless boosted) · Acceleraise Boost: willing creature, speed +20 ft, bonus Arrow Dice · Imposed Directive: forced movement on failed Strength save · Projectile Redirection: redirect ranged attacks. · A willing creature you permit may activate your arrows on its turn (up to PB activations) · Follows Arrowpath rules; gains no Vector Edge unless affected by Acceleraise Boost. · Choose one willing creature other than you within 60 ft · Until the end of its next turn: speed +20 ft · Once during that duration, after it activates ≥1 of your arrows and hits with a weapon attack: add your Arrow Dice per arrow it activated (max half PB, rounded up) as force damage. · Once per turn · After you hit a creature with a weapon attack: choose a direction, spend 2 CE · Target: Strength save vs your CE save DC · Failure: moved your Arrow Distance without provoking · Solid obstruction: stops, falls prone, takes 1d6 force per 5 ft untraveled (max PBd6) · Another creature: Dexterity save — failure: collision damage + prone; success: half damage, standing. · Reaction · When you see a ranged attack roll against a creature or object within 10 ft of an active arrow (after the roll, before resolution): expend that arrow, spend 1 CE · The attack continues from the arrow's space in the arrow's displayed direction; the first legal creature/object in a 5-ft-wide line within its normal max range becomes the new target (compare the original roll to its AC) · Each attack can be redirected only once."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfect Inscription","rules":"Overview · Placement 120 ft, Arrow Distance 30 ft, Arrow Die d8 · Once per turn: leave an activated arrow active · Unlock Maximum: Dominion of Borrowed Speed (mobile Force Field transferring movement from hostiles to your side). · Passive · Placement range becomes 120 ft; Arrow Distance 30 ft; Arrow Die becomes d8. · Once per turn · When you activate an arrow: you may leave it active instead of expending it (movement resolves normally). · Unlock Maximum Technique: Dominion of Borrowed Speed — a mobile Force Field that transfers movement from hostile creatures to your side."},{"level":18,"title":"Absolute Course","rules":"Overview · Arrow Distance 40 ft, Arrow Die d10, capacity 3×PB · Quick Inscription up to PB times per turn · Routebreaker: free weapon attack after a 3-arrow chain · Domain: Palace of the Predestined Road. · Passive · Arrow Distance becomes 40 ft; Arrow Die becomes d10; active capacity 3 × PB. · Passive · Quick Inscription may occur up to PB times per turn (max once per weapon attack). · Once per turn · After activating ≥3 arrows as one uninterrupted chain: make one weapon attack without an action (not the Attack action; otherwise resolves normally). · Domain · Unlock Palace of the Predestined Road: every point is an arrow; every hostile creature is assigned an unavoidable route."}],"e039":[{"level":1,"title":"First Light","rules":"Overview · Gain Solar Station, Solar Memory, and Cruel Sun · Choose Wisdom or Charisma as the technique's CE ability (if not already chosen). · Passive · Gain Solar Station and Solar Memory as defined above, plus Cruel Sun as defined below · Choose Wisdom or Charisma as the technique's CE ability if the character doesn't already have one. · Passive · Solar Strength floor, initiative temporary HP, and Lion's Heat on melee weapon, unarmed, and natural attacks. · Passive · Rank-scaled flight, per-target solar damage selection, and Solar Infusion on any qualifying attack carrying your CE. · Attack action (replace one attack) · Spend 1 to PB CE · Ranged CE attack, 120/480 ft · On hit: (X+1) Solar Dice + CE modifier fire or radiant damage (choose type when thrown) · Can critically hit and trigger Black Flash."},{"level":3,"title":"A Sun That Moves","rules":"Overview · Pride Flare: bonus action, 2 CE detonation after Cruel Sun (rank-scaled explosion) · Sun-Rider: ride solar fire; count as larger in daylight; Large near noon · Solar Fist: replace an attack with a line of solar force, sparing chosen creatures from Sunshine. · Bonus action · 2 CE · After Cruel Sun resolves: create a rank-scaled explosion (complete procedure in Solar Arsenal). · Passive · Ride solar fire through open space · Count as a larger creature in daylight; become physically Large as noon approaches. · Replace an attack with a line of solar force · Remove chosen creatures from your Sunshine areas."},{"level":6,"title":"The Battlefield Burns","rules":"Overview · Crazy Prominence: multi-sun attack sequence · Immunity to your own Sunshine; daytime fire/radiant resistance · Super Slash: PB melee attacks as one technique action · Sunspot: delayed solar judgment · Orbital Origin: attack origins away from your body. · Passive · Multi-sun attack sequence (Crazy Prominence) · Immune to your own Sunshine · Daytime resistance to fire and radiant damage. · Super Slash: as one technique action, make PB melee attacks · Prideful Endurance: when you take a damaging impact, spend 1 CE to reduce it by 2d12. · Sunspot: plant a delayed solar judgment · Orbital Origin: create attack origins at controlled points away from your body."},{"level":11,"title":"True High Noon","rules":"Overview · Solar Authority: upgrades below (range, dice, resistance-ignoring; immunity becomes resistance at rank 3+) · The One: 1-minute transformation at true Zenith · Perfect Grace: doubled flight, reroll 1s/2s on Solar Dice, Maximum: Greatest Sun. · Passive · Solar Memory no longer uses Technique Focus · Cruel Sun: 300/1,200 ft, X up to 2×PB · Crazy Prominence: +3 Solar Dice per hit, 300-ft range · Solar Fist: 5 Solar Dice · Orbital Origin: 150 ft · Solar Strength floor +2 · Sunshine damage ignores resistance; at rank 3+, fire/radiant immunity becomes resistance. · At true Zenith · Gain the complete 1-minute transformation and its Divine Sword and Divine Spear applications. · Passive · Double Solar Grace flight speed · Reroll each 1 or 2 on Solar Dice once · At rank 4: Solar Infusion on each qualifying hit, up to PB times per turn (1 CE per hit) · Unlock Maximum: Greatest Sun."},{"level":18,"title":"A Calamity Wearing Daylight","rules":"Overview · The One Ultimate: fatal vow — burn maximum HP each round, end in Final Prominence and death · Sun Without Horizon: never below High Sun, one preserved true Zenith, multiplied Solar Infusion, uncapped overcharge · Unbounded Sunshine: Cruel Sun 600/2,400 ft, X uncapped · Unlock your incarnation's Domain. · Passive · Cruel Sun: 600/2,400 ft, X CE uncapped · Crazy Prominence: 600 ft, 4 Solar Dice per hit · Solar Fist: 7 Solar Dice · Orbital Origin: 300 ft · Solar Strength floor +2 · Unlock your incarnation's Domain. · Fatal vow · Refuse the end of The One: burn maximum HP each round, then release Final Prominence before the vessel disappears. · Passive · Never fall below High Sun · Preserve one true Zenith · Multiply Solar Infusion at every station · Overcharge Greatest Sun without a ceiling."}],"e040":[{"level":1,"title":"Loaded Matter","rules":"Overview · Charge inorganic objects (2 Kinetic Dice per Charge) · Loaded Toss, one Bound Conduit, and Fine Charge · Kinetic Die d6. · Passive · 2 Kinetic Dice per Charge · Selectable 5-ft-per-Charge radius · Direct-hit rule and ordinary-object destruction procedure as printed. · Passive · Gain Loaded Toss, one Bound Conduit, and Fine Charge · Your Kinetic Die is d6. · Touch an inorganic object · Spend a positive amount of CE up to the deposit limit for its scale · Object gains that much Charge, up to capacity · Charge lasts 1 minute; no separate active-object cap. · Throw a charged Token or throwable Handheld at a creature within 60/180 ft · Ranged CE attack · Hit: 1 Kinetic Die + CE modifier force, then detonate as direct delivery · Miss: ordinary area detonation at an unoccupied impact point within 10 ft · Thrown weapons/ammunition may use their normal attack, range, and damage; charge still joins a hit. · Touch one inorganic lock, latch, simple machine, power input, or mechanism (≤5-ft cube) · CE ability check vs DC set by construction/security · Success: quietly open, close, power, depower, or move one mechanism for up to 1 minute, no explosion · Failure: nothing changes, CE spent."},{"level":3,"title":"The Loaded Hand","rules":"Overview · Trigger Discipline: timed and commanded detonations · Vector Discharge: convert blast to movement · Kinetic Footwork: +10 ft speed, reposition after your release · Cardsharp Barrage: charge and throw up to PB Tokens as one technique action. · Passive · Unlock timed and commanded detonations in addition to impact. · Spend Charge to launch an object, enemy, ally, or yourself as movement instead of dealing explosive damage. · Passive · +10 ft speed and a short reposition after your own release. · One technique action · Charge and throw up to PB Tokens at once (playing cards are traditional, never mandatory)."},{"level":6,"title":"Saboteur’s Geometry","rules":"Overview · Chain Reaction: one blast detonates every charged object it reaches · Saboteur's Touch: melee CE attack charges hostile equipment · Static Mind: held charge disrupts mind reading, psychic intrusion, and control. · Passive · A blast detonates every charged object it reaches; each resolves as its own paid explosion. · A melee CE attack can charge inorganic equipment carried by an unwilling creature. · Passive · A held charge interferes with mind reading, psychic intrusion, and control."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfect Conversion","rules":"Overview · Kinetic Die d8; charge lasts 10 minutes · Remote Charge: charge within 60 ft, no touch · Advanced Agility: kinetic speed, Evasion, cross walls/water · Maximum: Fifty-Two Pickup (60-ft kill zone) · Trigger Discipline: 1 mile on the same plane; Vector Discharge: 20 ft per Charge. · Passive · Kinetic Die becomes d8 · Charge lasts 10 minutes · Set Piece/Landmark steps may deposit 2 × PB. · Passive · Use charge steps on inorganic objects within 60 ft without touching them. · Passive · Increased kinetic speed; gain Evasion; cross walls or water while moving. · Unlock Maximum: Fifty-Two Pickup — a selectable 60-ft kill zone made from an entire storm of charged Tokens."},{"level":18,"title":"Ambient Mastery","rules":"Overview · Trigger Discipline: anywhere on the same plane (known location) · Vector Discharge: 30 ft per Charge · Remote Charge: 300 ft · Kinetic Die d10, charge 1 hour, mass deposit 3×PB · Ordinary kinetic damage ignores resistance and immunity · Domain: House of the Loaded World. · Passive · Kinetic Die becomes d10 · Charge lasts 1 hour · Mass deposit 3 × PB · Ordinary kinetic damage ignores resistance and immunity. · Passive · Remote range becomes 300 ft · One no-action allocation loads several unattended objects each turn. · Command any number of charges together · Ride self-generated motion through the air. · Domain · Unlock House of the Loaded World (the optional New Sun module remains a separate Tier V decision)."}],"e041":[{"level":1,"title":"Bungee Gum","rules":"Action · 1 CE · CE-ability attack vs a creature, object, or surface within 60 ft; on hit: strand sticks (up to 3). Strands stretch 60 ft; contract/extend/detach at will (no action). Bonus action: contract a strand anchored to something heavier: pull yourself 30 ft (no opportunity attacks) or pull a stuck creature 15 ft (Str save negates)."},{"level":3,"title":"Texture Surprise","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Touch a surface or object: change its apparent texture until dismissed or long rest. Investigation vs your CE save DC sees through; touch alone doesn't betray it."},{"level":6,"title":"Slingshot","rules":"Passive · Slingshot movement 90 ft; fling a willing creature or object up to 60 ft along a strand (same bonus action); flung object: improvised ranged attack, 2d8 bludgeoning on hit. Strand anchored overhead: no falling damage."},{"level":11,"title":"Web of Strings","rules":"Passive · Up to 6 strands; feel vibrations on any strand within 120 ft (size, number, direction); creatures touching the web can't surprise you. Bonus action: contract any number of strands."},{"level":18,"title":"Prosthetic Gum","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · When damage would drop you to 0 HP: drop to 1 HP instead. 1 CE: grow a gum prosthetic (hand, foot, eye); restores function for 24 hours."},{"level":20,"title":"Post-Mortem Heartbeat","rules":"Once per long rest · If you die (body not destroyed): return to life at half max HP after 1 minute."}],"e042":[{"level":1,"title":"Prayer Palm","rules":"Attack action (replace one attack) · 1 CE each · Ranged CE attack within Palm Reach (60 ft); on hit: Prayer Die (d6) + CE mod force/radiant + intention effect (Driving: hurl 30 ft; Grasping: grapple; Focused: harder hit). Requires one free hand and a prayer gesture."},{"level":3,"title":"Prayer Before Violence","rules":"Reaction · 1 CE + Palm cost · When a perceived creature within Palm Reach declares an attack, movement, or technique: answer with a Palm before it resolves; if it removes the activation's conditions, the declared action is expended. Third Hand: Converging Mercy: action · 3 CE · two ranged CE attacks vs one creature in Reach; each hit: Prayer Dice force/radiant + move 10 ft; both hit: restrained until start of your next turn (escape: action, Athletics/Acrobatics/CE-ability check vs CE save DC)."},{"level":6,"title":"Faster Than Sound","rules":"Passive · Prayer Die d8, Palm Reach 120 ft. Bonus action · 1 CE · After an Attack action containing a Palm: one additional Palm."},{"level":11,"title":"Prayer of the Heart","rules":"Passive · Prayer Die d10, Palm Reach 300 ft; no free hand needed; vector origins ignore half/three-quarters cover. Ninety-Ninth Hand: action · CE = PB · 2×PB ranged CE attacks within Reach; each hit: 2 Prayer Dice force/radiant and move the target 5 ft along any vector."},{"level":18,"title":"Hundredfold Response","rules":"Passive · Reactions per round = PB (first unrestricted; rest on Guanyin features only; max one Guanyin reaction per creature's turn). Guarding Palm: reaction · 1 CE · when you or a creature in Reach takes damage: reduce by Prayer Dice + CE mod, then move a willing protected creature 10 ft along a vector."},{"level":20,"title":"Prayer Outside Time","rules":"Passive · Prayer Die d12, Palm Reach 600 ft. Start of each turn: one ordinary Palm, no action or CE."}],"e044":[{"level":1,"title":"The first four names","rules":"Level 1 setup · Create four Regalia with the GM; three may be active at once; learn Household Answer. · Creation rite (with GM) · Create four Regalia with names, appearances, Vows, personalities, and vessel forms. · Passive · Up to three active Regalia (weapons, passives, or mounts); still only your own actions and hands. · 10-minute rite · 3 CE · A willing unclaimed soul you can perceive; on acceptance it becomes your Regalia (name, Vow, vessel form chosen; telepathy on the same plane). · No action · 1 CE · Once per turn, after a Regalia weapon hit or Art resolves: apply a different active Regalia’s Concord to that activation (one Answer per activation; no Regalia answers twice per turn)."},{"level":3,"title":"Borderline","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Draw a 30-ft line between two seen points within 60 ft; until the start of your next turn, the first hostile to touch or cross: Strength save or 6 × PB force + returned to its original side + speed 0 for the turn (half damage and crosses on success). · Passive · Active Limit becomes 5."},{"level":6,"title":"The Guidepost","rules":"Level 6 · Appoint a Guidepost; first Household Answer each round is free; swap one Regalia as no action once per turn; Sky Lion gains a 60-ft flying speed. · Long-rest appointment · While the Guidepost is active: add your CE modifier (min +1) to initiative; you cannot be surprised while conscious. Bonus action · 1 CE · Designate a quarry for 1 hour with Focus: know its direction and distance on the same plane; your Regalia attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover against it. · Passive · The first Household Answer you use each round costs 0 CE. · No action · Once on each of your turns: call, dismiss, or exchange one Regalia. · Passive · An active Sky Lion gains a 60-ft flying speed (still uses your movement; carries only what its form permits). · Passive · Active Limit becomes 7."},{"level":11,"title":"Blessed Vessel","rules":"Level 11 · Gain the Hafuri Vessel (story-earned), Sacrificial Bloom, and Sevenfold Muster; Borderline’s line may be 60 ft and last up to 1 minute with Technique Focus, triggering on the first hostile each turn. · Story-earned (GM-agreed breakthrough event) · One Regalia becomes Blessed: Integrity doubles, gains its form’s Blessed benefit, and may supply Art and Concord in the same activation. · Reaction · Once per long rest · When you would drop to 0 HP while your Blessed Vessel is active: it becomes Broken, you stay at 1 HP and gain 5 × PB temporary HP. · Action · 5 CE · Choose up to PB+1 different active Regalia: each makes one CE attack vs targets within 120 ft; hit: 1d8 damage of a type fitting its form; add CE modifier to one hit only. · Passive · Active Limit becomes 8."},{"level":18,"title":"Sovereign Household","rules":"Level 18 · Active Limit 10; reset your full active loadout at the start of each turn (no action/CE); Sevenfold Muster becomes Tenfold; a second Blessed Vessel; two Answers per turn; Domain unlock. · Passive · Active Limit becomes 10; at the start of each of your turns reset your entire active loadout (no action or CE). Sevenfold Muster becomes Tenfold Muster (up to ten different active Regalia). · Passive · A second Regalia may become Blessed after its own breakthrough event (keeps its own form benefit and Sacrificial Bloom use). · No action · 1 CE each · Twice per turn: Household Answer after two different activations, naming two different Regalia (first Answer of the round remains free via Coordination). · Unlock Domain · Golden Citadel of Ten Thousand Names."}],"e045":[{"level":1,"title":"Dimension at Your Fingertips","rules":"Level 1 toolkit · Panel Strike, Panel Step, Paper Defense, Fold the Panel · Snap Range 60 ft · Reality Die d6 · Active Edit capacity PB. · Attack action (replace one attack) · 1 CE · Weapon/unarmed attack (that bonus or CE attack bonus) or ranged CE attack within Snap Range: normal damage + 2 RD (melee) or 2 RD + CE modifier force (ranged) · After either hit: move the target 20 ft along a legal path, make it Planar until your next turn, or turn one nonmagical held object into harmless paper until its next turn. · Bonus action · 1+ CE · Teleport 30 ft to a seen unoccupied space, a point reflected in a visible image, or a point on a contiguous surface; each extra CE (max PB) adds 10 ft; +1 CE brings one willing adjacent creature. · Reaction · 2 CE · When you take damage: reduce it by PB RD + CE modifier, become Planar and move up to 15 ft along a surface (no opportunity attacks); reduced to 0: the triggering attack or effect misses, no on-hit riders. · Bonus action · 2 CE · One Planar creature or object within Snap Range: Strength save or PB RD + CE modifier force, folded hand-sized and restrained until the end of your next turn (half damage, no fold on success)."},{"level":3,"title":"The Scene Supplies Its Own Props","rules":"Level 3 toolkit · Prop Extraction (Action, 1–5 CE: pull a 3D copy from an image, up to Huge, 1 hour), Matter Recast (Action, 3+ CE: transform a nonliving object, 10 min), Perfect Trajectory (once per turn, 1 CE: reroll a missed ranged attack or bend forced movement). · Action · 1–5 CE · Active Edit · Pull a 3D copy from an image of a nonliving object (touch or within Snap Range): Tiny 1, Small 2, Medium 3, Large 4, Huge 5 · Lasts 1 hour, AC 15, 10 HP per CE spent; mundane functions only. · Action · 3+ CE · Active Edit · Transform one nonliving object within Snap Range into a different object of equal or smaller size for 10 minutes (Large or smaller at 3, +1 size per extra CE to Gargantuan); attended objects make a Dexterity save with the holder’s bonus; recast weapons use your CE attack bonus and deal 3 RD + CE modifier. · Once per turn · 1 CE · After a ranged attack, Panel Strike, thrown prop, or forced movement misses: reroll the attack or bend the forced movement around corners (remaining distance kept); a rerolled hit may continue 15 ft into an unattended object or structure for the same rolled dice, no flat modifier."},{"level":6,"title":"Scene Transition","rules":"Level 6 · Style Shift, Freeze Frame, Private Panel Battlespace · Snap Range 120 ft · Reality Die d8 · Panel Step distance doubled. · Bonus action · 3 CE · Active Edit · For 1 minute, switch once per turn (no action) between Ink Form (Planar without penalties, surface movement, one-inch gaps, ungrappleable without CE, resist bludgeoning/piercing/slashing) and Rendered Form (flying speed = walking speed, +2 AC, once per turn +2 RD to one damaging attack or technique). · Reaction · 3 CE · When a creature within Snap Range begins movement, declares an action, or becomes the target of an effect: suspend it (willing auto; unwilling Intelligence save or it vanishes, its turn ends, activity committed but unresolved); returns at the start of its next turn and resolves the suspended activity first if legal. · Action · 6 CE · Technique Focus · Active Edit · 30-ft-radius area within Snap Range, up to PB creatures (willing auto, hostile Charisma save): 2D pocket scene for 3 rounds; effects cannot cross the boundary; inside, orient gravity per surface at each turn’s start and Panel Step between any two visible points for 0 CE."},{"level":11,"title":"Fourth-Dimensional Access","rules":"Level 11 · Energy Recast, Continuity Edit, Cross-Scene Cut, Fourth-Dimensional Archive · Snap Range 300 ft · Reality Die d10 · Active Edit capacity 2 × PB. · Reaction · 4 CE · Active Edit · When an attack, projectile, line, cone, or burst would deal damage within 30 ft: CE ability check vs the source’s DC; success: negate damage and riders for all targets, bottled as a prop token (stores type and dice, capped 10 RD + CE modifier). Bonus action within 1 minute: throw it within Snap Range — Dexterity save or stored damage (half), or a 20-ft burst with every creature saving. · Reaction · 5 CE · Once per round · After a perceived d20 is rolled (before narrated): roll 1 RD and add or subtract it. Cannot change the natural face for critical hits, natural 1s, or Black Flash confirmation. · Action · 6+ CE · Teleport to a same-plane location you have visited or currently perceive through live image, recording, reflection, or remote sense; +1 CE each brings up to PB willing creatures within 10 ft. Static image of an unfamiliar destination: DC 15 CE ability check or arrive at a GM-chosen safe point within 1 mile. · Action · 5 CE · Touch a location or object and name a connected event (within the last year): truthful 10-minute reconstruction; ask the GM up to PB factual questions the scene can answer. Shows events, evidence, and spoken words — not thoughts or a guaranteed future."},{"level":18,"title":"The Author Is Present","rules":"Level 18 · Authorial Privilege (once-per-round Rewrites) · Snap Range 600 ft · Reality Die d12 · Panel Step may target any point in Snap Range; Cross-Scene Cut crosses planes (DC 20 check); Archive reaches any point in a target’s history. · Once per round · No action · Even on another creature’s turn: spend the listed CE to apply one Rewrite. Neither an action nor a reaction; interrupts after its trigger, before resolution; extra turns do not refresh it. · Authorial Privilege · Redline Result · 5 CE · After a perceived d20 is rolled (before resolution): set the face to any number 1–20 (counts as natural for crits and natural 1s); the Black Flash confirmation d20 cannot be rewritten. · Authorial Privilege · Cut Turn · 8 CE · When a hostile within Snap Range begins its turn: Charisma save or its turn ends immediately, unused movement, actions, bonus actions, and reactions lost. · Authorial Privilege · Insert Panel · 8 CE · A willing creature within Snap Range immediately takes a full turn, interrupting the current event; no creature receives another inserted turn until the end of its next normal turn. · Authorial Privilege · Reblock Scene · 5 CE · Teleport up to PB creatures or movable objects within Snap Range to legal spaces elsewhere in that range; willing move automatically, hostile Charisma save or stays. · Authorial Privilege · Scene Law · 6 CE · A 60-ft-radius scene around a point within Snap Range: until the next initiative count 20, one law holds (directional gravity, compressed/extended distance, damage palette swap, or foreground/background cover). · Passive · Active Edit capacity 3 × PB outside your Domain, unlimited inside; perceive and physically interact across your own 2D, 3D, and pocket-dimensional boundaries."}],"e046":[{"level":1,"title":"Starscourge Fundamentals","rules":"Level 1 · Gain Gravity Mark, Vector Command, Gravity Collision, Redmane Weight (Gravitas); any wielded weapon can act as a gravity focus (Greatsword Conductor) · Range 30 ft · 2 Gravity Marks. · Foundation · Gain Gravity Mark, Vector Command, Gravity Collision, and Redmane Weight; once per turn, self-mark without a save or action as part of activating the technique. · Passive · Any weapon you wield can act as a gravity focus: once per turn on a weapon hit, spend 1 CE to place a Gravity Mark on the target after damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Starcaller Arts","rules":"Level 3 · Starcaller Cry, Collapsing Stars, Cragblade · Range 60 ft · 3 Gravity Marks. · Action · 3 CE · Creatures of your choice in a 20-ft-radius sphere within 60 ft: Strength saves; failure: pulled up to 30 ft toward the center and knocked prone; success: moved 10 ft, no prone. · Action · 2 CE · Create PB violet gravity orbs; each makes a ranged CE attack within 90 ft; hit: 2d8 force and a 10-ft pull. Several orbs may strike one target. · Bonus action · 2 CE · 1 minute · Coat one weapon in gravity stone: once per turn after hitting a marked creature, force a Strength save; failure pushes or pulls it 10 ft without spending Vector Command."},{"level":6,"title":"General of the Battlefield","rules":"Level 6 · Conqueror’s Orbit, Meteor Sling, Weightless Step · Range 90 ft · PB Gravity Marks. · Reaction · 2 CE · When a physical projectile or line attack crosses within 20 ft: redirect one orbiting marked projectile or object (up to Huge) into its path, imposing disadvantage on the attack or granting +PB to the relevant save. · Action · 4 CE · Hurl up to PB marked unattended objects within range at creatures or spaces within 120 ft: one CE attack per object; hit: 3d8 bludgeoning/force; a Large or larger object also knocks prone on a failed Strength save. · No action · Once per turn: command one self-mark to leap, hover, or move up to 20 ft in any direction (gravity-assisted movement, not teleportation)."},{"level":11,"title":"Lord of the Wailing Dunes","rules":"Level 11 · Absolute Vector, Orbital Arsenal, Maximum: Festival of Falling Stars · Range 150 ft · PB+2 Gravity Marks. · Passive · Vector Command now moves failed-save creatures 30 + 5 × PB ft; Huge creatures gain no special size benefit; Gargantuan creatures keep only advantage. · Passive · Up to PB marked objects remain in orbit without Technique Focus; once per turn when you attack, launch one orbiting object as part of the same action: 2d8 damage on a hit. · Action · 10 CE · Focus · 1 minute · Create a 60-ft-radius orbital field: at the start of each of your turns form three meteor masses; as a bonus action launch any number, each a 10-ft burst for 4d8 (Dexterity half); unlaunched meteors stay in orbit, maximum nine."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain of the Stars","rules":"Level 18 · Domain Expansion (Wailing Firmament), Consort’s Meteor Rain, Perfect Gravity · Range 300 ft · PB + CE modifier Gravity Marks. · Unlock Domain · Wailing Firmament (Starcaller Cataclysm). · Action · 8 CE · Vanish upward until the start of your next turn (untargetable except by effects that reach your declared altitude/space); on return, choose a point within 300 ft: creatures in a 30-ft radius make Dexterity saves for 8d8 + CE modifier force (half on success), thrown 30 ft on failure. · Passive · Your own Gravity Marks no longer count against your ordinary mark limit; you can stand, run, and stop on open air while the technique is active."},{"level":20,"title":"Prime Conqueror","rules":"Level 20 · Mass Bows to the General, Heaven-Shattering Reentry, Army of One · Range: sight · No ordinary mark cap during Prime Conqueror. · No action · Once per turn: issue Vector Command without an action in addition to any bonus-action command; you may command the same mark in both. · On Consort’s Meteor Rain’s return · +10 CE · Radius doubles to 60 ft, damage becomes 12d8; you take 4d8 unavoidable force. Named pinnacle: cannot receive Maximum Output. · Passive · While below half HP, hostile creatures have disadvantage on saves against your Vector Command."}],"e047":[{"level":1,"title":"A Fragment of the Rune","rules":"Level 1 · Deathbrand (add Fate Scars), Healing Interference, Black Blade Conductor; Beast Step · Scars last 1 minute. · On a direct hit · 1 CE · Add one Fate Scar (no damage die; scars last 1 minute). Each scar: target’s max HP reduced by 5% of its original max (never below 25% from scars alone); healing received reduced 10% per scar (max 50%); RCT removes one scar (spending at least 3 CE) instead of restoring HP. Any melee weapon can carry the technique; bonus action: form a cursed black blade using any proficient melee weapon’s statistics. · No action · Once per turn after you hit a scarred creature: move 10 ft without provoking from that creature."},{"level":3,"title":"Beast Clergyman","rules":"Level 3 · Bestial Sling, Black Blade Wave, Stone of Gurranq. · Action · 2 CE · 30-ft cone: Dexterity save; failure: one Fate Scar and prone; success: no effect. · Attack action (replace one attack) · 2 CE · Ranged CE attack to 60 ft; hit: weapon base damage and apply Deathbrand for 0 additional CE. · Action · 3 CE · One creature within 90 ft: Strength save; failure: one Fate Scar and prone."},{"level":6,"title":"The Blade is Unsealed","rules":"Level 6 · Death in Motion, Mortal Wound, Black Blade Spiral. · Passive · Jump distance doubled; once per turn, after moving at least 20 ft directly toward a creature, your next melee hit applies Deathbrand for 0 CE. · Passive · At 3 Fate Scars, ordinary healing cannot raise the target above its reduced maximum, and RCT must first remove a scar before it can restore HP on the same activation. · Action · 5 CE · Move up to half speed through spaces adjacent to enemies; make one melee attack against up to PB different creatures; each hit can gain Deathbrand by paying separately."},{"level":11,"title":"Destined Death Released","rules":"Level 11 · Greater Fate Scar (scars deepen to 7.5%), Maximum: Thousand Black Blades, Death Denies Death. · Passive · Each scar now reduces original max HP by 7.5% (still respecting the scar cap); healing reduction remains 10% per scar. · Action · 10 CE · Creatures of your choice within 30 ft: Dexterity saves; failure: two Fate Scars and prone; success: one Fate Scar. Named Maximum. · Passive · When a scarred creature would be revived from 0 HP, it returns with one Fate Scar still active unless the revival explicitly repairs soul/fate damage."},{"level":18,"title":"Rune Unbound","rules":"Level 18 · Domain Expansion (Night of Destined Death), Black Blade Eclipse, Fourth Scar (scar cap 4). · Unlock Domain · Night of Destined Death (Rune Unbound). · Bonus action · 8 CE · Focus · 1 minute · Every direct weapon hit adds a Fate Scar for 0 CE; healing you receive is halved while it lasts. · Passive · Fate Scar cap becomes 4."},{"level":20,"title":"Death Restored to the World","rules":"Level 20 · True Destined Death (scars 10%, floor 10%), Fifth Scar (cap 5), Final Black Blade. · Passive · Each Fate Scar now reduces original max HP by 10%; the scar floor becomes 10% instead of 25%; healing reduction can reach 50%. · Passive · Fate Scar cap becomes 5. · On hit vs a creature with 5 Fate Scars · 10 CE · Once per long rest or major scene · Force a Constitution save: failure reduces it to 0 HP; success stuns it until the end of your next turn and it cannot regain HP until then. Creatures immune to instant defeat take the success result automatically. Not a Domain sure-hit; cannot be Maximum Output."}],"e048":[{"level":1,"title":"The Cold Moon Watches","rules":"Level 1 · Lunar Bolt, Lunar Sigil, Cold Moon Guard, Moon Shard; Snow Witch’s Step · Lunar Range 60 ft · Hold up to PB shards (shards vanish on a long rest). · Action (or replace one attack) · 1 CE · Ranged CE attack within Lunar Range (60/90/120/180/300 ft at L1/3/6/11/18, line of sight at L20); hit: 2d8 cold or force (your choice) and one Lunar Sigil for 1 minute (3d8 at L11, 4d8 at L18). Also gain: Lunar Sigil (a sigiled creature’s resistance to technique damage drops one step; maintain up to PB sigils), Cold Moon Guard (Reaction · 2 CE · reduce an incoming ranged technique/projectile attack roll by PB or add PB to your save; if it misses/fails because of this, absorb it and gain 1 Moon Shard), Moon Shard (spend one instead of 1 CE on a Dark Moon feature). · Passive · When you deal cold damage, difficult terrain made of ice, snow, or your own technique does not hinder you until end of turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Spirit Bell","rules":"Level 3 · Ashen Familiar, Devour Memory, Freezing Mist, Moonlit Guidance. · Action · 3 CE · Summon one spectral familiar for 1 hour (two different familiars at L11): Wolf (melee CE attack) or Marionette (60-ft ranged CE attack), a hit places 1 Lunar Sigil with no damage; Scholar (Help/knowledge). It acts immediately after you and takes one simple action. · Bonus action · Command your familiar to consume all Lunar Sigils on one creature within 10 ft of it: 4 cold damage per sigil; you gain 1 Moon Shard per 2 sigils (minimum 1). · Action · 3 CE · Focus · 20-ft-radius cloud for 1 minute: creatures entering or starting their turn there make Constitution saves; failure: gain 1 Lunar Sigil and −10 speed until the end of their next turn; success: nothing. · Passive · Perceive through your familiar within 1 mile and cast Lunar Bolt from its space by paying +1 CE."},{"level":6,"title":"Doll-Soul Art","rules":"Level 6 · False Body, Four-Armed Casting, Lunar Rupture. · Reaction · 4 CE · When hit (once per round): leave a frost-doll shell in your space and teleport up to 30 ft to a visible space; reduce the triggering damage by 4 × PB. · Passive · Hold or manipulate two additional light objects with spectral hands; grants no extra attacks or actions. · Trigger · When a creature bearing a Lunar Sigil fails a save against your cold effect: consume the sigil to restrain it in frost until the end of its next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Ranni’s Dark Moon","rules":"Level 11 · Dark Moon, Moon of Weakness, Spirit Court. · Action · 7 CE · Create a 15-ft-diameter moon within 30 ft and send it up to 60 ft in a line: suppresses one non-Domain technique manifestation it touches (your CE ability check vs DC 10 + the effect’s CE cost, or the creator’s technique DC, whichever is higher); creatures hit make Dexterity saves: failure, 30 cold or force damage and two Lunar Sigils; success, half damage and one sigil. · Passive · A creature bearing 2+ Lunar Sigils has disadvantage on its first save each round against your cold or force technique. · Passive · Maintain two different Ashen Familiars at once; commanding both uses the same bonus action."},{"level":18,"title":"Age of Stars","rules":"Level 18 · Domain Expansion (Age of Stars), Black Moon Transit, Greater Dark Moon. · Unlock Domain · Age of Stars (Moon Beyond Causality). · Action · 8 CE · You and up to PB willing creatures step into a dark lunar reflection and reappear in spaces you can see within 300 ft. Teleportation. · Passive · Dark Moon can now contest a Domain barrier segment, Maximum Technique projectile, or Special Grade manifestation (never automatically deletes it; make opposed refinement/CE checks)."},{"level":20,"title":"Sever the Fingers","rules":"Level 20 · Causal Severance, Moon Without Master, Cold Cosmos. · Action · 10 CE · Choose one creature or object within 120 ft and one external ongoing binding on it (summoner control, tracking curse, borrowed buff, remote command, possession tether, barrier lock): make a CE ability check vs the source DC/refinement; success suppresses that link for 1 minute. Cannot erase the target’s own innate technique, Heavenly Restriction, soul, or the consequences of a voluntary Binding Vow. · Passive · Moon Shards no longer expire on a long rest; maximum becomes PB + CE modifier. · Passive · You are immune to your own cold effects and resistant to cold and psychic damage."}],"e049":[{"level":1,"title":"A Spark Behind the Eyes","rules":"Level 1 · Madness meter (starts 0; Frenzy features add listed Madness; short rest −2, long rest resets to 0), Madness Thresholds, Frenzied Burst, Yellow Flame, Burn the Pain · Frenzy Die d6 · Range 60 ft. · Action · 1 CE · +1 Madness · Ranged CE attack; hit: 2 Frenzy Dice fire/psychic (split as you choose); a creature hit twice by Frenzy before the end of your next turn makes a Wisdom save or is frightened until the end of its next turn. Yellow Flame: Frenzy fire is cursed fire with a psychic component; immunity to ordinary fire does not prevent the psychic half. · Reaction · +1 Madness · When you fail a save against frightened, charmed, or pain-based incapacitation: reroll it and use the new result. · Passive · Frenzy Die d6; range 60 feet."},{"level":3,"title":"Eyes of Shabriri","rules":"Level 3 · Frenzy Gaze, Howl of Frenzy, Flame Fan · Frenzy Die d6 · Range 90 ft. · Action · 2 CE · +1 Madness · One creature within 60 ft that can see your eyes: Wisdom save; failure takes 3 Frenzy Dice psychic and cannot take reactions until its next turn. · Bonus action · 2 CE · +1 Madness · Focus · 1 minute: your melee hits deal +1 Frenzy Die; while Madness is 7+, attack rolls against creatures other than the nearest hostile have disadvantage. · Action · 3 CE · +1 Madness · 30-ft cone: Dexterity save; 4 Frenzy Dice fire, half on success. · Passive · Frenzy Die d6; range 90 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Inescapable Frenzy","rules":"Level 6 · Face of Chaos, Contagious Despair, Kindled Contagion · Frenzy Die d8 · Range 120 ft. · When you grapple a creature · 3 CE · +1 Madness · Once per target per round · Force a Wisdom save: failure takes 5 Frenzy Dice psychic/fire and is stunned until the end of your current turn. · Trigger · A frightened creature damaged by Frenzy spreads a debuff to adjacent hostiles: Wisdom saves or −PB to their next attack before the end of their next turn. · Trigger · At Madness 3+: when a hostile fails a save against a Frenzy feature (once per round per creature), it becomes Kindled until the end of its next turn: it cannot benefit from advantage on attack rolls, the Help action, or any ally-granted spell or feature. At the start of a Kindled creature’s turn, each other hostile within 10 ft makes a Wisdom save vs your Technique DC or is also Kindled until the end of its next turn. No damage. · Passive · Frenzy Die d8; range 120 feet."},{"level":11,"title":"Midra’s Flame","rules":"Level 11 · Apparition of the Lord, Unendurable Frenzy, Madness Feeds Madness · Frenzy Die d10 · Range 180 ft. · Action · 6 CE · +2 Madness · Focus · Up to 1 minute: a flaming void-head hovers over you; at the start of each of your turns it fires PB bolts, distributed among targets within 90 ft, each a ranged CE attack for 2 Frenzy Dice. · Action · 7 CE · +2 Madness · 60-ft cone: Constitution save; failure: 8 Frenzy Dice split fire/psychic and blinded until next turn; success: half damage, no blind. · Passive · Whenever a hostile fails a Wisdom save against Frenzy, gain temporary HP equal to PB; your Madness does not change. · Passive · Frenzy Die d10; range 180 feet."},{"level":18,"title":"The One Great","rules":"Level 18 · At Madness 6+ unlock the Domain (One Great, No More Distinction); Lord’s Emergence; Chaos Crown · Frenzy Die d12 · Range 300 ft. · Unlock Domain · One Great, No More Distinction (available at Madness 6+). · Trigger · Once per long rest · If you would die at Madness 8+: immediately set Madness to 10 and enter Lord state instead, returning to 1 HP. · At Madness 10 · Up to 1 minute: immune to frightened/charmed, Frenzy dice become d12, 30-ft flight; at the end of each turn make a Wisdom save (DC 10 + rounds elapsed) or the GM chooses your movement and one non-suicidal hostile action next turn. · Passive · Frenzy Die d12; range 300 feet."},{"level":20,"title":"Lord of Frenzied Flame","rules":"Level 20 · May Chaos Take the World, Melt Distinction, Last Ember of Self · Frenzy Die d12 · Range: line of sight. · Bonus action · 5 CE · +enough Madness to reach 10 · Voluntarily enter Lord state; the control save begins at DC 10. · Passive · While Lord state is active, your Frenzy damage ignores resistance and treats immunity as resistance. · Trigger · Once per Lord state · After failing the control save: choose to succeed instead and take 4d12 psychic damage that ignores reduction. · Passive · Frenzy Die d12; range: line of sight."}],"e050":[{"level":1,"title":"Vestments of the Godhunt","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · 1 minute · Choose Apostle (+10 speed, +5-ft melee reach, Dex mobility) or Noble (+1 AC, advantage vs forced movement, counts one size larger for grapples); on entering, form a Godskin Armament (Twinblade in Apostle, Stitcher in Noble; counts as cursed). On hit (no action, 1 CE): the target is Kindled until the start of its next turn — it cannot regain HP, and at the start of its turn takes necrotic damage equal to 2% of its max HP (minimum PB, maximum 5 × level), once per round. · Trigger · Once per turn when your direct melee attack deals damage: gain temporary HP equal to PB (or heal 1 HP per PB if you already have temporary HP); you cannot be healed above half your maximum HP by this feature. · Passive · Range 30 feet."},{"level":3,"title":"Black Flame Scripture","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Ranged CE attack, 90 ft; on a hit the target is Kindled. · Action · 3 CE · 30-ft cone: Dexterity saves; failure: Kindled and blinded until the start of your next turn; success: no effect. · Once per turn · No action · 1 CE · When you hit a Kindled creature while in the opposite stance from the one that Kindled it: consume the Kindling (delayed burn triggers immediately) and force a Strength save; failure knocks the target prone. · Action · 3 CE · Focus · Create a 15-ft-radius black-flame ring for 1 minute; the first time each turn a creature crosses its edge, it is Kindled. · Passive · Range extends to 60 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Second Skin","rules":"Passive · Apostle melee reach becomes 15 ft; once per turn after a hit, move 10 ft without provoking from that target. · Bonus action · 2 CE · Move up to your speed in a line through hostile spaces; each creature whose space you enter makes a Strength save; failure: knocked prone and dragged 10 ft along your path; success: no effect. · Trigger · Once per turn after resolving a stance-specific feature: switch stance without an action and without CE. · Passive · Range extends to 90 feet."},{"level":11,"title":"The Duo Rite","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Focus · 1 minute · Manifest the opposite stance as a Medium shikigami-like partner (AC 14+PB, HP 8 × level, speed 40): it acts after you, moving plus making one Godskin Armament attack (applies Kindling for 0 CE on a hit); it cannot use your Domain/Maximum. · Reaction · When your partner takes damage: take any amount of that damage instead. Passive: when you take damage, your partner may absorb up to 5 × PB of one damage instance per round. · Action · 7 CE · Creatures within 15 ft: Dexterity saves; failure: Kindled and pulled 10 ft toward you; success: no effect. · Passive · Range extends to 120 feet."},{"level":18,"title":"Apostasy Refuses Death","rules":"Trigger · If Skinbound Partner reaches 0 HP while you remain conscious: spend 5 CE at the end of each of two rounds to reform it at full HP; damage to you can interrupt this via Technique Focus checks. · Action · 10 CE · You and your partner (or a phantom opposite form if absent) sweep a 60-ft path: creatures crossed make Dexterity saves; failure: knocked prone and Twin-Kindled (the delayed burn triggers twice at the start of their turn); success: Kindled only. · Passive · This technique does not naturally form a Domain; its binding identity is two bodies sharing one rite. · Passive · Range extends to 180 feet."},{"level":20,"title":"Godhunt Restored","rules":"Passive · The delayed Black Flame burn becomes 3% of maximum HP (minimum PB, maximum 10 × your level); it ignores fire resistance but not fire immunity; the necrotic portion remains. · Passive · Skinbound Partner no longer requires Technique Focus, though only one partner may exist. · Trigger · Once per turn: when both you and your partner hit the same creature before your next turn, the second hit consumes any Kindling for the immediate double-burn; the target cannot regain HP until the start of your next turn. · Passive · Range extends to 300 feet."}],"e051":[{"level":1,"title":"Godspeed: Whirlwind","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Enter Godspeed (Whirlwind) for up to 1 minute · While active: attacks against you have disadvantage, you can't be surprised, resistance to lightning damage · 1 CE upkeep at the start of each of your turns."},{"level":3,"title":"Speed of Lightning","rules":"Bonus action (requires Godspeed active) · Switch to Speed of Lightning (switching back is also a bonus action; the 1 CE per-turn drain continues) · +30 ft. speed, opportunity attacks against you have disadvantage, unarmed strikes deal +2d8 lightning damage · Once per turn, a hit forces a Con save vs your CE save DC or the target is stunned until the end of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Thunderbolt","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Target a point within 90 ft (works with or without Godspeed) · Each creature within 10 ft: Dex save vs your CE save DC or 5d8 lightning damage (half on success)."},{"level":11,"title":"Counter-Program","rules":"Reaction · While Godspeed (Whirlwind) is active, when an attack misses you: move up to your speed toward the attacker without provoking opportunity attacks, then make one unarmed strike."},{"level":18,"title":"Arc Discharge","rules":"Passive · While Godspeed is active, when a lightning-charged unarmed strike or Thunderbolt damages a creature: arcs to one other creature within 20 ft of the first · Dex save vs your CE save DC or lightning damage equal to half the lightning dice rolled (rounded down)."},{"level":20,"title":"The Storm, Perfected","rules":"Once per long rest · Bonus action · For 1 minute: Godspeed costs no CE to maintain, Whirlwind and Speed of Lightning run simultaneously, +30 ft. additional speed · When it ends, gain 1 level of exhaustion."}],"e052":[{"level":1,"title":"Undefeated Blade","rules":"Passive · Gain Blade Lifesteal (heal one Scarlet Die per direct melee hit dealing HP damage; capped at PB × Scarlet Die max per turn, never above half your max HP), Rot Marks, and Scarlet Rot as described above. · Passive · On a turn you make at least one melee attack: +10 ft. movement and you may move through a hostile creature's threatened space without extra cost (you still provoke unless another feature prevents it). · Scaling · Scarlet Die is a d4; range: melee."},{"level":3,"title":"Prosthetic Precision","rules":"Replace one attack · 1 CE · On hit: add one Scarlet Die piercing damage and one Rot Mark. · Bonus action (after a melee hit) · Target must Str save or be pushed 10 ft · Spend 1 CE to knock it prone as well. · Reaction · 2 CE (when targeted) · Impose disadvantage on one attack, then move 10 ft after it resolves (hit or miss). · Scaling · Scarlet Die becomes d6; range extends to 30 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Waterfowl Dance","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Make up to PB melee attacks while moving up to your speed (max 2 against the same creature; you don't provoke) · Hits after the first deal one fewer weapon base die (min 1); all can crit and Lifesteal. · Passive · Once per turn, a melee critical automatically adds one Rot Mark (no CE). · Passive · Advantage on saves against your own Scarlet Rot backlash and against effects that would charm or dominate you. · Scaling · Scarlet Die becomes d8; range extends to 60 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"First Scarlet Aeonia","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Leap to a point within 60 ft and bloom in a 20-ft radius · Creatures: Dex save or 6 Scarlet Dice + CE modifier damage, plus 2 Rot Marks on failure · Flower remains until end of your next turn; creatures entering or starting there: Con save or gain 1 Rot Mark. · Passive · Blade Lifesteal can now heal you to full maximum HP. · Bonus action · 4 CE · Focus · 1 minute · Gain 40-ft flying speed; once per turn, a melee hit adds +1 Scarlet Die. · Scaling · Scarlet Die becomes d10; range extends to 90 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Second Bloom, Goddess of Rot","rules":"Once per long rest · When reduced to 0 HP: bloom instead of falling unconscious — regain half max HP, activate Scarlet Wings at no cost, create Scarlet Aeonia centered on yourself · Gain one permanent Bloom count. · Domain Expansion · Unlock Haligtree of the Third Bloom if you have at least one Bloom count · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius · Duration 1 minute · Barrier of pale roots, red water, and endless butterfly wings. · Action · 6 CE · Make PB melee CE attacks against creatures within 90 ft · Each hit: 2 Scarlet Dice damage + one Rot Mark, but cannot Lifesteal. · Scaling · Scarlet Die becomes d12; range extends to 120 ft."},{"level":20,"title":"Third Bloom","rules":"Passive · When your third lifetime Bloom occurs (or a GM-approved campaign milestone): your technique permanently reaches True Goddess state · Scarlet Die remains d12 · Immune to poison/disease, resistant to necrotic. · Passive · Scarlet Aeonia costs 6 CE and no longer requires you to land in the bloom; you may reappear in any open space at its edge. · Passive · Once per turn when Scarlet Rot damages a hostile creature: gain temporary HP equal to PB (this is not healing and does not trigger Lifesteal caps). · Scaling · Scarlet Die remains d12; range extends to 180 ft."}],"e053":[{"level":1,"title":"Twin-Blade Oath","rules":"Passive · Gain Twin Blades, Moon/Flame Imbuement, and Concordant Alternation as described above. · Passive · While wielding both blades and wearing no heavy armor: +1 AC. · Scaling · Twin Die d6; range: melee."},{"level":3,"title":"Carian Retinue","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Create PB glintblades for 1 minute · Once per turn after you attack: fire one at a target within 60 ft as a CE attack for 1 Twin Die force. · Replace one weapon attack · 2 CE · 60-ft ranged CE attack · 3 Twin Dice force/cold (you choose). · Action · 3 CE · Creatures within 10 ft: Dex save or 4 Twin Dice fire (half on success) · Move 10 ft after resolution. · Scaling · Twin Die remains d6; range extends to 60 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Moon-and-Fire Stance","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Until the start of your next turn: Moon Blade gains 15-ft spectral reach and Moonlight Wave costs 1 less CE. · Bonus action · 2 CE · Until the start of your next turn: Flame Blade hits deal +1 Twin Die and you may move through hostile reach without provoking from creatures you hit. · Passive · Once per turn, when Concordant Alternation triggers: fire one stored Carian Phalanx blade without consuming the once-per-turn phalanx launch. · Scaling · Twin Die becomes d8; range extends to 90 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Carian Sovereignty","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Melee CE attack vs one target within 20 ft: 8 Twin Dice force on hit · Then creatures in a 30-ft cone: Dex save or 4 Twin Dice force (half on success). · Reaction · 3 CE · Moon: reduce technique damage by PB Twin Dice · Flame: reduce weapon/unarmed damage by PB Twin Dice. · Passive · After triggering Concordant Alternation twice in one turn: +10 speed and advantage on the next Dex save before your next turn. · Scaling · Twin Die becomes d10; range extends to 120 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Rellana’s Twin Moons","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Rise 20 ft and create two moons · Three sequential 20-ft-radius ground shockwaves centered below you: 4, 4, then 6 Twin Dice force (Dex save for half each) · Failing any: knocked prone; failing two or more: also launched 20 ft upward. · Passive · Twin Blades remain manifested without duration or CE maintenance until dismissed · Once per turn: apply both imbuements to the same hit for 2 CE (does not count as Alternation by itself). · Scaling · Twin Die becomes d12; range extends to 180 ft."},{"level":20,"title":"Perfect Concordance","rules":"Passive · Concordant Alternation can trigger twice per turn; its bonus becomes +2 Twin Dice. · Passive · When you take the Attack action with Twin Blades, once per turn make one additional Twin Blade attack as part of that action. · When using Maximum: Twin Moons, spend +5 CE · Create a third moon before your own slam: add another 4 Twin Die shockwave · Named pinnacle; no Maximum Output. · Scaling · Twin Die remains d12; range extends to 300 ft."}],"e054":[{"level":1,"title":"First Communion","rules":"Passive · Choose your Draconic Lineage and gain Dragonclaw, Heartfire Surge, and Gravel Scales as described above. · Passive · Darkvision 60 ft (or +60 ft if you already have it) · Advantage on smell-based Perception while transformed. · Once per turn · After Dragonclaw hits, no action, 1 CE · Target Con save vs your Technique DC or suffer your lineage's surge — Flame: ignited, 1d8 fire at the start of its next turn; Ancient Lightning: loses reactions until the start of its next turn; Glintstone Frost: −15 ft speed until the start of its next turn; Magma: its space becomes difficult terrain until the start of your next turn (no save); Scarlet: one Rot Mark (3 marks = Scarlet Rot: 1d8 necrotic at the start of each of its turns, ends after two successful Con saves). · Scaling · Dragon Die is d8 (fixed); range: touch."},{"level":3,"title":"Breath of the Heart","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 30-ft cone · 4d8 lineage damage (half on success) · Save set by lineage (Flame/Lightning/Magma: Dex; Frost/Scarlet: Con) · Scarlet: poison/necrotic + one Rot-like mark; Magma: leaves difficult terrain until next turn. · Action · 2 CE · Hostiles within 15 ft: Wis save or frightened until the end of your next turn · Success grants immunity to your Roar for 24 hours. · Action · 3 CE · Manifest Dragonmaw and make a melee CE attack · 5d8 bludgeoning/piercing (you choose) and the target is knocked prone on a failed Str save. · Scaling · Dragon Die remains d8 (fixed); range extends to a 30-ft cone."},{"level":6,"title":"Half-Dragon","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · 1 minute · Flying speed equal to your walking speed · Shares Gravel Scales' Focus if active (no second slot). · After a long rest, choose one · Tail: reaction shove on adjacent hit · Horn: after moving 20+ ft in a straight line immediately before the attack, your Dragonclaw forces a Str save or the target is knocked prone and pushed 10 ft. · Passive · Breath becomes a 60-ft cone or a 90-by-5-ft line (chosen each use), dealing 5d8. · Scaling · Dragon Die is d8 (fixed); range extends to 60 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Ancient Blood","rules":"Passive · Gravel Scales becomes +2 AC · While active, reduce nonmagical/unenhanced weapon damage by PB. · Passive · Gain a second lineage resistance and one secondary breath rider from another lineage · Primary damage type remains the original. · Action · 6 CE · 30-ft radius centered on you · Creatures: Dex saves vs 7d8 damage plus a lineage rider (red lightning, firestorm, moonfrost shards, erupting ground, or rotburst). · Scaling · Dragon Die remains d8 (fixed); range extends to 90 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"True Dragon Incarnation","rules":"Passive · Gravel Scales improves to +3 AC. · Full-turn action · 12 CE · Focus · Up to 10 minutes · Become Huge: reach +10 ft, fly 80 ft, Gravel Scales +3 AC, Dragonclaw 2d8, breath 8d8 recharging on a d6 roll of 4–6 at the start of your turn (no CE), Heartfire Surge costs 0 CE · Cannot wield normal weapons or fit human spaces. · Passive · Hostiles entering within 30 ft of True Dragon for the first time: Wis save or frightened for 1 minute (repeat save at the end of turns). · Scaling · Dragon Die remains d8 (fixed); range extends to 120 ft."},{"level":20,"title":"Dragonlord Ascendant","rules":"Once per True Dragon transformation · Vanish into a rift at the end of your turn and reappear at the start of your next turn within 300 ft with one advantaged Dragonclaw attack. · Once per turn · When Breath recharges naturally, spend 5 CE · Turn it into a 120-ft cone for 12d8 · You take 2d8 unavoidable overpressure damage. · Passive · No age-related physical decline · Immunity to your primary lineage damage while transformed. · Scaling · Dragon Die remains d8 (fixed); range extends to 180 ft."}],"e055":[{"level":1,"title":"Rock, Charging Fist","rules":"Action · Plant your feet and declare \"Jajanken… Rock!\" aloud: gain 1 charge (max 3) · While charging: speed halved, attacks against you have advantage · Release as part of the Attack action: unarmed strike, on hit 2d12 bludgeoning + 2d12 per charge held (charges spent) · Charge fizzles if unused for 1 minute."},{"level":3,"title":"Paper","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Declare \"Paper!\": ranged CE attack, range 60 ft · On hit: 3d8 bludgeoning · Ignores half cover."},{"level":6,"title":"Scissors","rules":"As part of the Attack action · 1 CE · Declare \"Scissors!\": melee unarmed strike dealing 3d8 slashing damage."},{"level":11,"title":"Held Gambit","rules":"Reaction · While holding a Rock charge, when a creature enters your reach or hits you with a melee attack: release the charge and resolve the Rock strike against that creature immediately (charge spent)."},{"level":18,"title":"Crater","rules":"Passive · Rock charge cap rises to 6 · When you release Rock with 4+ charges: each creature within 10 ft of the target (other than you): Str save vs your CE save DC or take half the Rock's total damage and be knocked prone (no damage on success)."},{"level":20,"title":"Everything I Have","rules":"Once per long rest · Bonus action · For 1 minute: charging Rock becomes a bonus action, Paper and Scissors cost no CE, holding a charge no longer halves your speed or grants attackers advantage · When it ends: your CE pool empties to 0 and you cannot spend or regain CE until a long rest."}],"e056":[{"level":1,"title":"Ripper Cyclotron","rules":"Bonus action · Wind your arm: gain 1 wind (max 10) · While you hold any winds: attacks against you have advantage · Release as part of the Attack action: unarmed strike, on hit 1d12 bludgeoning per wind held (winds spent) · Winds decay after 1 minute without winding or releasing."},{"level":3,"title":"Shockwave Release","rules":"When you release, instead of a melee punch: each creature in a 30-ft line originating from you: Dex save vs your CE save DC or take your wound punch's damage (half on success) · Winds spent."},{"level":6,"title":"Bleed-Off","rules":"No action · When you take damage while holding winds: lose any number of winds to reduce the damage by 1d8 per wind lost."},{"level":11,"title":"Split Winding","rules":"When you release a melee punch: split winds between two targets within reach (min 1 each) · Separate unarmed strike against each, each dealing 1d12 per wind assigned · Winds spent."},{"level":18,"title":"Ground Zero","rules":"Passive · Max winds rise to 15 · When you release a melee punch with 10+ winds: each creature within 15 ft of the target (other than you): Str save vs your CE save DC or take half the punch's damage and be knocked prone (no damage on success)."},{"level":20,"title":"The Arm Never Stops","rules":"Once per long rest · Bonus action · For 1 minute: winding is a free action once per turn (in addition to your bonus-action wind), no maximum winds, winds never decay · When it ends: gain 1 level of exhaustion."}],"e057":[{"level":1,"title":"Doctor Blythe","rules":"Passive · Gain Doctor Blythe (action, 3 CE, Focus) and Predatory En (action, 1 CE per minute) as described above. · Reaction · 2 CE (while Blythe is active) · Reduce damage to a creature within Blythe's reach by 4 × PB. · Scaling · Doctor Blythe's tether: 20 ft · Predatory En: 25-ft radius at 1st level, growing to 2 miles at level 18."},{"level":3,"title":"Puppeteer","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Attach a shikigami to a corpse within 10 ft · It rises with HP equal to half its former max (cap 8×level), AC 12+PB, and can take Move + one simple action after your turn · Cannot use its former CT. · Passive · Give a puppet a simple standing order (guard, patrol, follow, attack marked targets) · It continues within 1 mile without using your action economy. · Bonus action · Perceive through one puppet until the start of your next turn. · Scaling · Predatory En range extends to 60 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Terpsichora","rules":"Bonus action · 5 CE · Focus · 1 minute · Ballerina shikigami strings your body: speed +20 ft, jump distance tripled, +PB to Athletics/Acrobatics, one extra unarmed/natural weapon attack per Attack action. · At the start of your turn while Terpsichora is active, spend 2 CE · Advantage on Dex saves and +2 AC until your next turn; take 5 force recoil at the end of the turn. · Bonus action · 1 CE · Destroy one puppet within 60 ft; choose Snare (hostiles within 10 ft: Dex save or restrained until the end of your next turn), Sling (pull one willing creature within 10 ft up to 20 ft in a straight line of your choice; doesn't provoke), or Suture Surge (one creature within 10 ft heals 10 HP). · Passive · Switch signature shikigami once per turn without a bonus action (still 1 CE); a new Focus ends the previous one. · Scaling · Predatory En range extends to 90 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Royal Guard Control","rules":"Passive · A corpse repaired by Doctor Blythe retains one mundane proficiency and one non-Domain, non-Maximum combat feature from life · Using that feature costs you its printed CE through the puppet. · Passive · Maintain up to 5×PB simple corpse puppets · Groups of five act as one swarm stat block in mass scenes. · Passive · Doctor Blythe's healing becomes 8 HP per CE; tether range 40 ft. · Scaling · Predatory En range extends to 1 mile."},{"level":18,"title":"Postmortem Terpsichora","rules":"Passive · If you die while Terpsichora is active: it persists until the end of your next turn; your body may move and make one final Attack action under its last command · Cannot revive you; ends if the body is destroyed. · Passive · Predatory En range becomes 2 miles and can branch around obstacles along a continuous path. · Action · 10 CE · For 1 minute: Terpsichora no longer uses Focus and grants a second reaction each round (movement or basic attack only) · At the end: gain one level of exhaustion."},{"level":20,"title":"Royal Theater","rules":"Passive · Maintain Doctor Blythe, one Puppeteer network, and Terpsichora simultaneously · Blythe's 40-ft tether and healing/action restrictions remain. · Passive · Puppet cap becomes 10×PB; five-puppet swarms gain +PB to attack and saves. · Scaling · Predatory En range extends to 5 miles."}],"e058":[{"level":1,"title":"A.P.R. (Potclean)","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Conjure Potclean; it flies to a creature within 60 ft · Make a CE-ability attack roll vs its AC; on a hit it latches: the debtor's current and max CE both increase by twice your level (the principal) · Whenever you deal damage to the debtor, add it to the debt · At the start of the debtor's turn, interest accrues: new debt = (old debt + damage dealt since last tick) × 1.10, rounded down · Bankruptcy: debt exceeds the debtor's max CE → can't spend CE until a long rest; Potclean returns · Damage the debtor deals to you shrinks the debt · One loan at a time; Potclean can't be damaged while a loan is active."},{"level":3,"title":"Audit","rules":"Passive · You know the debtor's current debt, max CE, and rounds until bankruptcy at the current rate · Sense the debtor's direction and distance within 1 mile."},{"level":6,"title":"Branch Offices","rules":"Passive · Maintain loans on up to two debtors at once, each with its own ledger, interest, and bankruptcy."},{"level":11,"title":"Garnish Wages","rules":"Passive · The first time each round a debtor spends CE, the debt grows by the amount spent."},{"level":18,"title":"Chapter 7 Bankruptcy","rules":"Passive · A bankrupt creature can't spend or regain CE until it finishes a long rest · Your loans' principal becomes three times your level."},{"level":20,"title":"Bailout","rules":"Once per long rest · Action · Forgive an active loan: the debtor is freed, and you regain CE equal to half the forgiven debt (up to your max)."}],"e059":[{"level":1,"title":"Smoke, Obey","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Conjure PB smoke soldiers (min 2) in unoccupied spaces within 60 ft · They act on your initiative immediately after you and obey verbal orders freely · Melee attacks with your CE ability modifier; 1d6 + CE modifier bludgeoning on hit."},{"level":3,"title":"Eyes in the Fog","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Designate a soldier within 120 ft: perceive through it (see and hear) while your own body is blinded and deafened until dismissed · The soldier still fights."},{"level":6,"title":"The Ranks Swell","rules":"Passive · Maintain up to 5 × level soldiers; each conjuring still costs 2 CE per PB-sized batch · Screen: reaction, 1 CE when targeted by an attack you can see — a soldier within 5 ft interposes and dissipates, taking the attack instead."},{"level":11,"title":"Hands of Smoke","rules":"Passive · Soldiers can grapple/shove (using your CE save DC), carry (two soldiers move a Medium or smaller creature 20 ft per round), and perform simple tasks: open doors, drag the wounded, hold ropes."},{"level":18,"title":"The General Vanishes","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Dissolve into smoke and re-form in an unoccupied space adjacent to a soldier within 120 ft · Bring only what you wear and carry."},{"level":20,"title":"The Fog Itself","rules":"Once per long rest · Bonus action · For 1 minute: become living smoke — attacks and single-target effects can't target you, pass through 1-inch gaps, resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning/piercing/slashing · Can't attack or spend CE except through your soldiers · End early as a bonus action."}],"e060":[{"level":1,"title":"Dancing Tops","rules":"Passive · Gain Dancing Top, Top Strike, and Ricochet as described above. · During a short rest: prepare PB replacement tops from mundane materials · Prepared tops count as technique focuses and are not consumed unless destroyed. · Scaling · Top Die d6; range 30 ft."},{"level":3,"title":"Battle Waltz","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 1 minute · Command up to 2×PB tops to swarm a 20-ft-radius area within 60 ft: difficult terrain for hostiles · Stagger Step: the first time each round a hostile moves 10+ ft inside, Dex save vs your Technique DC or falls prone and slides 5 ft in a direction of your choice. · Passive · Ranged attacks through your Battle Waltz area have −2 to hit unless the attacker ignores moving cover. · Passive · One top may travel up to 60 ft through up to three visible ricochet points before its shared Top Strike. · Scaling · Top Die remains d6; range extends to 60 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Tornado Top","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Focus · 1 minute · +2 AC vs melee attacks, advantage vs shove/prone, creatures entering your reach take one Top Die bludgeoning once per turn · Speed reduced by 10. · Reaction (while Tornado Top is active) · Reduce melee damage by PB Top Dice · Push the attacker 10 ft if reduced to 0. · Once per turn (while Tornado Top is active) · Create/launch a Dancing Top as part of Tornado movement without a bonus action · Still costs 1 CE. · Scaling · Top Die becomes d8; range extends to 90 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Shotgun Blues","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Choose up to PB active tops · 60-ft line: Dex save or 5 Top Dice thunder (half on success) · Single target: one CE attack with advantage, PB Top Dice + CE modifier thunder on hit. · Passive · Top commands may now include one condition and one action, but still cannot plan tactics or recognize complex deceptions. · Passive · Tops last until a long rest unless destroyed or dismissed. · Scaling · Top Die becomes d10; range extends to 120 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Fifty-Top Funeral","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Manifest 50 spectral tops for 1 minute as five swarms (each a 15-ft square; you move each 30 ft at the end of your turn; AC 15, HP 10×level) · Hostiles entering or starting in a swarm: Dex save or 5 Top Dice thunder (half on success). · Passive · Tornado Top no longer reduces speed; its collision damage becomes 2 Top Dice. · Scaling · Top Die becomes d12; range extends to 180 ft."},{"level":20,"title":"Perfect Gyroscope","rules":"Passive · Ordinary Dancing Tops don't expire while you remain conscious and on the same plane. · Once per turn · A Top Strike may ignore line of sight if you can describe a continuous ricochet path within 120 ft. · Bonus action · Stand on a Large technique top: hover 40 ft until the end of your turn (falling rules apply afterward unless another top/support catches you). · Scaling · Top Die remains d12; range extends to 300 ft."}],"e061":[{"level":1,"title":"Inherited Stockpile · Localized Output · Succession","rules":"Gain Stockpiled Strength, Safe Output 5%, Stockpile Die d6, and Smash. You cannot Full Cowl yet: select one arm, leg, or weapon as the output carrier for each Smash. You also gain Yoichi's Succession, allowing voluntary transfer of Anime & Manga during a 10-minute ritual.100% technically available · 1 Smash/turn · Transferable inheritance · Your technique carries accumulated physical power. You gain a Stockpile Die that scales with level and fuels Smash damage, Air Force, Kinetic Surge, and several combination techniques."},{"level":2,"title":"Air Force · Burst Step","rules":"Air Force: replace one attack with a ranged physical-pressure attack, range 60 ft. Make a ranged CE attack; on hit deal 1 Stockpile Die + your Strength or Dexterity modifier bludgeoning damage. You may make it a Smash normally. Burst Step: when you Smash, move 5 feet × the Output Band without provoking from the target you hit."},{"level":3,"title":"Full Cowl · Fifth Vestige: Blackwhip","rules":"Gain Full Cowl and awaken Blackwhip. As a bonus action for 1 CE, manifest up to PB tendrils for 1 minute. They have 30-ft reach; you can replace an attack to lash for 1 Stockpile Die force, grapple on hit against a Large-or-smaller target, or anchor to terrain. One creature can be grappled by your Blackwhip at a time."},{"level":4,"title":"Fine Distribution","rules":"While Full Cowl is active, you may choose one limb to operate one Output Band higher than the rest of your body for one attack or movement without raising your entire Cowl. Overdraw is calculated for that limb only. This is the foundation of precise percentage control."},{"level":5,"title":"Blackwhip Mobility · Rescue Line","rules":"Once on each of your turns, if Blackwhip is anchored to a surface, pull yourself up to 20 feet without an action and without provoking opportunity attacks. As a reaction when a willing creature within Blackwhip range falls or is forcibly moved, spend 1 CE to catch it and move it up to 15 feet toward you or a safe anchor."},{"level":6,"title":"Fourth Vestige: Danger Sense","rules":"You cannot be surprised by a creature whose hostile intent you could perceive. When a creature you can perceive intentionally targets you with an attack or forces you to make a Dexterity save, you may spend 1 CE as a reaction to roll your Stockpile Die and add it to AC against that attack or to the save. Accidents and impersonal hazards do not trigger Danger Sense."},{"level":7,"title":"Air Force Mastery · Delaware Pressure","rules":"Air Force range becomes 90 ft. Once per turn, when it hits, spend 1 extra CE to create a 15-foot cone behind the target; creatures in the cone make a Dexterity save, taking 2 Stockpile Dice bludgeoning on failure or half on success. This secondary cone cannot crit or Black Flash."},{"level":8,"title":"Sixth Vestige: Smokescreen","rules":"Action · 2 CE: exhale a 20-foot-radius cloud centered on yourself for up to 1 minute. The area is heavily obscured to sight. Strong wind disperses it; rain halves its maximum radius. Danger Sense still functions inside your own smoke, but does not grant sight."},{"level":9,"title":"Blackwhip Reinforcement · Tendon Bracing","rules":"Wrap Blackwhip around or through one limb as a bonus action. While braced, ignore disadvantage caused by that limb being broken, though it remains injured. When that limb causes Anime & Manga recoil, reduce Recoil Steps by 1 (minimum 1). A severed limb cannot be replaced by this feature."},{"level":10,"title":"Seventh Vestige: Float","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE: for 1 minute, gain a flying speed equal to your walking speed and hover. Full Cowl's speed bonus also increases this flying speed. While carrying a creature with Blackwhip, your flight is not reduced unless normal carrying capacity is exceeded."},{"level":11,"title":"Third Vestige: Kinetic Surge · Continuous Smashes","rules":"Former name: this vestige was previously called “Fa Jin”; “Kinetic Surge” is the same feature, and “Kinetic Surge Charges” are the former Fa Jin Charges.Kinetic Surge Charges: maximum PB. Once per turn after you voluntarily move at least 20 feet, make at least two physical attacks, or spend an action performing repetitive motion, gain 1 Charge. When you move or Smash, spend any Charges; each contributes +15% effective output to that movement or Smash without increasing actual body output or recoil. You may now Smash up to twice per turn. Your Blackwhip reach increases to 60 feet."},{"level":12,"title":"Faux 100%","rules":"If actual output + Kinetic Surge contribution reaches 100%, treat one Smash or movement burst as 100% for its benefits while calculating recoil only from the actual output. Example: 40% Full Cowl + four Kinetic Surge Charges = one effective 100% burst with no overdraw if 40% is safe."},{"level":13,"title":"Vestige Council · Full Blast","rules":"The Vestiges can communicate coherently during rests and moments of extreme focus. Once per short rest, after failing an Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, or technique-related check, add your Stockpile Die to the result. Smokescreen's radius increases to 40 feet; spending +2 CE creates Full Blast, radius 60 feet."},{"level":14,"title":"Second Vestige: Gearshift","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE, up to 3 rounds. Apply Gearshift to yourself, a willing creature/object you touch, or a hostile creature hit by a physical attack (Constitution save negates). Once per turn choose Low, Second, Third, or Top Gear. Gearshift changes velocity without conventional acceleration; see the Vestige section for exact states. Gearshift normally remains gated until this level because it changes the action and velocity game dramatically."},{"level":15,"title":"Transmission · Suspended Smoke","rules":"Once per turn when you physically hit a creature while Gearshift is active, change its Gear without an extra action; a hostile target makes the normal Constitution save. You may also apply Low Gear to your own Smokescreen for 1 CE, causing it to remain fixed in place and ignore ordinary wind dispersal until the start of your next turn."},{"level":16,"title":"Deku Overlay · Blackchain","rules":"Overlay: bonus action, 2 CE; Blackwhip braces your entire body until the start of your next turn, reducing Full Cowl Recoil Steps by 2 (minimum 1) and allowing a broken limb to function. Blackchain: when Blackwhip pulls or slams a creature, spend Kinetic Surge Charges; each adds one Stockpile Die to the collision and 10 feet to the forced movement."},{"level":17,"title":"Overdrive · Quintuple Sequence","rules":"While Gearshift and Full Cowl are both active, spend at least 2 Kinetic Surge Charges when you Smash to enter Overdrive: effective output may reach 120%. Treat 101–120% as 100% for Smash dice but add +2 Stockpile Dice and +20 ft movement. After the sequence ends, Gearshift immediately applies its recoil. Once per turn, after moving at least 30 feet under Gearshift, you may make one additional unarmed/weapon attack as part of your Attack action; this extra attack cannot itself grant another extra attack."},{"level":18,"title":"Anime & Manga Unbound","rules":"Stockpile Die becomes 2d8. Full Cowl can support every unlocked Vestige simultaneously. The first time each turn you activate a different Vestige feature, reduce its CE cost by 1 (minimum 0). You may Smash up to PB times per turn, still paying each Smash normally. Kinetic Surge can gain up to 2 Charges per turn if you satisfy two different charging conditions. Your Blackwhip reach increases to 120 feet."},{"level":19,"title":"Forbidden Succession · Vestige Sacrifice","rules":"When a physical Smash hits, you may attempt to forcibly transfer one inherited Vestige into the target. Permanently lose access to that Vestige's sub-technique and its combinations; the target makes a Charisma save. On failure, it takes 8 Stockpile Dice psychic/force damage, cannot use reactions until its next turn, and one soul/technique effect of the GM's choice is fractured or suppressed for 1 round. On success, half damage and no suppression. This is a story-altering sacrifice, not a repeatable damage rotation."},{"level":20,"title":"The Ninth's Completion","rules":"Safe Output becomes 100% and Stockpile Die becomes 2d10. Full Cowl at 100% costs 1 CE to activate but no maintenance. The first 100% Smash you make on each turn costs 0 CE. Once per turn, one Vestige feature that normally uses a bonus action may be activated as a free action. Your body is finally capable of treating the inherited stockpile as its natural state.Safe 100% · 2d10 Stockpile Die · Vestige orchestra"}],"e099":[{"level":1,"title":"One-Way Road","rules":"Reaction · 1 CE · When a known external attack/effect would hit you: force the attacker to reroll the attack against itself or redirect a line/projectile up to 60 ft; against save effects: advantage and no damage on success. Vector Touch: 1 CE on a weapon/unarmed hit: +1 Vector Die force and push/pull 10 ft. · Passive · Vector Die scales with character level: d6 (1–4) → d8 (5–10) → d10 (11–16) → d12 (17–20)."},{"level":3,"title":"Vector Rewrite","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · 1 minute: alter your gravity/momentum: +20 speed, move along walls/ceilings, standing leaps use running distance. The Filter answers mundane weapon/projectile attacks without your reaction (still 1 CE, once/round)."},{"level":6,"title":"Atmospheric Weapon","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 60-ft line of compressed air: Dex save, 4 Vector Dice slashing/force. Bioelectric Rewrite: on a successful grapple/touch attack, 3 CE: Con save or 3 Vector Dice lightning and lose reactions until next turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Advanced Filter","rules":"Passive · Maintain PB adaptation entries through a long rest; permit harmless vectors (light, sound, oxygen, allies' touch, chosen healing). Once/round: attempt the Calculation check vs an unknown effect without spending a reaction."},{"level":11,"title":"Vector Transformation","rules":"Action · 5 CE · A point within 90 ft, 20-ft radius, violently attracts or repels: Str save or 6 Vector Dice force and moved 30 ft (success: half, no movement). Reflected damage may be converted to force, lightning, or thunder."},{"level":13,"title":"Black Wings","rules":"Bonus action · 6 CE · Once per long rest · 1 minute: fly 80 ft; the Filter's first CE cost each round drops to 0; Vector Touch adds two dice; reflect one failed-save external damage effect as though you had succeeded."},{"level":15,"title":"Plasma Geometry","rules":"Action · 7 CE · 120 ft: plasma spear or sphere: Dex save, 8 Vector Dice lightning/fire, Blinded until next turn on failed save. Requires atmosphere (no vacuum)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion, One-Way World","rules":"Domain · 175-ft barrier · 1,000 clash points · 3-round burnout · At initiative 20 choose PUSH, PULL, or REVERSE: every hostile makes a Str save or takes 8 Vector Dice force and moves 40 ft in the chosen direction (REVERSE knocks prone instead). Anti-domain protection restores the save normally."},{"level":20,"title":"Platinum Calculation","rules":"Passive · The Filter answers any analyzed external phenomenon, including bizarre CE interactions, until explicitly changed. Once/round: Calculation check as no action. Black Wings: no daily limit (still costs CE); at 10 CE becomes Platinum Wings: +2 damage per Vector Die."}],"e100":[{"level":1,"title":"Leash","rules":"Action · 2 CE · One Eligible creature within 30 ft: Cha save; failure: Charmed and Compelled for 1 minute (obeys simple commands, not obvious self-destruction). Repeat save after taking damage from you. · Passive · Dominion Die scales with character level: d6 (1–4) → d8 (5–10) → d10 (11–16) → d12 (17–20)."},{"level":3,"title":"Public Safety Contract","rules":"Long rest · Voluntary Binding Contract with a willing creature: one benefit, one real price. Maintain PB active written contracts. Contracts cannot grant features neither party possesses."},{"level":6,"title":"Borrowed Authority","rules":"Passive · Fail Dominion by 5+: Dominated for 24 hours instead of 1 minute. While within 120 ft: action + normal CE cost to use one of its non-Domain, non-Maximum features with your CE DC; it can't use that feature until your next turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Eyes and Ears","rules":"Action · Perceive through controlled Tiny beasts within 1 mile. Rat Road: action · 3 CE · teleport between two spaces within 1 mile if controlled vermin stand at both ends."},{"level":11,"title":"Chain Invocation","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Spectral chains to one Dominated creature within 120 ft for 1 minute: once/turn use one eligible feature through the chain. Damage through Borrowed Authority capped at 6 Dominion Dice."},{"level":13,"title":"Sacrificial Contract","rules":"Downtime · One major contract with a willing polity/organization (GM sets the price). Once per long rest: redirect a fatal hit to the contract's stated payment if the agreement supports it."},{"level":15,"title":"Invisible Force","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Creature within 90 ft: Con save, 6 Dominion Dice force; failure also prone and cannot take reactions. Dominated targets auto-fail the prone/reaction portion."},{"level":18,"title":"Rule Domain, Cabinet of Necessary Evil","rules":"Domain · Level 18 · 8 CE · No sure-hit; a rule instead. On entry each creature declares or conceals an allegiance; at initiative 20 hostiles make a Cha save: failure gains a Rank Below token (2 = Charmed, 3 = Dominated until the Domain ends). Damaging you removes one token from the attacker."},{"level":20,"title":"Conquest Devil","rules":"Passive · Dominion range 120 ft. Creatures you reduce to 0 HP may be stabilized and offered a final Cha save; failure: Dominated for 7 days. Maintain 2× CE modifier Dominated (only CE modifier as active combatants)."}],"e101":[{"level":1,"title":"Rip Cord","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · 1 minute · Manifest arm/head chainsaws: unarmed strikes deal 1d8 slashing, plus one Devour Die once per turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Blood-Fed Engine","rules":"Passive · When you deal slashing damage: gain 1 Blood token (max PB) · Bonus action: spend any tokens to regain one Devour Die HP per token (technique healing, not RCT)."},{"level":6,"title":"Hero's Rush","rules":"Passive (while Rip Cord active) · +10 speed · When you reduce a creature to 0 HP: as a reaction, move half your speed and make one chainsaw attack."},{"level":9,"title":"Devil Butcher","rules":"Passive · Chainsaw attacks ignore resistance to slashing and necrotic · Criticals vs summons, curses, or shikigami suppress regeneration until the start of your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Partial Devour","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Over an eligible supernatural creature at 0 HP: CE ability check vs DC 10 + target's PB (proxy PB 2 + CR÷4 rounded down, min 2 for CR creatures) · Success: remove one named feature, damage immunity, or summon form from its future manifestations for 24 hours · Bosses may use Legendary Resistance."},{"level":13,"title":"Hero of Hell","rules":"Bonus action · 6 CE · 1 minute, once/long rest · Large size, +20 speed, climb speed, advantage on Str checks/saves, chainsaw reach 10 ft, +2 Devour Dice on attacks · Cannot speak intelligibly while transformed."},{"level":15,"title":"Fear Resonance","rules":"Passive · A creature within 60 ft that is Frightened of you: your first attack against it each round has advantage · If a creature publicly survives or defeats you, the GM may deny this benefit against witnesses until you reestablish terror."},{"level":18,"title":"True Devour","rules":"10 CE + 1 uninterrupted minute consuming the manifested core of a unique supernatural entity you personally reduced to 0 HP · Cha save · Failure: erase one core concept from the campaign until a Maximum-level reversal (success: Partial Devour for 7 days) · Player and GM must agree beforehand on what the erasure means."},{"level":20,"title":"Chainsaw Man","rules":"Passive · Hero of Hell loses its daily limit · Once/long rest, when killed with 3+ Blood tokens or a willing ally's blood: return at 1 HP after 1 round with Rip Cord auto-activated."}],"e102":[{"level":1,"title":"Dark Cloaked Slash","rules":"On a weapon hit · 1 CE · Add one Dark Die necrotic or force · Ki Read also grants +2 initiative while active."},{"level":3,"title":"Black Hole","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · When a ranged attack or line effect crosses within 10 ft: technique contest vs the attacker · Success: consume the projectile/effect before it hits you · Failure: reduce its damage by 2 Dark Dice."},{"level":6,"title":"Avidya Wild Slash","rules":"Action · 3 CE · One weapon attack vs every hostile within reach, +2 Dark Dice per hit · Move up to 10 ft total between attacks."},{"level":9,"title":"Mana Zone","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Focus, 1 minute · 30-ft aura: know the location of moving creatures inside; your Dark techniques may originate from any point in the aura."},{"level":11,"title":"Dimension Slash","rules":"Action · 6 CE · 120-ft line: technique attack vs each creature/object in the line, 7 Dark Dice force or slashing · Ignores mundane cover and slashing resistance; barriers take maximum dice."},{"level":13,"title":"Black Moon","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · While Mana Zone is active: 15-ft selective nullification field around you until your next turn · Hostile CE projectiles/effects entering it make a technique contest or are erased; allied effects pass untouched."},{"level":15,"title":"Iai: Death Draw","rules":"Reaction · 4 CE · When a creature within Mana Zone attacks, teleports, or enters your reach: move up to 15 ft and make one weapon attack with advantage · +4 Dark Dice on hit; can Black Flash."},{"level":18,"title":"Equinox","rules":"Maximum-style technique · Action · 10 CE · Dimension Slash becomes a 300-ft line at 12 Dark Dice · Cuts barrier seams and spatial constructs (Domains still use normal clash/counter rules)."},{"level":20,"title":"Captain's Black Moon","rules":"Passive · Mana Zone: 60-ft radius, no longer occupies Technique Focus · Once/round: Black Hole or Iai costs 0 CE · Dimension Slash attacks within the zone crit on 19–20."}],"e103":[{"level":1,"title":"Time Theft","rules":"On a weapon/CE hit · 1 CE · Target Con save · Failure: +2 TU and speed −10 ft until your next turn · Once/turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Chrono Step","rules":"Bonus action · 2 TU · Move up to half speed without provoking, OR +2 AC until the start of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Stasis Sphere","rules":"Action · 3 CE + 3 TU · One creature within 60 ft: Con save · Failure: Restrained and Incapacitated until the end of your next turn (your damage ends it after resolving)."},{"level":9,"title":"Stored Future","rules":"Reaction · 4 TU · When you fail a Dex save or are hit: rewind to where you began your previous turn and reroll the triggering save/attack · Once/round."},{"level":11,"title":"Accelerate","rules":"Bonus action · 4 CE + 5 TU · Until end of turn: one additional action usable only for Attack (one attack), Dash, Disengage, or one technique of 3 CE or less · Once/round."},{"level":13,"title":"Age to Dust","rules":"Action · 6 CE + 8 TU · Creature within 60 ft: Con save, 8 Time Dice necrotic · Failure: max HP also reduced by half the damage until long rest/RCT repair · Constructs take maximum dice instead (no max-HP loss)."},{"level":15,"title":"Chrono Anastasis","rules":"Action · 10 CE + all TU (min 15) · Once/long rest · Rewind a 30-ft radius to its state at the end of the previous round: restore destroyed terrain, HP lost since then, and prior positions · Does not restore CE, limited uses, Domains, dead creatures, or erased concepts."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion, Archive of the Stolen Hour","rules":"Domain Expansion · 175-ft barrier · At initiative 20 declare FREEZE, AGE, or RETURN: hostiles Con save — FREEZE loses reactions and speed becomes 0 until next initiative 20; AGE takes 8 Time Dice necrotic; RETURN teleports failures to their position at the previous initiative 20 · Anti-domain protection uses the normal save; your ordinary attacks roll normally."},{"level":20,"title":"Time Emperor","rules":"Passive · TU maximum doubles · Start every combat with 10 TU if lower · Once/round: successful Time Theft grants +2 additional TU · Accelerate may instead grant one full extra action for 8 TU + 6 CE."}],"e105":[{"level":1,"title":"Five-Finger Decay","rules":"On a successful unarmed/grapple touch · 1 CE · +1 Decay Die necrotic and 1 Mark · Objects take double dice."},{"level":3,"title":"Crumbling Hold","rules":"Passive · A creature you are grappling gains 1 additional Mark at the start of your turn · You may voluntarily suppress Decay on touched targets."},{"level":6,"title":"Crumble","rules":"On a hit vs a 5-Mark target · 3 CE · +4 Decay Dice necrotic, clear all Marks · If the single-hit damage meets the injury threshold: qualifies as a targeted catastrophic hit without disadvantage."},{"level":9,"title":"Four Fingers","rules":"Passive · Direct Decay needs only deliberate hand contact (no full-hand condition) · Once/turn: when a Marked creature touches another creature or solid structure, spend 1 CE to put 1 Mark on the second target."},{"level":11,"title":"Awakening","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Touch solid ground: Decay spreads through connected solid surfaces in a 30-ft radius · Creatures touching affected matter Dex save: 5 Decay Dice necrotic + 2 Marks on failure, half damage + 1 Mark on success."},{"level":13,"title":"Selective Ruin","rules":"Passive (Awakening upgrade) · When using Awakening, spare up to your CE modifier creatures/objects entirely · Awakening radius becomes 60 ft."},{"level":15,"title":"Avalanche","rules":"Passive (Awakening upgrade) · Awakening propagates through the debris it creates until end of turn · Radius 90 ft · Failed saves also knock prone; ruined ground becomes difficult terrain."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique, Deika Collapse","rules":"Maximum technique · Action · 10 CE · 150-ft radius through connected solid matter: Dex save, 10 Decay Dice necrotic + 3 Marks on failure, half damage + 1 Mark on success · Structures take maximum damage · Recoil: 4 Decay Dice unpreventable damage to you and one arm suffers a Break check."},{"level":20,"title":"Liberated Decay","rules":"Passive · Awakening radius 120 ft at normal cost · Direct touch applies 2 Marks · Once/turn: a creature reaching 5 Marks triggers Crumble for 0 CE · Precisely route chain Decay around chosen creatures/objects."}],"e106":[{"level":1,"title":"Disassemble","rules":"Action (or replace one Attack) · Touch attack · 1 CE · 2 Overhaul Dice force/necrotic; objects take maximum dice · Reconstruction: action · 1 AP + 1 CE · Restore one mundane object or heal a touched creature 2 Overhaul Dice."},{"level":3,"title":"Ground Spikes","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Reshape a 15-ft line of ground: Dex save, 3 Overhaul Dice piercing and prone · Or create cover/terrain instead if desired."},{"level":6,"title":"Biological Repair","rules":"Action · 2 AP + 3 CE · Heal 4 Overhaul Dice + CE modifier; end one poisoned/blinded/deafened or broken-limb penalty if enough tissue remains · Cannot restore soul damage."},{"level":9,"title":"Instant Reassembly","rules":"Reaction · 2 AP + 3 CE · When you or an adjacent willing creature takes a qualifying physical injury: prevent the injury condition after the damage resolves · Once/round."},{"level":11,"title":"Fusion","rules":"4 AP + 5 CE · During 1 minute of contact with a willing/incapacitated creature: fuse for up to 10 minutes · Gain temp HP equal to half the target's max HP and one physical trait/proficiency; with explicit GM approval, one borrowed non-Domain active feature using your CE · Ending fusion restores separate bodies at current proportional HP."},{"level":13,"title":"Terrain Dominion","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Restructure a 30-ft cube of contiguous nonmagical terrain (walls, spikes, pits, ramps, open paths): creatures caught Dex save or take 6 Overhaul Dice and move to the nearest legal space."},{"level":15,"title":"Complete Rebuild","rules":"Action · 4 AP + 6 CE · Restore a severed limb/eye, or rebuild a creature reduced to 0 HP within the last round to 1 HP if its soul has not departed · Once/long rest per creature."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion, Operating Theater of Perfect Matter","rules":"Domain Expansion · 175-ft barrier · At initiative 20 declare DISASSEMBLE or REASSEMBLE: DISASSEMBLE — hostiles Con save, 8 Overhaul Dice force/necrotic and one carried non-artifact item broken on failure; REASSEMBLE — chosen allies heal 5 Overhaul Dice and may end one physical condition · Anti-domain protection affects the event normally; ordinary Overhaul still needs rolls/touch."},{"level":20,"title":"Perfect Reconstruction","rules":"Passive · AP maximum doubles · Reconstruction healing uses maximum Overhaul Dice once/turn · Disassemble crits add 2 injury-threshold dice for Break only · Once/long rest: Complete Rebuild affects creatures dead up to 1 minute if the soul is willing and available."}],"e107":[{"level":1,"title":"Blood Drinker","rules":"Action over a helpless/0-HP eligible creature · 1 CE · Absorb one soul · Bonus action: spend 1 soul to heal 2 Crimson Dice (not RCT)."},{"level":3,"title":"Black Hound","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 1 minute · Manifest a shadow familiar occupying your space/reach: once/turn after your attack lands, +2 Crimson Dice necrotic to one target you hit."},{"level":6,"title":"Extra Life","rules":"Reaction · 3 souls · When reduced to 0 HP (not conceptual/soul destruction): drop to 1 HP instead and immediately heal 2 Crimson Dice · Once/round."},{"level":9,"title":"Named Familiar","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 1 minute · Manifest one stored Elite/Named soul: AC 13 + PB, HP 6 × your level, 30-ft speed, one attack at your CE attack bonus for 2 Crimson Dice · Acts after you, one action/round; no Domains/Maxima."},{"level":11,"title":"Vampiric Body","rules":"Passive · Resistance to necrotic and nonmagical B/P/S; climb 30 ft · Bonus action · 2 CE · Become mist/shadow until your next turn: pass through 1-inch gaps, no attacks."},{"level":13,"title":"Control Art Restriction Level One","rules":"Bonus action · 5 CE · 1 minute · Release up to PB familiars at once; command all with one bonus action · While active, Extra Life costs 2 souls."},{"level":15,"title":"True Vampire","rules":"Passive · Blood Drinker absorbs a qualifying creature you reduced to 0 HP as a reaction (once/round) · Named Familiar may use one approved signature feature from its life."},{"level":18,"title":"Control Art Restriction Level Zero","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Release any number of stored souls as a 120-ft-radius army for up to 10 minutes (abstracted as up to CE modifier swarms + Named Familiars, not hundreds of initiatives) · While active you cannot use Extra Life · When it ends, surviving souls return; destroyed ones are lost."},{"level":20,"title":"Everywhere and Nowhere, Optional Schrödinger Pinnacle","rules":"Story prerequisite (not a purchase) · Permanently consume all souls but one paradox soul: thereafter no Soul Stock/Level Zero · Once/long rest, when killed or removed from space: reappear at the start of your next turn in a perceivable space within 120 ft at half HP."}],"e108":[{"level":1,"title":"Negate Death","rules":"Passive · At 0 HP: no unconsciousness; speed halved, attacks/checks at disadvantage until above 0 · Start of each turn: heal at least 1 HP from Repair Reserve before acting (if points remain) · Soul-destroying or technique-suppressing effects can still kill you."},{"level":3,"title":"Parts Bullet","rules":"Action (or replace one Attack) · Voluntarily lose 1d6 HP (unpreventable; triggers normal regeneration) · Ranged attack 60 ft: 2 Undead Dice piercing."},{"level":6,"title":"Blood Propulsion","rules":"Bonus action · Lose up to PB HP · Move 10 ft per HP lost, vertically included, without provoking · Dead Line: action, lose 5 HP · 60-ft line: Dex save, 4 Undead Dice slashing."},{"level":9,"title":"Repair Boost","rules":"On a melee weapon/unarmed attack · Lose 1–PB HP · Add that many Undead Dice · Once/turn · May regenerate around implanted weapons for quickdraw attacks."},{"level":11,"title":"Division","rules":"Action · Lose 10 HP + 3 CE · 1 minute · Up to PB severed-part pseudo-clones, abstracted as one swarm in your or an adjacent space · Once/turn, bonus action: CE attack vs one creature within 30 ft, 3 Undead Dice bludgeoning/piercing on hit."},{"level":13,"title":"Dead Road","rules":"Action · Lose 10 HP + 5 CE · 90-ft line: Dex save, 7 Undead Dice slashing/force · Blood/bone bends around one corner, ignoring half cover."},{"level":15,"title":"Interpretation Shift","rules":"After a long rest, choose one: AGE IS DEATH (immune to magical aging), STASIS IS DEATH (advantage vs petrify/stasis; 10 Repair ends it), DISMEMBERMENT IS DEATH (sever repair costs halved), or UNCONSCIOUSNESS IS DEATH (cannot be knocked unconscious while Repair remains)."},{"level":18,"title":"Victor","rules":"Bonus action · 6 CE · 1 minute, once/long rest · Repair healing doubles; Parts Bullet and Dead Line gain +2 dice; Division swarm becomes two swarms; voluntary HP costs cannot reduce you below 1."},{"level":20,"title":"Undead Completion","rules":"Passive · Repair Reserve doubles and refreshes whenever you finish a combat at 1+ HP · Choose a second Interpretation Shift · Once/long rest: if an effect would kill you despite Undead, CE ability/Constitution save vs the source DC to reinterpret the death condition and survive at 1 HP (records that death method; not vs conceptual/soul erasure)."}],"e109":[{"level":1,"title":"Yamato","rules":"Passive (manifested cursed katana) · Once/turn: on a hit, spend 1 CE for +1d8 force with a 10-ft spatial extension."},{"level":3,"title":"Trick","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Teleport 20 ft to a visible space or marked target (30 ft at 5 Concentration)."},{"level":6,"title":"Judgement Cut","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Target a point within 60 ft: creatures in a 10-ft sphere Dex save, 4d10 force/slashing · At 10 Concentration: may replace one Attack once/turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Mirage Blades","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Create PB blades (spend before next long rest): +1d8 force on attacks, pin movement 10 ft, or make a 60-ft ranged technique attack."},{"level":11,"title":"Doppelganger","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Spectral double repeats one weapon attack or Judgement Cut at the end of each of your turns for half dice, no extra riders."},{"level":13,"title":"Devil Trigger","rules":"Action · 5 CE · 1 minute · 40-ft fly, +10 speed, resistance to bludgeoning/piercing/slashing and necrotic, heal PB HP at the start of your turn, Yamato +1d8."},{"level":15,"title":"Judgement Cut End","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Requires 10 Concentration · 40-ft radius: Dex save, 10d10 force/slashing, half on success · Concentration becomes 0."},{"level":18,"title":"Sin Devil Trigger","rules":"Action · 8 CE · 1 minute, once/long rest · 80-ft fly, resistance to all but psychic/radiant, Yamato +2d8, Trick free once/turn, regain 1 Concentration at the start of your turn."},{"level":20,"title":"Motivated","rules":"Passive · Concentration maximum 12; being hit removes only 1 · At 10+: the first Judgement Cut each round costs 0 CE · Once/long rest: enter Sin Devil Trigger at 10 Concentration for 0 CE."}],"e110":[{"level":1,"title":"Style Switch","rules":"Bonus action · Choose a Style: Swordmaster (+1 weapon die once/turn), Gunslinger (+30 ranged range, ignore half cover), Trickster (+10 speed, Disengage), or Royalguard (reaction: reduce damage by 1d10 + level)."},{"level":3,"title":"Devil Arm Arsenal","rules":"Passive · Bind up to PB cursed weapons · Draw/swap freely once/turn; all qualify for your Style features."},{"level":6,"title":"Royal Release","rules":"Passive · Each Royalguard reduction stores 1 Guard (max PB) · On a melee hit: spend any Guard for +1d10 force each."},{"level":9,"title":"Devil Trigger","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 1 minute · 30-ft fly, heal PB HP/turn, resistance to bludgeoning/piercing/slashing, attacks +1d8 · Cost becomes 3 CE at S rank."},{"level":11,"title":"Devil Sword Dante","rules":"Once/turn · 2 CE · Weave four Mirage Swords: +2d8 force on an attack, +2 AC until your next turn, or four 1d8 bolts split among targets."},{"level":13,"title":"Quadruple Style","rules":"Passive · Switch Style once/turn without spending the bonus action · At SS+: benefit from two Styles simultaneously."},{"level":15,"title":"Sin Gauge","rules":"At SSS: convert 6 CE into a full Sin Gauge · Bonus action (consume gauge): Sin Devil Trigger for 3 rounds — 80-ft fly, resistance to all but psychic/radiant, attacks +2d10, access to Sin Stinger and Demolition · Sin Stinger (action, 2 CE): melee CE attack, 4d10 force, target Str save or launched 20 ft upward and prone · Demolition (action, 4 CE): 20-ft burst within 60 ft, Dex save, 6d10 force (half on success)."},{"level":18,"title":"Quadruple S","rules":"Passive · At SSS, once/short rest: Sin Devil Trigger for one round without consuming the Sin Gauge."},{"level":20,"title":"Legendary Dark Knight","rules":"Passive · Style cannot fall below B while conscious · First Style switch each round is free · At SSS: all four Styles function simultaneously."}],"e111":[{"level":1,"title":"Masamune","rules":"Passive · 10-ft reach cursed odachi, 1d10 slashing · On hit, spend 1 CE: +1d8 force and may pull or push 10 ft."},{"level":3,"title":"Shadow Flare","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Ranged, 60 ft, Dex save · 3d8 force; three dark orbs may split among targets."},{"level":6,"title":"Octaslash","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Make three Masamune attacks; each attack after the first deals weapon dice only, no ability modifier."},{"level":9,"title":"Heartless Angel","rules":"Action · 5 CE · One creature within 60 ft, Con save · 6d10 necrotic; on failure the target cannot regain HP until the start of his next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"One Wing","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 1 minute: fly 60 ft, +10 speed, Masamune +1d8, immune to Frightened."},{"level":13,"title":"Hell's Gate","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · After falling at least 20 ft: plunge to the point below · 15-ft radius, Dex save, 6d10 piercing/force and prone on failure."},{"level":15,"title":"Pale Horse","rules":"Action · 6 CE · 90 ft, Con save · 8d10 necrotic plus Poisoned until the end of his next turn; failed by 5+ also inflicts 1 Despair."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Nibelheim's Burning Memory","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20 each hostile chooses FACE (Wis save, 8d8 psychic on failure) or FLEE (moved 30 ft toward the boundary, +1 Despair) · At 3 Despair the FACE save is at disadvantage."},{"level":20,"title":"Safer Sephiroth","rules":"Passive · One Wing loses its daily restriction; flight becomes 80 ft · At 3 Despair the Masamune crits on 19–20 · Once per long rest, survive lethal damage at 1 HP and immediately gain One Wing."}],"e112":[{"level":1,"title":"Bullet Arts","rules":"Free · Once per turn after a melee attack: 30-ft ranged attack, 1d6 piercing, no ability modifier."},{"level":3,"title":"Witch Time","rules":"Reaction · 1 Tempo · After avoiding an attack or save: the attacker’s speed becomes 0, it has no reactions, and she has advantage against it until the end of her next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Wicked Weave","rules":"Trigger · 2 CE · After two hits in the same turn: a giant infernal limb strikes, 3d10 force, Str save or launched 20 ft."},{"level":9,"title":"Beast Within","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · For the round, movement form: Panther (+30 speed), Crow (50-ft flight), or Bat (reaction: resistance to one hit)."},{"level":11,"title":"Infernal Summon","rules":"Action · 4 CE · One demon attack: Gomorrah’s bite (melee CE attack, 10-ft reach, 6d10); Madama’s punch (melee CE attack, 5d10, Str save or launched 20 ft); Phantasmaraneae (20-ft burst within 60 ft, Dex save, 5d8 fire, half on success)."},{"level":13,"title":"Demon Masquerade","rules":"Action · 5 CE · 1 minute: choose a bound demon; gain its flight or climb, resistance to one type, attacks +1d10, and a unique movement trait."},{"level":15,"title":"Umbran Climax","rules":"Free · 3 Tempo · For one turn, every qualifying melee hit manifests Wicked Weave: +1d10 without CE, maximum once per attack."},{"level":18,"title":"Queen Sheba Contract","rules":"Action · Once per long rest · 10 CE + all Tempo · Colossal infernal strike: 60-ft line or 30-ft burst, Str save, 12d12 force/fire, hurled 60 ft on failure."},{"level":20,"title":"Witch Without Equal","rules":"Passive · Tempo maximum 10 · The first Witch Time each round costs 0 Tempo if triggered by a natural-20 save or an attack missing by 10+ · May maintain two Demon Masquerade traits simultaneously."}],"e113":[{"level":1,"title":"Lightning Bolt","rules":"Attack · 1 Charge · 60-ft ranged technique attack, 2d8 lightning · You resist lightning and can safely drain ordinary electrical systems."},{"level":3,"title":"Shock Grenade","rules":"Attack · 1 CE + 1 Charge · 15-ft burst, Dex save · 3d8 lightning/force."},{"level":6,"title":"Induction Grind","rules":"Utility · Ride power lines/rails at double speed · Static Thrusters: while falling, descend 60 ft per round, move horizontally up to your speed, and take no falling damage if you land during the glide · EMP: action, 2 CE, 30-ft cone, Str save or pushed 20 ft (half push on success)."},{"level":9,"title":"Bio-Leech / Healing Pulse","rules":"Long rest · Choose your karmic expression at dawn (holds until next dawn): Leech — a grappled enemy makes a Con save, you drain 3d8 HP and regain 2 Charge; Heal — spend 2 Charge to heal a touched ally 3d8."},{"level":11,"title":"Lightning Tether","rules":"Attack · 1 Charge · 60-ft grapple line · Pull yourself to terrain, or the target makes a Str save: on failure pull a Large-or-smaller target 20 ft."},{"level":13,"title":"Ionic Power","rules":"Attack · 3 Charge + 4 CE · Ionic Freeze (30-ft cone, Con save, 6d8 cold + restrained on failure) or Ionic Drain (20-ft radius, 5d8 necrotic, heal half the damage dealt)."},{"level":15,"title":"Lightning Storm","rules":"Focus · 6 CE + 4 Charge · 60-ft moving storm for 3 rounds · Bonus action: strike a 10-ft point for 5d10 lightning, Dex save."},{"level":18,"title":"Ionic Storm","rules":"Action · 8 CE + 6 Charge · Call a direct sky bolt at a visible target, Dex save, 12d10 lightning (half on success); adjacent creatures take 4d10."},{"level":20,"title":"Beast of the Grid","rules":"Passive · Charge max doubles · While standing in an active city grid, regain 1 Charge/round · Lightning immunity · Ionic Storm costs no Charge once per long rest."}],"e114":[{"level":1,"title":"Smoke","rules":"Attack · Smoke Shot: ranged CE attack, 60 ft, 2d8 fire · Smoke Dash: bonus action, 1 CE, teleport-like 20-ft movement through gaps."},{"level":3,"title":"Conduit Absorption","rules":"Downtime · 1 minute of contact with a willing or incapacitated supernatural elemental user, then a CE check · Success unlocks a GM-approved Mode after a milestone · Cannot copy Domains, innate passives, or whole cursed techniques."},{"level":6,"title":"Neon","rules":"Attack · Precision Beam: ranged CE attack, 90 ft, 3d8 radiant · Neon Dash: 40 ft including walls · A crit against a marked weak point reduces its speed to 0 until your next turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Video","rules":"Attack · Video Blade: ranged CE attack, 60 ft, 4d8 force · Bonus action, 2 CE: invisible until you attack or end of your next turn · Wings grant glide or fly 40 for the round."},{"level":11,"title":"Concrete","rules":"Attack · Concrete Barrage: ranged CE attack, 60 ft, 4d10 bludgeoning · +2 AC while active · Boulder Dash: move 30 ft; a creature you move through makes a Str save or is knocked prone."},{"level":13,"title":"Source Cache","rules":"Passive · Store one charge of each unlocked Mode · Spend a charge to switch anywhere without an environmental source · Refill: 1 minute of contact with a matching source, or an action to drain a willing or incapacitated elemental user."},{"level":15,"title":"Karmic Finishers","rules":"Special · Each Mode gains a 6 CE finisher, once per short rest per Mode · Each deals exactly 8d10 damage with its own area, save, rider, and duration (see below). · Action · 6 CE (finisher, once/short rest) · Point within 120 ft, 30-ft radius · Dex save: 8d10 fire and prone on failure; half damage, no prone on success. · Action · 6 CE (finisher, once/short rest) · 90-ft-long, 10-ft-wide line · Dex save: 8d10 radiant and blinded until the end of your next turn on failure; half damage, no blindness on success. · Action · 6 CE (finisher, once/short rest) · Point within 120 ft, 20-ft radius · Dex save: 8d10 force and no reactions until the end of your next turn on failure; half damage and no reaction loss on success. · Action · 6 CE (finisher, once/short rest) · Point within 90 ft, 20-ft radius · Dex save: 8d10 bludgeoning and restrained until the end of your next turn on failure; half damage and no restraint on success · Leaves a 1-minute raised rampart (half cover, AC 15, HP = 5 × your level)."},{"level":18,"title":"Hybrid Conduit","rules":"Action · 4 CE + two cached sources · 1 minute: combine two Modes, gaining both movement and passive traits, but attacks come from one Mode at a time."},{"level":20,"title":"Second Son","rules":"Passive · Maintain two Modes freely after unlocking Hybrid · Source Cache holds two charges each · Once per long rest, absorb one hostile elemental technique used on you: negate half its damage and gain its damage type as a temporary Mode until combat ends (damage type and basic use only)."}],"e115":[{"level":1,"title":"Consume","rules":"Action · Target a helpless or 0-HP biological creature: Consume it, gaining Biomass (5/10/20 by threat) and one Disguise memory profile · You may spend up to your PB in Biomass per turn to heal an equal number of HP."},{"level":3,"title":"Claws / Musclemass","rules":"Bonus action · Switch between consumed forms: Claws (1d8 slashing, and you can climb with them) or Musclemass (unarmed strikes deal 1d10, advantage on Athletics checks)."},{"level":6,"title":"Blade / Hammerfist","rules":"Passive · Blade form: 1d12 slashing · Hammerfist: 1d10; for 2 CE you can slam the ground — creatures in a 10-ft radius make a Str save or fall prone and are pushed 10 ft (the slam deals no damage to creatures); structures and unattended objects take 3d8 bludgeoning."},{"level":9,"title":"Whipfist","rules":"Passive · Whipfist form: 20-ft reach, 1d8 damage; on a hit you may spend 1 CE to grapple the target and pull it 20 ft · Shield form: as a reaction, spend 5 Biomass to reduce damage you take by 2d10 + your level."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfect Disguise","rules":"Passive · Consumed Disguise profiles copy the target’s appearance, voice, mundane memories, and proficiencies · They never copy cursed techniques, CE pools, Domains, souls, or supernatural bloodline features."},{"level":13,"title":"Armor","rules":"Bonus action · 10 Biomass · 1 minute: +3 AC, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing, speed reduced by 10 ft · Critical melee hits against you shed 1d4 Biomass."},{"level":15,"title":"Viral Ascendancy","rules":"Action · 5 CE · 1 minute: you may Consume as a bonus action at 30 ft (target helpless or 0 HP), and you may hold up to three consumed profiles’ traits at once, swapping between them as a bonus action."},{"level":18,"title":"Critical Mass","rules":"Passive · While you hold 75+ Biomass: your attacks deal +1d8 damage and your speed increases by 10 ft · When reduced to 0 HP, spend 30 Biomass to remain at 1 HP instead (once per round)."},{"level":20,"title":"Blacklight Apex","rules":"Passive · Biomass maximum doubles · Once per turn you may switch forms freely · You may Consume elite targets as a bonus action at 0 HP · Once per long rest, if your body is destroyed you may reform from 50 Biomass, unless your soul or concept has been erased."}],"e117":[{"level":1,"title":"Living Suit","rules":"Bonus action · Manifest the symbiote as a living suit: +1 AC, climb speed = walking speed, 10-ft tendril reach · Once per turn, on a melee hit you may spend 1 CE to deal +1d8 bludgeoning or slashing · Ablative Weave: once per round, when you take damage from an attack, reduce it by your PB + CE modifier."},{"level":3,"title":"Web & Tendril","rules":"Attack · 1 CE · Ranged grapple vs a Large-or-smaller creature at 30 ft using your CE attack; pull either creature 15 ft · At Bond 3 the range becomes 60 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Predatory Morphology","rules":"Bonus action · Choose one morphology: claws (1d12 slashing); blade tendrils (15-ft reach, 1d10 slashing); rampart (+2 AC, and use your reaction to interpose between an attacker and an ally within 15 ft — you become the target, and your Ablative Weave applies even if used this round); or bulk (advantage on Athletics, Powerful Build)."},{"level":9,"title":"Adaptive Camouflage","rules":"Action · 2 CE: become invisible while motionless · 3 CE (requires Focus): active camouflage for 1 minute; attacking ends it until the start of your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Symbiotic Recovery","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE: heal 4d10 + your CE modifier · Once per short rest, repair one Break injury · Ablative Tithe: when you take damage, use your reaction and spend 1 CE to reduce it by 3d8 · Fire or sonic damage taken since your previous turn halves this feature’s healing."},{"level":13,"title":"Host Override","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · When you would become Stunned or Paralyzed, or be knocked unconscious: the symbiote moves your body until the end of your next turn, suppressing one such condition · Once per short rest."},{"level":15,"title":"Perfect Bond","rules":"Passive · At Bond 6: +10 speed, +1 AC, +10 ft tendril reach, and once per turn swap morphology without a bonus action · Ablative Weave reduces damage by twice your PB + your CE modifier; rampart interception reaches 30 ft · Allies within 10 ft gain +1 AC."},{"level":18,"title":"King in Black Echo","rules":"Action · 6 CE · 1 minute: wing-like tendrils, fly speed 60, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing · Command up to PB detached symbiote fragments as one swarm: as a bonus action the swarm attacks one creature within 30 ft (CE attack, 4d10 slashing on hit)."},{"level":20,"title":"Lethal Protector","rules":"Passive · Bond cannot fall below 3 except through true separation · Your first morphology change and first tendril grapple each round are free · Once per long rest, survive at 1 HP when reduced to 0 HP and heal 5d10 · Once per long rest, when an ally within 30 ft takes damage from an attack, the symbiote intercepts on its own: you take the damage instead."}],"e118":[{"level":1,"title":"Red Weapon","rules":"Passive · Gain your Mass allocation (PB + 2); after each long rest distribute it among arsenal configurations · Switch configurations as a bonus action · Base configuration: Reaper Blade (1d8)."},{"level":3,"title":"Kill Chain","rules":"Passive · Gain the Kill Chain engine (see Core law above) · Striking a creature before it has acted builds +2 Chain · Adds the Shard Volley configuration (60-ft ranged, 2d8 piercing, 2 Mass) to your arsenal."},{"level":6,"title":"Autonomous Tendrils","rules":"Passive · At Chain 4+, immediately make one free Red Weapon attack per round vs a creature within 15 ft (the free attack builds Chain) · 2 CE, 1 minute: once per round as a reaction, make a tendril attack vs a creature that enters within 15 ft of you or attacks you."},{"level":9,"title":"Red Feast","rules":"Passive · When you deal slashing or piercing damage to a living creature with a Red Weapon, regain HP = your PB (once per turn), no cost · Fire or sonic damage you take suppresses this until your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Twin Manifestation","rules":"Passive · Your Mass allocation increases by 2 · You may keep two configurations manifested at once."},{"level":13,"title":"Red Finale","rules":"Trigger · When you hit with a Red Weapon at Chain 6+: reset your Chain to 0 to add +1d10 slashing damage per Chain point consumed · Once per turn."},{"level":15,"title":"Carnage Rules","rules":"Passive · Chain maximum becomes 12 · Reducing a living creature to 0 HP with a Red Weapon doesn’t reset Chain — it carries to your next target, and you may switch configurations without a bonus action · While Frightened or Charmed, use your bonus action to manifest a configuration and end the condition."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Carnage","rules":"Action · 8 CE · 1 minute: every committed configuration manifests at once, you become Large, tendril reach 30 ft, two reactions per round (tendrils only), Red Feast healing maximized once per turn, missing no longer resets Chain (only a hitless turn) · Costs no Mass."},{"level":20,"title":"Red Event","rules":"Passive · Mass allocation doubles · Death by a Thousand Cuts: at Chain 6+, make one extra Red Weapon attack as a bonus action each turn · Once per turn on a hit, creatures within 10 ft of the target (excluding you) take 4d10 slashing, Dex save for half."}],"e119":[{"level":1,"title":"Invisibility","rules":"Action · 2 CE (requires Focus): become invisible for 10 minutes · 3 CE: one additional willing creature also becomes invisible · If a target attacks, it is revealed only until the start of its next turn (the effect does not end)."},{"level":3,"title":"Force Screen","rules":"Reaction · 1 CE · Create a panel (AC 16) with up to PB×5 Integrity from your pool, intercepting one attack or line effect · Unspent Integrity remains in your pool."},{"level":6,"title":"Force Shapes","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Create within 60 ft for 1 minute: platform, bridge, bubble, ram, or 10-ft wall (platform/bridge: 10-ft square; bubble: 10-ft sphere; each costs Integrity = 5 × its longest dimension in feet) · The ram makes a melee CE attack (reach 15 ft): 3d10 force and push 15 ft on a hit."},{"level":9,"title":"Selective Dome","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 15-ft-radius dome with up to 40 Integrity · Creatures you choose may pass; others cannot except by breaking through or teleporting."},{"level":11,"title":"Flight","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Grant a 50-ft fly speed to you or one willing creature for 10 minutes."},{"level":13,"title":"Internal Bubble","rules":"Action · 5 CE · One creature within 60 ft makes a Con save: on failure takes 6d10 force damage and cannot speak until the end of its next turn."},{"level":15,"title":"City Wall","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Create up to six connected 10-ft panels, allocating up to 80 Integrity among them · You may reshape them as a bonus action."},{"level":18,"title":"Absolute Sphere","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Enclose one Huge-or-smaller target (Dex save to avoid); allocate up to 100 Integrity to the sphere · While trapped the target has total cover and cannot leave by ordinary movement."},{"level":20,"title":"Unseen Architect","rules":"Passive · Integrity pool doubles · Maintain PB constructs without Focus · The first Force Screen you create each round costs 0 CE · Invisibility affects PB creatures for the base 3 CE."}],"e120":[{"level":1,"title":"Flame On!","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · 1 minute: you are aflame — fire resistance, melee attackers take PB fire damage once per turn, and you can hurl a fire bolt (60 ft, 2d8)."},{"level":3,"title":"Jet Flight","rules":"Passive · While aflame: fly speed 50 ft · When you take the Dash action, leave a 5-ft fire trail until your next turn; enemies crossing it take 1d8 fire damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Fire Sculpting","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 15-ft cone or 60-ft line of flame: creatures in the area make a Dex save, taking 4d8 fire on failure · Or harmless shaped flame or light."},{"level":9,"title":"Superheated Body","rules":"Passive · At Heat 5+: fire immunity, your attacks deal +1d8 fire damage · Creatures grappling you take 2d8 fire damage."},{"level":11,"title":"Plasma Burst","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 20-ft burst within 90 ft: creatures in the area make a Dex save, taking 6d10 fire on failure."},{"level":13,"title":"White Flame","rules":"Passive · At Heat 8+: your fire ignores resistance and treats immunity as resistance · Ordinary flammable terrain ignites instantly."},{"level":15,"title":"Nova Instability","rules":"Passive · At Heat 10: +2 fire dice to your damaging techniques, but you take unpreventable damage = your PB at the end of each turn unless you vent 2 Heat as a bonus action."},{"level":18,"title":"Nova Flame","rules":"Action · 10 CE, at Heat 10 · Creatures in a 40-ft radius make a Con save, taking 12d10 fire/radiant on failure (half on success) · Your Heat becomes 0 and you gain exhaustion."},{"level":20,"title":"Living Star","rules":"Passive · Heat cannot fall below 3 while Flame On is active · Fly speed becomes 90 · The first fire technique you use each round gains +1 damage die · Once per long rest, Nova Flame causes no exhaustion."}],"e121":[{"level":1,"title":"Hex","rules":"Reaction · 1 CE · When a creature within 60 ft makes an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw: subtract 1d6 from the roll after it is made; once per round."},{"level":3,"title":"Telekinesis","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Move a Large-or-smaller object or creature 30 ft (unwilling creature makes a Strength save); you may hurl the target for 3d8 force damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Probability Collapse","rules":"Free (after a visible roll) · Spend 1 Chaos Die · Force one attack, save, or check within 60 ft to be rerolled; the new result stands; once per round."},{"level":9,"title":"Chaos Construct","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Create one: barrier (40 Integrity, AC 12 + PB), binding bands (restrained; escape vs your CE save DC), flight (40 ft), or a melee CE weapon (4d8 force); lasts 1 minute (requires Focus). Chaos Dice become d8s (d10s at L17)."},{"level":11,"title":"Mental Hex","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Target makes a Wisdom save; on a failure it is Charmed, Frightened, or trapped in a sensory illusion (your choice) until the end of its next turn; it repeats the save if damaged."},{"level":13,"title":"Rewrite Wound","rules":"Reaction · 5 CE + 1 Instability · When a creature within 30 ft takes damage: change the damage to half."},{"level":15,"title":"Localized Reality","rules":"Action · 6 CE + 2 Instability · Alter one 20-ft cube for 1 minute: gravity, terrain state, weather, harmless appearance, or one resistance/vulnerability relation (GM-approved)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, House of M","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20 declare one Rule (e.g. “flight fails”); affected creatures make a Charisma save or obey it until the next initiative 20. Rules cannot kill, erase techniques, or leave the Domain. Clash 1,000; burnout 3 rounds."},{"level":20,"title":"Scarlet Witch","rules":"Special · Once per long rest: 10 CE + 5 Instability for one GM-adjudicated, scene-level reality revision (never a PC's identity or agency without that player's consent). Chaos Dice become d12s; pool grows by 2."}],"e122":[{"level":1,"title":"Hulk Out","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · For 1 minute: you become Large, your unarmed strikes deal 1d10, you have advantage on Strength checks and saves, and you add your Rage (max +PB) to melee damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Thunder Clap","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 15-ft cone: creatures in the area make a Constitution save, taking 3d10 thunder damage on a failure and being pushed 15 ft."},{"level":6,"title":"Hulk Leap","rules":"Passive · Your jump distance is multiplied by 5. Special: when you land after jumping 30 ft or more, spend 2 CE for a 10-ft burst — creatures in it make a Dexterity save, taking 3d10 force on a failure, half on a success."},{"level":9,"title":"Regeneration","rules":"Passive · At Rage 5 or higher: heal hit points equal to your proficiency bonus at the start of each of your turns; suppressed by acid damage or explicit anti-healing effects."},{"level":11,"title":"Worldbreaker Grip","rules":"Passive · You count as two sizes larger for grappling and lifting; you may wield a grappled target as an improvised weapon (2d10 + Strength modifier damage)."},{"level":13,"title":"Rage 8","rules":"Passive · At Rage 8: resistance to all physical damage; your unarmed strikes deal 1d12 plus 1d10 force once per turn; Wisdom and Intelligence checks requiring patience have disadvantage."},{"level":15,"title":"Gamma Quake","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Creatures in a 30-ft radius make a Dexterity save, taking 7d10 force damage on a failure and falling prone; structures take maximum damage."},{"level":18,"title":"Worldbreaker","rules":"Action · 8 CE (requires Rage 10) · For 1 minute: you become Huge, reach 15 ft, resistance to all damage except psychic, +2d10 damage on your attacks; moving 20+ ft forces creatures within 10 ft of your path to make a Dexterity save or fall prone, and the ground becomes difficult terrain until your next turn. Your Rage cannot decrease."},{"level":20,"title":"Strongest One There Is","rules":"Passive · Rage maximum becomes 12; at Rage 10+ your Strength may reach 26 while transformed. Special · Once per long rest: when reduced to 0 HP, immediately enter Worldbreaker at 1 HP instead."}],"e123":[{"level":1,"title":"Doom Armor","rules":"Passive · Worn armor: AC 16 + Dexterity (max +2); integrated gauntlet (ranged, 60 ft, 2d8 force); environmental seal."},{"level":3,"title":"Arcane Bolt","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Fire an arcane bolt at a creature within 60 ft: 2d10 force or necrotic damage. Reaction · 2 CE · Counterspell Scheme: contest a technique when it manifests (see Rules, Shared Resolutions)."},{"level":6,"title":"Doombot","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Summon one 1-HP Doombot decoy for 1 minute (moves, speaks, gauntlet attack 2d8, impersonates you); only one at a time."},{"level":9,"title":"Latverian Arsenal","rules":"Passive · Choose two armor modules: flight (50 ft), force shield (reaction, +3 AC), tractor beam, micro-missiles (15-ft burst, 4d8), or mystic sensor."},{"level":11,"title":"Power Siphon","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · After you succeed on a save against a technique: gain a Siphon token; within 1 minute spend it to add 3d10 matching damage or gain +2 on a technique contest (see Rules, Shared Resolutions)."},{"level":13,"title":"Master of Science & Sorcery","rules":"Passive · You may maintain one technological Focus effect and one magical Focus effect at the same time."},{"level":15,"title":"Time Platform","rules":"Special · 6 CE, once per long rest: rewind only yourself to the position and hit points you had at the start of your previous turn; spent resources do not return."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Castle Doom","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20 the Domain executes one prepared Scheme autonomously: suppress a projectile lane (10-ft-wide, 60-ft-long zone; ranged attacks have disadvantage), deploy cover (10-ft wall, 30 Integrity), bind one target within 60 ft (Strength save or restrained until the next initiative 20), or fire a 6d10 gauntlet blast (ranged CE attack, 120 ft; Dexterity save for half). Change the Scheme each round."},{"level":20,"title":"Doom Above All","rules":"Passive · Prepare twice your PB in Schemes; the first Scheme each round costs 1 less CE; maintain two Doombots. Special · Once per long rest: declare a plausible preparation against a revealed threat to retroactively fill one unused Scheme slot."}],"e124":[{"level":1,"title":"Solar Body","rules":"Action · 1 Charge · For 1 minute: resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing; your unarmed strikes deal 1d10; your jump distance is multiplied by 4."},{"level":3,"title":"Heat Vision","rules":"Action · 1 Charge + 1 CE · Affect a 90-ft line: creatures in it make a Dexterity save, taking 3d10 fire/radiant on a failure, half on a success; or strike one target with a ranged CE attack for 3d10 fire/radiant on a hit."},{"level":6,"title":"Flight","rules":"Action · 1 Charge · Fly at 60 ft for 10 minutes. You also gain Super Breath: 2 CE to exhale a 30-ft cone; targets make a Strength save, and on a failure they are pushed 30 ft or take 3d8 cold damage."},{"level":9,"title":"Super Senses","rules":"Passive · See and hear up to 1 mile with a clear line; advantage on Perception checks; x-ray vision is blocked by dense special materials and supernatural concealment."},{"level":11,"title":"Man of Steel","rules":"Passive · Solar Body resistance now includes acid, cold, fire, lightning, and thunder (still not psychic, necrotic, or named weaknesses). Reaction · 1 Charge: halve one damaging hit against you."},{"level":13,"title":"Solar Flare","rules":"Action · Spend all your Charge (minimum 5) + 5 CE · Creatures in a 30-ft radius take 2d10 radiant damage per Charge spent (Constitution save for half); your Charge becomes 0 and Solar features go dormant until you recharge."},{"level":15,"title":"World of Cardboard","rules":"Action · 2 Charge · For 1 minute: your unarmed attacks deal +2d10 force damage and your lifting capacity becomes colossal."},{"level":18,"title":"Sun-Dipped","rules":"Action · 8 CE + 5 Charge · For 1 minute: fly 120 ft; resistance to all damage except psychic, kryptonite, and red-sun effects; your attacks deal +3d10 radiant damage; regenerate hit points equal to your PB each turn."},{"level":20,"title":"Last Son","rules":"Passive · Charge maximum 15, begin each day at 10; the first Charge you spend each round is free in direct yellow sunlight. Special · Once per long rest: survive lethal physical damage at 1 HP."}],"e125":[{"level":1,"title":"Amazon Arms","rules":"Passive · Divine weapon of your choice (sword, spear, or shield; 1d10). Reaction · 1 Favor: reduce ranged damage you take by 1d10 + your level; if reduced to 0, redirect a mundane projectile to its sender."},{"level":3,"title":"Lasso of Truth","rules":"Action · Make a 30-ft cursed tool attack; on a hit the target is grappled (escape: Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) vs your tool save DC); a Restrained target cannot knowingly speak a lie but may stay silent; supernatural deception contests your tool DC."},{"level":6,"title":"Amazon Leap","rules":"Passive · Jump distance ×4; reduce falling damage by 5 × your level; once per turn after moving 20 ft, your weapon hits deal +2d8 damage."},{"level":9,"title":"Divine Guard","rules":"Free · 1 Favor: advantage on a Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom save. Reaction (shield wielded) · Interpose your shield: an ally gains +2 AC against the triggering attack, or you take the damage in its place."},{"level":11,"title":"Flight","rules":"Passive · 50-ft fly speed; your divine weapon ignores mundane resistance and deals +1d8 radiant damage once per turn."},{"level":13,"title":"Godkiller Training","rules":"Passive · Against creatures larger than you or of higher grade: critical range becomes 19–20, and the first time you hit each round you gain 1 Favor."},{"level":15,"title":"Bracelet Shockwave","rules":"Action · 3 Favor + 4 CE · Clash your bracelets: creatures in a 30-ft cone make a Constitution save, taking 7d10 thunder/force on a failure and being pushed 30 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Champion of Themyscira","rules":"Action · 6 CE · For 1 minute: resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, slashing, radiant, and necrotic; fly speed 80; +2d10 weapon damage; your Favor cannot fall below 1."},{"level":20,"title":"Truth & War","rules":"Passive · Favor maximum 10; the first Favor cost for bracelets or lasso each round is 0; your lasso binds Huge creatures and suppresses teleportation while the target remains grappled."}],"e126":[{"level":1,"title":"Emerald Construct","rules":"Action · 1 Charge · Create a weapon or projectile construct (60 ft, 2d8 force) or a simple tool; your ring provides environmental life support."},{"level":3,"title":"Flight & Shield","rules":"Action · 1 Charge per 10 minutes: fly at 60 ft. Reaction · 1 Charge: gain +3 AC or reduce damage you take by 2d10 + your proficiency bonus."},{"level":6,"title":"Complex Constructs","rules":"Action · 2 Charge + 1 CE · Create a Large-or-smaller complex construct within 60 ft for 10 minutes (Focus): vehicle, cage, giant hand, platform, etc.; attacks use your CE attack bonus and deal 4d8 (+2d10 at Mecha scale); 30 Integrity, AC 12 + PB."},{"level":9,"title":"Willpower","rules":"Free (after the roll) · 1 Will: add 1d10 to a construct's damage, a saving throw, or a Focus check."},{"level":11,"title":"Ring Scan","rules":"Action · Analyze energy, language, or life signs within 1 mile. Special · 2 Charge: detailed supernatural scan — your CE ability check vs the target's Stealth check or technique save DC (target's choice)."},{"level":13,"title":"Mecha Construct","rules":"Action · 5 Charge + 4 CE · For 1 minute: wear Large construct armor (+2 AC, fly 80, reach 15 ft; construct attacks deal +2d10)."},{"level":15,"title":"No Evil Shall Escape","rules":"Passive · While holding 3 or more Will: immune to the Frightened condition; the first construct you create each round costs 1 less Charge."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Sector 2814","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20: create one autonomous construct event — an 8d10 force blast (Dexterity save), a 40-Integrity wall, or a giant hand (Strength save or Restrained until the next initiative 20). Your ordinary attacks still roll."},{"level":20,"title":"Indomitable Will","rules":"Passive · Charge maximum doubles; Will maximum 10. Special · Once per long rest: at 0 Charge, operate for 3 more rounds on will alone, then gain 1 exhaustion."}],"e127":[{"level":1,"title":"Shapeshift","rules":"Passive · Alter your humanoid appearance freely; in Solid form your unarmed strikes deal 1d8 and you have Powerful Build; telepathy (60 ft) with willing creatures."},{"level":3,"title":"Light Density","rules":"Passive · In Light density: fly speed 40, squeeze through tiny gaps, +10 speed."},{"level":6,"title":"Phase","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Until the start of your next turn: move through creatures and objects, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing, and you cannot make physical attacks while Phased; if you end your turn inside an object you are shunted to the nearest unoccupied space and take 4d10 force damage."},{"level":9,"title":"Mind Link","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Target makes a Wisdom save; on a failure you read its surface thoughts for 1 minute (requires Focus); willing allies can form a telepathic network of up to PB members."},{"level":11,"title":"Martian Strength","rules":"Passive · In Solid form: unarmed strikes deal 1d12, you count as two sizes larger, and once per turn you deal +1d8 force damage."},{"level":13,"title":"Deep Telepathy","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Target makes a Wisdom save; on a failure it is Stunned by psychic intrusion until the end of its next turn, or you alter one of its recent sensory memories (never its identity or personality)."},{"level":15,"title":"Selective Phasing","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · Phase only part of your body to impose disadvantage on one physical attack against you, without losing your ability to attack on your next turn."},{"level":18,"title":"True Martian","rules":"Action · 6 CE · For 1 minute: you become Large, fly speed 80, telepathy to 300 ft, +2d10 psychic/force on your unarmed strikes, and you may switch Density freely once per turn."},{"level":20,"title":"Last Martian","rules":"Passive · Fire weakness manageable: after your first exposure, advantage on the fear/disruption save; phasing costs 0 in the first round of each combat; telepathic network range becomes 1 mile."}],"e128":[{"level":1,"title":"Omega Beam","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Ranged technique attack, 90 ft: 3d10 force/necrotic damage. Special · 1 Dominion: bend the beam around cover or retarget after a miss (once)."},{"level":3,"title":"God of Tyranny","rules":"Passive · Advantage on saves against the Frightened and Charmed conditions. Action · 1 CE: one creature makes a Wisdom save or is Frightened until your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Omega Pursuit","rules":"Passive · Omega Beam turns corners and chases a target up to 120 ft (target defends normally). Special · 2 Dominion: advantage on the attack."},{"level":9,"title":"Boom Tube","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Open a portal between two visible spaces within 120 ft; willing creatures can cross until the start of your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Avatar","rules":"Action · 5 CE · For 1 minute: you become Large, +2 AC, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing; your unarmed strikes deal 1d12 + 1d10 force."},{"level":13,"title":"Omega Sanction","rules":"Action · 6 CE + 3 Dominion · Target makes a Constitution save; on a failure it takes 7d10 force/necrotic and is banished to a hostile pocket dimension until the end of its next turn, then returns prone."},{"level":15,"title":"Anti-Life Fragment","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Target makes a Charisma save; on a failure it is Charmed/Compelled until the end of its next turn (Legendary Resistance works; no suicide or permanent betrayal)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Apokolips Is","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20 choose TYRANNY (hostiles make a Charisma save or kneel — prone, speed 0 — until the next initiative 20) or OMEGA (one autonomous beam per hostile, up to PB: Dexterity save, 6d10 force). Your ordinary attacks still roll. Clash 1,000; burnout 3 rounds."},{"level":20,"title":"Darkseid Is","rules":"Passive · Dominion maximum 15; first Avatar each long rest costs 0; Omega Beam base damage 4d10. Special · Once per round: spend 3 Dominion to turn a beam miss into a hit (never a critical)."}],"e129":[{"level":1,"title":"Telepath","rules":"Passive · Telepathy (60 ft). Action · 1 CE: target makes a Wisdom save; on a failure you read its surface thoughts until the end of its next turn, and the failure grants you 1 Thought."},{"level":3,"title":"Illusory Double","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Create PB illusory doubles for 1 minute (requires Focus); the first attack against you each round has disadvantage, and a miss destroys one double."},{"level":6,"title":"Unsummon","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · When a summon or construct manifests within 60 ft: make a technique contest (see Rules, Shared Resolutions); on a win it is dismissed until the end of its controller's next turn (a mundane creature is instead pushed 30 ft)."},{"level":9,"title":"Memory Mill","rules":"Action · 3 CE + 1 Thought · Target makes an Intelligence save; on a failure it loses one declared proficiency, prepared technique option, or reaction until the end of its next turn (never deletes permanent features)."},{"level":11,"title":"Mind Palace","rules":"Passive · Advantage on Intelligence saves and concentration/Focus checks. Action · 2 Thought: telepathic communication with up to PB creatures within 1 mile for 10 minutes."},{"level":13,"title":"Thoughtseize","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Target makes a Wisdom save; on a failure you learn its available named combat options and choose one, which costs +2 CE (or equivalent) until the end of its next turn."},{"level":15,"title":"Perfect Illusion","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Create a 30-ft cube of multisensory illusion for 10 minutes (requires Focus); an Investigation check against your DC reveals it; you can make its terrain count as difficult terrain through psychosomatic hesitation."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Infinite Library","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20: choose one hostile; it makes an Intelligence save, and on a failure you gain one Page (Attack, Defense, Movement, or Technique). Until the next initiative 20, its first matching action is predicted: disadvantage on it, or advantage to its target."},{"level":20,"title":"Living Guildpact","rules":"Passive · Thought maximum 12; the first Thought you spend each round is free. Special · Once per long rest: after seeing a creature take its turn, declare you foresaw it — it must repeat its movement path and first action on its next turn, if legally possible."}],"e130":[{"level":1,"title":"Raise Dead","rules":"Action · 2 CE + 1 Corpse card · Summon a Zombie (AC 12, HP 5 + your level, 1d8 + PB necrotic attack); commands share one bonus action; at most PB undead active."},{"level":3,"title":"Dark Bargain","rules":"Bonus action · Sacrifice one of your summons: regain 1 CE or gain 2d8 temporary hit points."},{"level":6,"title":"Death's Majesty","rules":"Passive · Your undead add your proficiency bonus to damage (once per round total). Action · 3 CE: turn one Corpse card into an elite Wight with twice a Zombie's HP and a 2d8 attack."},{"level":9,"title":"Diabolic Tutor","rules":"Special · Once per short rest: spend 2 Corpse cards to recover one expended technique feature costing 4 CE or less (never a Domain or Maximum)."},{"level":11,"title":"Mass Reanimation","rules":"Action · 5 CE + up to PB Corpse cards · Summon that many Zombies in a single action (replaces the normal per-Zombie creation actions); they obey your active cap + 2."},{"level":13,"title":"Contract of Four Demons","rules":"Passive · Each long rest choose one pact: +2 undead cap, +2 curse DC against wounded creatures, your sacrifices heal 4d8 instead, or your death magic ignores necrotic resistance."},{"level":15,"title":"Dreadhorde General","rules":"Passive · Undead active cap becomes 2×PB; your undead move together and resolve attacks in two grouped swarms."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The Chain Veil","rules":"Domain · At initiative 20: every hostile within 5 ft of one of your undead makes a Constitution save, taking 6d10 necrotic on a failure (half on a success); each failed save creates a temporary 1-HP Zombie adjacent to it until the next initiative 20."},{"level":20,"title":"Death Cannot Hold Me","rules":"Reaction · Once per long rest: when reduced to 0 HP, sacrifice 4 Corpse cards to remain at 1 HP instead. Passive · Corpse capacity doubles; elite Wights no longer cost extra active slots."}],"e131":[{"level":1,"title":"Pyrobolt","rules":"Action · 1 CE · ranged technique attack, 60 ft · 2d8 fire damage on hit."},{"level":3,"title":"Chandra's Ignition","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 15-ft burst centered on self · Dex save: 3d8 fire on failure · may catch yourself in the burst to gain 1 Ember through Blood for fire."},{"level":6,"title":"Flame Dash","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · move 30 ft without provoking opportunity attacks · leave a burning path until your next turn: each creature takes 2d8 fire damage once · running through your own path can gain 1 Ember."},{"level":9,"title":"Spontaneous Combustion","rules":"Action · 3 CE · one creature within 60 ft · Con save: 5d8 fire on failure, then Burning for 1d8 at the end of its next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Regulator Off","rules":"Passive · Taking it head-on now grants 2 Ember instead of 1."},{"level":13,"title":"Elemental Incarnation","rules":"5 CE · 1 minute · fire immunity, fly speed 50, may pass through occupied spaces as living flame, attacks deal +1d10 fire damage."},{"level":15,"title":"Inferno","rules":"Action · 6 CE · 30-ft-radius inferno within 90 ft · Dex save: 8d10 fire on failure · unattended objects ignite · may catch yourself in it to gain Ember through Blood for fire."},{"level":18,"title":"Emblem of Flame","rules":"Passive · Taking it head-on no longer imposes disadvantage · your first fire technique each turn rolls one additional damage die."},{"level":20,"title":"Torch of Defiance","rules":"Passive · Ember cannot drop below 3 while you are conscious · once per long rest, cast Inferno for 0 CE with maximum dice."}],"e132":[{"level":1,"title":"Leyline","rules":"Passive · while standing on one of your Lands: once per turn reduce a Worldwaker feature's CE cost by 1 (minimum 1) · shape mundane plants and stone within a 10-ft cube."},{"level":3,"title":"Awaken Land","rules":"2 CE · 1 minute · one of your Lands becomes an Elemental (AC 14, HP 10 + 2x your level, speed 30 ft; slam 2d8 + PB with your CE attack bonus) · commanding it is a bonus action, one command per round · maintain at most one."},{"level":6,"title":"Vine Snare","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 20-ft square touching one of your Lands · Str save: Restrained until the end of their next turn; the area becomes difficult terrain."},{"level":9,"title":"Elemental Bond","rules":"Passive · maintain two Awakened Lands · when one of them hits, you may move 10 ft without provoking opportunity attacks or gain 1d8 temporary hit points."},{"level":11,"title":"World Shaper","rules":"Action · 3 CE · raise a wall, ramp, or trench from one of your Lands: up to six 5-ft cubes · each structure AC 15, 15 HP."},{"level":13,"title":"Animist's Awakening","rules":"Action · 5 CE · animate up to PB of your Lands for one round: each makes one 3d8 slam as an autonomous coordinated event · then all but your normal active elementals return to terrain."},{"level":15,"title":"Vastwood","rules":"Passive · your Lands become 30-ft patches and may overlap · allies standing on them gain +10 speed and advantage against forced movement."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Zendikar Risen","rules":"Initiative 20 · choose QUAKE, GROWTH, or ELEMENTAL · Quake: Dex save, 6d10 damage and prone on failure · Growth: Str save or Restrained · Elemental: create two 20-HP land spirits until the next initiative 20."},{"level":20,"title":"Soul of the World","rules":"Passive · your Land maximum becomes 10 · once per long rest, for 1 minute, treat the entire battlefield within 120 ft of you as your Land."}],"e133":[{"level":1,"title":"Phase","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · gain +3 AC against one attack · if it misses, briefly phase and move 10 ft without provoking opportunity attacks."},{"level":3,"title":"Delay","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · when a creature within 60 ft uses a 1-action technique: make a technique contest · if you win, its resolution is delayed until the start of its user's next turn; resources remain spent."},{"level":6,"title":"Temporal Step","rules":"Bonus action · spend 1 Time Counter · teleport to a space you have occupied since the start of your previous turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Time Raveler","rules":"Action · 3 CE + 1 Time Counter · one creature · Wis save: on failure it loses its reactions and cannot take the Ready action until the end of its next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Hero of Dominaria","rules":"Passive · at the end of your turn, if you spent 3 or more CE that turn, regain one reaction, usable only for Phase or a defensive temporal feature."},{"level":13,"title":"Temporal Reversal","rules":"Reaction · 5 CE + 2 Time Counters · restore one creature within 30 ft to the position and hit points it had at the start of the current turn · spent resources and consequences caused by choices do not rewind."},{"level":15,"title":"Stasis","rules":"Action · 6 CE · one creature · Con save: on failure it is phased out until just before its next turn, unable to affect or be affected by anything."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The Slow Sunset","rules":"Initiative 20 · place three temporal markers among creatures · hostile marker: Dex save, on failure its action is delayed to the end of its turn (after bonus action and movement) · ally marker: immediately move up to half speed · never grants extra full turns."},{"level":20,"title":"Master of Time","rules":"Special · once per long rest, after completing your turn, spend 6 Time Counters for a Temporal Window: move and take one action, which cannot be a Domain, a Maximum, or another turn-granting effect · Time Counter maximum becomes 10."}],"e134":[{"level":1,"title":"Elder Dragon","rules":"Passive · claw 1d10 · flight 40 for 1 CE per 10 min · resistance to fire and psychic · 2 CE: 15-ft cone breath, 3d8 fire/force."},{"level":3,"title":"Mind Shatter","rules":"Action · 2 CE · one creature · Wis save: 3d10 psychic on failure, and disadvantage on its next Int/Wis/Cha save."},{"level":6,"title":"Spellbreaker","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · when a technique within 60 ft is used: make a technique contest · if you win, its damage is halved or one non-damaging rider is suppressed."},{"level":9,"title":"Slave of Bolas","rules":"Action · 4 CE + 2 Supremacy · one creature · Wis save: Charmed until the end of your next turn; it immediately uses its reaction to move or make one basic attack you choose."},{"level":11,"title":"God-Pharaoh's Theft","rules":"Trigger · after Spellbreaker succeeds, spend 2 Supremacy to store an Echo of the broken technique until long rest · use once at half dice/scale for its CE cost +2."},{"level":13,"title":"Ruinous Ultimatum","rules":"Action · 6 CE · three targets or objects within 60 ft · each Dex save: 6d10 force/necrotic · structures take maximum dice."},{"level":15,"title":"Planeswalker","rules":"Action · 4 CE · teleport yourself and PB willing creatures up to 1 mile to a known location · combat use limited to 120 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Meditation Realm","rules":"Initiative 20 · choose DISCARD (Int save or lose reaction + one named option until next count 20), DESTROY (Dex save, 7d10 force), or DOMINATE (Wis save or forced 20-ft movement + one basic interaction) · 1,000 clash points · barrier AC 12+PB, barrier HP = 10x max(1, your CE modifier) + 2,000 · Technique Burnout: 3 rounds."},{"level":20,"title":"Dragon-God","rules":"Passive · Supremacy maximum 15 · fly 80 · claw +2d10 force · store PB Echoes · once per long rest, spend 10 Supremacy to use two different stored Echoes in the same action."}],"e135":[{"level":1,"title":"Silver Body","rules":"Passive · +1 AC while unarmored · poison resistance, no need to breathe · 1 CE: touch a construct or object for 2d8 force damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Animate Artifact","rules":"2 CE · 1 minute · one marked object becomes a construct (AC 15, HP 10 + level, attack 2d8) · maximum one."},{"level":6,"title":"Liquimetal","rules":"2 CE · reshape a marked metal object or tool (change weapon form or create cover/bridge) without changing its magical properties."},{"level":9,"title":"Null Rod","rules":"Reaction · 3 CE · against a cursed tool within 30 ft: its wielder makes a Cha save · on failure its activated properties are suppressed until the end of your next turn; mundane weapon function remains."},{"level":11,"title":"Construct Legion","rules":"Passive · maintain PB animated Artifacts (each AC 14, HP 20, speed 25 ft) · they act as one group and collectively make at most PB attacks (each at your CE attack bonus for 2d8 force) · commanding the group is a bonus action."},{"level":13,"title":"Legacy Weapon","rules":"5 CE · 1 minute · combine three marked objects into one temporary Large construct or tool: AC 18, 60 HP, attack 5d10 or barrier 60 Integrity."},{"level":15,"title":"Creator's Touch","rules":"3 CE · repair constructs or cursed tools for 4d10 · once per long rest, with 10 minutes and surviving pieces, restore one destroyed non-legendary cursed tool."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Argentum","rules":"Initiative 20 · choose ANIMATE (two environmental objects attack for 4d10 each against different targets, Dex save) or SILENCE (one hostile cursed tool: its wielder Cha save or loses activated properties until next count 20)."},{"level":20,"title":"Father of Machines","rules":"Passive · Artifact cap 10 · first animation each combat costs 0 CE · mark an object as an action · Legacy Weapon may incorporate one cursed tool activation once per round."}],"e136":[{"level":1,"title":"Vampiric Thirst","rules":"Trigger · on a melee hit, spend 1 CE: +1d8 necrotic damage and heal the same roll · once per turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Blood Needle","rules":"Action · 1 CE · 60-ft technique attack · 2d8 piercing/necrotic on hit · on hit gain 1 Blood."},{"level":6,"title":"Aristocrat's Command","rules":"Action · 2 CE + 1 Blood · one target · Wis save: it cannot willingly move closer to you or attack one named creature until the end of your next turn."},{"level":9,"title":"Vampire Spawn","rules":"4 CE + 3 Blood · 1 minute · summon one blood shikigami (AC 15, HP 30, bite 3d8, heals itself half the damage dealt)."},{"level":11,"title":"Blood Magic","rules":"Passive · when casting a damaging feature, you may spend up to PB Blood; each adds 1d8 necrotic damage · max once per turn."},{"level":13,"title":"Markov Immortality","rules":"Bonus action · spend 3 Blood: heal 5d10 · halved if radiant damage touched you since your last turn."},{"level":15,"title":"Lord of Innistrad","rules":"Passive · maintain two Spawn · allies within 15 ft gain 1d8 temporary hit points the first time each combat they reduce a hostile to 0."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Castle Markov","rules":"Initiative 20 · hostile living creatures Con save: on failure lose 2d10 HP · distribute the total HP lost as healing among yourself and your Spawn, capped 6d10."},{"level":20,"title":"Ancient Vampire","rules":"Passive · Blood maximum 15; begin combat at 3 Blood · at 10+ Blood: fly 60, resist B/P/S · once per long rest, at 0 HP, spend all Blood (minimum 5) to remain at 1 HP."}],"e137":[{"level":1,"title":"Nightmare Touch","rules":"Action · 1 CE · one creature within 60 ft · Wis save: 2d8 psychic on failure + 1 Fear Mark. · When Nightmare Touch damages a creature bearing Fear Marks, you may consume any number of its Marks: +1d8 psychic per Mark consumed."},{"level":3,"title":"Dream Token","rules":"Action · spend 1 Fear Mark from a creature within 60 ft · create a 1-HP Nightmare until the end of your next turn: it acts on your turn without requiring an action (speed 30 ft; melee CE attack for 2d8 psychic)."},{"level":6,"title":"Blueprint","rules":"Passive · when a creature reaches 3 Marks, record one fear theme · at rest build one Blueprint (Hunter, Swarm, Cage, Doppelganger, or Abyss), each with its own movement or control rider."},{"level":9,"title":"Nightmare Shikigami","rules":"4 CE · 1 minute · summon one Blueprint (AC 15, HP 8x level; attacks use your CE attack bonus for 3d8 psychic) · commanding it is a bonus action · one active."},{"level":11,"title":"Exile Thought","rules":"Action · 3 CE · one reaction, summon, or Focus effect · Int save: on failure it is phased into nightmare until the end of your next turn; ongoing durations continue ticking."},{"level":13,"title":"Fear Made Flesh","rules":"Passive · your Nightmare gains one trait drawn from its source fear: fly, burrow, +10 ft reach, resistance to one damage type, or +1 attack die · GM approves the thematic fit."},{"level":15,"title":"Nightmare Harvest","rules":"Trigger · when a marked creature drops to 0: preserve all its Marks as permanent Dream tokens · max PB stored."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The Unwritten Nightmare","rules":"Initiative 20 · each hostile chooses REVEAL or RUN · Reveal: Wis save, 6d10 psychic on failure, and you learn its fear theme for the round · Run: the Domain moves it 30 ft to a space of your choice and gives it 1 Mark."},{"level":20,"title":"Fear Has No Face","rules":"Passive · maintain two Nightmare Shikigami · Blueprint HP becomes 10x level · once per long rest, summon one from a stored Dream token for 0 CE."}],"e138":[{"level":1,"title":"Beast Call","rules":"2 CE · 1 minute · summon a basic Beast (AC 14, HP 8 + 2x level, speed 40 ft; bite uses your CE attack bonus, 2d8) · commanding your beasts is a bonus action; one command directs all."},{"level":3,"title":"Hunter's Mark","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · mark a visible creature: your beasts gain +PB damage once per round against it and track it for 1 hour."},{"level":6,"title":"Trophy Trait","rules":"Passive · your Beast gains one equipped trait: Flight, Pack Tactics, Charge, Venom, Armor, Burrow, Amphibious, or Reach."},{"level":9,"title":"Primal Might","rules":"3 CE · 1 minute · you gain +10 speed, advantage on Strength, weapon attacks +1d8; your beasts gain the same speed bonus."},{"level":11,"title":"Two Beasts","rules":"Passive · maintain two summons · they share one command and collectively make at most two attacks per round."},{"level":13,"title":"Apex Trophy","rules":"Passive · after defeating a major monster, the GM may grant an Apex trait (e.g. 30-ft cone breath 6d10 Dex save once per short rest; regeneration 5 HP/round; magic resistance; huge size, reach +5 ft, +1d8 damage) · only one Apex equipped at a time."},{"level":15,"title":"Overrun","rules":"5 CE · once per short rest · all your beasts and chosen allies within 30 ft move half their speed and make one basic melee attack as a reaction."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The Great Hunt","rules":"Initiative 20 · designate a Prey: spectral beasts stampede a 20-ft-wide line ending at the Prey · Dex save: 7d10 bludgeoning and prone · marked Prey has disadvantage."},{"level":20,"title":"Apex Predator","rules":"Passive · three active beasts; one may carry two normal Trophy traits plus the Apex · first Beast Call of each combat costs 0 CE."}],"e139":[{"level":1,"title":"Artificer's Blueprint","rules":"Devices, prepared (1-2 CE each) · Beam: action, 1 CE, ranged CE attack, 120 ft, 2d8 force · Shield: reaction, 1 CE, +2 AC vs the triggering attack · Sensor: action, 1 CE, detect CE effects, hidden creatures, traps within 60 ft for 10 min · Grapnel: bonus action, 1 CE, pull yourself up to 40 ft to a surface within 60 ft or pull a Medium-or-smaller object to you · Drone: action, 2 CE, Tiny drone 1 hr (fly 40, AC 14, HP 10, scouts and relays) · Utility Construct: action, 2 CE, Small construct 1 hr (AC 13, HP 20, speed 25, carries/holds/simple tasks)."},{"level":3,"title":"Powerstone","rules":"Passive · create PB Powerstones · each substitutes 2 CE toward an Artifact activation, never toward a Domain or Maximum."},{"level":6,"title":"Thopter Foundry","rules":"2 CE · 1 minute · field PB 1-HP Thopters: swarm attack 3d8 force, or grant one ally half cover."},{"level":9,"title":"Mightstone / Weakstone","rules":"3 CE · 1 minute Focus · choose Might (+2d8 weapon/construct damage once per turn) or Weak (one hostile within 30 ft Str save or -2 to attacks and damage)."},{"level":11,"title":"Tolarian Academy","rules":"Downtime · during a short rest construct a temporary workshop: +2 prepared Blueprints and restore all Powerstones · once per long rest."},{"level":13,"title":"Prototype Portal","rules":"4 CE · duplicate one non-legendary cursed tool activation you personally analyzed for 10 minutes · use once at reduced scale (half damage dice, half range/area, half duration), then the Blueprint burns until long rest."},{"level":15,"title":"Titan Engine","rules":"6 CE + 2 Powerstones · 1 minute · summon a Large mech (AC 18, HP 80, two 3d10 attacks, rideable)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The Sylex Workshop","rules":"Initiative 20 · execute one prepared Blueprint as an autonomous battlefield version: 6d10 beam (ranged CE attack, 120 ft); 50-Integrity wall (three 10-ft panels, 1 min); repair up to three constructs within 60 ft for 5d10; or a 20-ft cube restraining lattice within 60 ft (Str save or restrained until next count 20) · 1,000 clash points · Technique Burnout: 3 rounds."},{"level":20,"title":"Urza Planeswalker","rules":"Passive · Blueprint cap doubles · Powerstones to 10 · once per long rest, declare one plausible device the situation requires and draft a temporary Blueprint, subject to GM numerical adjudication."}],"e140":[{"level":1,"title":"Glistening Oil","rules":"Attack option · natural weapon 1d8 · on a hit spend 1 CE: target Con save or gains 1 Infection (max 3); each Infection gives -5 speed."},{"level":3,"title":"Adapt","rules":"Passive · at Oil 3 choose one adaptation: +1 AC, climb 30, darkvision/sensors, natural weapon +1 attack die once per turn, or resistance to the last damage type until rest."},{"level":6,"title":"Proliferate","rules":"2 CE · choose PB creatures or objects within 30 ft already bearing your counter/mark · increase each by 1, respecting caps."},{"level":9,"title":"Compleat Limb","rules":"Trigger · at Oil 5 manifest a modular limb · blade; cannon (action, ranged CE attack, 60 ft, 3d8 force); shield (reaction to being hit, +2 AC against that attack); injector (bonus action, advantage on grapple checks for 1 minute)."},{"level":11,"title":"Perfected Form","rules":"Passive · choose a second Adaptation; the resistance adaptation can be maintained alongside another · at Infection 3 the victim also has disadvantage on Con Focus checks."},{"level":13,"title":"Praetor Evolution","rules":"Passive · at Oil 7 choose one major evolution: wings 60, regeneration PB HP per turn, +10 ft reach, magic resistance (advantage on saves vs CT), or two modular limbs at once."},{"level":15,"title":"Corrupted Conversion","rules":"Action · 5 CE · one target at Infection 3 · Cha save: on failure Charmed until the end of your next turn and may be ordered one basic action · Infection then resets to 0."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, New Phyrexia","rules":"Initiative 20 · Proliferate all your counters once for free · then each hostile with Infection Con save: 5d10 necrotic/metal damage per Infection on failure, capped 10d10."},{"level":20,"title":"All Will Be One","rules":"Passive · Oil maximum 15 · maintain three normal Adaptations plus one Praetor Evolution · once per long rest, when you would die: become a 1-HP cocoon and reform next turn with 50 HP if the cocoon survives."}],"e141":[{"level":1,"title":"Void Limb","rules":"Attack action · 1d10 force, 15-ft reach · On hit, spend 1 CE: target makes a Con save or loses 1 CE (max once/turn); you gain 1 Void instead of the drained CE."},{"level":3,"title":"Warp Space","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Teleport 30 ft yourself, or force a target within 60 ft to make a Strength save or be shifted 20 ft through folded space."},{"level":6,"title":"Scion","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Summon two 1-HP Eldrazi Scions (AC 12, 30 ft) for 1 minute · Sacrifice one to reduce a CE cost by 1, or as a bonus action command one to make a 2d8 melee CE attack (10-ft reach, your CE attack bonus)."},{"level":9,"title":"Annihilator","rules":"Passive trigger · Spend 2 Void · When you hit the same target twice in a turn, it chooses: lose its reaction, drop what it holds, or take 3d10 extra force damage."},{"level":11,"title":"Reality Hunger","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 15-ft sphere, Con save · 6d10 force or necrotic damage; summoned creatures and barriers take 8d10."},{"level":13,"title":"Titan Anatomy","rules":"Passive · At Void 6+: Large size, reach +5 ft, resistance to bludgeoning/piercing/slashing and force, speed +10 ft · Below Void 6 you return to normal."},{"level":15,"title":"Exile","rules":"Action · 6 CE + 3 Void · Charisma save: phase the creature out until the end of your next turn; on return it cannot regain CE until the end of that turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, Blind Eternities","rules":"Domain Expansion · Initiative 20: DISTORT (Dex save; creatures swap positions per your chosen legal permutation and take 4d10 force) or CONSUME (Con save; 7d10 void damage, and lose 1 CE on failure) · 1,000 clash points."},{"level":20,"title":"Titan Manifest","rules":"Passive · Void max 15; at Void 10+: Huge size, 25-ft reach, attacks +2d10, resistance to all but psychic/radiant · Once per long rest, enter at 10 Void for 1 minute regardless of current Void."}],"e142":[{"level":1,"title":"Sliver Brood","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Summon 2 Slivers for 1 minute (AC 13, HP 5+level, 30 ft; attacks 1d6+PB with your CE attack bonus) · Commanding the brood is a bonus action · Choose 2 Hive Traits: Claw, Carapace, Swift, or Sinew."},{"level":3,"title":"Hive Mind","rules":"Passive · Brood shares one initiative and one command; Slivers can Help one another without spending an action, once per round."},{"level":6,"title":"Trait Library","rules":"Passive · Learn new Hive Traits (Flying, Venom, Reach, Regeneration, Ward) · Equip up to 3 traits at once."},{"level":9,"title":"Brood Growth","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Summon 3 Slivers · Their attacks may be resolved as one grouped roll."},{"level":11,"title":"Adaptive Sliver","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · After the hive takes a damage type, the whole brood gains resistance to it until the start of your next turn."},{"level":13,"title":"Advanced Traits","rules":"Passive · Learn new Hive Traits (Double Strike, Leech, Psionic, Diffusion) · Equip up to 4 traits at once."},{"level":15,"title":"Sliver Queen","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Summon the Sliver Queen for 1 minute (AC 18, HP 100, two 3d10 attacks; counts as all Slivers and shares every trait) · Ordinary brood may remain."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The First Hive","rules":"Domain Expansion · Initiative 20: create one temporary Sliver token adjacent to each of up to PB hostiles; each makes one 3d8 shared-trait attack, then dissolves at the next initiative 20."},{"level":20,"title":"Sliver Overlord","rules":"Passive · Equip up to 6 Hive Traits; brood becomes 5 Slivers · Bonus action (once/turn): swap one equipped trait · First Sliver Queen summon per long rest costs 0 CE."}],"e143":[{"level":1,"title":"White / Blue","rules":"Reaction or action · 1 CE · White: +2 AC shield (reaction) or 2d8 healing (action) · Blue: illusion or 30-ft push (action), or 2 CE reaction to impose −1d8 on a hostile technique attack."},{"level":3,"title":"Black / Red / Green","rules":"Action · Black: pay 1d8 HP to add 2d8 necrotic to a hit, or animate a 1-HP token · Red: 60-ft ranged CE attack, 3d8 fire/lightning · Green (2 CE): +10 speed and +1d8 melee, or summon a vine restraint."},{"level":6,"title":"Two-Color Gold","rules":"Passive · With two colors at rank 2+, unlock one two-color pair spell (choose two known at rest) · Pair spells are actions or bonus actions costing 2–3 CE at 60 ft (see dossier for each spell’s full text)."},{"level":9,"title":"Color Signatures","rules":"Action (Blue’s counter is a reaction) · 3–4 CE each · White: 10-ft wall of 40 Integrity, 1 min · Black: 5d10 necrotic drain on one creature in 60 ft, Con save half · Red: 20-ft blast in 60 ft, 6d10 fire, Dex save half · Green: 60-HP elemental (AC 14, slam 3d8 with your CE attack bonus; commanding it is a bonus action) · Blue: technique contest counter."},{"level":11,"title":"Three-Color Shard/Wedge","rules":"Action · 5 CE, once per short rest · 20-ft radius within 90 ft, Dex save · 7d10 damage (type set by represented color; half on success) plus up to two color riders. · Passive · Convergence damage type set by represented color: White radiant, Blue cold or force, Black necrotic, Red fire or lightning, Green bludgeoning · Hostiles in the area make a Dex save: 7d10 damage, half on success. · Passive · Choose up to two different riders from the represented colors; enemy riders apply only to creatures that failed the save, while White protects chosen allies instead. · Passive · Riders: White = chosen allies gain PB + CE modifier temp HP · Blue = push or pull each failed target 15 ft · Black = failed targets can’t regain HP until end of your next turn · Red = failed targets ignite, taking 1d10 fire at start of next turn · Green = failed targets’ speed 0 until end of your next turn. · Passive · The same rider does not stack on repeated applications; the Convergence’s default save is Dexterity (specific features may change it)."},{"level":13,"title":"Mana Fixing","rules":"Free (once/turn) · Convert 2 CE into one temporary Mastery rank until end of turn (max rank 3) · Cannot unlock a Signature more than once per round this way."},{"level":15,"title":"Four-Color Mastery","rules":"Passive · With four colors at rank 2+, the first spell each turn using a different color than your previous spell costs 1 less CE."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain, The World Tree","rules":"Domain Expansion · Initiative 20: choose one color’s edict — White: allies gain 4d10 temp HP · Blue: hostiles Int save or lose reactions · Black: hostiles Con save, 5d10 necrotic, you heal half · Red: hostiles Dex save, 7d10 fire · Green: summon two 30-HP elementals until next initiative 20 · 1,000 clash points."},{"level":20,"title":"WUBRG","rules":"Passive · Mana Mastery pool becomes 15 (rank 3 in all five colors) · Once per long rest for 1 minute: the first feature of each color used costs 0 CE and gains +1 die."}],"e144":[{"level":1,"title":"Fracture Sense, Lacquer Pot, Mend the Break, Exploit the Break","rules":"No action · Once per round when a creature, object, construct, or barrier you can see within 60 ft takes damage, designate it as a Fracture · A target holds up to 3 Fractures (5 at 11th level); Fractures last 1 minute. · Passive · Lacquer token pool: max PB + CE modifier (min 2) · You begin each long rest with PB tokens. · Bonus action · 2 CE, 30 ft · Choose a willing creature bearing your Fracture: consume the Fracture and spend 1 Lacquer token · It regains 5 + CE modifier HP (objects/constructs/barriers regain 10 + twice CE modifier); can’t restore a destroyed limb. · Passive trigger (once/turn) · When you hit a hostile bearing your Fracture: consume the Fracture and spend 1 Lacquer token · +5 damage, and the target can’t regain HP until the start of your next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Seal the Seam, Reinforced Seam —","rules":"Ally’s bonus action · No CE · An ally consumes one of its own Fractures and 1 Lacquer token to heal 5 + your CE modifier HP · Beautiful Scar does not trigger on this. · Passive · After you Mend a creature, it gains +1 AC or advantage vs forced movement until start of your next turn; Mending the same creature twice before end of your next turn also grants 5 temp HP."},{"level":6,"title":"Living Kintsugi —","rules":"Passive · Your Mend ends bleeding and stabilizes automatically · Spend 4 CE and 2 Lacquer tokens to repair a non-severed limb injury by one step (requires appropriate mundane treatment; once per creature per long rest)."},{"level":11,"title":"Catastrophic Break —","rules":"Passive · Targets may hold up to 5 Fractures each · When you hit, consume up to 3 Fractures at once (1 Lacquer token each); if 3+ consumed, target makes a Con save or its AC is reduced by 2 until start of your next turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: Golden Reassembly —","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 12 CE, once per long rest · Choose up to PB creatures/objects within 30 ft: willing targets heal 15 + twice CE modifier and may repair one non-severed limb injury; hostile targets detonate every Fracture they bear, taking 5 force damage per Fracture and falling prone on a failed Con save."}],"e145":[{"level":1,"title":"Supports, Brace the Structure, Load, Discharge","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE, 30 ft · Designate a willing creature, unattended object, structure, or 5-ft section of terrain as a Support · Maintain up to PB Supports; a Support lasts 10 minutes, ends beyond 120 ft, or when dismissed. · Passive · Your Stress Die is a d6, growing to d8 at 6th, d10 at 11th, and d12 at 18th. · Reaction · 1 CE · When a creature Support within 30 ft takes damage: roll your Stress Die and reduce the damage by the result + CE modifier · If damage is reduced, gain 1 Load (max PB + CE modifier, min 3). · Passive trigger (once/turn) · When you hit with a weapon or cursed attack, spend up to 2 Load · Add one Stress Die of bludgeoning or force damage per Load; if 2 spent, a Large or smaller target makes a Str save or is pushed 10 ft."},{"level":3,"title":"Weight Distribution —","rules":"Passive · When Brace the Structure reduces damage, you may take up to half the remaining damage yourself (after resistances) to gain 1 additional Load · You can also use Brace against forced movement, adding the Stress Die to the Support’s check/save."},{"level":6,"title":"Continuous Truss —","rules":"Passive · Support range becomes 60 ft, maximum Supports +2 · Bonus action: spend 2 Load to let one creature Support move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks."},{"level":11,"title":"Controlled Demolition —","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Choose one Support within 60 ft and spend 3–6 Load · Creatures of your choice within 15 ft make a Dex save: one Stress Die per Load spent, half on success; failed targets are knocked prone · The Support remains unless it lacked the HP to survive."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: Cathedral of Supports —","rules":"Maximum Technique · Bonus action · 10 CE, 1 minute · Every willing creature within 60 ft becomes a Support (no limit) · Brace the Structure gains 60-ft range and costs no CE the first time each round; at the start of your turn gain 1 Load if any Support took damage since your last turn."}],"e146":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Cord, Anchor Knot, Hitch Knot, Stitch Knot","rules":"Passive · You manifest cursed cord from your hands: 30-ft reach for technique purposes, unusable as mundane rope by others, vanishes when detached from all your Knots. · Passive · Your Knot Die is a d6. · Bonus action · 1 CE per Knot · Tie a Knot after touching the target or hitting it with a weapon/cursed attack this turn · Maintain up to PB + CE modifier Knots; a creature bears at most 3 (4 at 6th, 5 at 11th) · Knots last 1 minute, end if dismissed (no action), if the cord is cut (AC 12, 10 HP), or if the bearer leaves 120 ft of you. · Passive · Creature’s speed −10 ft; it adds your Knot Die to checks/saves vs forced movement; it can’t willingly teleport more than 30 ft at once without first succeeding on a CE save. · Passive · Tie two creatures/objects within 30 ft of each other: they can’t willingly move more than 30 ft apart · Attempting to exceed the tether: Strength save, on failure movement ends at the boundary. · Reaction · 1 CE, once per round per Stitch Knot · When one of a tied pair of willing creatures would take damage, the other takes it instead (same amount/type; original takes none) · A damage instance travels a Stitch Knot only once."},{"level":3,"title":"Snare & Slip —","rules":"Snare: bonus action · 2 CE · A hostile bearing 2 of your Knots makes a Str save or its speed becomes 0 until end of its next turn · Slip: reaction when a knotted creature moves · 1 CE to shift it 5 ft to an unoccupied space it could occupy (Dex save negates if hostile)."},{"level":6,"title":"Compound Knot —","rules":"Passive · A creature can bear 4 Knots · When two different Knot types affect the same creature, your first damaging hit against it each turn deals one extra Knot Die of force damage · You may tie or remove one Knot as part of the Attack action, once per turn. · Passive · Your Knot Die becomes a d8."},{"level":11,"title":"Gordian Binding —","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Consume 3 Knots on one creature (it may now bear 5 Knots) · It makes a Str save: failure restrains it for 1 minute, repeating the save at end of each turn; on success its speed is halved until end of its next turn. · Passive · Your Knot Die becomes a d10."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Temple of the Nine Ties —","rules":"Domain Expansion · 10 CE · At initiative 20, choose one ephemeral Knot effect for every hostile creature in the Domain: Anchor, Hitch (to a fixed point), or Snare — this is the sure-hit, lasting until next initiative 20 · Your cord, attacks, and Gordian Binding still resolve normally. · Passive · Your Knot Die becomes a d12."}],"e147":[{"level":1,"title":"Inscribe Fault, Accumulate Strain, Survey, Rupture","rules":"No action (once/turn) · When you damage a creature, object, or surface, place a Fault on it · Maintain up to PB Faults; Faults last 1 minute. · Passive · A Fault gains 1 Strain (max 6) the first time each round its subject: moves 10+ ft, is forcibly moved, falls, or takes bludgeoning/force/thunder damage (your own attacks can trigger this) · A Fault gains at most 2 Strain per round before 11th level. · Bonus action · 1 CE, 60 ft · Choose one Fault you can see and add 1 Strain to it. · Passive trigger (once/turn) · On hit, spend 2–6 Strain from the target’s Fault (no damage dealt) · 2 (Tremor): Dex save or prone + difficult terrain until start of your next turn · 4 (Fissure): Str save or prone + loses reactions until start of its next turn + 15×5-ft fissure for 1 min · 6 (Upheaval): Str save or prone + pushed 15 ft + 20-ft radius difficult terrain until start of your next turn (success: pushed 5 ft, stays up) · 8 (Cataclysm, needs Deep Fault): Con save or −2 AC until end of your next turn + prone + 20-ft difficult terrain."},{"level":3,"title":"Mapped Ground —","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Place a Fault on a 10-ft section of terrain · When a creature crosses it, use your reaction to add 1 Strain and make that area difficult terrain until start of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Aftershock —","rules":"Passive · When you Rupture a Fault using 4+ Strain, choose another Fault within 30 ft: it gains 1 Strain."},{"level":11,"title":"Deep Fault —","rules":"Passive · Maximum Strain becomes 8; a Fault can gain up to 3 Strain per round · Unlocks the 8-Strain Cataclysm Rupture tier."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: World Beneath the Cracks —","rules":"Domain Expansion · 10 CE · At initiative 20, every hostile creature gains a Fault if it lacks one, and every hostile Fault gains 2 Strain · Choose one Fault: it erupts automatically at Cataclysm without consuming Strain (sure-hit) — affected creatures are knocked prone and the ground in 20 ft becomes difficult terrain until next initiative 20 (no save), and each makes a Con save or suffers −2 AC until end of your next turn."}],"e148":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Stones, Influence, Atari, Capture","rules":"Passive · The Influence Die grows with mastery: d4 → d6 (6th) → d8 (11th) → d10 (18th). · Passive · Cursed Stones are the technique’s whole resource: six at first, more with mastery. · Passive · You carry or manifest 6 Stones (1st level) · A deployed Stone is Tiny, AC 15, HP 5 + your sorcerer level, immune to poison/psychic · Destroyed Stones return after a short or long rest. · Bonus action · 1 CE, 30 ft · Place one Stone on an unoccupied surface (retrieve one within reach for free on your turn) · Each Stone projects 10 ft of Influence. · Passive · A hostile inside the overlapping Influence of 2+ Stones is in Atari: speed −10 ft and cannot take the Dash action. · Passive · A hostile starting its turn in the overlapping Influence of 3+ Stones makes a Str or Dex save (its choice); on failure it is Captured until start of its next turn: speed 0, no reactions · A creature suffers Capture only once per round."},{"level":3,"title":"Sente —","rules":"Reaction · When a hostile enters one of your Influence zones: move one deployed Stone up to 10 ft across a surface · This movement can’t trigger another Sente this round."},{"level":6,"title":"Cut and Connect —","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Draw a cursed line between two Stones within 40 ft until start of your next turn (you now have 8 Stones) · The first hostile each turn to cross it makes a Dex save: 2 Influence Dice force damage and stops at the line on failure, half damage on success."},{"level":11,"title":"Living Board —","rules":"Passive · You have 10 Stones; Influence radius becomes 15 ft · Once per turn when you hit a creature, place one Stone in an unoccupied space within 5 ft of it without spending an action (still costs 1 CE)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Nineteen-by-Nineteen Funeral Board —","rules":"Domain Expansion · 10 CE · Nine spectral Stones appear throughout the Domain (not against your set); at initiative 20 relocate up to 3 anywhere on the ground · Every hostile influenced by 3+ Stones is Captured until next initiative 20 and takes 3 Influence Dice force damage — this Capture/damage is the sure-hit."}],"e149":[{"level":1,"title":"Nodes, Remote Fruiting, Symbiotic Pulse, Nutrients","rules":"Passive · The Spore Die grows with the network: d6 → d8 (6th) → d10 (11th) → d12 (18th). · Passive · Nodes and Nutrients are the network’s body and its fuel. · Bonus action · 1 CE, 30 ft · Plant a Node on a surface; maintain up to PB Nodes · Nodes are Tiny, AC 13, HP 5 + twice your sorcerer level; Nodes within 30 ft of another Node or you are Connected. · Passive · Your Mycelial Testament abilities may originate from you or any Connected Node; measure auras/ranges from the chosen origin. · Bonus action · 1 CE · One willing creature within 10 ft of a Connected Node regains one Spore Die + CE modifier HP · A creature benefits once per round. · Passive · Hold up to PB Nutrients · When a Small or larger creature drops to 0 HP within 10 ft of a Node, gain 1 Nutrient (once per creature) · Once per turn, spend 1 CE to gain 1 Nutrient · Nutrients vanish after a long rest."},{"level":3,"title":"Grasping Mycelium —","rules":"Action · 2 CE or 1 Nutrient · A 10-ft radius around one Node becomes difficult terrain for 1 minute · A hostile entering or starting there makes a Str save or is restrained until start of its next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Fruiting Bodies —","rules":"Bonus action · Spend 2 Nutrients · Convert one Node for 1 minute into one Bloom (one per Node): Bulwark grants half cover to adjacent allies; Lantern reveals invisible creatures within 15 ft that fail a Dex save; Puffball uses your reaction when a hostile enters 10 ft to deal 2 Spore Dice poison/necrotic (Con save half)."},{"level":11,"title":"Distributed Organism —","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE, once per round · When a willing creature within 10 ft of a Connected Node would take damage: it sinks into the mycelium and re-emerges in an unoccupied space within 10 ft of another Connected Node within 60 ft · The triggering damage is negated entirely; no die is rolled."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: Worldroot Fruiting —","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE, 1 minute · Ground within 60 ft counts as Connected network terrain · Start of each turn: gain 1 Nutrient · Symbiotic Pulse may target two creatures; hostile creatures starting within your network make a Con save or take 2 Spore Dice necrotic damage and have speed −10 ft until their next turn."}],"e150":[{"level":1,"title":"Revision Dice, Records, Position Note, Restore Object","rules":"Passive · Records and Revision Dice are the drafts she keeps and the ink she spends. · Passive · Revision Dice = PB + CE modifier (min 2), regained on a long rest · Die size scales d6/d8/d10/d12 at levels 1/6/11/18. · Passive · Maintain up to PB Records · A Record captures an unattended object, a 5-ft cube of terrain, or a creature’s position only at the instant of inscription · Records last 10 minutes at 1st level. · Bonus action · 1 CE, 60 ft · Record a creature’s current space until start of your next turn · Reaction after it moves, spend one Revision Die: a hostile makes a Dex save — on failure it returns to the recorded legal space, on success its remaining speed becomes 0 · Willing targets return automatically. · Action · 2 CE + one Revision Die · Restore a recorded unattended object or 5-ft terrain section toward its recorded state: HP/integrity equal to twice the die + twice your CE modifier · Can’t duplicate: if the recorded original still exists elsewhere, the restoration fails."},{"level":3,"title":"Persistent Margins —","rules":"Passive · Object/terrain Records last 1 hour; you may record an object held by a willing creature · When restoring a broken weapon/tool, also remove one mundane jam, bend, tear, or similar impairment."},{"level":6,"title":"Living Layer —","rules":"Action · 4 CE + 2 Revision Dice · Record a willing creature for 1 round; before the Record ends, restore it as a reaction: it heals both dice + CE modifier and may end one frightened, poisoned, grappled, or restrained condition gained after the Record · Each creature benefits once per short rest."},{"level":11,"title":"Redaction —","rules":"Action · 5 CE, 60 ft · Choose a creature or manifested technique effect; make a CE ability check contested by the creator’s CE check (or the target makes a CE save) · On success, suppress one temporary buff, summoned construct, aura, or movement-altering technique effect until end of your next turn · Can’t erase innate techniques, Domains, or permanent effects."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: First Draft —","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 12 CE, once per long rest · Choose a 30-ft radius area you personally observed within the last minute: terrain and unattended objects return toward the recorded layout · Willing creatures may return to their recorded positions and heal 4 Revision Dice · Hostile creatures make a Dex save: on failure they return to their recorded position and lose one temporary buff gained since then · Never restores expended CE, class resources, Domain uses, or dead creatures."}],"e151":[{"level":1,"title":"Traffic Lane, Green/Yellow/Red Signals, Citations","rules":"Main resource: Lanes & Citations · Traffic Lane: One bonus action, one coin of CE: five feet wide, thirty long, one minute of law painted onto the ground. Bonus Action • 1 CE. Create a 5-foot-wide, 30-foot-long Lane on a surface within 30 feet. It lasts 1 minute. You can maintain one Lane at 1st level. Choose its direction and current Signal: Green, Yellow, or Red. · Green Signal: The benevolent signal: allies traveling with the current gain speed, and their first ten feet ignore the enemy's reach. Willing creatures moving in the Lane’s direction gain +10 feet speed for that movement. The first 10 feet they move inside the Lane each turn does not provoke opportunity attacks. · Yellow Signal: The warning signal: the hostile who rushes through it anyway is fined, one Citation for the voluntary step. A hostile creature that voluntarily moves 10+ feet while inside the Lane gains 1 Citation at the end of that movement. A creature can gain only one Citation from Yellow each round. · Red Signal: The absolute signal: the first crossing each round demands the save, failure ends the movement and issues the Citation. The first time each round a hostile creature enters or crosses a Red Lane, it makes a Dexterity save. Failure ends its current movement and gives it 1 Citation; success allows movement normally. · Cash Citation: The fines, collected: one Citation steals reactions and speed, two steal movement, three steal footing and the bonus action, and the law takes no blood, only liberty. Bonus Action • 60 feet. Spend one creature’s Citations (a creature can hold at most 3 Citations): 1 Citation: its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of your next turn and it cannot take reactions; 2 Citations: its speed becomes 0 until the start of your next turn; 3 Citations: it makes a Strength save, on a failure it is knocked prone, its speed becomes 0 until the start of your next turn, and it cannot take bonus actions. Cash Citation deals no damage at any tier."},{"level":3,"title":"Signal Controller —","rules":"She is the authority, not the paint: signals change without action, and every hostile Citation buys one ally five feet. once per turn change one Lane’s Signal without using an action. Reaction when a hostile gains a Citation: one willing creature in that Lane may move 5 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Intersection —","rules":"Passive · Maintain 2 Lanes (40 ft each) · A hostile crossing a Lane intersection: Dexterity save; on failure it gains 1 Citation and its movement ends."},{"level":11,"title":"Priority Vehicle —","rules":"Passive · Maintain 3 Lanes · You and one ally (chosen at the start of your turn) may move through hostile creature spaces as difficult terrain in a Green Lane · Your first attack after moving 20+ ft in a Lane has advantage."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Metropolitan Gridlock —","rules":"Domain Expansion · 10 CE · The Domain becomes a luminous road network · At initiative 20, choose Green, Yellow, or Red as the global Signal until the next count 20: every hostile that moved 10+ ft since the prior count gains 1 Citation — this automatic Citation is the sure-hit and deals no damage · Your own Lanes remain available for their normal effects."}],"e152":[{"level":1,"title":"Scent Notes, Courage Accord, Funeral Myrrh, Hunter’s Trace","rules":"Main resource: Scent Notes · Scent Notes: After each long restHer inventory is measured: proficiency plus resolve, minimum three, and even a short rest may distill one more from the air itself. , prepare Scent Notes equal to your proficiency bonus + CE modifier (minimum 3). A Note is spent when you use a Formula. You may recover one Note during a short rest by spending 2 CE and ten minutes distilling nearby scents. · Scent Die: The weight of a formula's effect, growing with mastery. Your Scent Die scales d6 at 1st, d8 at 6th, d10 at 11th, d12 at 18th. · Formula — Courage Accord: The fortifying perfume: a veil of temporary health and a steadied nerve, and when the veil breaks, it blooms loudly into the enemy's face. Bonus Action • 1 Note + 1 CE • 30 feet. One willing creature gains a Scent Veil: temporary HP equal to your CE modifier + twice your proficiency bonus (a measured dose; no roll). It also has advantage on its next saving throw against frightened/charmed before the end of your next turn. Bloom: when the Veil is fully depleted by damage, it breaks loudly, each hostile within 10 feet of the veiled creature makes a Wisdom save vs your CE save DC or has disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn. One bloom per Veil. · Formula — Funeral Myrrh: The dulling pall: one failed save, and the target's next attack or save carries the subtraction of her craft. Action • 1 Note + 2 CE • 30 feet. One creature makes a Wisdom save. On failure subtract your Scent Die from its next attack roll or saving throw before the end of your next turn (minimum total result 1). · Formula — Hunter’s Trace: The tracking accord: the quarry's direction known for an hour, the nose does not forget what it has marked. Bonus Action • 1 Note + 1 CE. Mark the scent of one creature/object you can perceive within 30 feet. For 1 hour you have advantage on checks to track it and know its direction while within 120 feet unless the trail is completely sealed."},{"level":3,"title":"New Formulas —","rules":"Her organ grows two new stops: the Veil of Familiarity for passing unseen, and Anesthetic Fog for stilling the rushing. Veil of Familiarity: 1 Note + 2 CE, one creature gains advantage on Deception/Stealth checks to pass as belonging in the immediate environment for 10 minutes (does not alter appearance). Anesthetic Fog: Action, 1 Note + 2 CE, 10-foot-radius cloud for 1 round; Constitution save or speed -10 and no reactions until next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Bottled Memory —","rules":"Action · 2 Notes + 3 CE · Touch a willing creature or object: capture up to 1 minute of recent sensory impression; releasing it recreates an illusory scent, sound, or feeling replay in a 10-ft area for up to 1 minute · Counter-Scent: Reaction · 1 Note + 2 CE · Let an ally within 30 ft reroll a save against charmed, frightened, or poisoned."},{"level":11,"title":"Synesthetic Poison —","rules":"Action · 2 Notes + 4 CE · 30 ft · Constitution save: failure takes 2 Scent Dice poison or psychic damage and you choose blinded, deafened, or speed halved until the end of its next turn (success: half damage, no condition) · Group Accord: Courage Accord may affect up to PB creatures (1 Note per target)."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: Perfect Accord —","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE + 3 Notes · 30-ft aura, 1 minute · Choose Courage, Dread, and Clarity: allies entering or starting in the aura gain temp HP equal to your CE modifier + 2×PB (once per round) and advantage vs frightened/charmed; hostiles entering or starting inside make a Wisdom save or subtract 1 Scent Die from their first attack or save that round; you and allies have advantage on sense-based Perception/Investigation."}],"e153":[{"level":1,"title":"Claim Tickets, Archive, Weapon/Barricade/Restraint Loaners","rules":"Claim Tickets: Her measure of the archive's generosity: a ticket per proficiency, renewed with rest. You have Claim Tickets equal to your proficiency bonus, regained after a short or long rest. Your Claim Die scales d6/d8/d10/d12 at levels 1/6/11/18. · Archive: The lost-and-found itself: one action, one coin of CE, and any unclaimed nonliving object within reach is shelved, possession tested, never philosophized. Action • 1 CE. Touch an unattended, nonliving object that no creature within 60 feet currently possesses, wears, wields, or actively claims. Store it in your Archive. At 1st level, maximum size is Medium and the Archive holds items equal to 5 + your sorcerer level. Retrieving a stored object within your reach is a bonus action and 1 CE. · Loaner — Weapon: The archive lends a weapon for a minute, proficient in her hands, cursed in its edge, but it will not serve a second master. Bonus Action • 1 Ticket + 1 CE. Create a temporary cursed weapon for 1 minute. Choose melee (1d8, versatile 1d10) or ranged (1d8, range 60/180). You are proficient and may use your CE ability modifier for attack/damage. The Loaner vanishes if another creature ends its turn holding it. · Loaner — Barricade: The archive lends a wall: five feet square, half cover, one minute of borrowed shelter. Action • 1 Ticket + 1 CE. Create a 5-by-5-foot panel within 10 feet, AC 15, HP equal to 10 + 3×sorcerer level; it grants half cover and lasts 1 minute. · Loaner — Restraint: The archive lends its straps: a CE attack that grapples until escape or the minute's end. Action • 1 Ticket + 2 CE • 30 feet. Make a CE attack. Hit: the target is grappled by cursed straps/chains (escape check vs CE save DC) until it escapes or 1 minute."},{"level":3,"title":"Return to Sender —","rules":"The archive intercepts: an unattended missile passing within thirty feet is shelved, and she gains the loan of any tool-kit for ten minutes. Reaction, 2 CE, when an unattended projectile/thrown object passes within 30 feet after resolving its attack. Archive it if it fits your size limit. If it missed you or an ally, this costs no Claim Ticket; retrieving it later follows normal rules. Also gain Loaner Tool: 1 Ticket, conjure one artisan/tool kit for 10 minutes and gain proficiency while using it."},{"level":6,"title":"Evidence Locker —","rules":"Passive · Maximum Archive size becomes Large · May archive unattended cursed tools and objects (their active effects and recharge cease while stored) · Cannot archive an item attuned or bonded to another creature unless the bond is relinquished or broken."},{"level":11,"title":"Repossession Notice —","rules":"Repossession Notice: Bonus action · 3 CE · Mark one visible non-body item wielded or carried by a creature within 60 ft for 1 minute; the first time it becomes unattended, use your reaction to Archive it if eligible · Loaner Charge: Action · 1 Ticket + 3 CE · Throw a temporary charge 30 ft: Dexterity save or 3 Claim Dice force damage (half on success)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Department of Lost Property —","rules":"Domain Expansion · 10 CE · Sure-hit: at initiative 20, each hostile makes a Wisdom save; on failure, choose one non-body item it is wielding or actively using — it becomes Misplaced until the next count 20 (present but unusable: cannot be activated, attacked with, or grant passive bonuses); if no eligible item exists, it takes 2 Claim Dice force damage instead."}],"e154":[{"level":1,"title":"Observation Protocol","rules":"Observe.: Observation protocol: the watcher must commit a reaction at the start of every turn, or the interval goes unguarded. No exceptions have been recorded. At the start of its turn, a hostile creature within 60 feet that can see you may spend its reaction to Observe you until the start of its next turn. Observation ends early if it loses line of sight, becomes blinded or incapacitated, or an effect suppresses its senses. A creature cannot Observe if it has no reaction available. · Source Rule.: Confirmed across all trials: under even one watchful eye, the Step and the Reflex do not occur. Hypothesis: the subject's movement requires a true gap in observation, not mere inattention. Test personnel have stood motionless for minutes awaiting a single blink. The hypothesis holds. While at least one Observer has direct line of sight to you, you cannot use Blind Spot Step, Blink Reflex, or another feature in this technique that says it requires an unobserved interval. Your ordinary movement and class features still work; this is the playable translation of SCP-173 being immobile under direct observation. · Blind Spot Step.: Twenty feet through the unobserved interval. Note: no opportunity attacks are possible, there is no observer present to take them. Unobserved movement cannot be punished by the unobserving; the logic is airtight and, frankly, rude. Bonus action, 1 CE. If no hostile Observer can currently see you, teleport up to 20 feet to an unoccupied space you can perceive. This movement provokes no opportunity attacks. · Blink Advance: Unexpected result: when an observer's reaction is spent or lost for any reason, the subject advances fifteen feet, even while otherwise watched. The expenditure itself appears to constitute a micro-lapse. We are revising the observation protocol. When a creature Observing you spends or loses its reaction for any reason, you may move up to 15 feet without provoking. This works while observed. · Snap Strike.: Arrival-event analysis: the strike carries no bonus force. The effect is neurological, subjects who resist lose their reactions; subjects who fail are knocked prone and likewise cannot react. The subject does not need to wound. It needs you still. Once per turn, the first melee weapon or unarmed hit you land after a Blind Spot Step deals no bonus damage. The target makes a Constitution save: on a success it cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn; on a failure it is knocked prone and cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Blink Reflex","rules":"Reflex event: when the final observer stops watching, the subject Steps as a reflex, half range, no energy expended, no apparent decision made. Hypothesis: the Step is triggered, not willed. Like a knee-jerk. This disturbs me more than the teleportation does. Once per round when the final Observer currently watching you stops Observing, you may use your reaction to teleport up to half your Blind Spot Step range without spending CE."},{"level":6,"title":"Peripheral Failure","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Up to PB Observers within 60 ft: Constitution saves · On failure, their Observation ends and they cannot Observe you again until the end of their next turn, and they are blinded until the end of their next turn (Snap Strike upgrade)."},{"level":11,"title":"Impossible Interval","rules":"Passive · Blind Spot Step range becomes 60 ft · Once on your turn, pay its CE cost and use it immediately before one attack in your Attack action instead of as a bonus action · Snap Strike upgrade: the blind lasts until the end of your next turn, and you may move 10 ft without provoking after the Step."},{"level":18,"title":"Containment Chamber: DON’T BLINK","rules":"Passive · Snap Strike upgrade: a failed save denies the target reactions until the end of your next turn and blinds it until the end of your next turn · You gain the Domain below."}],"e155":[{"level":1,"title":"Witness / Pursuit","rules":"Pursuit Die: The approach is measurable: a die that grows as the hunt lengthens. We plot it like a fever chart. d6 → d8 → d10 → d12. · Covered Face.: Containment note: averting the gaze prevents cataloging, but leaves the observer blind to the subject in every way that matters. The defense and the vulnerability are the same posture. We have no better recommendation. You normally keep your face covered. A creature may declare that it averts its gaze from you; while doing so it cannot become a Witness, but has disadvantage on sight-based attacks and Perception checks involving you and cannot use a sight-dependent reaction against you. · Witness.: Cataloging event: no defense is permitted, to see the face is to be entered, and the entry persists twenty-four hours. Hypothesis: the face is not an image but an address. Once it has yours, distance is bookkeeping. As a bonus action you may reveal your face. Any creature within 60 feet with direct sight that is not averting its gaze becomes a Witness for 24 hours. There is no save; seeing the face is the trigger. A Witness remains marked even if it later closes its eyes or leaves your sight. · Pursuit.: Quarry designation: one Witness is selected, direction and distance known across the plane, speed multiplied, terrain and obstacles processed as paperwork. The subject does not navigate. It is drawn. Bonus action, 1 CE: choose one Witness as your Quarry. Until Pursuit ends, you know the Quarry’s direction and approximate distance while on the same plane, gain +10 feet × PB speed, ignore nonmagical difficult terrain while moving toward it, and have advantage on Strength checks to break obstacles between you and it. · Fury.: Fury mechanics: every turn spent closing the gap accrues Fury, discharged as Pursuit Dice on the arriving blow. Note: voluntary retreat burns the ledger. The subject's economy punishes only hesitation, never commitment. At the end of your turn, if the Quarry remains more than 10 feet away and you spent at least half your movement moving toward it, gain 1 Fury, maximum PB. If you willingly move away from the Quarry without being forced, lose all Fury. On a melee hit against the Quarry, spend any amount of Fury to add that many Pursuit Dice to the damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Nothing Stops the Pursuit","rules":"Obstacle response: barriers between subject and Quarry are destroyed at maximum effect, damage doubled, and the subject climbs what it cannot break. In trial 12 it went through a reinforced wall rather than around it. The wall was load-bearing. We have relocated the trials. Your attacks against unattended objects and structures between you and the Quarry deal maximum weapon dice and double damage. During Pursuit you gain a climb speed equal to your speed."},{"level":6,"title":"Four Pixels","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Imprint a cursed image of your face on a touched Tiny or larger surface or object; the first creature that clearly sees it without averting its gaze becomes a Witness · Maintain up to PB imprints for 24 hours."},{"level":11,"title":"No Known Material","rules":"Passive · While moving toward the Quarry: advantage on saves vs being shoved, grappled, restrained, or knocked prone · Reaction: when you take damage during Pursuit, spend up to PB Fury to reduce the damage by that many Pursuit Dice."},{"level":18,"title":"Face in Every Frame","rules":"Passive · Pursuit speed bonus doubles · You gain the Domain below."}],"e156":[{"level":1,"title":"Diagnosis / Symptoms","rules":"Diagnosis Die: The prognosis is measurable: a die that grows as the practice deepens. We have stopped calling it a die and started calling it a dosage. d6 → d8 → d10 → d12. · Clinical Examination.: Examination event: costs nothing, reveals everything, above or below half health, poisoned or diseased, energy above or below half. The body's ledger, read in a glance. Our own intake examinations take forty minutes and miss things. The subject's take a glance and miss nothing. Bonus action, no CE: choose one creature you can perceive within 30 feet. Learn whether it is above or below half HP, whether it is poisoned or diseased, and whether its current CE is above or below half its maximum. You have advantage on Medicine checks concerning that creature for 10 minutes. · Clinical Touch.: Annotation event: one unit of energy after a hit writes a Symptom where there was none. The body, annotated. The subject is not discovering illness. It is authoring it, in the margins of healthy tissue. Once per turn after you hit a creature with a melee weapon, unarmed strike, or CE attack, spend 1 CE to give it 1 Symptom. A creature may hold up to your PB Symptoms; they last 1 minute after the most recent application. · Symptomatic Decline.: Compound effect: every two Symptoms decay the body's healing and weaken its Constitution against the practice. The treatment degrades the patient's ability to receive treatment. This is, technically, iatrogenic. The subject does not seem to mind the term. For every 2 Symptoms a creature has, reduce healing it receives by one Diagnosis Die and subtract 1 from Constitution saves against this technique. Healing reduction cannot reduce healing below 0."},{"level":3,"title":"The Cure","rules":"The Cure.: The Cure: every Symptom consumed becomes necrotic damage, and at maximum dosage on the dying, the body is simply told to stop. No trauma is visible post-termination. The subject considers this gentleness. We have logged a formal disagreement. Action, 2 CE, melee CE attack. On hit, consume every Symptom on the target and deal (2 + Symptoms consumed) Diagnosis Dice + CE modifier necrotic damage. At 3+ consumed Symptoms the target cannot regain HP until the start of your next turn. If you consume the target’s maximum possible Symptoms while it is at or below one-quarter of its maximum HP, it makes a Constitution save after the damage; on failure it drops to 0 HP."},{"level":6,"title":"Crude Surgery","rules":"Downtime: spend 5 CE and 10 minutes operating on a corpse to create one Patient · You may maintain one Patient at a time."},{"level":11,"title":"Systemic Pestilence","rules":"Passive · Symptom cap becomes PB + 2 · A corpse reduced to 0 HP by The Cure may be converted into a Patient (Action · 4 CE) · Maximum Patients becomes PB, but only one Patient attack per round."},{"level":18,"title":"Ward of the Final Physician","rules":"Passive · Clinical Touch may apply a Symptom twice per turn to different targets · You gain the Domain below."}],"e157":[{"level":1,"title":"Corrosion / Slough / Threshold Walk","rules":"Corrosive Touch.: The preparation begins at the point of contact: fixed necrotic damage and one Corrosion Mark, the prey, softened. Action or attack replacement, 1 CE, melee CE attack. Hit: 1d8 + CE modifier necrotic damage (fixed) and 1 Corrosion Mark. A creature may hold up to 3 Marks for 1 minute. · Predigestion.: Mark analysis: each one saps five feet of speed and feeds the subject's grip, at three, the quarry is held. The subject does not chase. It seasons. Each Corrosion Mark reduces the creature’s speed by 5 feet and grants you +1 on Athletics checks to grapple or shove it, maximum +3. This does not reduce AC. · Surface Corrosion.: Environmental finding: every surface may carry a five-foot Mark, the network of doors growing with the subject's mastery. The room is no longer a room. It is a menu. As part of touching a solid unattended surface, spend 1 CE to place a Surface Mark on a 5-foot section. Maintain up to PB + CE modifier Surface Marks for 10 minutes. Corrosive Touch deals maximum damage to mundane unattended objects. · Threshold Walk.: The doors open: a bonus action, one coin of CE, and he is somewhere else, teleportation through his own residue. Bonus action, 1 CE: enter a Surface Mark within 5 feet and emerge from another Surface Mark within 30 feet. This is teleportation; you leave black residue but do not damage creatures merely by passing through. · Slough — the detonation.: Detonation event: two or more Marks within thirty feet may be triggered, failure burns necrotic per Mark and consumes them; three Marks deepen the odds against the prey. The subject prefers to let the seasoning finish before the swallowing. Bonus action, no CE: choose a creature within 30 feet bearing at least 2 Corrosion Marks. It makes a Constitution save; on failure it takes 5 necrotic damage × the Marks it bears and the Marks are consumed; on success it takes half damage and the Marks remain. If it bears 3 Marks, it makes the save with disadvantage."},{"level":3,"title":"Predatory Emergence","rules":"Arrival weaponized: the first melee hit after the Walk carries additional necrotic dice, and the Walk now reaches sixty feet. It exits the wall already swinging. We have moved the observation post back another ten feet. Once per turn, the first melee hit you land before the end of the turn after Threshold Walk deals +2d8 necrotic. Threshold Walk range becomes 60 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Dragging Hand","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · When grappling a creature with at least 2 Corrosion Marks: it makes a Charisma save; on failure, you and it vanish into the pocket space until the start of your next turn, then return adjacent to any Surface Mark within 60 ft · No other creature can enter."},{"level":11,"title":"Rotting World","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Technique Focus · A creature with 3 Corrosion Marks within 10 ft: Charisma save or enter your pocket dimension with you for up to 1 minute (it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, escaping on success) · Your bonus action each turn creates one 10-ft wall, pit, bridge, or patch of difficult terrain there · Damage and attacks resolve normally."},{"level":18,"title":"House Beneath Every Surface","rules":"Passive · Threshold Walk costs 0 CE once per turn; range becomes 120 ft · You gain the Domain below."}],"e158":[{"level":1,"title":"Voiceprint / Amnestic Breath","rules":"Voiceprint Archive.: The collection begins with a single sentence heard within sixty feet, recorded without action, kept to proficiency's count, reproduced perfectly. After hearing a creature speak a complete sentence within 60 feet, you may record its Voiceprint without an action. Maintain PB Voiceprints; recording another replaces one. You can reproduce an archived voice perfectly. · Thrown Voice.: The voice, displaced: a bonus action, one coin of CE, and the archived voice speaks from any point within sixty feet, suspicion may name it anomalous, but never its author. Bonus action, 1 CE: cause one Voiceprint to originate from any point within 60 feet for up to 1 minute. A suspicious listener may use an action for Insight against your CE DC; success reveals that the sound is anomalous, not who created it. · Amnestic Breath.: Breath event: a fifteen-foot cone, two energy, and the failed save loses a Moment. The present, unbreathed. Witnesses describe the interval afterward as 'the part where nothing happened, loudly.' Action, 2 CE, 15-foot cone. Creatures make Constitution saves; on failure gain 1 Lost Moment, maximum 3. A creature outside your amnestic effects may repeat the save at the end of each turn, removing 1 Lost Moment on success. · Lost Moment 1:: Tier analysis: first the reactions against the subject, then the senses themselves, then, at three Moments, its ten-foot movements leave it hidden from the hollowed mind. The victim's own locomotion becomes unobservable to the victim. We have no precedent. We checked. the creature cannot take reactions against you or your auditory decoys. 2: it has disadvantage on Perception and Insight checks involving you and cannot benefit from Help on attacks against you. 3: whenever you move at least 10 feet, you become hidden from that creature until you attack, speak in your natural voice, or it succeeds on a Search action against your CE DC. · Predatory Strike.: Hunt pattern: strikes land on the hollowed, the hidden, the unreacting, and failed resistance herds the frightened toward the nearest projected voice. It does not chase. It calls, and the called come. Once per turn when you hit a creature with at least 1 Lost Moment while you are hidden from it or it cannot take reactions against you (no action): it makes a Wisdom save vs your CE DC. On failure it is frightened of the nearest point where you have a projected Voiceprint (or of you, if none) until the end of its next turn, and it cannot willingly move farther from that point while frightened."},{"level":3,"title":"Troglobitic Senses","rules":"Physiology note: thirty feet of blindsight, a climber's speed, and the dark's own advantage in stealth. The body is built for a hunt conducted entirely in the erased present. It is, anatomically, a listener that eats. Gain blindsight 30 feet, a climb speed equal to walking speed, and advantage on Stealth in dim light or darkness. Bright light does not damage you but prevents advantage from this feature."},{"level":6,"title":"Borrowed Distress","rules":"Passive · Once per round, when a creature with at least 1 Lost Moment hears one of your Voiceprints from a point it can reach: force a Wisdom save; on failure it must use its reaction (if available) to move up to half its speed toward the sound by the safest route · Predatory Strike no longer requires you to be hidden or the target unable to react — 1+ Lost Moment suffices."},{"level":11,"title":"AMN-C227 Saturation","rules":"Bonus action · 4 CE · Technique Focus, 1 minute · A 15-ft aura surrounds you: a hostile ending its turn inside makes a Constitution save or gains 1 Lost Moment · A creature failing its Predatory Strike save is frightened for 1 minute (repeating the save at the end of each of its turns)."},{"level":18,"title":"Corridor Without Memory","rules":"Passive · Amnestic Breath becomes a 30-ft cone; a creature failing its Predatory Strike save is also stunned until the end of its next turn · You gain the Domain below."}],"e159":[{"level":1,"title":"Exposure / Adaptation","rules":"Adaptation Die: Every grudge needs its unit of measure. d6 → d8 → d10 → d12. · Threat Tag.: Ledger protocol: the pain must be named exactly, or it is not entered. Vagueness is rejected at intake. The subject's bookkeeping is more rigorous than ours, and we are a research laboratory. A Tag is one exact damage type, one named condition, or one recurring environmental hazard. “Fire damage,” “restrained,” and “vacuum” are valid; “this enemy” and “all cursed techniques” are not. · Exposure Record.: The record is written while the wound is fresh: reaction, one CE, one Data. When you take damage or fail a save that imposes a condition, use your reaction and 1 CE to record one relevant Threat Tag and gain 1 Data in that Tag, maximum 3. You can gain at most 1 Data in the same Tag per round. Data lasts until your next long rest. · Install Adaptation.: Expenditure event: one Data, one Slot, one refusal the flesh will honor. The subject spends its suffering the way other organisms spend energy. The exchange rate is obscene and the subject accepts it gladly. Bonus action, 1 CE, spend 1 Data and fill an Adaptation Slot until you replace it or finish a long rest. At level 1 you have 1 Slot. For a damage Tag, gain resistance to that damage type. For a condition Tag, gain advantage on saves against that condition and reduce any duration measured in rounds by 1, minimum 1. Environmental Tags grant an appropriate survival trait such as a climb/swim speed, water breathing, or tolerance to extreme temperature, subject to GM approval. · Biological Rule.: Localization finding: Adaptations live in the body, not in the technique's focus, the flesh keeps its own counsel. The immunity is biological, not technical. You cannot counterspell scar tissue. We checked, at some expense. Installed Adaptations are internal biology and do not use Technique Focus. You may replace one as a bonus action by paying the normal install cost and Data."},{"level":3,"title":"Regenerative Hate","rules":"Once per round when you take damage that matches an installed damage Adaptation Below half health, the grudges start paying dividends, the body rewards what it has already forgiven. and you are below half HP, regain 1 Adaptation Die + CE modifier HP at the start of your next turn. This healing cannot trigger from self-inflicted damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Reactive Morphology","rules":"Passive · Slots become two · Each installed Adaptation also grants one morphology: +10 ft speed, climb speed, swim speed, +5-ft melee reach, +1 AC, or +1 Adaptation Die damage once per turn with a natural or unarmed attack (the same morphology cannot be chosen twice)."},{"level":11,"title":"Hardened Adaptation","rules":"Passive · Slots become three · A normal elemental or physical damage Tag becomes immunity; force, psychic, radiant, necrotic, soul, spatial, conceptual, and Domain-derived damage remain resistance and let you reduce one matching damage instance per round by PB Adaptation Dice · A standard condition Tag may become immunity, except unconscious or incapacitated from 0 HP or a Domain's unique rule."},{"level":18,"title":"Termination Failure","rules":"Passive · Slots become four · Once per long rest, when damage would reduce you to 0 HP: remain at 1 HP, heal 4 Adaptation Dice + CE modifier, gain 3 Data in the triggering Threat Tag, and immediately install a Hardened Adaptation to it without using Slots until the encounter ends."}],"e160":[{"level":1,"title":"Mask / Temptation","rules":"Prime Host.: Prime Host identified: the original body, the one the mask calls home. All continuity, consciousness, energy, technique, belongs to the mask-bound soul, not to whichever body currently wears it. The host is a vehicle. The mask is the driver. The driver has never once asked directions. Your original body is your Prime Host. Your consciousness, CE, HP, class features, and technique belong to the mask-bound soul, not to whichever body currently wears it. · Manifest Mask.: Donning event: porcelain on the face, the performance can begin. Average donning time, four seconds. Average host compliance afterward, total. We time it anyway. Bonus action, 1 CE. A porcelain mask forms on your face. While worn by your Prime Host, gain telepathy 30 feet and proficiency in Deception or Persuasion; if already proficient, add PB again to checks with that skill. · Corrosive Secretion.: Ichor analysis: black, viscous, restraining, how the mask holds its audience still. Chemically unremarkable. Theatrically devastating. Once per turn, after you hit a creature with a melee attack, succeed on a grapple check, or touch an unattended object (no action), spend 1 CE. Creature: it makes a Constitution save vs your CE DC; on failure black ichor binds its limbs, its speed is halved and it cannot take reactions until the start of your next turn. Unattended nonmagical object: it corrodes, a Tiny or Small object is destroyed; a larger object gains a 1-foot-diameter hole or loses one component of your choice. · Temptation.: Grooming pattern: seduction in three marks, the slow work of making a host volunteer. Each mark is accepted. Each acceptance is documented. The paperwork of consent, completed just before consent becomes irrelevant. Action, 1 CE: a creature within 30 feet that can see or hear the mask makes a Wisdom save. On failure it gains 1 Temptation, maximum 3, for 1 minute. At 1 it has disadvantage on Insight against you; at 2 its speed is halved when willingly moving farther from the mask; at 3 it becomes a valid conscious target for Host Transfer. At the end of each turn it may repeat the Wisdom save, removing 1 Temptation on success. · Shared Vitality.: Damage routing: one ledger for all bodies, damage follows the soul, not the meat. Wounding the host wounds the subject. The subject considers this a fair trade. The hosts have not been consulted, except through the mask, which confirms they agree. Possessing another body never creates a second HP or CE pool. Damage to your current Host damages your normal HP."},{"level":3,"title":"Host Transfer","rules":"Action, 3 CE: place the mask The curtain rises on a new body; the old one goes dark. on a willing or incapacitated humanoid-shaped creature within 5 feet, or a conscious living creature at 3 Temptation. An unwilling living target makes a Charisma save. On failure your consciousness moves into it and your Prime Host falls unconscious but stable. The host repeats the save at the end of each turn, ejecting you on success."},{"level":6,"title":"Borrowed Bodies","rules":"Passive · Corpses, mannequins, statues, and other humanoid-shaped nonliving vessels automatically accept Host Transfer · They use STR 16, DEX 12, CON 16, AC 13 + half PB (rounded down), speed 30 (unless construction suggests otherwise) · They lose 1 Host Integrity per minute rather than per turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Mind Under the Mask","rules":"Passive · Telepathy 120 ft, Temptation 60 ft; at 3 Temptation you may read a target's surface thoughts within telepathy range · Reaction · 2 CE: when your current Host reaches 0 Integrity, transfer to another valid Host within 30 ft; otherwise return to the Prime Host."},{"level":18,"title":"Theater of the Anguished Mask","rules":"Passive · A creature failing its Corrosive Secretion save is restrained until the start of your next turn instead · Unattended objects corrode at no CE cost · You gain the Domain below."}],"e161":[{"level":1,"title":"Rough / Coarse / 1:1","rules":"Portable Clockworks.: Manifestation spec: two frames, ten minutes, one machine-spirit with opinions. The opinions are the load-bearing component. We have tried manifesting it without them; it refines nothing and sulks, mechanically. Action, 2 CE: manifest adjacent Intake and Output frames for 10 minutes. Only one set may exist. At level 1 they accept Tiny or Small nonliving objects that are not being worn or carried by an unwilling creature. · Scrap.: Currency analysis: Scrap, the machine's coin, minted from ruin. Every destruction is a deposit. The subject is the only entity in the facility with a positive savings rate. Rough and Coarse processes generate Scrap, a technique resource with a cap of PB + CE modifier. Unspent Scrap vanishes after a long rest. · Rough.: Destruction, itemized by size. Action: destroy a mundane input and gain Scrap by size: Tiny 1, Small 2, Medium 3, Large 4. Cursed or magical objects do not automatically yield Scrap and may resist destruction at the GM’s discretion. · Coarse.: Rough process: disassembly with an eye for parts worth keeping. The subject wastes nothing. Our disposal budget has fallen 40%. Our unease has risen proportionally. Action: disassemble an input into usable components and gain 1 less Scrap than Rough, minimum 1, or remove one mundane mechanical property such as armor plating, a lock, a blade, or a wheel while preserving the remainder. · 1:1.: Fine process: transmutation's honest middle, nothing from nothing. Mass is conserved; quality is not. The subject considers this a fair trade. Physics has filed no objection, which troubles physics. Action, 1 CE: turn a mundane input into another mundane object of similar size, material value, and complexity. It cannot create currency, ammunition in bulk, explosives, poisons, rare components, or supernatural items from nothing."},{"level":3,"title":"Fine","rules":"Action, 3 CE + 1 Scrap: enhance one item Four small mercies, one per item, one minute at a time. for 1 minute. Choose Keen (+1 attack and damage), Reinforced (+1 AC if armor/shield, otherwise +5 × PB object HP), Specialized (once per round, add +2 to one ability check made with the item), or Efficient (first CE cost paid through a cursed tool each round is reduced by 1, minimum 1). One Fine upgrade per item."},{"level":6,"title":"Rapid / Compound Cycle","rules":"Passive · Clockworks may accept Medium objects and up to PB inputs in one cycle · Once per turn, process one valid item as a bonus action · Fine may affect a non-Special-Grade cursed tool you willingly place in the Intake (its innate abilities are not copied or permanently altered)."},{"level":11,"title":"Very Fine","rules":"Action · 5 CE + 3 Scrap · Roll d10 minus current Refinement Risk (minimum result 1), then gain 1 Risk after resolving · Risk resets on a long rest; spend 2 Scrap before rolling to reduce Risk by 1 · Large objects become valid inputs."},{"level":18,"title":"Master Dial","rules":"Passive · Very Fine uses d12 instead of d10 · Once per long rest, declare a controlled result of 10 before rolling (resolve Impossible, then set Risk to 5) · Fine upgrades may last 10 minutes instead of 1 minute."}],"e162":[{"level":1,"title":"Level 1: Flat-Pack Catalog","rules":"Manifestation catalog: cover, carts, fixtures, and signs, the founder's catalog: civilization, flat-packed. Assembly required. The instructions are pictographic and, witnesses report, judgmental. · Store Die:: The store's own unit of measure. d6 at levels 1–5, d8 at 6–10, d10 at 11–17, and d12 at 18+. · Flat-Pack Manifestation.: Barricade doctrine: furniture as fortification, the founder builds before the battle. Ten by five feet of retail-grade courage. Our engineers have requested the specifications. The store has not responded. Action, 1 CE: create one Merchandise object in an unoccupied space within 30 feet. Maintain up to PB Merchandise at once for 10 minutes; creating beyond the cap dismisses one of your choice. Dismiss your own Merchandise as a bonus action. · Shelf Wall.: Barricade spec: ten by five feet of retail-grade courage. It provides cover normally, which is more than can be said for most of our cover. Large 10-by-5-foot object, AC 13, HP = 5 × level. It provides cover normally. · Shopping Cart.: Cart dynamics: fifteen feet of straight-line momentum, then the ram, a bludgeoning strike with a prone rider. The store's logistics department has weaponized momentum. Our logistics department has requested a transfer. Medium object, AC 13, HP = 3 × level. A creature may push it while moving. After pushing it at least 15 feet in a straight line, replace one attack with a CE attack against a creature ahead of it: 1 Store Die + CE modifier bludgeoning and a Strength save or prone. · Display Fixture.: Fixture finding: difficult terrain for the enemy, a staircase for friends. The store's furniture practices hospitality with a bias. We have begun to suspect the furniture likes us. Occupies a 10-foot square. Enemies treat the square as difficult terrain; allies you designate can climb or move across it normally. · Floor Lamp / Sign.: Illumination finding: thirty feet of bright honesty, the hidden stay hidden nowhere near it. The store believes in transparency. The transparency is load-bearing. Medium object, AC 12, HP = 2 × level, bright light 30 feet and dim light 30 more. Creatures within 10 feet have advantage on Perception checks to locate hidden creatures that are not invisible."},{"level":3,"title":"Infinite Retail, Closing Shift","rules":"Closing Shift — early rule Domain: Mercy pricing: an early Domain, priced by mercy, the store's guaranteed laws never wound; only its Staff may. The building is neutral. The employees are not. This is the most honest labor policy we have on file. Full-turn action, 6 CE, enclosed 60-foot-radius Domain for up to 1 minute. Binding vow: the Domain’s guaranteed laws never deal damage themselves, that non-lethal limitation is what permits level-3 access at the reduced CE cost. Ordinary attacks, techniques, hazards, and Staff can still cause damage normally. · Everyone Is Stranded: Egalitarian finding: no employees, no customers, only the Stranded, and the store does not play favorites. The founder included. The store's fairness is absolute and, during Closed Hours, absolute is the problem. There is no Employee/Customer hierarchy. You and every other creature inside are Stranded and subject to the same store cycle; Staff can attack you at night. Your advantage is knowledge: you always know the current Store Phase, the locations of Store Nodes and Settlements, and which objects are your Merchandise. Impossible Interior: ordinary doors, emergency exits, and attempts to walk to the barrier’s edge turn into additional aisles, they do not leave the Domain. · Store Cycle & Nodes: Cycle analysis: the liturgy of the store, Open, Warning, Closed, and the Nodes that feed the faithful: Restaurant, Warehouse, Showroom. The store keeps holy days. The holy days keep a schedule. We keep to the schedule. The Domain begins in Open Hours. At initiative count 20, advance Open Hours → Closing Warning → Closed Hours → Open Hours. When the Domain forms, place three indestructible 10-foot Store Nodes at least 15 feet apart: Restaurant, Warehouse, and Showroom. Once during each Open Hours, a Stranded creature adjacent to any Node may use an action to Scavenge: Restaurant heals 1 Store Die + PB HP; Warehouse creates one 10-by-5-foot Barricade within 5 feet (AC 13, HP = 3 × caster level); Showroom repairs one unattended object or Merchandise within 10 feet for 2 Store Dice + CE modifier HP. · Settlements & the shifting Exit: Settlement finding: hearths in the fluorescent wilderness, two barricades and a declared home, a fifteen-foot radius of half cover and held breath. The Stranded build homes the way our ancestors did: quickly, together, and facing outward. A creature adjacent to at least two Barricades, Merchandise objects, or substantial pieces of cover may use an action to establish a 15-foot-radius Settlement. Creatures inside gain half cover against Staff and advantage on checks or saves against Staff grapples; Staff outside must attack an obstructing founding structure before targeting a sheltered creature. During Open Hours, a Stranded creature may use an action to Search for an Exit (Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Survival) vs your Technique DC). On failure it gains a cumulative +2 to its next Search, maximum +6; on success an Exit manifests within 10 feet until the end of its turn, and moving through it (5 feet of movement) removes that creature from the Domain. You cannot use Search for an Exit to abandon your own Domain. · Staff & Staff Remains: PB staffing report: passive by day, hostile by night, and the founder retains one autonomous command each Closed Hours. The employees work the night shift. The night shift works the Stranded. PB Staff manifest when the Domain opens, passive during Open Hours and Closing Warning unless attacked, hostile to living Stranded creatures during Closed Hours. You get 1 autonomous Staff Action each round during Closed Hours: one Staff moves up to its speed and then Strikes (CE attack bonus, 2 Store Dice + CE modifier bludgeoning) or attempts Customer Removal (grapple and drag 15 feet). You do not choose their targets; the GM follows Staff priority. When a Staff is reduced to 0 HP, leave a Staff Remains marker; at the start of each Closed Hours, for every two Remains in the Domain, one additional Staff manifests (maximum PB additional), Remains near a Settlement draw the new Staff toward it. Killing every Staff is sometimes the worst strategy."},{"level":6,"title":"Settlement Founder","rules":"Passive · Flat-Pack Manifestation becomes a bonus action · Merchandise you created that forms part of a Settlement gains +1 AC and HP equal to 2× your level · When Closing Warning begins, willing creatures of your choice within 30 ft may use their reactions to move up to half their speed toward a Settlement they can perceive."},{"level":11,"title":"Restocking Cycle","rules":"Passive (Open Hours upgrade) · Cost 5 CE, radius 90 ft · Staff Actions become 2 per Closed-Hours round · Each time Open Hours begins: restore one destroyed Merchandise or Barricade you created to full HP in an unoccupied space within 30 ft of where it was destroyed, or remove one Staff Remains marker anywhere in the Domain."},{"level":18,"title":"Infinite Floorplan","rules":"Passive (Open Hours upgrade) · Cost 4 CE, radius 120 ft · Staff Actions become 3; Flat-Pack capacity becomes PB + CE modifier · Each time Open Hours begins: move one Store Node up to 30 ft to a legal space and teleport one of your Merchandise to another unoccupied space you can see within 60 ft; your chosen Settlement may be declared Exchange (its founding structures resist damage from Staff; creatures inside restore 1 Store Die + PB HP when Open Hours begins, once per creature per cycle)."}],"e163":[{"level":1,"title":"Eyes Before the Storm","rules":"Omen cap: The stockpile has a ceiling; the debt has a schedule. Proficiency bonus. You begin combat with 1 Omen if you are not surprised. Omens vanish on a short or long rest. · Omen Sight: One mark, one minute, sixty feet, the watching begins. Bonus action, 1 CE, 60 feet. Mark one creature, unstable object, barrier, or obvious environmental danger for 1 minute. You may maintain one mark. · Gain Omen: The threat must move first: warnings are earned only when the danger advances. Once per round when a marked threat hits with an attack, forces a saving throw, spends 3+ CE on one activation, causes a creature to fall prone/restrained/unconscious, or materially worsens a marked environmental hazard, gain 1 Omen. · Eyes Before the Storm: One Omen, one reaction: a creature moved out of harm's way before the blow lands. Spend 1 Omen as a reaction when a creature you can see within 60 feet is attacked or forced to make a saving throw: that creature may immediately move up to 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks. If the movement takes it out of the attack’s reach or range, behind total cover, or out of the effect’s area, the triggering attack misses, or the creature automatically succeeds on the saving throw. You must declare this before the result is declared."},{"level":3,"title":"Disaster Clock","rules":"Disaster Clock: Tick by tick, the future becomes legible, ask the GM what it is best positioned to do. One marked creature may carry a 0–3 Clock. The first time each round it uses an action, bonus action, reaction, or movement to directly advance the same dangerous objective, add 1 tick. At 3 ticks you may ask the GM which one of the following it is currently best positioned to do before the end of its next turn: attack, move/reposition, defend, or activate a technique. The answer is truthful but does not force its behavior."},{"level":6,"title":"Winged Intercession","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Manifest black wings for 10 minutes: 40-ft fly speed · Once per round, when you spend an Omen to protect another creature, fly up to half your speed toward it without provoking; if you end adjacent, interpose yourself — you become the target of the triggering attack or effect."},{"level":11,"title":"Catastrophe Map","rules":"Passive · Omen cap becomes PB + CE modifier (minimum PB); maintain three Omen Sight marks · Reaction · 2 Omens: when a marked creature scores a critical hit, make it a normal hit · When a marked creature begins Domain Expansion, Maximum Technique, or another full-turn charge you perceive, gain 1 Omen immediately."},{"level":18,"title":"Point Pleasant","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Every surface shows red-eyed afterimages of near futures · At initiative 20, name Attack, Movement, or Technique for each hostile: until the next initiative 20, the first time it performs the named category, every ally you choose may move up to 10 ft without provoking, and the next attack roll against the named creature has advantage (it never compels the target to perform the named action) · Clash 500 (Tier III); Technique Burnout 10 rounds."}],"e164":[{"level":1,"title":"Unnatural Atmosphere","rules":"Veil: Fifteen feet of nausea, centered on you, following you. Bonus action, 2 CE, Focus, 1 minute. A 15-foot aura centered on you moves with you. · Exposure: Four is the maximum; each failure is a line of testimony. The first time each turn a hostile creature enters the Veil or starts its turn there, it makes a Constitution save. Failure adds 1 Exposure, maximum 4. Leaving the Veil for a full round removes 1 Exposure; a short rest removes all. · Exposure thresholds: Speed, sight, reactions, then poison, the testimony compounds. 1 = speed −10 feet inside the Veil; 2 = subtract 1d4 from Perception and Technique Focus/Concentration checks; 3 = cannot take reactions while inside; 4 = poisoned while inside and cannot benefit from advantage on attacks against you. · Mode: Sulfur, Crimson, Gravitic, Static, four flavors of wrongness. Choose Sulfur, Crimson, Gravitic, or Static when activated and switch as a bonus action for 1 CE. Sulfur: creatures with Exposure 2+ regain only half as many HP while inside (this includes healing from Reverse Cursed Technique). Crimson: the Veil is lightly obscured; creatures with Exposure 2+ treat you as heavily obscured beyond 10 feet. Gravitic: hostile movement inside costs +5 feet per 5 feet when moving toward you. Static: creatures with Exposure 2+ cannot sense cursed energy beyond 15 feet and subtract 1d4 from reaction attacks."},{"level":3,"title":"Atmospheric Pulse","rules":"Action, 3 CE. Each creature of your choice in the Veil The Veil exhales: Exposure and poison in one pulse. makes a Constitution save vs your Technique DC. Failure: it gains 1 Exposure and is poisoned until the end of its next turn; success: no Exposure, unaffected."},{"level":6,"title":"Floating Apparition","rules":"Passive · Veil radius becomes 20 ft · Gain a 30-ft hover speed while the Veil is active and may maintain two Veil Modes at once · Forced movement against you is reduced by 10 ft while hovering."},{"level":11,"title":"Wrong Physics","rules":"Passive · Veil radius becomes 30 ft; Exposure cap becomes 5 · At Exposure 5, a creature is disoriented: at the start of its turn it chooses movement or reactions — it cannot use both before that turn ends · Your Veil may originate from a point within 30 ft and remain stationary instead of following you · Atmospheric Pulse rider: failing the Pulse save at Exposure 4+ grants 2 Exposure (cap 5)."},{"level":18,"title":"The Hill Beneath the Red Star","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · The whole barrier becomes the Veil with all four Modes active · Sure-hit: at initiative 20, each chosen hostile automatically gains 1 Exposure and is poisoned until the next initiative 20 (a creature protected from the sure-hit makes a Constitution save: success means no Exposure, not poisoned) · Exposure cannot exceed 5."}],"e165":[{"level":1,"title":"Pine Barrens Predator","rules":"Pursuit cap: The hunger's purse, and its ceiling. PB. Gain 1 Pursuit once per turn when you move at least 20 feet before hitting a creature, descend at least 10 feet, leap a gap, Dash, or willingly pass within 5 feet of a hostile without stopping. The same movement event grants only 1. · Cooling: The one honest law: end your turn planted, and the hunt cools. If you end your turn having moved less than 10 feet, lose all Pursuit. · Cryptid Body: Wings, hooves, horns, the manifestations are the hunter, not its tools. Your unarmed strikes may deal bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing and can use Strength or Dexterity. Wings, hooves, horns, and elongated limbs are visible manifestations, not separate creatures. · Pine Barrens Predator: Glide, hoofbeat, horn toss, the chase made flesh. You can glide: during your turn, after moving at least 10 feet, you may fly up to 30 feet but must end on a surface that can support you. Hoofbeat: after moving 20+ feet toward a target, on a hit you may spend 1 Pursuit (no action): push the target 10 feet; it makes a Strength save, knocked prone on failure. Horn Toss: spend 1 Pursuit (no action, invented) after a melee hit; target makes Strength save or is launched 10 feet upward or horizontally."},{"level":3,"title":"Marked Quarry","rules":"Bonus action, 1 CE: mark one creature Mark the prey and its fleeing becomes your fuel. you can see for 1 minute. Once per round when it voluntarily moves 10+ feet away from you, gain 2 Pursuit and may use your reaction to move up to half your speed toward it. Devil’s Cry: action, 2 CE, 30-foot cone; Wisdom save or frightened until the end of your next turn. The shriek’s fantasy is terror, not a thunderbolt, it deals no damage."},{"level":6,"title":"True Flight","rules":"Passive · Gain 50-ft fly speed while conscious; Pursuit cap becomes PB + 2 · Dive Rake: if you descend 20+ ft before a melee hit, spend 1 Pursuit (no action) — the target makes a Strength save; on failure it is knocked prone and frightened until the end of your next turn, and you may move through its space to an unoccupied space within 10 ft without provoking from it · Up to 2 additional Pursuit each force one more creature within 5 ft of the target to make the same save."},{"level":11,"title":"Night Pursuit","rules":"Passive · Pursuit cap becomes 2×PB · Once per turn after you spend Pursuit, move 10 ft without provoking · Marked Quarry no longer costs CE against a creature you damaged this turn · Reaction · 2 Pursuit: when a Quarry teleports or is forcibly moved, move up to your speed toward its new position after the movement resolves."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: The Leeds Devil Takes Flight","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Become Large: fly speed 80 ft, reach +5 ft, Pursuit cap 12, begin each turn with at least 3 Pursuit · Once on each turn when you move 30+ ft, make one unarmed attack without an action against a creature you pass within reach (it cannot itself grant Pursuit) · Devil's Cry becomes a 60-ft cone: failure frightened 1 minute (repeating the save at the end of each of its turns) and no reactions while frightened · When it ends, lose all Pursuit and gain 1 exhaustion level."}],"e166":[{"level":1,"title":"The First Invitation","rules":"Offer: A concrete kindness, freely given, movement, Help, temp HP, or the dignity of standing up. Once per turn as a bonus action, spend 1 CE and make a concrete offer to one creature within 30 feet: 10 feet of movement without provoking opportunity attacks, Help on one check or attack before your next turn, PB temporary HP, or allowing it to end prone for free. If it knowingly and voluntarily accepts the benefit, record 1 Open Door: choose one Threshold the creature meaningfully controls. Maximum 3 Open Doors per creature. Charm, domination, threats of immediate technique harm, or mind control cannot open Doors. · Open Door: Permanent, unspent, unfading, the gift outlives the giver. An Open Door is permanent. It does not fade on a rest and it is never spent. It closes only when the granting creature genuinely revokes permission, a deliberate, communicated revocation (spoken to your face, sent by messenger, or sealed in a warding rite), never an accident, a trick, or a coerced retraction. A creature that does not know you hold its Door cannot revoke it. If revocation drops a Welcomed creature below 3 Doors, the welcome ends. · Cold Knock (the fallback): When no one bargains, the technique wedges a door by force, the one honest breach. When no one will bargain, the technique does not stall. Once per short rest, when a hostile creature within 30 feet refuses or ignores your Offer, you may spend 2 CE to wedge a door by force: record 1 temporary Open Door to one Threshold it controls. It lasts until the end of your next turn, then slams shut, and the creature knows you forced it. A wedged door works like a genuine Door except it can never count toward Welcomed. Forced consent never becomes genuine; this is leverage, not permission. · Threshold: A home, a room, a ward, whatever a creature meaningfully controls. A home, room, vehicle, barrier, camp, ward, or space that a creature meaningfully controls can count as its Threshold. Domains are not automatically bypassed by this feature. · The First Invitation: Every Door marks its granter; direction within three hundred feet, and saves that slip by one. Each Open Door marks its granter. You know the direction to a creature whose Door you hold while it is within 300 feet. Once per turn when such a creature makes a save against your technique, subtract 1 from that save. You may ask permission to cross a mundane locked or guarded Threshold; if a creature whose Door you hold explicitly allows it, you can open or cross that Threshold as though physically authorized."},{"level":3,"title":"Access","rules":"Your Doors deepen. The Doors deepen: cover ignored, Thresholds stepped through. Your attacks and technique effects ignore half cover created by a granter’s own possessions, summons, or mundane fortifications. As a bonus action and 2 CE, step through a held Door: teleport to an unoccupied space just inside a non-Domain Threshold you hold a Door for, provided it is within 300 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Welcome","rules":"When a creature has granted you 3 Open Doors (three separate accepted bargains, Welcomed permanently until revoked below 3) · Price of Welcome: once per turn (no action), when a Welcomed creature within 60 ft damages you with an attack or harmful effect, it makes a Wisdom save; on failure it cannot willingly move farther from you until the end of its next turn and has disadvantage on attacks against you until then · Action · 3 CE: a Welcomed creature within 60 ft makes a Wisdom save; on failure it is charmed by you until the end of your next turn and cannot willingly cross a Threshold away from you during that time (on success it is immune to this use until your next turn)."},{"level":11,"title":"Once Welcomed, Never Gone","rules":"Passive · Your Doors persist until genuinely revoked, and you know the direction and approximate distance to every granter on the same plane · Once per short rest · Reaction · 3 CE: when a granter activates a barrier, Curtain, or non-Domain ward, make a CE ability check vs its save DC; on success you count as authorized for that effect for 1 round (never defeats a Domain barrier or its sure-hit)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Please, We’re Cold Outside","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Rules-based: outside the house, movement costs +5 ft per 5 ft and creatures cannot regain temp HP · Anyone may enter the house willingly: removes frightened, grants temp HP = 5×PB, and records 1 Open Door to that creature (max 3) · At initiative 20, each creature outside gains one Cold stack (2 stacks: speed −10 ft; 3: disadvantage on Constitution saves; 4: cannot take reactions); entering the house removes all Cold · Anti-domain protection prevents gaining Cold but not the house or its voluntary bargain · The Domain never forces anyone to enter · Clash 800 (Tier IV); Technique Burnout 5 rounds."}],"e167":[{"level":1,"title":"Impossible Stride","rules":"Step cap: The purse for distance; two Steps per turn, no more. PB. The first time each turn you move 10 feet without being forcibly moved, gain 1 Step for every full 10 feet moved, up to 2 Steps per turn. Steps vanish if you end two consecutive turns without moving at least 10 feet. · Long-Legged Body: Absurdity made doctrine: ten feet of reach on a pale torso. Your reach for unarmed strikes is 10 feet while you have at least 1 Step. Your appearance may become a pale torso balanced on absurdly long legs. · Impossible Stride: Difficult terrain, gaps, occupied spaces, the stride ignores them for a Step. Spend 1 Step during movement to ignore up to 10 feet of difficult terrain, a gap, low obstacle, or creature-occupied space; you cannot end inside another creature. Stilt Kick: once per turn on an unarmed hit, spend 1 Step (no action): push the target 10 feet; it makes a Strength save, knocked prone on failure."},{"level":3,"title":"Procession Path","rules":"After moving at least 20 feet, spend 2 Steps The ground remembers: a glowing path that carries allies and hinders the rest. (no action, invented) to leave a glowing path in the spaces you crossed until the start of your next turn. Allies entering the path may move 10 feet along it without provoking once per turn. Hostiles treat it as difficult terrain. The Toll, the ground remembers your stride: the first time each turn a hostile creature enters or crosses your Path, it makes a Strength save; on failure it is knocked prone."},{"level":6,"title":"Between the Frames","rules":"Reaction · When targeted by an attack you can perceive: spend 2 Steps to move 10 ft · If you leave the attack's reach or range or gain total cover, the attack misses; otherwise it resolves normally · Cannot be used after seeing the attack roll."},{"level":11,"title":"Processional Echoes","rules":"Passive · At the end of your turn, if you moved 30+ ft: create up to PB Echoes in spaces you occupied (last until the start of your next turn) · Attacks against you from more than 10 ft away have disadvantage while at least one Echo is visible · Bonus action · 2 Steps: swap positions with one Echo within 60 ft · When an attack misses you because of the Echo disadvantage, swap with one Echo within 60 ft without spending Steps or an action (once per round)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Footage That Should Not Exist","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Every creature leaves a translucent frame at the position where it ended its previous turn · At initiative 20, choose each hostile and one of its own frames within 60 ft: the target is snapped to that frame and cannot react until the movement ends (a creature protected from the sure-hit makes a Dexterity save, preventing the snap on success) · You may swap with one of your own frames at initiative 20 without spending Steps · Only position rewinds — never HP, CE, conditions, or actions · Clash 200 (Tier II); Technique Burnout 10 rounds."}],"e168":[{"level":1,"title":"False Member","rules":"Doubt Die: The technique's own unit of disbelief. Your Doubt Die follows the shared d6 → d8 → d10 → d12 progression. · Headcount: The technique reads togetherness, not affection, and records the original count. Action, 2 CE: choose up to PB creatures you can see within 60 feet that regard themselves as one group, a shared camp, patrol, crew, or vehicle counts; the technique reads togetherness, not affection. For 10 minutes you know whenever one enters or leaves 60 feet of you, and the technique records the original count. · False Member: You read as one of them, without copying any of them. While your Headcount is active, you can make your appearance, voice, scent, and superficial CE signature read as “one member of the group” without copying a specific individual. A creature that spends its action inspecting you may make an Insight check against your CE save DC; on success it sees through you. · The Contradiction (automatic field): Help becomes hazard: coordination itself is taxed. While your Headcount is active and you are within 60 feet of at least two of its members, the contradiction stands. While it stands, no coordination within the group is certain: whenever a Headcount member uses the Help action on another Headcount member, or uses a reaction that benefits another Headcount member (a granted attack, a reaction buff or heal, a formation or flanking bonus), it must first succeed on an Insight check against your CE save DC. On a failure it hesitates, the Help, reaction, or bonus is wasted (the action or reaction is still spent). The creature feels the wrongness but does not learn why. · Exposure (fallback & counterplay): The field is belief, one successful Inspection collapses it. The field is belief. A creature that spends its action looking for the impostor makes an Insight check against your CE save DC; on success it sees through your guise and the Headcount collapses entirely, spend another action and 2 CE to establish a new one. If the group never coordinates, the field has nothing to corrode, but the technique still works as infiltration: Headcount tracking, the False Member guise, and your decoy still bait attacks and waste enemy actions."},{"level":3,"title":"There Were Six of Us","rules":"Bonus action, 2 CE: create a False Member decoy A decoy with your AC and one HP, whoever wastes an attack on it becomes certain of the wrong thing. in an unoccupied space within 30 feet for 1 minute. It has your AC, 1 HP, no attacks, and can move 30 feet on your turn without an action. Maintain one decoy. A creature that wastes an attack or reaction on the decoy becomes certain of the wrong thing: it has disadvantage on Insight checks against your CE save DC until the end of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Wrong Voice in the Dark","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Choose one Headcount creature within 60 ft: until the start of your next turn, sounds you make may originate from its space and your decoy may look specifically like it · While this holds, a creature that fails a field Insight check takes 1 Doubt Die psychic damage."},{"level":11,"title":"Someone Is Missing","rules":"Passive · Headcount may affect up to PB + CE modifier creatures · Single-target beneficial actions (buffs, heals) that a Headcount member targets on another Headcount member now trigger the field check; on a failed check the action is delayed until the end of the creature's turn, when it may retarget legally (resources are not spent unless it resolves)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Campfire of Seven","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Law of Verify Before You Trust, made absolute: hostile creatures inside cannot use the Help action on each other, cannot use reactions that benefit each other, and cannot target each other with single-target beneficial effects — no check is offered (anti-domain protection lets a creature trust its own senses and coordinate normally) · Your False Member decoys cost 0 CE and you may maintain up to PB during the Domain · Clash 500 (Tier III); Technique Burnout 10 rounds."}],"e169":[{"level":1,"title":"Predatory Metabolism","rules":"Feeding Wound: One piercing or slashing hit marks the livestock. Once per turn after a piercing/slashing melee hit, spend 1 CE to mark the target for 1 minute. Maximum active wounds = PB (PB + your CE modifier at 11th level). A target may use an action for Medicine or Constitution check vs your technique DC to end its wound. · The Metamorphosis Track (automatic): Feeding grants no currency, only stages: Gaunt, Fed, swollen Apex. Feeding never grants a currency. Each time you Feed successfully, advance one stage (the track resets to Gaunt after a long rest without feeding). Stages are fixed: Gaunt Predator (0–1 feedings): advantage on Stealth in darkness; your attacks deal +2 damage against creatures at full HP, the hungry strike hardest first. Fed Hunter (2–3 feedings): +10 feet speed; the first time each round you Feed successfully, heal 5 HP; disadvantage on checks to hide or pass as harmless, the fed body shows. Swollen Apex (4+ feedings): your melee attacks deal +2 damage and you gain advantage on Intimidation; but your speed drops 10 feet, you have disadvantage on Dexterity saves, and you cannot benefit from the Hide action, nothing this swollen hides. · Feed: Five feet, a bonus action, a Constitution save, and the hunger advances. Bonus action while within 5 feet of a wounded creature. It makes a Constitution save. On failure: if it has CE, it loses 1 CE; otherwise it takes 4 necrotic damage (8 at 6th level, 12 at 11th). Either way, a failed save counts as one feeding and advances your metamorphosis. On success, no loss and no feeding. A creature can be Fed from only once per round."},{"level":3,"title":"Night Scent","rules":"You know the direction of every wounded creature Three hundred feet of knowing: every wound is a scent on the wind. within 300 feet and have advantage on tracking them. Pounce: if you move 20+ feet toward a wounded target before hitting it, your first successful Feed after the hit needs no bonus action."},{"level":6,"title":"Bloodless Drain","rules":"Passive · Feed drains CE equal to half your PB (minimum 1) on a failed save · Reaching Fed Hunter grants +10 ft speed, heals 5 HP the first time each round you Feed successfully, and imposes disadvantage on checks to hide or pass as harmless."},{"level":11,"title":"Empty the Pen","rules":"Passive · Active Wound cap becomes PB + CE modifier · Once per turn, when a wounded creature within 30 ft spends 3+ CE on one activation: Reaction — Feed on it as though within 5 ft · Feeding from a creature at 0 CE prevents it from regaining CE until the start of your next turn (on a failed save)."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Night of the Empty Pens","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Gain blindsight 60 ft, speed +30, climb 40 · Your first Feed each round needs no bonus action and may target a wounded creature within 15 ft through a spectral feeding tether · Each successful Feed advances the metamorphosis by one additional stage and heals 5 HP automatically · When it ends, the track resets to Gaunt."}],"e170":[{"level":1,"title":"Buried Static","rules":"Tremor Die: The desert's own unit of measure. Your Tremor Die follows the shared d6 → d8 → d10 → d12 progression. · Burrow: Twenty feet through loose earth, but never through worked stone. Bonus action, 2 CE, Focus, up to 1 minute. Gain burrow speed 20 feet through earth, sand, soil, snow, or comparable loose terrain; you cannot burrow through worked stone/metal. You may end your turn underground, but you cannot attack or perceive beyond tremorsense 30 feet while fully buried. · Tremor Path: Every segment remembers where you passed; you know who stands on them. Every 10-foot segment you burrow remains marked for 10 minutes, maximum number of segments = 2 × PB. You know every creature standing on a Path within 120 feet. · Path counterplay: Ten times PB damage, or fill it, or reshape it, the paths can be collapsed. A creature can use an action to inspect a suspected segment with Investigation/Survival against your CE DC. On success it identifies it; dealing 10 × PB damage to the ground, filling it, or reshaping the terrain collapses that segment. · Buried Static: Erupt from a Path, or wire a segment live, the ground testifies. Erupt: spend 1 CE (no action, invented) when leaving a Path to make one melee CE attack against a creature within 10 feet; hit deals 1 Tremor Die acid or lightning in addition to normal unarmed damage. Live Wire: action, 2 CE, choose one Path segment within 60 feet; creatures standing on it make Dexterity save or take 2 Tremor Dice lightning, half on success."},{"level":3,"title":"Caustic Tunnel","rules":"When creating a Path, designate it Acidic Acidic segments: the desert learns to burn as well as swallow. for +1 CE. First hostile to enter/stand on it each round makes Dexterity save, taking 2 Tremor Dice acid and having speed reduced 10 feet until end of turn on failure. Maintain PB Acidic segments."},{"level":6,"title":"Drag Under","rules":"Free (no action, invented) · 2 CE · After Erupt hits a Large or smaller creature: it makes a Strength save; on failure it is pulled into an adjacent Path space, knocked prone, and restrained until the start of your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Network Predator","rules":"Passive · Burrow speed 40 ft, tremorsense 60, Path cap 3×PB · Bonus action · 2 CE: while on a Path, emerge from any connected Path segment within 120 ft · Once per round when a creature triggers an Acidic segment, also trigger Live Wire there for 1 CE without an action."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Olgoi-Khorkhoi","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Become Huge: burrow 60, tremorsense 120, resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing, burrow through worked stone at half speed · Erupt becomes a 15-ft burst: Dexterity save, 5 Tremor Dice acid + 5 Tremor Dice lightning (half on success); failed creatures are knocked prone · Once per turn after moving underground 30+ ft, collapse a 20-ft-square Path area: creatures there make a Dexterity save or fall prone and become restrained by rubble until they use an action to escape · No new Acidic segments during the Maximum."}],"e171":[{"level":1,"title":"Blurry Sighting","rules":"Evidence Die: The rumor's own unit of measure. Your Evidence Die follows the shared d6 → d8 → d10 → d12 progression. · Evidence cap: PB plus two, and Evidence is earned by being seen, then lost. PB + 2. Gain 1 Evidence once per creature per encounter when it clearly sees you and you later break its line of sight for at least one full turn. You may also gain 1 when a creature succeeds on a check to track you. Evidence vanishes on long rest. · Impossible Specimen: Ambiguity as camouflage: tracks, hair, residue, all arguable. Your tracks, hair, silhouette, and CE residue are always just ambiguous enough to be argued over. This grants no automatic invisibility; it fuels the features below. · Blurry Sighting: One Evidence to Hide as a bonus action; false trails three hundred feet long. Spend 1 Evidence to Hide as a bonus action while lightly obscured or behind half cover. False Trail: action, 1 CE or 1 Evidence, create 300 feet of tracks/scent/residue leading in a direction you choose; checks to distinguish them use your CE DC."},{"level":3,"title":"Patterson-Gimlin Principle","rules":"The first ranged attack each round The first distant shot each round is made with disadvantage, and a miss is Evidence. made against you from beyond 30 feet while you are moving is made with disadvantage. If it misses, gain 1 Evidence. Spend 2 Evidence when a creature starts tracking you to make its next tracking check with disadvantage."},{"level":6,"title":"Wrong Ridge","rules":"Bonus action · 2 Evidence · Create a life-sized decoy sighting within 60 ft until the start of your next turn (moves 30 ft, produces tracks and sound, has 1 HP) · A creature that attacks it or spends an action investigating it gives you 1 Evidence (maximum once per round)."},{"level":11,"title":"Misfiled Proof","rules":"Passive · Evidence cap becomes PB + CE modifier · Reaction · Spend 3 Evidence when you would be revealed from hidden by an attack: after the attack resolves, move 15 ft without provoking and attempt to Hide immediately with any cover or obscurity · Once per short rest, erase or spoil one mundane recording, photograph, track set, or CE-trace sample of you within 60 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: No Specimen Exists","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 8 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Gain +20 speed, advantage on Stealth, Hide with only light obscurement · The first time each round a hostile sees you after you were hidden, gain 1 Evidence · Spend 1 Evidence after breaking line of sight to teleport up to 30 ft to a space also out of that creature's sight · Decoy sightings may persist for the Maximum's duration (max PB) · Not invisible while directly observed."}],"e172":[{"level":1,"title":"Window Visitors","rules":"Swarm Tricks: Rattle: one creature within swarm space makes Wisdom save or cannot take reactions until start of your next turn. Grab: contest your CE ability vs target Athletics/Acrobatics; on win one non-heavy held object is pulled 10 feet and dropped. Cling: one creature’s speed −10 until it leaves swarm space. Hurl Clutter: ranged CE attack from the swarm, 30 feet; on a hit, no damage, the target has disadvantage on its next attack roll or ability check before the start of your next turn, and if it is concentrating it must make a Constitution save to maintain concentration as if it had taken damage. · Mischief bank:: Frustration, banked: failed saves and wasted actions become currency. you have a bank of Mischief, maximum PB banked. Bank 1 Mischief whenever a hostile fails a save against a Swarm Trick, or spends an action removing, repairing, securing, or identifying a Visitor effect. · Pile On:: Spend the banked Mischief, every two buys another Trick against another target. bonus action, 1 CE, expend any amount of banked Mischief; for every 2 expended (round up, minimum 1), command one additional Swarm Trick this turn beyond the tricks your bonus action normally commands, each against a different target."},{"level":3,"title":"Night Siege","rules":"When swarm shares a space with a door, window, light source Sabotage: the mundane becomes unusable until someone spends an action. , vehicle, turret, or unattended object, command it to Sabotage: relevant mundane object becomes unusable until a creature spends an action repairing/clearing it; cursed/magical objects instead make a durability/CE check determined by the GM and are suppressed for only one round on failure."},{"level":6,"title":"They Came Back","rules":"Passive · When the swarm reaches 0 HP it disperses instead of dying · At the start of your next turn, spend 2 CE to reform it with half HP in a space within 30 ft of you (once per short rest, reform for 0 CE) · Mischief bank cap becomes PB + 2; the first extra trick from Pile On each turn costs no CE."},{"level":11,"title":"Every Window","rules":"Passive · Choose two tricks per bonus action; swarm space becomes 15 ft (Pile On's extra tricks stack on top; each 2 Mischief spent still commands one trick beyond the two) · Creatures inside have disadvantage on ranged attacks made through the swarm · On a successful Grab, hand the item to yourself or an ally within 15 ft of the swarm instead of dropping it · Mischief bank cap becomes 2×PB."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Siege at Kelly-Hopkinsville","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 8 CE · Focus, 1 minute · The swarm becomes a 30-ft-radius Visitor Perimeter centered on a point within 60 ft (no HP, indestructible; moving 60 ft from the center ends it) · At the end of each of your turns, choose up to PB Tricks against different targets or objects in the Perimeter; Hurl Clutter may target up to three creatures · Mischief bank uncapped during the Maximum · Once per round, when an enemy spends an action solely removing, repairing, securing, or identifying a Visitor effect, one ally you choose gains advantage on its next attack or check before your next turn."}],"e173":[{"level":1,"title":"The Gorgon’s Eyes","rules":"Gain Unveil. You also gain Serpent Lash: Serpent Lash: ten feet of reach, and advantage against those who Avert. a melee CE attack with 10-foot reach that deals 2 + your CE modifier piercing damage. Against a creature that is Averting, you have advantage on Serpent Lash once per turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Bronze Reflection","rules":"You may project the Gaze through one polished reflective surface The law finds new judges: one polished surface within thirty feet. within 30 feet; creatures can avert from that surface as though it were your face. Action, 2 CE: force one creature with 2+ Calcification within 30 feet to save Constitution; failure adds 1 Calcification, success removes none."},{"level":6,"title":"Stone-Blooded","rules":"Passive · Resistance to poison; advantage on saves vs petrification · Shell-Crack: when you hit a creature with 3+ Calcification with Serpent Lash, shatter its calcifying shell — it sheds 1 Calcification and falls prone."},{"level":11,"title":"House of Mirrors","rules":"Passive · Maintain up to PB reflected Gaze surfaces within 60 ft (each lasts while Unveil does); a creature can be forced to choose Avert or Look only once at the start of its turn · When a creature reaches Calcification 4, gain PB temp HP."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Garden of the Unblinking Queen","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Every surface becomes polished black stone reflecting your eyes · Sure-hit: at initiative 20, each chosen hostile automatically gains 1 Calcification (a protected creature makes a Constitution save, gaining none on success) · During their own turns creatures still choose Avert or Look normally; anti-domain protection affects only the initiative-20 stage · Petrified creatures appear as statues and return to their spaces when the Domain ends · Clash 800 (Tier IV); Technique Burnout 5 rounds."}],"e174":[{"level":1,"title":"Many-Necked Body","rules":"The opening lesson: a neck is an offering. Shed the Neck turns a struck blow into a pending wound, the attack deals no damage, and the neck regrows unless the enemy thinks in fire. Shed the Neck. Reaction, when you are hit by an attack, sever one of your Heads (Head Count −1, minimum 1). The offered neck lunges into the blow: the attack deals no damage to you. The severed neck becomes a Neck Wound under the Severing Trigger rules: at the start of your next turn it regrows (+1 Head, and you heal 1 Head Die + CON modifier) unless you took fire or radiant damage since the trigger. No damage threshold, no CE cost, no additional reaction to regrow, offering the neck is the cost. Bite: once per turn after an unarmed/weapon hit, spend 1 Head Die to add the die as piercing damage. If you have 4+ Heads, reach for Bite becomes 10 feet."},{"level":3,"title":"Hydra Venom","rules":"The heads learn poison. Spend one CE on a Bite to force a Constitution save, and venom stacked on venom turns a poisoned wound into necrotic pressure. When Bite adds a Head Die, spend 1 CE to force Constitution save. Failure is poisoned until end of target’s next turn. A poisoned target that is hit by another Bite before then takes one extra Head Die necrotic."},{"level":6,"title":"Two From One","rules":"Passive · When a Neck Wound regrows, spend 2 additional CE to gain 2 Heads instead of 1 · Head cap becomes PB + 3 · Area damage that hits you consumes one extra Head Die from your current pool after resolving."},{"level":11,"title":"Unkillable Neck","rules":"Passive · At the start of your turn, if you have 4+ Heads and a Head regrew since your last turn: heal one Head Die without spending CE · Spend 2 Head Dice instead of a reaction to Shed the Neck · When you succeed on a death save, immediately create a pending Neck Wound that cannot be cauterized until after your next turn begins."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Ninefold Lernaean Body","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Head Count 9, size Large, reach 15, Head Dice become d12 · Once each turn after the Attack action, spend 3 Head Dice to make three Bite CE attacks against one or several creatures in reach · At the start of each turn in which a Head regrew, heal 2 Head Dice (fire or radiant damage reduces this to one die that turn) · When it ends, Head Count returns to normal cap; excess heads vanish without healing."}],"e175":[{"level":1,"title":"Feather and Heart","rules":"The scale opens with its first two verdicts: Measured, which lends his attacks necrotic weight once per turn, and Found Wanting, which erodes the target's saves. Gain Weigh Heart and Temptations. Weight stages 1–2 are active from the start: 1: Measured: your attacks deal +1 Scale Die necrotic to the Weighed target once per turn. 2: Found Wanting: it subtracts 1 from saves against your technique."},{"level":3,"title":"Crocodile Maw","rules":"The devourer's jaws. Three CE for a melee strike that scales with the Weight already gathered, the jaws take what the track allows, no decision required. Action, 3 CE: make a melee CE attack against a Weighed target. On hit: 2 Scale Dice + CE modifier piercing/necrotic, plus 1 additional Scale Die per 2 Heart Weight, no decision; the jaws take what the Weight allows."},{"level":6,"title":"Heavier Than the Feather","rules":"Passive · Offer up to two different Temptations per round (a creature may accept only one per turn) · Track deepens to stages 3–6: 3 Slowed (speed −10 ft while moving away from you); 4 Suppressed (cannot regain CE); 5 Crushing Jaws (at the start of its turn it takes 1 Scale Die necrotic and loses 1 CE, automatically); 6 Doomed (your Crocodile Maw has advantage against it and ignores resistance to its necrotic portion)."},{"level":11,"title":"Hall Without a Judge","rules":"Passive · Maintain Weighed on up to PB creatures; once per round when a target refuses a Temptation, immediately offer a different Temptation (refusal never adds Weight) · Action · 4 CE: move up to 2 Heart Weight from one willing Weighed ally onto yourself, or from yourself onto another willing Weighed creature."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum Technique: Devour the Heavy Heart","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE · One Weighed creature within 30 ft with 5+ Heart Weight: Constitution save; failure takes 10 Scale Dice necrotic, loses CE equal to its Heart Weight, and cannot use its Innate Technique until the end of its next turn (success: half damage, no CE or technique loss) · If this reduces it to 0 HP, consume the Heart's cursed imprint: regain CE equal to its Heart Weight and all Weight on it ends · A creature can be targeted by this Maximum only once per long rest."}],"e176":[{"level":1,"title":"Bound Wolf","rules":"The wolf enters the field already leashed. Two Bonds, and Ragnarök spent for +4 to a strike, fifteen feet of unmolested movement, or a save steadied. Gain Bonds and Ragnarök. After a long rest, choose 2 Bonds from the list. Once per turn, you may spend 1 Ragnarök token to add +4 to one melee hit, to move 15 feet without provoking opportunity attacks, or to add +4 to a Strength or Constitution save."},{"level":3,"title":"The Chain Remembers","rules":"Other people's chains feed her too. Grappled, restrained, paralyzed, slowed, moved against her will, each becomes a temporary Chain token, and ending the condition on herself earns temporary HP. When an enemy grapples, restrains, paralyzes, slows, or forcibly moves you, gain 1 temporary Chain token, maximum 1. Spend it like a Ragnarök token before the end of your next turn. If you end the condition on yourself, gain temporary HP equal to 3 × your PB."},{"level":6,"title":"Wolf at the Rope","rules":"Passive · Prepare 3 Bonds · When you break a Bond, creatures of your choice within 10 ft make a Wisdom save or are frightened until the end of your next turn · Spend 2 Ragnarök tokens on a melee hit: +8 damage and a Large or smaller target is knocked prone on a failed Strength save."},{"level":11,"title":"Five Impossible Bindings","rules":"Passive · Prepare 5 Bonds · Once per turn, if you are currently obeying at least 3 unbroken Bonds, reduce the CE cost of one Gleipnir Breaker feature by 1 (minimum 0) · When you break your third Bond in an encounter, immediately end grappled and restrained on yourself and move 20 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Ragnarök Unbound","rules":"Maximum Technique · Prerequisite: at least 3 broken Bonds · Bonus action · 8 CE · Consume all Ragnarök tokens · Focus, 1 minute · Gain +10 ft speed and 8 temp HP per consumed token; once per turn add +4 per consumed token (max +24) to one melee hit · Immune to frightened; cannot be restrained by non-Domain effects · The first time each round a creature tries to reduce your speed, grapple, restrain, or forcibly move you, make one melee attack against it if in reach · When it ends, every prepared Bond counts as broken until your next long rest and you gain 1 exhaustion level."}],"e177":[{"level":1,"title":"Serpent Boundary","rules":"The boundary and the fang. Segments gained, plus World Fang, a ten-foot melee strike that poisons what it finds standing on his lines. Gain Coil Segments. You also gain World Fang: a melee CE attack with 10-foot reach that deals 2 + your CE modifier poison damage. If the target is standing on or crossing a Segment, it makes a Constitution save vs your technique DC, failure: it is poisoned until the end of your next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Three Ring Laws","rules":"The closed circle declares its law, once, unreversed: Guard for allies within, Venom for trespassers, Constrict for those who would leave. When completing a Ring choose: Guard allies inside gain +1 AC against attacks from outside; Venom a hostile that enters the Ring or starts its turn inside makes a Constitution save; failure: it is poisoned until the start of its next turn and cannot regain HP until then; success: no effect; Constrict moving from inside to outside costs double movement, and when a hostile attempts to cross the boundary it makes a Strength save, failure: its movement stops at the boundary and it is grappled (escape DC = your technique DC). A creature saves against each Ring at most once per turn."},{"level":6,"title":"World Venom","rules":"Passive · A creature failing its Venom Ring save is poisoned for 1 minute instead (repeats the Constitution save at the end of each of its turns) · Reaction · 1 CE: when a hostile crosses a Segment, make a World Fang attack against it from the Segment's space."},{"level":11,"title":"Nested World","rules":"Passive · Segment cap becomes 2×PB; one segment may support two overlapping Rings · Bonus action · 2 CE: Tighten one Ring until the start of your next turn, moving each of its segments inward up to 10 ft while preserving a legal closed shape; creatures crossed by a moving Segment make a Strength save or are pushed with it (forced movement does not trigger Constrict)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Midgard Encircled","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius, 1 minute · A colossal serpent forms the Domain boundary; six free Coil Segments appear in legal positions · Each turn, create or move one Segment without an action or CE · Sure-hit: at initiative 20, choose one Ring — every hostile inside it suffers that Ring's law as if it had just triggered, and you may Tighten it 10 ft (a protected creature makes the relevant Ring save: success avoids the initiative-20 effect and the forced Tighten movement for that event); ordinary Ring triggers still resolve normally · Clash 800 (Tier IV); Technique Burnout 5 rounds."}],"e178":[{"level":1,"title":"Masquerade","rules":"The wardrobe opens. Masks gained, Strain tallied, and Backward Tell: a missed melee strike answered with five feet of deliberately wrong footwork. Gain Masks and Identity Strain. You also gain Backward Tell: once per turn while you are masked, when a creature misses you with a melee attack, you may move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks from it, using deliberately wrong body language."},{"level":3,"title":"Borrowed Habit","rules":"Two proficiencies per Mask, and a minute of watching the routine buys advantage on the first Deception of the scene. Each Mask records two proficiencies instead of one; choose one to gain when assuming it. After 1 minute observing a masked identity’s normal routine, advantage on your first Deception check to impersonate it in a scene."},{"level":6,"title":"Predator Behind the Face","rules":"Passive · When recording a Mask, also record one mundane movement mode or sense the target naturally has: climb speed up to walking speed, swim speed up to walking speed, darkvision 60 ft, or +5-ft reach if anatomically appropriate — gain that trait while masked · Supernatural flight, tremorsense, regeneration, and special senses cannot be copied."},{"level":11,"title":"Many Faces, One Turn","rules":"Passive · Switch Masks as a bonus action for 1 CE · Mask cap becomes PB + CE modifier · Once per round when you switch, clear 1 Strain if the new Mask was unused since your last short rest · You may maintain one purely cosmetic disguise over armor or equipment without merging mechanics."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Palace of a Hundred Borrowed Faces","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 8 CE · Focus, 1 minute · Switch between any stored Mask once per turn without an action or CE; Identity Strain is ignored · Each switch: choose +1 AC, +10 speed, proficiency in one skill, or advantage on your next weapon or unarmed attack roll until your next switch · Once: combine the movement or sense traits of three stored Masks simultaneously · When it ends, immediately gain 4 Identity Strain and cannot assume a Mask until the end of your next turn."}],"e179":[{"level":1,"title":"Sacred Coil","rules":"The two gestures. Tighten spends a Constrict Coil for damage and possible restraint; Interpose spends a Ward Coil to take an ally's blow whole, and catches the striking limb in the coil. Gain Place Coil. One creature may hold at most 2 Coils. Tighten: as a bonus action, spend one Constrict Coil on a creature within 60 feet; it takes 1 Sacred Die bludgeoning damage and makes a Strength save, becoming restrained until the end of its next turn on a failure. Interpose: as a reaction when an ally within 60 feet is hit by an attack, spend one Ward Coil. The coil wraps the ally and takes the blow: the ally takes no damage from the attack. The striking limb is caught in the coil, the attacker must make a Strength save vs your CE save DC or be grappled (escape DC = your CE save DC) until the end of its next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Shed Skin","rules":"The shed coil cleanses: poisoned, grappled, frightened ended on a willing bearer, once per short rest, by their bonus action or her reaction. A willing bearer may spend one Ward Coil as a bonus action to end poisoned, grappled, or frightened on itself. You may instead spend your reaction to do this for it. A creature can benefit once per short rest."},{"level":6,"title":"River Venom","rules":"Passive · When Tighten damages a creature, spend 1 CE to force a Constitution save; failure is poisoned until the end of your next turn · Gain swim speed 40 ft and breathe underwater while at least one Coil is active."},{"level":11,"title":"Sevenfold Warding","rules":"Passive · Active Coil cap becomes PB + CE modifier; one creature can hold 3 · A Ward Coil may grant +2 AC against the triggering attack instead of +1 (still consumes itself) · If a creature has both Ward and Constrict Coils from you, you decide which type your Tighten or Interpose consumes."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Palace Beneath the Sacred River","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · A submerged jeweled palace appears without imposing drowning · At initiative 20, each ally you choose gains one Ward Coil and each hostile automatically gains one Constrict Coil (a protected hostile makes a Strength save and gains none on success) · Active Coil cap ignored inside; Domain-created Coils vanish when it ends · Once per round, Shed Skin can end one additional condition: charmed, restrained, or blinded · Clash 500 (Tier III); Technique Burnout 10 rounds."}],"e180":[{"level":1,"title":"First Tail","rules":"The engine opens with Lies one and two claimable, and the First Lie already told: Paper Fox, an illusion in a five-foot space, movable, broken only by direct inspection. Gain the Claim-a-Lie engine. You may claim Lies 1–2. You begin with the First Lie already told: I. Paper Fox (action, 1 CE, one visual/audio illusion in a 5-foot space within 30 feet for 1 minute; it may move 30 feet on your turn; no physical force; Investigation against your CE DC after direct inspection)."},{"level":3,"title":"Three Tails","rules":"Lies two through four: Stolen Voice, the wisp-kindling Foxfire with its luring light, Fox Wedding's obscuring procession, and the drift that follows the lured. You may now claim Lies 1–4. II. Stolen Voice (bonus action, 1 CE, speak with any voice you have heard; hearers need Insight against your CE DC to doubt it). III. Foxfire, Kindle Foxfire: action, 1 CE, place a foxfire wisp (a floating blue flame) in a 5-foot space within 60 feet; it lasts 1 minute with Focus and sheds dim light 10 feet. On your turn you may move each wisp up to 30 feet, no action. Maximum wisps = PB. When a hostile starts its turn within 10 feet of a wisp or moves within 10 feet of one, it makes a Wisdom save against your technique DC, failure: it is lured until the end of its next turn (it must spend its movement moving toward the wisp by the most direct route, as though charmed by the light); success: it is immune to that wisp’s lure for 24 hours. IV. Fox Wedding (action, 2 CE, 15-foot cube of illusory rain, lanterns, or procession within 60 feet; lightly obscured for 1 minute with Focus). Luring Drift: when a creature becomes lured by your wisp, you may move that wisp up to 15 feet (no action), the victim’s forced movement follows the light."},{"level":6,"title":"Five Tails","rules":"Passive · Claim Lies 1–6; maintain up to PB Paper Foxes · V. False Road: Action · 2 CE · Illusory path, bridge, or doorway up to 30 ft long within 60 ft for 1 minute; believers waste their movement on a failed Wisdom save · VI. Substitution: Reaction · 2 CE · When attacked, before the roll: swap with a Paper Fox within 30 ft; the attack destroys the illusion."},{"level":11,"title":"Seven Tails","rules":"Passive · Claim Lies 1–8; once per round when you claim a lie, move one illusion or wisp 30 ft without an action · VII. Possession's Echo: Action · 3 CE · One creature that can see an illusion: Wisdom save or it treats one 15-ft cube of your illusion as fully real for movement and targeting until the start of your next turn (damage from a contradiction grants a new save) · VIII. The Hidden Ball: Bonus action · 3 CE · Attacks against you have disadvantage until the start of your next turn; you may Hide as part of it."},{"level":18,"title":"True Form, Nine Tails Ascendant","rules":"IX. Nine Tails Ascendant (replaces Domain) · Bonus action · 10 CE · Once per long rest · 1 minute · All nine lies are available regardless of claims; Paper Foxes cost 0 CE (maintain up to PB); Foxfire wisps kindled as a bonus action for 0 CE; Substitution costs 0 CE; +10-ft speed; leave no tracks, cannot be followed non-magically · Not a Domain: no clash points, no barrier, no Burnout."}],"e181":[{"level":1,"title":"Bones of the Hungry","rules":"The first assembly: Arm for reach and damage, Ribs for temporary HP, Jaw for a grappling bite, Hunger spent as a bonus action. Spend Hunger as a bonus action: Arm (1) reach +10 feet until end of turn and one melee hit deals +4 damage; Ribs (1) gain temporary HP equal to 4 + your CE modifier; Jaw (2) melee CE attack with 10-foot reach, dealing 9 piercing damage and grappling on a failed Strength save until the end of your next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Rattle of the Giant","rules":"Fear as fertilizer. Two CE and an action frighten his chosen within twenty feet, and every failed creature feeds him one Hunger, up to PB, once per short rest. Action, 2 CE: creatures of choice within 20 feet make Wisdom save; failure frightened until end of your next turn. For each failed creature, gain 1 Hunger, maximum PB Hunger from this activation. Once per short rest."},{"level":6,"title":"Skeletal Armor","rules":"Bonus action · 3 Hunger · Focus, 1 minute · AC becomes at least 16 + half PB (rounded down); size Large if you choose; unarmed reach +5 ft · While active, Arm costs 0 Hunger once per turn but still adds only +4."},{"level":11,"title":"Torso of a Nation","rules":"Passive · Hunger cap becomes 3×PB · Action · 4 Hunger: manifest a 20-ft-tall rib-and-spine construct centered on you for 1 minute — allies inside gain half cover from outside attacks; enemies entering make a Strength save or are pushed 10 ft · Move it with you at half speed or leave it stationary."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Gashadokuro, Starvation Colossus","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action · 10 CE and at least 6 Hunger · Consume all Hunger · Focus, 1 minute · Become Huge with reach 20: gain temp HP equal to 10 per Hunger consumed; unarmed attacks deal 9 + STR/CE modifier · Once per turn after a melee hit, make a free Jaw grapple without spending Hunger · Colossus Hunger: at the end of each of your turns, if a creature within 60 ft took 20+ damage that round, regain 1 consumed Hunger; spend 2 for one extra Arm attack as a bonus action, or 3 to restore 12 temp HP · When it ends, all remaining temp HP and Hunger vanish and you take 5 unavoidable damage per 2 Colossus Hunger left."}],"e182":[{"level":1,"title":"Remembered Wisdom","rules":"The feathers open their account. Every borrowed success that lands also leaves the beneficiary temporary HP equal to her PB. Gain Memory Feathers. When a creature benefits from a Feather and the modified roll succeeds, that creature also gains temporary HP equal to your proficiency bonus."},{"level":3,"title":"Healing Plumage","rules":"Two CE and any feather buys eight plus her modifier in healing, technique healing, not RCT, with its restrictions honored; a Mercy feather also ends frightened or poisoned. Action, 2 CE and consume any Feather: one creature within 30 feet heals 8 + your CE modifier. This is technique-limited healing, not Reverse Cursed Technique: it cannot restore HP that RCT restrictions forbid. If consuming Mercy Feather, also end frightened or poisoned."},{"level":6,"title":"Wing of Rescue","rules":"Manifest radiant wings · 2 CE · Focus, 10 minutes · Fly 40 ft · When you spend a Journey Feather on another creature, fly up to 20 ft toward it (no reaction) · Healing Plumage becomes 12 + your CE modifier."},{"level":11,"title":"Ancient Counsel","rules":"Passive · Feather cap becomes PB + CE modifier · Once per short rest, spend two Feathers of different types: a willing creature rerolls one failed attack, save, or check and adds your PB to the reroll · Maintain one Great Feather (created from a natural 20); when spent it adds 2×PB."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Nest at the End of Time","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · 90-ft radius, 1 minute · Beneficial law, not hostile damage: when it opens, each ally you choose creates one Feather based on the last category it successfully performed this encounter (temporary; vanish when it ends) · At initiative 20, choose one Feather type: until the next initiative 20, the first time each ally performs that category it gains your PB to the roll, healing, or movement without consuming a Feather · Once per round, Healing Plumage costs 0 CE (still consumes a Feather)."}],"e183":[{"level":1,"title":"Hundred-Throated Storm","rules":"The opening volley: a thirty-foot line or fifteen-foot cone of fire, lightning, thunder, or poison for one CE, two d8 scaling with level, and thunder that pushes ten feet. Hundred-Throated Storm (action, 1 CE): unleash a 30-foot line or 15-foot cone of fire, lightning, thunder, or poison; creatures in the area make a Dexterity save. It deals 2d8 of the chosen damage type, plus 1d8 at 5th, 11th, and 17th level (invented: the technique die is a d8). A storm of thunder may push 10 feet."},{"level":3,"title":"Serpent Limbs","rules":"The storm grows limbs. Two CE for a minute: ten feet of speed, a climb speed, wings at high Cataclysm, and a Cataclysm spent after twenty feet of movement buys a grappling melee strike. Serpent Limbs (bonus action, 2 CE, 1 minute): gain +10 feet of speed and a climb speed, plus storm-wings at higher Cataclysm. After moving 20 feet, you may spend 1 Cataclysm for a melee technique strike dealing 2d8 of damage (invented) and a grapple. On a hit the target is grappled with no separate check; it may use its action to escape, DC = your CE save DC (invented)."},{"level":6,"title":"Many-Mouthed Tempest","rules":"Passive · When you unleash a Storm, spend up to 3 Cataclysm to add different riders: ignite, reaction denial, 15-ft push, or poisoned until the end of the target's next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Mountain-Buried Monster","rules":"Mountain-Buried Monster: Reaction · 3 CE · Reduce incoming damage by 3d8 + your CE modifier (invented) and create rubble terrain · Passive: while below half HP, your Cataclysm cap increases by 2 and you gain 30 ft of flight."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Siege of Heaven","rules":"Maximum Technique: Siege of Heaven · 8 CE · Lasts 3 rounds · Once per long rest · Activating it costs an action (invented); you assume a Huge storm form · At initiative 20 each round, choose a different catastrophe: eruption, thunderhead, hurricane, or venom rain — each creates a 30-ft zone; creatures make a save against 4d8 of damage plus a rider (invented)."}],"e184":[{"level":1,"title":"Hands Beyond Counting","rules":"The first three employments: reach extended five feet per Hand, a Hand Die of d8 added to damage after a hit, or a reactive +2 AC against one attack. You may spend your spectral Hands to extend your melee reach (+5 feet per Hand spent until the end of your turn, invented), to add a Hand Die to damage after a hit, or as a reaction to gain +2 AC against one attack. A Hand Die is a d8 (invented)."},{"level":3,"title":"Stone Barrage","rules":"The volley. Two CE and up to PB Hands buy one ranged technique attack per Hand within sixty feet, two per target, each hit a Hand Die plus his modifier, the modifier once per target. Stone Barrage (action, 2 CE): spend up to PB Hands. Make one ranged technique attack per Hand spent against targets within 60 feet, with a maximum of two attacks per target. Each hit deals one Hand Die + your CE modifier, with the modifier applying once per target."},{"level":6,"title":"Fifty Heads, Hundred Tasks","rules":"Passive · Your Hands can remotely manipulate objects, bolster your Strength checks, or maintain one 20-ft spectral grapple · Establishing the grapple costs 1 Hand: contested Strength (Athletics) vs the target's Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics); the target may spend its action to re-contest and escape; the grapple ends if the Hand is committed elsewhere (invented)."},{"level":11,"title":"Titan-Burying Volley","rules":"Passive · Once per turn after hitting a Large or larger creature, spend 3 Hands: it makes a Strength save or falls prone and is restrained beneath spectral stones until it breaks free with an action."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Three Hundred Stones","rules":"Maximum Technique: Three Hundred Stones · 7 CE · Once per long rest · Activating it costs an action (invented); expend all your Hands to bombard up to PB 15-ft squares within 120 ft: Dexterity save vs 1 Hand Die per 2 Hands expended, minimum 1 die (invented); the bombarded zones become difficult terrain."}],"e185":[{"level":1,"title":"Covetous Scale","rules":"The mark itself: one CE and a bonus action claims an eligible object, and Greed may be spent to blunt a hit, one Hoard Die per Greed, up to PB per round. Covetous Scale (bonus action, 1 CE): mark an eligible object as part of your Hoard. When you are hit, you may spend Greed to reduce the damage by one Hoard Die per Greed spent, up to PB per round."},{"level":3,"title":"Dragon's Claim","rules":"Theft has a scent. An unpermitted taker reveals its direction for an hour; her reaction carries her half her speed toward it, and her first hit each turn against the thief deals an extra Hoard Die. A creature that takes a Hoard Mark without your permission reveals its direction to you for 1 hour; as a reaction you may move up to half your speed toward it. Your first hit each turn against that thief deals one additional Hoard Die of damage (invented)."},{"level":6,"title":"Wyrm Shape","rules":"Wyrm Shape: Bonus action · 3 CE · 1 minute · Grow scales and claws: gain a climb speed, +1 AC, and +5 ft of reach · Action · 2 Greed: exhale a 30-ft cone (invented); each creature inside makes a Constitution save vs your CE DC, taking 3 Hoard Dice poison damage on failure and half on success (invented)."},{"level":11,"title":"Gold-Sick Immortality","rules":"Passive · Once per long rest · While near 3 or more Hoard Marks, when you are reduced to 0 HP: spend at least 3 Greed to remain at 1 HP and gain temp HP equal to 5 per Greed spent (invented)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Hall Beneath the Glittering Heath","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · When the barrier opens, every unattended object inside is catalogued · Domain Cycle begins at Claim and advances Claim → Covet → Reckon at initiative 20: Claim — choose up to PB unattended objects; they become Hoard Marks until the Domain ends; Covet — each chosen hostile carrying a Hoard Mark must drop it or become Dragon-Marked until the next initiative 20 (a creature protected from the sure-hit may make a Wisdom save to avoid the mark while keeping the object); Reckon — each Dragon-Marked hostile automatically takes 3 Hoard Dice necrotic (a protected creature makes a Constitution save, half on success), then all Dragon-Marks end and the cycle returns to Claim · Ordinary attacks still roll; Hoard objects remain stealable."}],"e186":[{"level":1,"title":"Restless Corpse","rules":"The mound's first manners: Restlessness spent for resistance to a hit's physical damage, or one Restlessness on a melee hit for a Grave Die of cold. When you are hit, you may spend Restlessness for resistance to that attack's physical damage. You may also spend 1 Restlessness on a melee hit to add +1 Grave Die of cold damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Mound-Dweller","rules":"Two CE and an action raise the fifteen-foot Grave Mound for a minute, difficult terrain for enemies, and movement inside it breeds Restlessness. Mound-Dweller (action, 2 CE): raise a 15-foot Grave Mound around your Anchor for 1 minute. It is difficult terrain for enemies, and movement inside it generates Restlessness."},{"level":6,"title":"Corpse-Swell","rules":"Corpse-Swell: Bonus action · 2 CE · 1 minute · Become Large if possible, advantage on Strength checks and saves, +5 ft reach · Targets you have grappled must pass a Charisma save vs your CE save DC (invented) to teleport."},{"level":11,"title":"Too Angry to Die","rules":"Passive · Once per long rest · When you drop to 0 HP inside your Mound: spend Restlessness equal to your PB (invented) + 4 CE to remain at 1 HP, stand up, and make one melee attack."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Barrow That Refuses the Dawn","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Your Grave Anchor becomes the center of a sealed barrow · Sure-hit: at initiative 20, each chosen hostile more than 15 ft from the Anchor is dragged 10 ft toward it and knocked prone (a protected creature instead makes a Strength save: success is neither moved nor knocked prone); gain 1 Restlessness per hostile actually moved, up to your PB · Teleportation cannot cross the barrier unless explicitly allowed · Ordinary attacks still roll."}],"e187":[{"level":1,"title":"Ride to the Fallen","rules":"The first rescue: one Deed and one CE carry her twenty feet to a wounded Deed-holder without provoking, softening the blow by a d8 plus her modifier. Ride to the Fallen (reaction, 1 CE): spend one of that creature's Deeds to move 20 feet toward it without provoking opportunity attacks, and reduce the triggering damage by one d8 + your CE modifier (invented: the die is a d8)."},{"level":3,"title":"Chosen Warrior","rules":"The empowering: two CE and one Deed name an ally Chosen for a minute, ten feet of speed and a Valor Die of d8 on one damage roll per turn. Chosen Warrior (bonus action, 2 CE): spend one Deed to empower one ally for 1 minute, +10 feet of speed and +1 Valor Die (a d8, invented) to one damage roll per turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Carry from the Field","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · When a creature within 30 ft drops to 0 HP: fly to it and carry it clear; it accrues no failed death saves from ordinary movement or the environment through its next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Einherjar's Second Breath","rules":"When a Chosen Warrior would drop to 0 HP: spend two of its Deeds + 3 CE — it stays at 1 HP, as a reaction moves up to half its speed, and gains temp HP equal to 2d8 + your CE modifier (invented) · Once per creature per long rest."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Hall Where the Worthy Rise","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Beneficial rule-Domain (no automatic damage): when it opens, every willing ally inside gains a temporary Deed (vanish when it ends) · At initiative 20, choose one willing creature inside with a Deed: it immediately moves up to half its speed without provoking, then makes one weapon attack, takes the Help action, or stabilizes a creature (never activates a Domain, Maximum, Extreme Magic, another extra-turn feature, or grants another action); spend one of its Deeds after it resolves · Hostiles receive no automatic damage or failure."}],"e188":[{"level":1,"title":"Breath of White","rules":"The exhale: one CE for a fifteen-foot cone of cold, two d8 scaling with level, and a failed Constitution save adds one Frost to the damage. Breath of White (action, 1 CE): exhale a 15-foot cone of cold; creatures make a Constitution save. On a failure it deals 2d8 cold damage (invented: a Frost Die is a d8) and adds +1 Frost; on a success it deals half damage and adds no Frost. The damage gains +1d8 at 5th, 11th, and 17th level (invented). Frostbite: a creature bearing Frost has its speed reduced by 5 feet per Frost it bears. The cold settles into the limbs long before it reaches the lungs — every flake of Frost is already doing its work."},{"level":3,"title":"Snowfield","rules":"The weather itself: two CE for a twenty-foot radius of snow for a minute, lightly obscured, difficult for enemies, and a hostile ending its turn there saves or gains Frost. Snowfield (action, 2 CE, Focus): create a 20-foot radius of snow for 1 minute. The area is lightly obscured and difficult terrain for enemies; a hostile ending its turn there makes a save or gains Frost."},{"level":6,"title":"Woman in the Storm","rules":"Passive · While in your Snowfield: bonus action teleport 20 ft between snow-obscured spaces; your next technique attack that turn has advantage."},{"level":11,"title":"Warmth Stolen Gently","rules":"Warmth Stolen Gently: Action · 3 CE · Target a Frostbound creature (Frost 3, invented) within 10 ft: Constitution save or 4d8 cold damage (invented); on failure, heal yourself or an ally for half the damage dealt."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Village Lost Beneath Snow","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Blizzard village: visibility beyond 30 ft heavily obscured · At initiative 20, each chosen hostile not adjacent to a meaningful heat source, substantial shelter, or another creature automatically gains 1 Frost (those precautions prevent the event entirely; a protected but exposed creature makes a Constitution save: success prevents the Frost) · Ordinary cold attacks and Snowfield saves still resolve normally."}],"e189":[{"level":1,"title":"Three Oni Masks","rules":"Three faces of the same performance, and the performer chooses the scene. I have watched sorcerers win battles in the moment they switched, not because the new mask was stronger, but because the enemy had finished studying the old one. Red for force, Blue for endurance, Black for terror: the mask is both the armor and the announcement. Three Oni Masks (bonus action, 1 CE, 1 minute): assume one mask. Red: your first melee hit after closing distance (you moved at least 10 feet toward the target before the hit, invented) deals +1d8 (invented: the die is a d8). Blue: reduce the first physical damage you take each round by your PB. Black: on a hit, you can prevent the target from moving closer until the end of your next turn on a failed Wisdom save (invented: duration)."},{"level":3,"title":"Kanabō Principle","rules":"Mark this: the mask promises force, and the Kanabō settles the promise, every weapon in his hand agrees to become the iron club, because the role of the oni was never subtlety. When the critic demands the ending, he obliges. Any melee weapon you wield becomes a magical iron club with a minimum versatile d10 damage die. Your critical hits push the target 10 feet or knock it prone."},{"level":6,"title":"Demon's Feast","rules":"Passive · When you score a takedown or succeed on a save vs a technique: gain 1 Revel (max PB) · Spend Revel for a free Mask switch once per turn, or add 1d8 (invented) to a Strength check or save."},{"level":11,"title":"Night Parade","rules":"Night Parade: Action · 3 CE · Summon three spectral oni silhouettes for 1 minute (appear in unoccupied spaces within 30 ft; stationary (invented); AC 15, 1 HP) · Once per turn originate your melee reach from one silhouette · Switching your Mask and gaining 1 Revel restores them."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Ō-Oni","rules":"Maximum Technique: Ō-Oni · Action (invented) · 7 CE · Once per long rest · 1 minute · Become Large, gain all three base Mask benefits, +10 ft reach, regain 1 Revel per turn · One Mask stays Dominant with doubled numeric benefit: Red +2d8, Blue reduces the first physical damage by 2×PB, Black forces the Wisdom save at disadvantage (invented)."}],"e190":[{"level":1,"title":"Earth-Spider Thread","rules":"The first tax of the hunt. Two anchors, one line between them, and suddenly the ground is no longer neutral, the hostile pays in footsteps or pays in blood when the thread snaps. Mark this: the thread is not a wall. It is a toll gate, and every toll gate teaches the prey which roads it no longer owns. Earth-Spider Thread (action, 1 CE): create two thread anchors within 30 feet. Threads last 1 minute, and you can maintain up to PB threads at once (invented). A hostile crossing a thread pays +10 feet of movement unless it succeeds on a Dexterity save; on a failed save you may use your reaction to snap the thread for 1d8 of slashing damage (invented: the die is a d8) and a 5-foot pull."},{"level":3,"title":"Ceiling Hunter","rules":"The spider's second truth: the battlefield has a roof, and it is his. I have watched the Tsuchigumo vanish upward and reappear twenty feet along his own web, untouchable, unhurried. The prey watches the floor; the predator owns the ceiling. That asymmetry is the whole plan. Ceiling Hunter: gain a climb speed equal to your speed and the ability to occupy ceilings. As a bonus action, travel 20 feet along your connected thread network without provoking opportunity attacks."},{"level":6,"title":"Loom Trap","rules":"Loom Trap: with 3 anchors and +2 CE, form a 15-ft triangular zone · The first hostile entering it or starting its turn inside: Dexterity save vs your CE save DC (invented) or restrained until it spends an action and succeeds on a Strength save · The trap has AC 13 and HP equal to 3× your level."},{"level":11,"title":"Buried Spider","rules":"Passive · Place anchors through earth or stone you touch, up to 10 ft deep · Once per turn when you hit a restrained target: consume an anchor to deal +2d8 (invented) and drag the target 10 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Castle Under Eightfold Silk","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Six indestructible Domain Anchors appear in legal spaces you choose · At initiative 20, choose any three Anchors: they define a triangular Law-Web until the next initiative 20 — each chosen hostile inside treats all movement as difficult terrain; the first time an unprotected hostile leaves the triangle, it is pulled to the triangle's center and restrained until the end of its current turn (a protected creature instead makes a Dexterity save when leaving: success avoids both) · No automatic damage; ordinary thread attacks still roll."}],"e191":[{"level":1,"title":"Fourfold Body","rules":"Four animals, one turn, one choice, and the choice may never repeat twice. Monkey's precision, tiger's fury, serpent's reach, tanuki's elusiveness: each a complete answer to a different question. I have watched the bearer answer four questions in four turns, and every answer was correct. You gain the four Aspects of the technique. Each turn you choose one active Aspect, Monkey, Tiger, Serpent, or Tanuki, and you cannot choose the same Aspect three turns consecutively. Monkey: skill and object precision. Tiger: +1d8 on your first melee hit (invented: the die is a d8). Serpent: one attack gains +10 feet of reach and a CE-based grapple. On a hit you may grapple the target using your CE ability modifier in place of Strength for the grapple check; the escape DC = your CE save DC (invented). Tanuki: +10 speed, and opportunity attacks against you have disadvantage."},{"level":3,"title":"Night Cry","rules":"The voice of the thing in the dark. Thirty feet of cone, a Wisdom to hold against it, and terror on a failed nerve, but mark this: the wail deepens when the Aspect has changed since last turn. The technique rewards the one who is already moving. Stillness has no voice. As an action for 2 CE, you loose the Night Cry in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a Wisdom save: on a failure it takes 2d8 of psychic damage (invented) and is frightened of you until the end of your next turn. If you changed Aspect since your last turn, the wail deals +1d8 of psychic damage (invented)."},{"level":6,"title":"Crossbred Transition","rules":"Passive · When you change Aspect: spend 1 CE to retain your previous Aspect through the current turn as well (max two Aspects active at once)."},{"level":11,"title":"Unclassifiable Beast","rules":"Reaction · Once per round · When targeted by an attack or effect: change Aspect immediately · If the new body meaningfully counters the attack (the GM decides), gain +2 AC or +2 to the relevant saving throw."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Chimera Beneath the Black Cloud","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action (invented) · 6 CE · 1 minute · Maintain two Aspects automatically; add a third Aspect for 1 CE per turn · Night Cry becomes a 60-ft cone; a creature failing its save by 5 or more is stunned until the start of your next turn."}],"e192":[{"level":1,"title":"Golden Pinions","rules":"The wings are the argument; the feathers are the receipts. Fly twenty feet and the technique drops one Pinion, already grown, finally released, to be spent on radiant or slashing judgment. Mark this: the sorcerer does not conjure ammunition. He molts it. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you grow golden wings for 10 minutes and gain a flying speed equal to your speed. Once per turn after you fly at least 20 feet, you gain 1 Pinion (maximum equal to your proficiency bonus). When you hit with an attack, you may spend 1 Pinion to deal +1d8 of radiant or slashing damage (invented: the die is a d8)."},{"level":3,"title":"Enemy of Venom","rules":"The rescuer's reflex. An ally failing against poison, grapple, restraint, the Garuda's reaction and one CE lends them a die, and if they stand, the feather returns. This is the whole technique in one exchange: someone else's freedom, paid for, and the wings grow stronger for it. When an ally makes a saving throw against poison, grapple, the restrained condition, or a serpent-like effect, you may use your reaction and spend 1 CE to add one d8 (invented) to their save. If the save succeeds, you gain 1 Pinion."},{"level":6,"title":"Wingbeat Deliverance","rules":"Wingbeat Deliverance: Action · 2 CE · Spend 1 Pinion per creature (invented) to move up to PB creatures within 60 ft (invented) 10 ft each · Willing targets move safely; hostile targets make a Strength save · One target may be moved twice (20 ft total for 2 Pinions, invented)."},{"level":11,"title":"Sunward Ascent","rules":"Passive · If you begin your turn airborne with open overhead space: gain 1 Pinion · Spend 3 Pinions to end the poisoned or restrained condition on yourself or a creature you touch (unless a superior Domain law prevents it)."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Wings That Eclipse the Serpent","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action (invented) · 7 CE · 1 minute · Fly speed 80 with hover; resistance to poison and acid damage · The first creature you move with Wingbeat Deliverance each turn is moved free; the first time you hit a creature that is actively poisoning or restraining another creature, the hit deals +3d8 radiant (invented)."}],"e193":[{"level":1,"title":"Swallow the Light","rules":"The first refusal. One CE buys a fifteen-foot radius of supernatural dimness, mundane flames inside it die, and at Depth 2 the dimness becomes true darkness. Mark this: the Serpent does not begin by striking the enemy. It begins by striking the enemy's visibility. As an action for 1 CE, you create a 15-foot radius of supernatural dimness centered within 60 feet for 1 round; mundane flames inside it are extinguished. At Night Depth 2 or higher, the area becomes darkness instead."},{"level":3,"title":"Coil of Night","rules":"The dark reaches out and takes hold. Twenty feet of reach, necrotic damage, the grapple, and the grappled creature's own light radius halves, as if the night were drinking it. This is the technique's close argument: come into the dark, and the dark keeps you. Make a technique melee attack (2 CE) with 20-foot reach: on a hit, it deals 2d8 of necrotic damage (invented: a Night Die is a d8) plus your CE modifier, and the target is grappled. The target may use its action to escape, DC = your CE save DC (invented). A grappled creature's emitted light radius is halved."},{"level":6,"title":"Solar Struggle","rules":"Solar Struggle: when at Night Depth 3, at initiative 20 you may spend 2 CE to unleash a 30-ft Eclipse Pulse — each creature in it makes a Constitution save: failure takes 2 dice of necrotic damage (invented) and cannot regain HP until your next turn · Your Night Depth then resets to 1."},{"level":11,"title":"Uncreated Darkness","rules":"Passive · At Night Depth 3: resistance to radiant damage, but each radiant hit still reduces your Night Depth by 1 · When a radiant hit knocks you from Depth 3 to Depth 2: Reaction — move up to half your speed."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Twelve Gates Before Sunrise","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Begins at Gate 1; at initiative 20 advance Gates 1→2→3→1 and increase Night Depth by 1 (max 3) · At Gate 3, Eclipse Pulse is the sure-hit: each chosen hostile takes 2d8 necrotic (invented) and cannot regain HP until the next initiative 20, then Night Depth becomes 1 (a protected creature makes a Constitution save: half damage, no healing lock) · Three Solar Braziers appear: a creature adjacent may use an action and a meaningful radiant/CE effect to light one; each lit Brazier reduces the next Pulse by 1 Night Die, all three lit suppress the healing lock; all Braziers extinguish after the Pulse · Clash 1,000 (Tier V); Technique Burnout 3 rounds."}],"e194":[{"level":1,"title":"Lioness Heat","rules":"The engine and the wound, in one track. Consecutive damaging turns raise Heat 0 to 5: speed at 1–2, fire on the first hit at 3, doubled at 5: but at 4+ the bearer takes unavoidable damage each turn, coolable by bonus action. This is the technique's whole education: the fire feeds you until it feeds on you. Learn the difference between 3 and 4, or the lesson is written in your own skin. You track Heat from 0 to 5, built by consecutive damaging turns: gain 1 Heat at the end of each of your turns in which you dealt damage; if you end a turn without dealing damage, Heat resets to 0 (invented). At Heat 1–2 you gain +5 speed. At Heat 3 or higher, your first hit each turn deals +1d8 of fire damage (invented: the die is a d8); at Heat 5 this becomes +2d8 (invented). At Heat 4 or higher you take unavoidable damage equal to your proficiency bonus at the end of each of your turns; as a bonus action you may lower your Heat by 1."},{"level":3,"title":"Breath of Pestilence","rules":"The plague, exhaled. Fifteen-foot cone, Constitution against it, fire or necrotic by choice, and the failed suffer healing reduced by PB. Mark this: the Fever's second weapon is not the flame but the denial. A wound that cannot be mended is worth two that can. As an action for 2 CE, you exhale a 15-foot cone of pestilence. Each creature in the cone makes a Constitution save, taking 2d8 of fire or necrotic damage (invented; your choice) on a failure. A creature that fails also has its healing reduced by your proficiency bonus until the end of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Blood-Red Draught","rules":"Blood-Red Draught: Action (or bonus action with a prepared red drink) · 1 CE · Once per short rest · Drink to reduce your Heat by 3, regain 1d8 HP (invented) + your CE modifier, and end the frightened condition on yourself."},{"level":11,"title":"Eye of Ra","rules":"Passive · While at Heat 5: attacks ignore fire resistance · Whenever you take your Heat self-damage, each enemy within 10 ft makes a Dexterity save or takes 1 die of fire damage."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Lady of Slaughter, Lady of Healing","rules":"Maximum Technique · Action (invented) · 7 CE · Lasts 3 rounds · Choose Slaughter or Mercy: Slaughter locks Heat at 5 and doubles your Heat self-damage; your first two hits each turn deal one additional die of fire (invented) · Mercy locks Heat at 0 and lets you use your action to heal 3d8 + your CE modifier (invented) and cleanse poison and fear — not Reverse Cursed Technique; cannot exceed the target's normal maximum healing from technique sources per campaign injury rules."}],"e195":[{"level":1,"title":"Black Steed","rules":"The journey begins with the mount. One CE, ten minutes, fifty speed, and Gallop accumulates at the end of every straight twenty-foot approach, spendable on necrotic strikes after the charge. Mark this: the steed is not transport. It is the first witness that the trip is happening. As a bonus action for 1 CE, you manifest a black steed for 10 minutes, gaining a speed of 50. Gain 1 Gallop at the end of any turn in which you moved at least 20 feet in a straight line while your steed is manifested, maximum PB (invented). After a 20-foot straight approach, you may spend 1 Gallop to add 1d8 of necrotic damage (invented: the die is a d8) to a melee hit."},{"level":3,"title":"Head Held High","rules":"The sight leaves the body. Detach the spectral Head within thirty feet and see and hear from it, AC 15, twice your level in hit points, a die of psychic pain if it is destroyed. The dullahan's oldest trick: the rider keeps his eyes where the road goes, not where his body is. As a bonus action you detach your spectral Head, placing it within 30 feet; your sight and hearing originate from the Head. The Head has AC 15 and hit points equal to twice your level; if it is destroyed, it returns to you and you take 1d8 of psychic damage (invented)."},{"level":6,"title":"Name on the Road","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Choose a creature your Head can see: Wisdom save; on failure it becomes your Road's End for 1 minute — you know its direction within 1 mile, and it cannot hide from your Head except behind total cover or anti-divination effects."},{"level":11,"title":"Whip of the Spine","rules":"Technique melee attack (2 CE) · 15-ft reach · On hit: 3d8 necrotic (invented) · On a failed Constitution save: loses reactions and speed −15 until the end of your next turn (invented) · If the target is your Road's End, pull it 15 ft toward you instead."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: The Road With No Turning","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · A moonless road loops through the barrier · At initiative 20, each chosen hostile must choose a disclosed route-law: Advance (move 15 ft in a legal direction without provoking) or Hear the Hooves (remain in place, gain 1 Doom) · At 3 Doom it becomes your Road's End until the Domain ends and its Doom resets to 0 · Rule-based: the choice itself is the law, not automatic damage · A protected creature may ignore the Doom gain but still forfeits Advance · Ordinary attacks still roll."}],"e196":[{"level":1,"title":"Warning Keen","rules":"The technique's whole confession in one feature. Ally at 0 HP within sixty feet: the keen fires, no action, no reaction, no CE, no choice, the falling ally's first death save succeeds, and hostiles within thirty feet must hold against fear. Once per short or long rest. It cannot be saved for later. Grief, here, is not a resource. It is a reflex. The Keen (automatic): whenever an ally you can see within 60 feet drops to 0 HP, the keen fires immediately, no action, no reaction, no CE, and no choice. You cannot hold it back, and it cannot be saved for later. The falling ally automatically succeeds on its first death saving throw (death heard it coming). Each hostile creature within 30 feet of you that can hear must succeed on a Wisdom save against your technique DC or be frightened of you until the end of your next turn. Once the keen fires, it cannot fire again until you finish a short or long rest."},{"level":3,"title":"Piercing Wail","rules":"The wail, aimed. Thirty-foot cone, 2d8 thunder, deafened and disadvantaged on failure, and the dying roll their save at disadvantage, because the technique is crueler around the dying. This is the answer to a quiet battlefield: the keen is a warning, but the wail is a weapon, and the bearer carries both. Action, 2 CE: each creature in a 30-foot cone makes a Constitution save, 2d8 thunder damage (invented: the die is a d8) on failure, half on success; a creature that fails is deafened and has disadvantage on its next attack. A creature currently at 0 HP has disadvantage on this save, the wail is crueler around the dying. This is the technique’s answer to a quiet battlefield: the wail is a weapon even when no one is falling."},{"level":6,"title":"Mourning Veil","rules":"Mourning Veil: Action · 2 CE · Focus · 20-ft aura for 1 minute · Allies inside have advantage on death saves · When an ally inside succeeds on a death save: Reaction — wail: one hostile within 30 ft that can hear makes a Wisdom save vs your technique DC or takes 1 die thunder damage and is deafened until the end of its next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"The Cry Arrives First","rules":"Passive · When initiative is rolled, you hear every coming death: you cannot be surprised by any visible creature below half HP · The keen sharpens: when it fires, the falling ally regains 1 HP instead of merely succeeding on the death save."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: House That Heard the Cry","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Omen-support Domain (no automatic damage): whenever any ally inside drops to 0 HP, the keen fires immediately even if it has not recharged, and its witness range extends across the whole Domain · When it forms, choose one creature inside to receive Forewarning: +2 AC and +2 to saving throws (disadvantage on attacks against you; not mind control) · An unwilling protected creature may make a Wisdom save to reject Forewarning entirely."}],"e197":[{"level":1,"title":"Blighted Breath","rules":"The seed, exhaled. Fifteen-foot cone, Constitution against it: failure plants 1 Wither and grows a five-foot patch beneath the victim for a minute. The patch is the technique's real argument, hostiles starting their turns inside it test again or wither further. One breath, and the ground has joined the plague. As an action for 1 CE, you exhale a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a Constitution save vs your technique DC; on a failure it gains 1 Wither and a 5-foot Blight patch grows beneath it for 1 minute; on a success, nothing happens. Blight patches are 5-foot, 1-minute terrain: a hostile that starts its turn standing in Blight makes a Constitution save, failure: it gains 1 Wither. Wither (formal definition): each Wither reduces all HP the creature regains by your PB. At 3 Wither, magical healing on the creature requires a Constitution save, failure halves it again after the Wither reduction. A creature loses 1 Wither at the end of each turn it spends entirely outside Blight. Contact with fresh running water removes all Wither immediately."},{"level":3,"title":"Horse-and-Rider Flesh","rules":"The plague takes a body. Two CE, one minute, Large: +20 speed, advantage against being knocked prone, and the bulk that cannot squeeze through ten-foot gaps. Mark this: the Blight is faster on the horse. Plagues have always traveled. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you assume a Large mounted silhouette for 1 minute: your speed increases by 20, you have advantage on ability checks and saving throws against being knocked prone (invented), and you cannot squeeze through spaces narrower than 10 feet without ending the form."},{"level":6,"title":"Withering Crop","rules":"Passive · Adjacent Blight patches merge into larger ones · Bloom of Rot: Bonus action · 1 CE · Detonate one Blight patch within 60 ft: each hostile standing in it makes a Constitution save; failure gains 1 Wither and is poisoned until the end of your next turn (success: no effect); the patch withers away after blooming."},{"level":11,"title":"Aversion to Fresh Water","rules":"Binding Vow · Your transformed form cannot willingly cross more than 5 ft of fresh running water without ending the transformation · In exchange: resistance to non-radiant technique damage while the attacker stands in your Blight."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Shore Where Nothing Grows","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · On opening, place three fresh-running-water streams across the battlefield (neutral, unremovable by you; Blight cannot cross them) · Bloom of Rot costs no action inside the Domain, once per round · At initiative 20, each chosen hostile standing in Blight automatically gains 1 Wither (a protected creature makes a Constitution save and avoids the Wither on success) · Any creature touching a stream at initiative 20 removes 1 Wither instead and cannot gain Wither from that event · Your Binding-Vow water weakness persists inside the Domain."}],"e198":[{"level":1,"title":"Bat House Sense","rules":"The senses, rebuilt. Blindsight twenty feet; swap as a bonus action to a node, the sound carries you; first attack each turn from unseen has advantage. This is the technique's foundation, and it is not an attack. It is an address book, and the bearer lives at every address. Blindsight 20 ft. Swap: as a bonus action, teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of one of your Echo nodes, the sound carries you. From the Sound: the first attack you make each turn from a position where the target cannot see you has advantage."},{"level":3,"title":"Razor Swoop","rules":"The strike, delivered by the architecture. Move up to speed in a straight line without provoking, one technique melee attack, no reactions on a hit, with advantage if the swoop began within five feet of a node. The bat strikes from its own sound. Mark this: the swoop's speed is not the weapon. The starting point is. Action, 2 CE: move up to your speed in a straight line without provoking opportunity attacks, then make one technique melee attack (2 + your CE modifier slashing); on a hit, the target cannot take reactions until the start of your next turn. If you began the swoop within 5 feet of an Echo node, the attack has advantage, the bat strikes from its own sound."},{"level":6,"title":"Ceiling of Wings","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Focus · 20-ft swarm zone for 1 minute · Dim light becomes darkness for your enemies inside; you know the position of every moving creature inside; place Echo nodes inside the zone without spending actions (still 1 CE each)."},{"level":11,"title":"Neck-Seeking Blade","rules":"Passive · When your Razor Swoop hits a target below one-quarter HP: swap with an Echo node within 30 ft of the target as part of the attack (no action); the strike comes from the sound itself · On a hit, the target makes a Constitution save; on failure the hit becomes critical · Normal injury thresholds; never automatic decapitation above 0 HP."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: House Where Dawn Was Tested","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · The interior becomes a black cave · When it forms, place up to PB Echo nodes anywhere inside at no cost · Swapping between nodes costs no action (once per round); every hostile inside in total darkness that moves more than 5 ft reveals its current position to you until the end of its turn · Rule-Domain, no automatic damage; anti-domain protection hides a protected creature's movement from the nodes but does not destroy them."}],"e199":[{"level":1,"title":"Plumed Road","rules":"The inn opens. Action, 1 CE: a thirty-by-five-foot Wind Road, both endpoints within sixty feet, one minute, up to three maintained. Allies with the direction gain speed; enemies against it pay double; full traversal earns a Plume. Mark this: the road does not choose who walks it. It only charges. As an action for 1 CE, you draw a 30-foot by 5-foot Wind Road (both endpoints within 60 feet of you) that lasts 1 minute. Maintain up to 3 roads. Allies moving with the Road's direction gain +10 speed; enemies moving against it pay double movement. Fully traversing a Road generates 1 Plume, once per turn; hold up to PB Plumes; unspent Plumes fade after 1 minute. · Ride the Wind: Bonus action, spend 1 Plume: one willing creature within 60 feet gains +20 feet speed until the end of its turn, usable only for movement along a Wind Road's direction."},{"level":3,"title":"Serpent of the Updraft","rules":"The host takes to the sky. Bonus action, 2 CE: forty-foot fly speed for a minute, ending each turn within ten feet of a Road or descending safely twenty. The serpent's view of its own roads is the whole point, the innkeeper should see the whole inn. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you gain a 40-foot fly speed for 1 minute; end each turn within 10 feet of a Wind Road or descend safely 20 feet."},{"level":6,"title":"Breath of Civilization","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Along one Wind Road: each ally may use its reaction to move 10 ft, and each hostile makes a Dexterity save vs your Technique DC or is pushed a fixed 15 ft along the Road's direction · Allies moved this way gain +PB to their next ability check before the end of your next turn."},{"level":11,"title":"Morning-Star Crossing","rules":"Passive · Wind Road intersections become Crossroads · Once per turn, a willing creature entering a Crossroad may teleport to another Crossroad within a fixed 60 ft, spending 10 ft of movement · Teleports cannot cross Domain barriers."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: City Beneath the Feathered Sky","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · On opening, six Wind Roads appear free of charge (Domain Roads do not count against your normal maximum of 3) · At initiative 20, rotate every Domain Road's direction, then choose one disclosed law until the next event — Ascent: a willing creature that moves at least 10 ft with a Road gains a 20-ft fly speed until the end of that movement; Descent: each chosen hostile that moved against a Road since the previous initiative 20 is knocked prone (a protected creature makes a Strength save to remain standing); Exchange: each willing creature currently at a Crossroad may move 15 ft without provoking · The Domain does not make your attacks automatic."}],"e200":[{"level":1,"title":"Guardian Threshold","rules":"The line is drawn. Action, 1 CE: designate a Threshold, door, bridge, hallway line, paired markers, for ten minutes, up to PB at once. First hostile crossing each turn generates Vigilance and forces the save; failure stops the crosser cold. Mark this: the technique's first act is not defense. It is declaration. The line exists now. Cross it and be counted. As an action for 1 CE, you designate a Threshold (a door, bridge, hallway line, or paired markers) for 10 minutes. You can maintain up to PB Thresholds at once (invented). The first hostile crossing each turn generates Vigilance (maximum PB, invented) and forces a Wisdom save; on a failure the creature's speed becomes 0 immediately after crossing. Unspent Vigilance vanishes when no Threshold is active or when you finish a long rest (invented)."},{"level":3,"title":"Bull-Lion Intercession","rules":"The guardian steps into the blow's path. When an ally within thirty feet is hit: reaction, 1 Vigilance, swap positions, the ally drawn safe, the bearer taking the hit in full with the stone body; resistance if within ten feet of a Threshold. The gate steadies its keeper. This is the technique's heart: the line does not merely stop enemies. It shelters friends. When an ally within 30 feet is hit by an attack, you may use your reaction and spend 1 Vigilance to interpose: you and the ally swap positions (the ally is drawn into the space you left; willing allies only). You become the attack’s target instead and take the hit in full with your stone body. If you are within 10 feet of one of your Thresholds when you intercept, the gate steadies you, you have resistance to the triggering attack’s damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Five-Legged Perspective","rules":"Passive · See and hear 10 ft around every Threshold · Bonus action · 2 CE · Teleport from one Threshold to another within 120 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Name on the Gate","rules":"Passive · Mark a number of creatures (or a category) equal to your PB as Welcome · Welcome creatures gain +10 speed when crossing your Thresholds · Other creatures that fail their Threshold save also take 2d8 force (invented: the die is a d8), once per turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Gate No Enemy Crosses Uncounted","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 60-ft radius centered on you · up to 1 minute · Technique Focus · Create four indestructible Domain Thresholds · At initiative 20, each chosen hostile that crossed any Threshold since the previous initiative 20 receives 1 Census Mark (a protected creature may make a Wisdom save to avoid that mark) · Spend any number of Census Marks, choosing per mark: push that creature 10 ft toward the Threshold it crossed; one ally gains +2 AC against that creature until the next initiative 20; or deal 1d8 force (invented: a Ward Die is a d8), maximum 3 damage marks per creature per event · Unspent Census Marks vanish after the event · Ordinary attacks still roll."}],"e201":[{"level":1,"title":"First Three Terrors","rules":"Passive · One Terror Face active at a time, 15-ft aura · Bonus action to switch Faces · Glare: Wis save or approach ends; Roar: Wis save or next attack −PB damage; Scent: unseen benefits defeated in aura."},{"level":3,"title":"Cedar Forest","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Three 10-ft cedar zones within 60 ft · 1 minute · Half cover; active Terror Face aura radiates from each zone within 60 ft of you."},{"level":6,"title":"Fourth & Fifth Terrors","rules":"Passive · Blaze: hostile ending its turn in aura, Wis save or frightened until end of its next turn · Maze: aura is difficult terrain, no Dash."},{"level":11,"title":"Sixth & Seventh Terrors","rules":"Passive · Majesty: allies have advantage on saves vs frightened · Doom: bloodied creatures entering aura, Wis save or frightened · When a cedar zone is destroyed, switch Face once per round with no action."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Cedar Forest Before the Axe","rules":"Full-turn action · 20 CE · Enclosed 90-ft radius, up to 1 min · Place seven 20-ft Terror zones (one per Face), non-overlapping; initiative-20 event moves each up to 10 ft; a chosen newly-covered hostile resolves its Face (max two per event); unprotected targets take the failed-save result automatically."}],"e202":[{"level":1,"title":"Tail Volley","rules":"Attack (replaces one attack) · 1 Spine · Ranged technique attack, 80/160 · 1 + CE modifier piercing; quill embeds (max 3 per creature); Barbed: −10 speed while quilled, or Heavy: push 5 ft · Embedded quills: −5 speed each; tear free costs an action · Rattle the Barbs: bonus action, 1/turn, no CE; each quilled creature Con save vs technique DC or speed 0 until end of its next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Lion's Maw","rules":"Melee technique attack · No Spine · 2 + CE modifier piercing · Advantage if target was quilled since your last turn; on hit recover 1 Spine · Worry: forgo recovery; target holding embedded quills Con save or frightened until end of your next turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Three-Quill Load","rules":"Passive · Unlock 2-Spine quill payloads · Venom: Con save or poisoned until end of your next turn (no damage); Screamer: no reactions until start of your next turn; Tether: movement anchored within 15 ft of impact point until an action tears free (removes embedded quills)."},{"level":11,"title":"Predator's Geometry","rules":"Once per turn · Ricochet a quill off a hard surface to ignore cover (two traced segments within range) · Missed ricochet's Spine embeds in the surface and can be recovered."},{"level":18,"title":"Maximum: Sky Black With Quills","rules":"Action · 6 CE, 1/long rest · Consume 6–10 Spines · All creatures in 30-ft radius: Dex save; failure: 3 quills embed + no reactions until end of your next turn; success: 1 quill embeds · Place PB embedded-quill hazards in unoccupied 5-ft spaces within 30 ft, lasting 1 minute."}],"e243":[{"level":0,"title":"Heroic Transformation","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Choose a loaded, subjugated form · Transform for up to 10 min; reverting is free on your turn."},{"level":0,"title":"No free healing or second sheet","rules":"Passive · HP, CE, conditions, and Technique Focus persist through every change — no second health bar, no healing on transform."},{"level":0,"title":"Genome Aptitude","rules":"Passive · Form Primary floors at 16 + PB (max 22), Secondary at 14 + PB (max 20) · Your CE modifier, max CE, attack, and save DC never change."},{"level":0,"title":"Alien AC","rules":"Passive · Use the form's printed AC or a compatible unarmored calculation; worn armor merges, no shield."},{"level":0,"title":"Your class still matters","rules":"Passive · Keep PB, proficiencies, feats, and compatible class features · Natural attacks are cursed weapon attacks and work with Extra Attack."},{"level":0,"title":"Attacks, checks, saves, and Black Flash","rules":"Passive · All offensive math uses your CE attack and save DC · Rolled attacks can Black Flash; set hazards and tremors cannot."},{"level":0,"title":"One concentration economy","rules":"Passive · Transforming costs no Technique Focus, but only one Focus-marked alien ability may run at a time · Concentration save: DC 10 or half damage taken, whichever is higher."}],"e244":[{"level":0,"title":"Rune Save DC","rules":"Passive · Every rune saving throw uses your normal cursed-energy save DC (8 + PB + CE modifier)."},{"level":0,"title":"Rune Attack","rules":"Passive · Any rune CE attack uses your normal cursed-energy attack modifier (PB + CE modifier)."},{"level":0,"title":"Inscription","rules":"Action · Inscribe a rune on a target within 5 ft (30 ft at level 11), unless the rune says otherwise."},{"level":0,"title":"Persistent Rune Limit","rules":"Passive · Maintain persistent runes up to your PB (PB + CE modifier at level 11); immediate effects don't count."}],"e246":[{"level":1,"title":"Comedy","rules":"Action · 1 CE · Activate for 1 minute, concentration · Reaction · 1 CE: when damaged, take no damage · Proficiency in Performance (Expertise at 11th)."},{"level":3,"title":"Commit to the Bit","rules":"Active-technique gags · Blasting Off: on a melee hit, 1 CE; hurl target up to 60 ft away, prone (scales at 6th/11th/18th) · Props: bonus action, 2 CE; conjure CE-modifier items in a 5-ft cube, last 1 minute (scales) · Powerful Punchline: action, 3 CE; 30-ft sphere within 80 ft / 60-ft line / 30-ft cone; Str, Dex, or Con save; PB + CE modifier d8s bludgeoning, piercing, slashing, or psychic + rider; cannot kill (drops to 1 HP)."},{"level":6,"title":"Comedic Foil","rules":"Passive (while technique active) · Creature starting its turn within 300 ft: CE save or cannot use interfering cursed techniques until its next turn · You may bar creatures from initiative and strip CE-sensing within 300 ft · Blasting Off 90 ft; Props cubes 10 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Peak Comedy","rules":"Action · 10 CE · Comedy at maximum for 1 minute · Once per turn free Gag; free damage negation CE-modifier times per round; double Punchline ranges; 2 CE for +PB damage dice · Action: scene-change teleport of creatures within 100 ft into a cutaway (Wis save vs CE DC resists); targets in the cutaway must fit attacks to the gag · Blasting Off 120 ft; Props 15-ft cubes."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Stand Up Comedy","rules":"Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius, up to 1 min, 800 clash (Tier IV) · Initiative-20: force a cutaway · Creatures acting against the gag take 8d8 psychic (audience boos), once per round. · While within your domain · Blasting Off 200 ft; Props 20-ft cubes; Peak Comedy props at 3× CE modifier · Full Turn Action (Action + Bonus Action + Movement): Charisma (Persuasion) joke; creatures in the domain may roll Wisdom (Insight) to counter; those who don't roll or roll lower take 8d8 psychic."}],"e247":[{"level":1,"title":"Seance","rules":"Full Turn Action · 2 CE (Physical or Soul), 4 CE (both) · Self or willing creature within 15 ft; dead humanoid of CR/level ≤ your level + 1 · Consume a body fragment of the dead · Maintain: 1 CE at the start of the target's turns; no alternate energy sources · Lose access to your Innate Technique features. · Seance: Physical Information · Gain the deceased's appearance, racial traits, features, proficiencies, and Str/Dex/Con scores · Temporary HP equal to PB. · Seance: Soul Information · Gain all memories + one Cursed/Innate Technique feature of the dead · At the start of the target's turns: Cha save (DC 8 + PB + Cha) or the dead takes control until CE runs out."},{"level":3,"title":"Blessing of the Grateful Dead","rules":"Passive (3rd) · Physical: temp HP = your level + PB · Soul: two technique features of your choice; keep your own Innate Technique · Cannot use features from different techniques simultaneously."},{"level":6,"title":"Ritual of Resurrection","rules":"Full Turn Action (Action + Bonus Action + Movement) each turn for 1 minute · Concentration · Then self or willing creature within 30 ft transforms into a dead humanoid of CR/level ≤ your level + PB · Lose concentration: restart."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Black Seance","rules":"On completing Ritual of Resurrection · +5 CE · Physical Overload: gain the dead's hit points as temp HP, or Soul Overload: all of the dead's Cursed/Innate features (no Domain Expansion; minimum CE costs only) · Cannot use both techniques' features at once."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Seance Parlor","rules":"Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius, up to 1 min, 500 clash (Tier III) · Initiative-20: extend Seance to a willing creature (hold, not consume, the body part) · No CE maintenance; possession saves auto-succeed; all channeled features gain the sure-hit · Seances end when the domain ends."}],"e248":[{"level":1,"title":"Rotten Blood · Rot Techniques","rules":"Passive · Resistance to poison and acid; advantage on saves vs poisoned · Below max HP: unarmed/melee attacks deal +1d8 acid once per turn (2d8 at 3rd, 3d8 at 6th, 4d8 at 11th) · Blood Bag: 1/long rest, $100 + up to PB HP; substitutes HP costs for Rot features; lasts 5 days; carry up to Con modifier. · Rot Techniques (each costs CE + HP) · Blood Spit: action, 1 CE + 2 HP; 15 ft, Con save or 2d6 acid + blinded until end of their turn · Rot Burst: 1/turn on a melee hit, 1 CE + 1 HP; +2d8 acid · Rotten Blood Beam: action, 3 CE + 4 HP; ranged attack, 30 ft; 2d8 piercing + 2d10 acid; Con save or −10 speed until end of your next turn · Corrosive Wave: action, 3 CE + 5 HP; 15-ft cone; Con save or 5d8 acid (half) · Blood Shield: reaction; spend CE (up to modifier) + twice that in HP; 10 shield HP per CE; melee attacker reduced to 0: Con save or 2d8 acid · Homing Blood Missile: action, 4 CE + 5 HP; 60 ft; on hit 5d10 + CE modifier acid; bonus action or reaction to reroll the attack · Blood Soak: bonus action, 3 CE + 3 HP; 1 minute; +10 speed; unarmed +2d6 + CE modifier acid · Crimson Spear: action, 2 CE + 3 HP; ranged attack 30/90; 1d6 piercing + 2d10 + CE modifier acid · Crimson Rain: action, 2 CE + 3 HP; point within 60 ft, 15-ft radius; Dex save, 1d10 piercing + 2d10 acid (half)."},{"level":3,"title":"Decay","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Infect all creatures damaged by your technique in the last minute, 1 minute · At the start of your turns they take your Rotten Blood dice; 3 CE to extend, free action to end · 6th: also poisoned; max HP reduced by damage dealt (restored on long rest)."},{"level":6,"title":"Scarlet Rot · Rot Techniques","rules":"Passive (6th) · Technique ignores acid resistance · Failed saves vs your technique: poisoned 1 minute (Con save ends at end of their turn) · Immune to poison, acid damage, and the poisoned condition · 18th: treats acid immunity as resistance."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Wing King · Rot Techniques","rules":"Bonus action · 8 CE · 1 minute · Movement quadrupled; fly speed = half of that; advantage on Dex saves · Replace an attack with a Rot Technique; free-action blood lines: three ranged attacks at 60 ft, each 4d10 + CE modifier acid or necrotic · Cannot use Decay."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Mind Palace of Corrupted Ego","rules":"Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius, up to 1 min, 800 clash (Tier IV) · All creatures in the domain suffer Decay; extra Decay damage at initiative 20 · Your Rot Techniques' HP costs drawn from willing creatures in the domain · 18th: treats acid immunity as resistance."}],"e249":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Corpse Creation","rules":"Downtime (long rest) · Start with 2 Tiny or 1 Small completed corpse · Cores up to Small per long rest (Medium 3rd, Large 6th, Huge 11th, Gargantuan 18th). · Downtime · Craft corpses up to Small (Medium 3rd, Large 6th, Huge 11th, Gargantuan 18th)."},{"level":3,"title":"Corpse Tactics","rules":"Bonus action (as part of command) · One tactic, lasts until the start of your next turn · Cooperative: advantage on one attack or save · Offensive: +1 damage die on a hit · Defensive: Dodge as a bonus action · Guerilla: Disengage as a bonus action · Mobility: Dash as a bonus action."},{"level":6,"title":"Cursed Corpse Mutation","rules":"Passive (6th) · On completing a corpse, roll d20; on a 20 it gains a random mutation. · Mutation table (d12) · 1 +20 ft speed · 2 30-ft climb or swim · 3 proficiency in 2 skills or 1 save · 4 +3 AC · 5 weapon use · 6 +2x level max HP · 7 core +30 CE · 8 Basic CE Manipulation · 9 +4 to an Ability and max · 10 Autonomy (no commands, sentient) · 11 +1d4 extra cores · 12 regain 1 CE/hour."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Prized Creation","rules":"Downtime · One Favorite corpse: +4 to two Ability scores and their maximums; damage dice up one tier; 3 chosen mutations (no repeats)."},{"level":18,"title":"Perfect Creations","rules":"Passive (18th) · Bonus action: command all corpses regardless of numbers or distance · Corpses function 1 week after CE runs out."}],"e250":[{"level":1,"title":"Blood Constructs · Blood Techniques","rules":"He draws blood and it holds shape, walls, tools, cages, spun from the red river. The constructs are crude but honest: semi-solid will, given form. Mark the economy: each is bought with coin from his own veins, or from a bagged store. A wise bearer banks his blood the way a state banks grain against famine. Starting at 1st level, you have been blessed with the Innate Technique of the Kamo clan, making you begin with the most basic technique, the blood constructs. You can pull blood from an available source to create a semi-solid construct. As an action for 1 CE and 1 HP, you can create a small construct smaller than a 5ft by 5ft space. For every 5 ft the price increases by 1 CE and HP. You can ignore the HP cost if you have an alternate source of blood. These constructs have HP equal to your level times CE spent. Once as part of a long rest, you can spend $100 and hit points up to your proficiency bonus to fill a Blood Bag with your own blood. This Blood Bag counts as a source of hit points for your Blood Manipulation features. A Blood Bag lasts 5 days outside of refrigeration before it goes bad. You can have a number of Blood Bags equal to your Constitution modifier at once. Starting at 1st level, you can harness your blood in a manner fit for battle. When you use a Blood Manipulation feature, you can ignore the HP cost if you have an alternate source of blood. You gain three of following techniques and gain an additional two at 6th and 11th level. · Crimson Binding. A net of red, thrown like a fisherman's cast. If it holds, the catch does not leave, strength may tear free, but the attempt costs the victim his motion. The patient weapon: it does not wound, it keeps. As an action for 1 CE and 1 HP, you unleash a red blood net, forcing a target Large or smaller within 30ft to make a Strength saving throw or be restrained. They can repeat the save at the start of their turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Flowing Red Scale","rules":"At 3rd level, this technique can increase the user's body temperature, pulse rate, and the number of red blood cells to give themselves greatly increased energy and physical capabilities. You can spend 3 Cursed Energy as a bonus action to gain the following benefits for 1 minute: Your speed is doubled. You will gain a +2 bonus to your AC. You gain advantage on Dexterity saving throws and Strength checks. You will gain an additional action on each of your turns. That action can be used only to take the Attack (one weapon attack only), Dash, Disengage, Hide, or Use an Object action."},{"level":6,"title":"Convergence","rules":"At 6th level, you compress and condense blood to its absolute limit. Before you use a blood manipulation technique with a casting time of one action, you can spend your bonus action, reaction and movement to enhance the technique's potency, gaining the following benefits: You deal additional damage die equal to your proficiency bonus. Your damage die increases by 1 level(d10->d12->2d8). The range increases by 30 feet. If you spend an additional turn using your action, bonus action, reaction and movement to charge up Convergence before using your technique, you gain these benefits an additional time and gain advantage on the first technique attack roll or can force creatures to make their first saving throw against your technique at disadvantage. Certain techniques may have additional or different bonuses if used with Convergence that are listed with each technique."},{"level":11,"title":"Piercing Blood","rules":"Beginning at 11th level, you can compress your blood into a deadly supersonic beam. As an action for 8 CE and 5 HP, you unleash a 100ft line of blood. Creatures in range must make a Dexterity save taking 10d8 piercing on a failure. If used with Convergence, you can continue shooting the beam for an additional round. Any creature that enters the lingering Piercing Blood must make the saving throw. As an action you can swing the line, making it into a 130 feet cone forcing an additional Dexterity save and the technique ends."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Bloodbath","rules":"The Domain of the blood heir: sixty feet wherein every heart is a traitor. At each toll of the unseen bell, the blood of all within turns against its bearer, veins become assassins. And under this red law, the master may spend the blood of the willing as his own. Consider what this means: he has made the battlefield his body, and every ally a vein. The perfect treasury, one that bleeds others. Deploying the Domain costs a full-turn action and 20 CE (invented): 60-foot radius, up to 1 minute, 800 clash points (Tier IV) (invented). At Initiative 20, all creatures take 4d12 necrotic damage as their blood attacks them from the inside. While in the domain your blood manipulation techniques can use hit points from willing creatures within the domain (invented)."}],"e251":[{"level":1,"title":"Storms of Disaster","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · 15-ft cone, Dex save · 2d8 slashing or thunder (your choice), half on success · Dice scale to 3d8/4d8/5d8 at 5th/11th/17th level."},{"level":3,"title":"Lightning","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Ranged CE attack, 60 ft · 3d6 lightning on hit; if another creature is within 10 ft of the target, attack them too for half damage · Scales to 4d6/6d6/8d6 at 6th/11th/18th."},{"level":6,"title":"Storm Creation","rules":"Action · 3 CE (+5 ft radius per extra CE, up to your PB) · 10-ft radius storm centered on you, 1 min · Difficult terrain; creatures starting their turn there: Str save or prone; ranged attacks inside at disadvantage; your lightning/thunder damage there + CE modifier."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Divine Storm Sovereign","rules":"Action · 10 CE · 100-ft radius sphere within 300 ft · Heavily obscured to all but you, difficult terrain, plus Storm Creation effects; creatures other than you starting their turn there take 3d10 lightning · On the Attack action, spend 2 CE to replace one attack with Lightning targeting anything in the sphere, even unseen."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Heavenly Throne of the Raging Tempest","rules":"Full-turn · 20 CE · 60-ft radius domain, up to 1 min · Initiative 20: all creatures take 6d12 lightning · Any Disaster Storms technique used inside strikes EVERY creature inside."}],"e252":[{"level":1,"title":"Vermin of Disaster","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Create an Insect Swarm in a space you can see within 5 ft · Command it as a bonus action (otherwise it Dodges) · Only one swarm at a time (cap grows at 3rd level)."},{"level":3,"title":"Earthen Insect Trance","rules":"Passive · Max Insect Swarms = your PB; command any number with one bonus action · Action · 2 CE each (max 2) · Summon insect-pouch shikigami in an unoccupied space within 10 ft; command swarms and shikigami with the same bonus action."},{"level":6,"title":"Almighty Swarm","rules":"Part of command bonus action · Swarms within 5 ft of each other merge into one Vermin Swarm: +1 size per extra swarm, pool HP and damage dice · Merged swarms still count toward your cap."},{"level":11,"title":"Parthenogenesis","rules":"Action · 8 CE (−1 per creature devoured by you or a swarm in the last 8 hrs, min 1) · Affix an insect egg to a wall/ceiling (AC = your CE save DC, HP = 2× your level; only one egg at a time) · If you die within 1 hour, the egg births a copy of you at half HP max with your remaining CE, no gear."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Brood Cathedral of the Crawling God","rules":"Full-turn · 20 CE · 60-ft radius domain, up to 1 min · Initiative 20: up to 3 chosen creatures take 6d10 necrotic as eggs burst from their skin · Creatures that die inside are devoured and become Insect Swarms that ignore your cap until the domain ends."}],"e253":[{"level":1,"title":"Antigravity","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 10-ft radius, 30-ft high cylinder centered on you (excludes you) until your next turn · Unanchored creatures/objects fall upward; Dex save to grab a fixed object · Fall damage ignores all reduction/immunity · Height rises to 50/100/200 ft at 3rd/11th/18th level (die d6/d8/d10/d12)."},{"level":3,"title":"Gravity Field","rules":"Upgrades · Light Fall (Reaction · 1 CE, when falling): you + PB creatures within 120 ft descend 60 ft/round, no fall damage · Focused System: CE mod + PB creatures unaffected by your technique · Disorienting Gravity: lifted creatures Con save or attacks at disadvantage and can't maintain concentration."},{"level":6,"title":"Antigravity Shield","rules":"Reaction · 2 CE · Attacks against you at disadvantage; non-psychic damage reduced by CE modifier + level until your next turn · If you are Dodging, can shield another creature within 5 ft instead."},{"level":11,"title":"Boosted System","rules":"Upgrades · Lasting Field: spend up to CE modifier CE, +10 ft radius and +1 round duration per CE · Sweeping Gravity: Dex score below your CE save DC = no Dex save vs your technique · Nauseating Gravity: failed Disorienting save also stuns to end of their next turn · Hard Fall: d12 fall damage."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Zero Gravity","rules":"Full-turn · 20 CE · 60-ft radius domain, up to 1 min · Initiative 20: creatures of your choice fail all saves vs Antigravity (you can release them at will) · Cylinder height 200 ft."}],"e254":[{"level":1,"title":"Dark Cube","rules":"Action · 2 CE · 10-ft opaque cube within 30 ft, 1 min (dismiss free) · Large or smaller creatures in range: Dex save or trapped inside (full cover from outside attacks; dark for all but you) · Cube AC = CE save DC +5, HP = PB × 2× CE modifier, immune to psychic and poison."},{"level":3,"title":"Black Box Reinforcement","rules":"Upgrade · Spend up to CE modifier extra CE (2× at 11th) · Per reinforcement: +10 HP; +1 AC per 2; +1 min duration per 3; reduce all damage taken by 1; +5 ft size per 2."},{"level":6,"title":"Perfect Cube","rules":"Upgrade · +5 CE (counts toward reinforcements) · The cube gains resistance to all damage and ignores features that deal extra damage to objects or would destroy, see into, or invade the barrier."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Midnight Armor","rules":"Action · 6 CE · 1 min: gain the cube's HP as temp HP, your AC = the cube's AC, unarmed strikes use CE modifier and deal 3d8 + CE modifier necrotic · Extra CE (up to 2× CE modifier): also gain any reinforcements except Size."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Primordial Gap","rules":"Full-turn · 20 CE · 60-ft radius domain, up to 1 min · All Dark Cubes count as Perfect Cubes inside · Initiative 20: create 3 Perfect Cubes trapping up to 3 creatures (treated as having CE-modifier reinforcements); cubes vanish when the domain ends."}],"e255":[{"level":1,"title":"Ignition","rules":"Bonus action (holding a melee weapon) · Spend up to CE modifier CE · Weapon ignited 1 min: +1d6 fire damage per CE spent on each hit (die rises to d8/d10/d12 at 6th/11th/18th) · Bright light 5 ft, dim 10 ft."},{"level":3,"title":"Mantle of Courage","rules":"Free action on your turn (while Ignition active) · 3 CE · 10-ft flame aura, 1 min · You gain fire and cold resistance · Enemies entering or starting their turn in the aura: Con save or take your Ignition damage, half on success."},{"level":6,"title":"Eternal Flames","rules":"Passive (needs ≥3 CE on Ignition) · Weapon reach +10 ft · Ignition ignores fire resistance · A miss by 2 or less still deals half Ignition damage (3 or less at 11th, 4 or less at 18th)."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Conflagration","rules":"Action (holding a melee weapon) · 10 CE · 30-ft cone · Con save: 10d12 fire damage + knocked prone, half on success · Fail by 5+: severe burns — take extra fire damage equal to your PB from any fire source until a long rest."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Fire of the Heart","rules":"Full-turn · 20 CE · 60-ft radius domain, up to 1 min · Melee weapons count as max Ignition with the domain's guaranteed hit · Initiative 20: all creatures of your choice take Mantle of Courage damage."}],"e256":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Centipede","rules":"Bonus action · First summon per long rest free, then 3 CE · Summon the cursed centipede; command as a bonus action (one at a time) · Worn as a shroud: +1d10 melee damage, AC + PB, bonus-action melee attack, transfer damage between you at will."},{"level":3,"title":"Insect Storage","rules":"Passive · Store items (no larger than a shield or polearm) in the centipede's stomach; capacity = 2 × your CE score × your PB · Stow or draw as an object interaction while summoned."},{"level":6,"title":"Earthquake","rules":"Action (bonus action if your centipede is summoned) · 3 CE · Ground within 30 ft: Str save or 6d6 bludgeoning + prone, half on success (10d6 at 11th, 14d6 at 18th) · +5 stat points to the centipede's ability scores (max 22); add your PB to its saves and checks."},{"level":11,"title":"Vermin of Disaster","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Launch up to 3 giant centipedes at targets within 120 ft: ranged CE attack each; on hit 8d10 necrotic, then Str save or pushed/pulled 30 ft (your choice) + prone · Also: up to two cursed centipedes at once; both as your shroud = 2 melee attacks as a bonus action; +5 more stat points (max 22)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Oomukade Banzai","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Inside: your cursed centipedes' attacks are guaranteed hits · Initiative 20: all creatures restrained by centipedes; escape with a Str (Athletics) check at the start of their turns (centipedes vanish when the grapple ends)."}],"e257":[{"level":1,"title":"Binding Vow","rules":"Bonus action · No CE · Forge a Binding Vow with a creature within 30 ft that can hear and understand you and is unwilling to abide by its terms (lasts until broken, Reconsidered, or 24 hrs) · Choose one mutual exchange: movement, unarmed damage dice, reactions/opportunity attacks, or advantage trade · If they break it: your reaction (once/turn) — advantage on all attacks vs them for 1 min, or an extra weapon/unarmed attack as a free action; if you break it, they get the same."},{"level":3,"title":"Retrial","rules":"Passive · Choose a Sorcerer spell you can cast: its CE cost is halved (rounded down) · Once per long rest."},{"level":6,"title":"Reconsideration","rules":"Action · End one Binding Vow with no consequences · Once per long rest."},{"level":11,"title":"Theft-Proof","rules":"Bonus action · Forge an unbreakable contract with yourself: gain the broken-vow benefit (advantage on all attacks for 1 min) with no target · No other technique features while active; end as a bonus action."}],"e258":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Circuitry","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Touch a surface within 5 ft to lay an invisible Circuit Pattern (AC 10, 2 HP; lasts until triggered or dispelled) · Trigger: bonus action when stepped on/touched, or action when a creature is within 5 ft · Choose one: Combustion (10-ft radius, Dex save, 3d6 fire); Lightning Surge (15-ft cone, Dex save, 2d8 lightning + stun on fail); Stasis Hold (10-ft radius, Str save or restrained to start of next turn); Burst Leap (up to two creatures within 10 ft propelled)."},{"level":3,"title":"Advanced Circuits","rules":"Upgrade · +2 CE when creating a pattern: choose an advanced effect instead · Binding Chains (15-ft radius, Str save or restrained 1 min, repeat save at end of each turn); Energy Discharge (20-ft radius, Con save, 4d6 force, allies unaffected); Energy Drain (20-ft radius, Wis save or lose 2d6 CE, you regain half); Cursed Detonation (30-ft radius, Dex save, 6d10 force; once per long rest)."},{"level":6,"title":"Linked Circuits","rules":"Upgrade · 1 CE: link a new pattern to one within 30 ft (60 ft at 11th, 120 ft at 18th); activating one can activate the other."},{"level":11,"title":"Circuit Mastery","rules":"Upgrades · Rapid Deployment: create patterns as a bonus action · Enhanced Circuitry: patterns deal +2d6 of the same type · Remote Activation (bonus action, 30 ft): activate a pattern without a trigger · Cursed Overclock (bonus action): spend up to 5 CE, +1d6 damage per CE for 1 min."}],"e259":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Transmutation","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Transmute a 10-ft cube of inanimate material/nonmagical object within 60 ft (grows to 20/30/40-ft cubes at 6th/11th/18th) · Weapons/tools only, no complex machinery · Unheld lasts 24 hrs, weapons/tools 1 hr, held lasts with concentration up to 1 hr; dismiss as a free action."},{"level":3,"title":"Elemental Manipulation","rules":"Upgrades · Fire (Action · 2 CE): transmute a 10-ft cube of flammable material into fire; creatures in the area Dex save, 3d6 fire · Water (Action · 2 CE): transmute a 10-ft cube into fresh or salt water · Earth (Action · 3 CE): reshape a 10-ft cube of earth/stone into walls or structures (AC 15, 30 HP per cube)."},{"level":6,"title":"Alchemy of the Soul","rules":"Upgrades · Healing (Action): touch a creature, spend any CE, heal 1d8 per 2 CE · Poison (Action · 3 CE): creature within 30 ft, Con save or 4d6 poison + poisoned 1 min, half on success · Flesh (Action · 5 CE): heal yourself 3d8 or grow an extra limb for 1 hr (holds/manipulates one object)."},{"level":11,"title":"Cursed Energy Transmutation","rules":"Action · Spend any CE: 60-ft line of raw force, Dex save, 1d8 force per 2 CE spent, half on success · OR Action · 10 CE: 20-ft radius sphere within 60 ft, Con save, 6d8 force + stunned to end of next turn, half on success."}],"e260":[{"level":1,"title":"Dark Claw","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Grow a large black claw for 1 min: unarmed strikes +1d8 slashing, use CE modifier for attack and damage, +2 AC."},{"level":3,"title":"Adaptation","rules":"Reaction (when you take damage) · 1 CE · Gain resistance to that damage type to end of your next turn (1 min at 6th; immunity at 11th)."},{"level":6,"title":"Eight-Handled Sword","rules":"Action · 10 CE (+2 CE per extra target) · Summon Mahoraga's massive sword for 1 min: 2d12 slashing, CE modifier for attack and damage, +1 to attack rolls."},{"level":11,"title":"Divine Adaptation","rules":"Spend 5 CE (+3 CE per condition) · Immune to one chosen condition (blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, poisoned, stunned) for 1 min · Spend 2 CE: unarmed strikes +2d8 of an adapted damage type for 1 min."}],"e261":[{"level":1,"title":"Flow of the Dragon","rules":"Passive (feet on the ground) · Add your PB to melee damage rolls · Advantage on checks and saves against being forcefully moved."},{"level":3,"title":"Ley Line Command","rules":"Bonus action (feet on the ground) · 3 CE · Ley Line for 1 min: immune to forced movement/teleport; reduce all damage taken by your PB; reaction when damaged: 1 CE for resistance to that type until your next turn · Lose benefits if your feet leave the ground · At 11th: also immune to grappled, restrained, and prone."},{"level":6,"title":"Earth Dragon Soul","rules":"Passive (while Ley Line active) · Once per turn: a melee hit deals +1d8 (2d8 at 11th, 3d8 at 18th) · If you haven't moved since the start of your last turn: twice per turn, but your speed is 0 until your next turn · Reaction resistance: spend 3 CE to extend it until Ley Line ends."},{"level":11,"title":"World Anchor","rules":"Passive · At the start of your turn (feet on the ground): gain temp HP = PB + CE modifier · If at half HP or less with Ley Line active: spend 3 CE to gain resistance to all damage until your next turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Of Primordial World","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Creatures inside can't teleport or fly more than 10 ft off the ground — crushed down for 5d10 force (once per turn) · You are always under Ley Line inside."}],"e262":[{"level":1,"title":"Excavation","rules":"Action · 1 CE per cube · Shape 5-ft cubes of stone within 30 ft (up to your CE modifier cubes, must connect) · AC = your CE DC, HP = 5× CE modifier each · Creature in a cube's area: Dex save or pushed to a space within 5 ft (end of connected cubes)."},{"level":3,"title":"Sculpted Earth","rules":"Action (can replace one attack) · 1 CE · Imbue a rock and launch it at a target within 30 ft: use CE or Str modifier for attack and damage; 1d12 bludgeoning on hit (or 1 more CE for necrotic). · Bonus action · Spend CE up to your PB · For 1 min: AC bonus equal to the CE spent. · Action · 3 CE · 20-ft radius around you: Dex save or 3d10 bludgeoning + prone, half on success (4d10 at 6th, 5d10 at 11th, 6d10 at 18th) · Structures auto-fail and take maximum damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Wall of Stone","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Stone wall within 60 ft, grounded, 1 hr: ten 10×10-ft panels, AC = your CE DC, HP = 10× CE modifier · Bonus action · 1 CE: move connected panels within 60 ft up to 30 ft along the ground (creatures in the way: Dex save or pushed)."},{"level":11,"title":"Stone Arms","rules":"Action · 5 CE · Target within 60 ft: Dex save or wedged between two stone arms — 6d12 bludgeoning + restrained to start of your next turn, half on success · 1 CE at the start of your turns to maintain (action to crush: Str save or 4d12, half on success; escape with an action vs your CE DC) · Arms: AC 18, HP = your HP max, you concentrate."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Trichiliocosm","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: creatures of your choice take 6d12 bludgeoning and are restrained by shifting stone to start of their next turn · Action: reshape the domain — a 20-ft radius chasm (falling damage, Dex save for a safe edge), a 100-ft stone tower, or a 100×5-ft path of difficult terrain (2d4 piercing per 5 ft moved)."}],"e263":[{"level":1,"title":"Eight Lives","rules":"Passive · When reduced to 0 HP or killed: spend 1 CE to revive at half HP max, harmful conditions (except exhaustion) removed · 8 lives; usable 3× per long rest (4 at 3rd, 8 at 6th); regain one life every 8 days."},{"level":3,"title":"Collective Will","rules":"No action · 1 CE · When you make an Int/Wis/Cha check or save: reroll, keep the new roll · Up to 8 times per long rest."},{"level":6,"title":"Fangs of Orochi","rules":"Action · Spend up to 8 CE: summon that many fang-shikigami in unoccupied spaces within 10 ft · Command any with a bonus action · They vanish if you fall unconscious · 10 HP (20 at 11th)."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Sacrifice","rules":"Action (needs ≥3 fangs summoned) · 6 CE · Fangs move up to 40 ft and encircle a creature, embedding in the ground: trigram cylinder (20 ft high, 15 ft diameter, AC 20, HP = all fangs' HP) · Trapped creature: CE save at start of turn or 10d4 necrotic, half on success · Humanoid killed this way: you regain one life (once per week)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Ama ga Fuchi","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: Yamata no Orochi forms from the earth (no actions, no turn) · On later initiative 20s: roll 1d8 — that many creatures of your choice each suffer a sure-hit bite: 8d10 piercing · The shikigami vanishes when the domain ends."}],"e264":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Painting","rules":"Spend 1 CE · Create an ink painting under a Medium or smaller creature within 30 ft: Dex save or sucked into a 30-ft subspace (120/600/1200 ft at 3rd/6th/11th) · Start of turn: 1 CE per occupied subspace or occupants reappear; max subspaces = CE modifier (2× at 11th) · Enter/exit/move items as a free action once per turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Impasto Canvas","rules":"Action · Spend up to CE modifier CE: create that many Ink Wolves anywhere in your painting; they act on your initiative and obey verbal commands (no action). · Action · Move the Exit Painting up to 80 ft (at 6th: to a new random accessible location). · Action · Create a 15-ft radius (30 ft at 6th) area of difficult terrain anywhere in your painting; lasts until the painting ends or you replace it. · Action · Create one structure (walls, towers, bridges, buildings) fitting in a 30-ft cube anywhere in your painting · AC = your CE save DC, each 5×5-ft section: 5× PB HP (10× PB at 6th) · Create, destroy, or replace while inside the painting. · Action · Create one trap in an unoccupied 5-ft square anywhere in your painting (lasts until triggered or the painting ends; detected vs your CE save DC) · Pit: Dex save or fall 20 ft (2d6 + prone); Spike: Dex save or 2d10 piercing + prone; Snare: Dex save or restrained (escape with an action vs DC); Rolling Stone: 30-ft line, Dex save, 4d10 + prone, half on success · +2 damage dice at 6th (+4 at 11th)."},{"level":6,"title":"Sgraffito","rules":"Upgrade · Manipulate your painting as a bonus action · New shikigami: Greater Ink Wolf (2 CE), Ink Crow (3 CE) · Ink Wave (Action · 2 CE): 30-ft cone from you or an Ink Shikigami; Con save or PB d6s necrotic + blinded to end of their next turn (usable outside the subspace) · Cursed Painting now targets Large or smaller (Huge at 11th)."},{"level":11,"title":"Panoramic Composition","rules":"Action · Spend CE up to 2× CE modifier: that many creatures within 60 ft Dex save or sucked into your paintings."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Magnum Opus","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Inside counts as your painting's subspace (expanded, same rules); Ink Shikigami and Traps carry the guaranteed hit · Initiative 20: two different Impasto Canvas effects of your choice (Ink Shikigami still costs CE)."}],"e265":[{"level":1,"title":"Self-Destruction","rules":"Payloads (X = your CE modifier; throwing is an action, or bonus action at 3rd) · Tiny — tooth/finger/hair (1 CE + Con mod HP, remove as free action, throw within 120 ft): 5-ft blast, Dex save, Xd6 force · Small — ears/nose (2 CE + Con mod×half level HP, remove as bonus action, 100 ft): 10-ft blast, Xd8 + prone · Medium — hands/feet (4 CE + Con mod×level HP, remove as action, 80 ft): 15-ft blast, Xd10 + prone · Large — arms/legs (6 CE + Con mod×level HP, remove as full-turn, 60 ft): 20-ft blast, Xd12 + prone · Half damage on success; double damage to objects/structures."},{"level":3,"title":"Faster Throws","rules":"Upgrade · Throw a removed body part as an action or bonus action."},{"level":6,"title":"Guerilla Tactics","rules":"Reaction (when you receive or land a melee attack) · Explode a body part on your body for its normal cost; all creatures roll the Dex save at disadvantage unless their passive Perception beats your CE DC."},{"level":11,"title":"Stronger Explosions","rules":"Upgrade · Failed saves vs your explosions also deafen for 1 min (Con save at start of turns ends; blinded too at 18th) · Triple damage to objects/structures; explosion radius +5 ft."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: True Art","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Detonate your own body parts for no CE cost · Initiative 20: detonate a limb (arm or leg) of a creature inside your domain."}],"e266":[{"level":1,"title":"Store and Release","rules":"Passive · Miss with a melee attack: gain 1 Jin charge (max PB + level) · Spend charges (up to PB at once, declared before the roll): +2 per charge to a melee or CE attack roll, or +1 damage die per charge (use the first damage die listed) · Spent charges lost on a miss; all charges lost on a long rest · You may also spend 1 CE instead of 1 charge."},{"level":3,"title":"Instantaneous Movement","rules":"Passive · At the start of your turn: forgo movement or spend 1 CE to gain a Jin charge · Spend 1 charge: speed +10 ft and triple jump distance to end of turn · Spend charges as a reaction: instantly move 10 ft per charge in any direction without provoking."},{"level":6,"title":"Fist of Explosive Power","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Blast of compressed air fueled by Jin charges, shaped by your weapon · Unarmed/bludgeoning: 15-ft cone, Con save, 2d6 bludgeoning per charge, prone on fail · Slashing/piercing: 30-ft line, Dex save, 2d10 slashing per charge."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximize Potential Energy","rules":"Upgrades · Keep up to CE modifier Jin charges when you miss an enhanced attack · Explosive Power with ≥3 charges: range +30 ft, deals thunder · CE spent for a charge now grants 2 charges · Action (touching a creature): give them up to CE modifier of your Jin charges."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Hall of Divine Bagua","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Inside: unlimited Jin charges for you · Initiative 20: all creatures gain a permanent negative Jin charge: −1d6 damage on their next attack or technique per charge (gone when the domain ends)."}],"e267":[{"level":1,"title":"Madness Inducement","rules":"Action · 5 CE · All creatures that can see you within 120 ft: Wis save; success = no Madness and immune 24 hrs; fail = 1d6 Madness (3d6 on a natural 1) · Start of each creature's turn: Wis save — success halves Madness; fail takes psychic damage = current Madness and adds 1d6 Madness · Becoming blinded/deafened/restrained voluntarily: Madness to 0, immune 24 hrs · At 50 Madness: berserk (attacks nearest perceived creature; no ranged; adv on Str saves and attack rolls; immune frightened; dis on other saves; exhaustion after 3 berserk turns) · Madness resets on a long rest."},{"level":3,"title":"Madness Enhancement","rules":"Upgrade · Madness inflicted: 2d6 (5d6 on critical failure) · A creature that goes berserk also gains 1 level of exhaustion."},{"level":6,"title":"Obsession and Insanity","rules":"Upgrade · Contagious: a creature failing its start-of-turn Madness save gives 1d6 Madness to all creatures within 30 ft · Berserk creatures gain exhaustion every turn (instead of every 3 turns)."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum Rumination","rules":"Bonus action · 5 CE · Glimpse the Faceless God: creatures within 30 ft gain Corruption (each point = disadvantage on all saves) · Start of turn: Cha save vs your CE DC — fail: 1d10 psychic per 10 corruption + 1d6 corruption (2d6 at 14th, 3d6 at 17th); success: no damage, immune 24 hrs · 3 failed saves: becomes an aberration (DM approval) · Long rest + Wis save removes corruption (half as much on fail, capped at 25)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Theia Mania","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Entering for the first time or starting a turn inside: 2d6 Madness; all attack rolls and saves at −2 · Initiative 20 (if more than half the creatures are berserk or corrupted): all creatures Wis save — 10d10 psychic on success, 20d10 on failure."}],"e268":[{"level":1,"title":"Fate Manipulation","rules":"Action · 2 CE (+1 CE per extra Fate, up to PB) · Bind two creatures within 30 ft with an invisible red thread for 1 min · Choose a Fate affecting both while within 30 ft of each other: Bonds (+2 AC); Promised Time (adv/dis on attacks vs each other); Mirrored (a 20/1 on one's turn flips the other's next roll); Magnetic (start turn within 30 ft: pulled 10 ft closer; within 5 ft: tangled and prone, Str save to pull away — requires Touch) · Touch Fates: touch both targets (not necessarily at once) · Effects that damage the soul can cut the thread; creatures with no cursed energy can't be bound."},{"level":3,"title":"Cursed Eyes of Fate","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · See the red threads connecting living creatures within sight · OR read one target's thread to learn one: resistances/immunities/vulnerabilities, CR or Level, remaining HP, AC or an ability modifier, current emotions."},{"level":6,"title":"Strong Destiny","rules":"Upgrade · Extend a Fate's duration by 1 min per extra CE (1 hr base at 11th, +1 hr per CE) · Shared Strengths: both targets share one of a target's damage resistances/immunities/vulnerabilities or condition immunities · Linked Suffering (requires Touch): linked targets split damage taken half and half."},{"level":11,"title":"Karmic Entanglement","rules":"Downtime · 8 uninterrupted hours: permanently intertwine the fates of two or more creatures (destined to meet; can carry an Inherited Technique or unique constitution past death) · Max PB creatures at once, including you · You can't die of old age (still age; assimilate every 500 years or evolve) · Destined Death (Touch Fate): both targets have adv or dis on saves against each other."},{"level":18,"title":"Road of Karma","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: designate a Destined Foe inside — all your attacks against them carry the guaranteed hit · The whole domain counts as in range; Touch requirements waived."}],"e269":[{"level":1,"title":"Warstaff","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Create a pen-like cursed tool (reach, two-handed, grade 4; uses CE modifier for attack/damage; 1d4 + CE mod piercing; martial-arts compatible; dismiss at will; one at a time) · Each hit attaches a manga panel: see 1 sec into that creature's future per hit (max PB seconds; max CE-mod creatures) · Reaction or bonus action · 1 CE: read one marked creature's future to your next turn — 1s: its attacks vs you at dis; 2s: adv on your saves vs it; 3s: adv on your attacks vs it; 4s+: DM reveals its next actions · Not usable while blinded."},{"level":3,"title":"Highlighted Panels","rules":"Passive · Against saving throws caused by a creature you see 2+ seconds into the future: half damage on a failed save, no damage on a success."},{"level":6,"title":"Predictable Strikes","rules":"Passive · Once per turn: turn a Warstaff hit into a critical vs a creature you see 3+ seconds into the future · No Black Flash roll from this."},{"level":11,"title":"Precognition","rules":"Passive · Advantage from your technique expands your crit range by half your CE modifier (rounded down); disadvantage it imposes expands the enemy's crit-fail range by the same."},{"level":18,"title":"Storyboard Dominion","rules":"Domain (18th level) · All creatures inside count as having 6 seconds marked (overriding the PB ceiling) · Initiative 20: see 6 seconds into every creature's future at no extra CE; lasts to the next initiative 20 or domain end."}],"e270":[{"level":1,"title":"Golden Hour","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Stop time until end of your turn (no CE use while stopped) · Adv on all attacks vs creatures in stopped time; ranged attacks suspend mid-air until time resumes; others auto-fail Str/Dex saves and can't use reactions (a creature may use its reaction vs your ranged attack once time resumes)."},{"level":3,"title":"Majestic Pose","rules":"Full-turn action · Spend up to 2× PB CE: take one turn per 3 CE spent in stopped time · After time resumes: speed 0 to end of your next turn · Speed +10 ft when stopping time (+5 at 6th/11th/18th)."},{"level":6,"title":"Golden Week","rules":"Action (bonus action at 6th via Quick Pose) · 4 CE · For 1 min instead of stopping time: speed doubled, +3 AC, adv on Dex saves, +1 extra action each turn (Attack for one weapon attack only, Dash, Disengage, Hide, or Use an Object) · Can't stop time until it ends."},{"level":11,"title":"Samsara Rewind","rules":"Full-turn action · 8 CE · Rewind 6 seconds: all creatures and objects within 100 ft return to the start of your previous turn; damage and CE spent that round are undone (except this technique's cost)."},{"level":18,"title":"The World","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: stop time and take one turn (two stopped turns under the combined printed clauses) · Any time you stop time inside with your technique, add one more turn; Majestic and Quick Pose gain one extra turn per activation."}],"e271":[{"level":1,"title":"Scorpion Hair","rules":"Attack action · 1 CE · Replace one attack with a barbed stinger: melee CE attack, 10 ft, 1d10 + CE modifier piercing · +1/+2/+3/+4 attack and damage at 3rd/6th/11th/18th."},{"level":3,"title":"Drill Hair","rules":"Attack action · 1 CE · Replace one attack with a ranged drill: 30 ft (60 ft at 6th), 1d6 + CE modifier piercing · Optional +2 CE: 5-ft explosion, Dex save, 3d6 fire (5d6/8d6/10d6 at 6th/11th/18th), half on success."},{"level":6,"title":"Aircraft Hair","rules":"Action · 3 CE (1 CE to extend 1 min; switching forms needs another activation) · Form hair into a Jet or Helicopter for 1 min · Helicopter: fly speed = walk speed, Dash as a bonus action; on the Attack action spend 2 CE to replace one attack with a blade slash — melee CE attack, 6d8 + CE mod slashing (8d8/10d8 at 11th/18th); opportunity attackers take CE-mod slashing (2× at 11th) · Jet: fly speed = walk speed; Dash while flying: no opportunity attacks, crash in a straight line through creatures — Dex save or Xd8 bludgeoning (X = CE mod) + pushed 30 ft + prone (+1d4 per 10 ft traveled if they hit a surface), half on success; Dash = 2× fly speed at 11th, 3× at 18th."},{"level":11,"title":"Hair Spray","rules":"Upgrades · Technique reach +5 ft; hair counts as a Grade 1 Cursed Tool (Special Grade at 18th) · Once per turn: use an attack-roll feature as a bonus action (+2 CE, advantage) or a save-forcing feature as a bonus action (+4 CE, disadvantage)."},{"level":18,"title":"Silken Strand Execution Ground","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Creatures other than you take 2d10 slashing per 5 ft moved inside; difficult terrain for them · Jet's failed 30-ft push can trigger 12d10 slashing inside."}],"e272":[{"level":1,"title":"Inversion","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE (1 CE to extend 1 min) · Inverse for 1 min · Damage taken is inverted around limit L (PB × CE score) and threshold T (PB × CE modifier): above T inverts down, below T inverts up; a negative result leaves damage unchanged (e.g. L 100, T 20: 90 → 70, 10 → 90) · Deactivate as a bonus action; before 11th, activation can't interrupt incoming damage."},{"level":3,"title":"Extreme Opposites","rules":"Passive (while Inverse active) · Damage below your threshold: you are vulnerable to it · Damage above your threshold: resistance, even if the damage would normally bypass resistances or immunities."},{"level":6,"title":"Break the Strong","rules":"Passive (while Inverse active) · Saving throws vs damaging effects: damage above threshold = advantage; below threshold = disadvantage; at threshold = neither · Roll the damaging effect before the save to decide; classify post-save damage for Inversion."},{"level":11,"title":"Quick Inversion","rules":"Upgrade · Activate or deactivate Inverse as a reaction to damage (activation for the normal 2 CE happens before mitigation) · Extra reactions (half PB rounded up; full PB at 18th) usable only for the inverse technique; refresh at the start of your turn; one reaction per trigger."},{"level":18,"title":"Synesthesia","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Activate Inverse inside as a free action any number of times for no cost · Initiative 20: chosen creatures roll a d4 and lose one sense (taste, smell, touch, sight) until they pass an end-of-turn CE check or the domain ends."}],"e273":[{"level":1,"title":"Demonic Intellect","rules":"Passive · Use Intelligence as your CE modifier · Bonus action · 1 CE: overclock for 1 min — spend 2 CE to take an action as a reaction; adv on Int checks; add Int modifier to AC and Dex saves; 2000 IQ: bonus action + Int (Arcana) vs the user's CE save DC (treat Int as 22) to understand a technique in play (adv with a full-turn observation)."},{"level":3,"title":"Future and Past","rules":"Passive · After a long rest: roll two d20s and record them · Reaction · 1 CE: replace any attack roll, save, or check you make (or a save you force) with one foretelling roll (before rolling; each used once) · Short rest: spend 1 CE to gain one more foretelling roll (one short-rest roll max)."},{"level":6,"title":"Overload","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Touch a creature: Int save or 5d10 psychic + stunned to end of its next turn, half damage on success · No attack roll."},{"level":11,"title":"Laplace’s Demon","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Elevated intellect for 1 hr: all your d20 rolls at advantage, all d20 rolls against you at disadvantage · Reaction: add your Int modifier to an attack roll, check, or save made by you or a creature within 5 ft (after the d20, before the outcome; no extra reaction granted)."},{"level":18,"title":"Laplace Threshold","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: creatures of your choice take a cumulative −2 penalty to all rolls against you · Inside: you know all creatures' HP, conditions, resistances, immunities, vulnerabilities; invisible creatures are visible to you; being unseen/hidden grants no advantage vs you."}],"e274":[{"level":1,"title":"Little Miracles & Blind Luck","rules":"Passive · Witness good fortune (Lucky!/Equal Numbers!/Treasure!/Overcoming Hardship): gain 1 Miracle (max 6; 2 per witness at 11th, 3 at 18th) · Blind Luck (once per round when damaged): spend a Miracle to reduce damage by CE-mod d4s + PB · OR as a reaction: spend a Miracle + 1 CE, roll d6s instead and add PB twice."},{"level":3,"title":"Miraculous Outcome","rules":"Reaction (when you fail a roll) · 1 Miracle + 1 CE · Add a d6 (d8 at 6th, d10 at 11th) to the roll, potentially turning failure into success."},{"level":6,"title":"Deadly Miracle","rules":"Trigger (hit or failed save that would drop you to 0 HP or kill you) · 2 Miracles + 2 CE · Succeed the save or survive with no damage/effects · Death saves at advantage while holding ≥1 Miracle · At 11th: also works vs effects that would drop you to half HP or below."},{"level":11,"title":"Fated for Fortune","rules":"Passive · A 20+ on a Miraculous Outcome die counts as a critical success (natural 20) — but no Black Flash rolls and no Miracle gained."},{"level":18,"title":"Luck of the Draw","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Expand for 2d20 CE (reaction-expansion: 20 CE or a 2d20 roll), lasts 1d4 minutes · Initiative 20: gain 3 Miracles with no maximum · Inside: spend a Miracle on yourself or another creature attacking/using a technique to grant the guaranteed hit."}],"e275":[{"level":1,"title":"Missile Impact","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · To end of your turn: replace attacks with Missile Fists — ranged CE attack, 20 ft, 1d8 + CE modifier necrotic (2d8/3d8/4d8 at 6th/11th/18th) · The activating bonus action includes one extra Missile Fist attack · Within 5 ft: may instead make a melee CE attack using Str or Dex."},{"level":3,"title":"Devastating Barrage","rules":"Upgrade · When using Missile Fist: spend CE up to CE modifier for one extra attack per CE · Range 30 ft (+20 ft at 6th/11th/18th) · Hit a Large or smaller creature: forgo damage to grapple it 1 min; hit a grappled one: forgo damage to restrain it 1 min · Escape: Str save vs your CE save DC at end of their turn; ends if you are incapacitated."},{"level":6,"title":"Unrelenting Fury","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 30-ft cone of Missile Fists: Str save or 2d8 necrotic per attack you can make as an action + prone, half on success · Bonus action: +2d8 · Spend CE up to CE modifier: +2d8 per CE."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Brutal Bombardment","rules":"Full-turn action (Action + Bonus + Movement) · 6 CE · One creature within 50 ft: Str save or (3d8 + 3d8) necrotic per attack you can make as an action + 4d10 bludgeoning (crushed) + prone; half necrotic and no bludgeoning on success · Objects/structures take maximum damage · Splash: all creatures within 5 ft of the target (+5 ft per Missile Fist) Str save or the same necrotic · Spend CE up to CE modifier: +3d8 per CE (counts as another Missile Fist)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Unrelenting Ring of Spirit","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: all creatures take 8d8 necrotic and are knocked prone · Action: target any creature in your domain with a single Missile Fist for no CE cost."}],"e276":[{"level":1,"title":"Lunar Jellyfish","rules":"Action · First summon per long rest free, then 5 CE · Summon a Jellyfish shikigami for 8 hrs (uses your PB) · Bonus action: command it (otherwise it Dodges) · Action + 1 CE: change its size between Tiny and Large · Destroyed: can't resummon for 1 min."},{"level":3,"title":"Poisonous Cursed Energy","rules":"No action · 1 CE (once per turn, on your turn) · When you or Moon Dregs hit with a melee attack: +2d6 poison (4d6 at 6th, 6d8 at 11th, 6d10 at 18th; not amplified by crits) · You can replace any of your attacks with a Moon Dregs attack."},{"level":6,"title":"Noxious Poison","rules":"Upgrade · Poisonous Cursed Energy: target Con save or poisoned 1 min (repeat at end of turns); while poisoned, they suffer a temporary level of exhaustion · Moon Dregs: two attacks with the Attack action; can grant a creature in its space three-quarters cover (full cover at 11th)."},{"level":11,"title":"Cleansing of Purity","rules":"Upgrade · Add your CE modifier to Moon Dregs' AC and its Str/Dex/Con · Moon Dregs makes three attacks with the Attack action."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Liberation Rite of Water and Land","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Difficult terrain unless you have a swim speed (creatures can still breathe) · Initiative 20: all creatures take 8d6 poison or acid (your choice each tick) · Moon Dregs attacks have the guaranteed hit; command CE-mod tiny jellyfish shikigami (guaranteed hit) as an action — they count as Moon Dregs, 1 attack each, 30 HP."}],"e277":[{"level":1,"title":"Pain Killer","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Touch a creature within 5 ft: it gains temp HP = CE modifier + your level for 1 hr · Stops ongoing damage-over-time (not new effects) · You gain Medicine proficiency."},{"level":3,"title":"Practiced Hands","rules":"Free action on your turn · 1 CE per creature · Pain Killer on all willing creatures within 5 ft (10 ft at 6th, 15 ft at 11th)."},{"level":6,"title":"Pain Breaker","rules":"Upgrade · Pain Killer also removes one condition of your choice and stabilizes creatures making death saves · You gain Medicine Expertise."},{"level":11,"title":"Analgesic","rules":"Reaction (a creature you can see within 10 ft takes damage) · 4 CE · Halve the damage."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Medical Clinic","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: you and creatures of your choice fall under full Pain Killer (incl. Pain Breaker's condition removal and stabilization) · Analgesic usable as a free action for no CE (no reaction), once per damage instance."}],"e278":[{"level":1,"title":"Immobilizing Eyes","rules":"Action · 2 CE · One creature within 60 ft in line of sight: Dex save or speed halved, attack rolls and AC − your CE modifier to start of your next turn · Bonus action · 1 CE: maintain each turn · Ends if line of sight breaks · Your eyes: HP = 1/3 your max HP (rounded up); take 1 damage per point a creature rolls above your save DC; regain 1 at the start of your turn (not at 0); at 0: blinded, recover only via RCT or long rest."},{"level":3,"title":"Peripheral Vision","rules":"Upgrade · Full-turn action (Action + Bonus + Movement): target up to CE-modifier creatures (1 CE per creature beyond the first) · Maintain: 1 CE per target each turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Reactive Eye Movement","rules":"Reaction (a target you can see within 60 ft makes an attack roll, or an attack targets you) · 2 CE · That creature Dex save or its attack roll at disadvantage · Creatures under Immobilizing Eyes auto-fail this save."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Paralyzing Gaze","rules":"Action · 6 CE · One creature you can see within 120 ft: Dex save or paralyzed (can't be moved, even suspended), AC − your CE modifier · Maintain: concentration + bonus action · 2 CE at the start of your turns · Target: Str (Athletics) at end of its turn — success deals 2 damage to your eyes per point above your save DC · Your eyes' HP = 1/2 your max HP (rounded up)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Chamber of Fractured Reflections","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: three creatures of your choice suffer Immobilizing Eyes · You may change the domain's guaranteed-hit target each initiative 20 · Line of sight can't be broken inside (mirrors reflect your gaze from every angle)."}],"e279":[{"level":1,"title":"Regalia","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Manifest a soul-weapon (any simple/martial melee weapon) for CE-modifier hours · +1 attack/damage · Once per turn on a hit: spend 1 CE for +1d8 necrotic (2d8/3d8/4d8/6d8 at 3rd/6th/11th/18th) · Vanishes beyond 30 ft; only you can wield it."},{"level":3,"title":"Cursed Wave","rules":"No action · 1 CE · Turn one Regalia attack into a 5-ft wide, 30-ft long cutting wave: creatures in the line Dex save, take your regalia damage as necrotic, half on success."},{"level":6,"title":"Divine Protection","rules":"Upgrade · Regalia attack/damage bonus: +2 (+3 at 11th, +4 at 18th) · Regalia gains HP = 5× your level · Reaction (when you take damage) · 1 CE: redirect the damage to the regalia's pool · At 0 pool: you take the remainder, regalia breaks (resummon CE-mod times, then only after a long rest)."},{"level":11,"title":"Soul Bound Treasure","rules":"Passive · Regalia is now a special-grade cursed tool (work with your GM for its technique) · Action · 10 CE · Hover for 1 min (AC = 12 + CE mod + PB, HP = its pool; destroyed at 0) · Action: move it up to 100 ft and originate your attacks from it (CE mod for attack/damage) · Action: 100-ft line attack — Dex save or regalia damage, half on success; appears at the end of the line · After 1 min: flies 100 ft back toward you or falls."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Cursed Soul Armory","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Filled with Lesser Regalia: initiative 20, enemies suffer a sure-hit attack for 8d10 necrotic · Soul Bound Treasure usable as an action for no CE; immune to all damage inside; one of its actions usable once per turn as a free action."}],"e280":[{"level":1,"title":"Reversion","rules":"Reaction (your failed attack/save vs a visible effect, or a failed attack roll targeting you) · 1 CE · Rewind a few seconds: reattempt the failed roll or force the attack to reroll · At 3rd: +2 to the second attempt (+3/4/5 at 6th/11th/18th); can target a creature within 30 ft for +2 CE (they get no bonus)."},{"level":3,"title":"Regression","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Rewind your movement to where you stood at the start of your turn (positional only — rolls, HP, conditions, resources don't change) · Opportunity attacks vs this movement at disadvantage · Blocked by a creature: Dex save or PB d8s bludgeoning + pushed out of your path (Large or smaller) · Blocked by an object: CE check (DC 10 + 3 per size above Medium) or you take 5 and it takes 10× PB bludgeoning · At 6th: +3 CE to regress to the start of your previous turn."},{"level":6,"title":"Enhanced Reversion","rules":"Upgrade · Reversion without spending your reaction, PB times per round · Spend +3 CE with Reversion to roll the second attempt at advantage."},{"level":11,"title":"Invert Causality","rules":"Reaction (after an attack or damaging effect from a creature within 30 ft damages you) · 8 CE · Time rewinds to before the attack: make one attack vs that creature that ignores range and is guaranteed to hit; the triggering action is wasted (resources not refunded)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Requiem of Retrograde","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: choose one creature — the first thing it does on its turn is reversed and wasted (retarget each initiative 20) · Creatures of your choice are under base Reversion; your Reversion-boosted attack rolls are guaranteed to hit."}],"e281":[{"level":1,"title":"Sound Amplification","rules":"Action (holding an instrument you're proficient in) · 1 CE · Ranged CE attack, 30 ft (60 ft at 6th): 2d10 thunder (3d10/4d10/6d10 at 6th/11th/18th); creature hit: Str save or pushed 10 ft · You gain Performance + one instrument proficiency."},{"level":3,"title":"Jacked Audio","rules":"Upgrade · Your Sound Blast action launches up to two Sound Blasts (1 CE each); up to three at 11th."},{"level":6,"title":"Resonating Music","rules":"Action · 5 CE · 15-ft cone (30 ft at 11th): Con save or Sound Blast damage + PB d10s thunder + pushed 20 ft + deafened to end of their next turn, half damage on success."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Epic Solo","rules":"Bonus action · 8 CE (+ extra CE up to half PB) · Solo for 1 min: your attacks +2d10 thunder (+2d10 more per extra CE); creatures failing saves vs your technique have dis on their next attack or check (expires end of their next turn); hostiles ending their turn within 15 ft of you take CE-mod + PB thunder."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Hall of Fame","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: creatures of your choice take your Sound Amplification damage and are deafened for 1 min."}],"e282":[{"level":1,"title":"Piercing Schrift","rules":"Passive · Use your CE modifier for ranged weapon attack or damage rolls · On a ranged attack: spend 1 CE to phase through one solid object (5 ft thick), ignoring cover · Pierces 2 objects at 3rd, 3 at 6th, 4 at 11th."},{"level":3,"title":"X-Axis Shot","rules":"Action (only if you haven't moved this turn; speed 0 after) · 3 CE · Automatically hit a creature in range with a ranged weapon attack: +2d6 necrotic (3d6/5d6/7d6 at 6th/11th/18th)."},{"level":6,"title":"Cursed Mark","rules":"Passive · You can have only one mark active at a time — using a mark ends the previous one. · Bonus action · 3 CE · Mark a target within 30 ft for 1 min · Hit the marked target: your next attack vs it has advantage; that attack is an automatic critical (roll all dice twice + modifiers), and the mark ends. · Bonus action · 3 CE · Mark up to CE-modifier targets within 30 ft for 1 min · Action: make one ranged attack roll vs each marked target in range (weapon or CE attack), normal damage on a hit; marks end."},{"level":11,"title":"Intangibility","rules":"Bonus action · 6 CE · Phase for 1 min (concentration): immune to bludgeoning/piercing/slashing, resistant to all other damage except psychic · Can't use innate technique features while active (normal attack actions only); end as a free action. · Upgrade · When activating Intangibility: resistant (not immune) to all damage except psychic, but you CAN use your innate technique features · Piercing Schrift usable free once per turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Divine Sight","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Inside: all your attacks benefit from Piercing Schrift and are guaranteed hits · Initiative 20: every creature inside receives a Cursed Mark of your choice."}],"e283":[{"level":1,"title":"Shadow Strike","rules":"No action (on an attack roll) · 1 CE · Attack a creature's shadow in its space: if unaware of your technique, auto-hit · Necrotic damage = your attack + CE modifier (2× at 3rd, 3× at 6th, 4× at 11th) · You can also cast Minor Illusion through your shadow in a 5-ft range · Requires seeing the target's shadow. · Passive · Attack roll above target's passive Perception: they don't know how they were hurt · Lower: they see the shadow attack and become aware · An aware creature gets a Dex save vs your shadow assault — fail: auto-hit; success: you roll vs AC."},{"level":3,"title":"Dark Binding","rules":"No action · 3 CE · When you make a weapon attack: target the shadow instead — on a hit, forgo damage and release the weapon to pin the shadow: creature grappled and restrained, can't move or be moved · Any creature can use one attack to remove the weapon (no roll), ending both conditions."},{"level":6,"title":"Void Steps","rules":"Passive · Darkvision 200 ft, sees through magical darkness in range · Spend 2 CE: cast Pass Without Trace · Hide in dim light/darkness: become invisible until you attack, use a technique, or enter bright light."},{"level":11,"title":"Shadows of Mortality","rules":"Upgrade · Shadow Strike as a free action once per turn for 1 CE · Vs a target that hasn't acted in combat or is surprised: the Shadow Strike is an automatic critical (roll all dice twice + modifiers); no Black Flash from this. · Action · 10 CE · Dark sun: 30-ft sphere, 300 ft up, 1 min (end early if incapacitated; +1 min per 1 CE) · Entering the sphere or starting a turn there: 4d6 necrotic · 600-ft magical darkness you see through normally (technique light under 5 CE suppressed; creatures with CE score or passive Perception above your save DC see it as dim light) · Inside: Shadow Strike free (no CE), targets at dis on shadow Dex saves, vulnerable to Shadow Strike if you spend CE on it."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Zero Hour","rules":"Domain (18th level) · All creatures' shadows are always visible to you and stretch to your feet (always targetable) · Initiative 20: three creatures of your choice suffer full Shadow Strike."}],"e284":[{"level":1,"title":"Minor Star Shikigami","rules":"Action · Spend CE up to your PB: summon that many minor shikigami in unoccupied spaces within 5 ft · Bonus action: command any of them (otherwise they Dodge) · Action: share senses with one (you are blinded and deafened while sharing) · Max = PB at a time."},{"level":3,"title":"Pseudo-Domain Constitution","rules":"Bonus action · Command any number of minor shikigami to orbit a point (they Dash in a circle within 5 ft of the center) · Bonus action each turn: expand radius by 5 ft or add more orbiters. · Passive · Creatures inside the orbit (not you): Dex save at the end of your turn or 1d6 slashing per orbiting shikigami, half on success · Max radius = 5 ft × orbiting shikigami · Killed orbiters shrink range and damage; ends if all stop orbiting."},{"level":6,"title":"Major Star Shikigami","rules":"Action · 6 CE · Summon one major star shikigami; bonus action to command (otherwise Dodges) · One at a time; if killed, can't resummon for 1 hr · Pseudo-domain now deals 1d8 slashing per orbiter. · Full-turn action (Action + Bonus + Movement) · Command the major shikigami to form a special pseudo-domain (completes at the start of your next turn): minors move freely inside without breaking range/damage (still scales with the number of minors inside)."},{"level":11,"title":"Army of the Dictator","rules":"Upgrade · Minor shikigami cap: 3× PB · Two major shikigami at once · Pseudo-domain: 1d10 slashing per orbiter (ignores slashing resistance/immunity); radius = 10 ft × orbiting shikigami."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Divine Mandate","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: creatures of your choice take 1d12 slashing per star shikigami you have summoned in the domain."}],"e285":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Fog","rules":"Action · Spend CE up to CE modifier · 10 ft of fog per CE around you, 1 min: spreads around corners, heavily obscures; you choose whether it follows you · Creatures inside: dis on Perception/Investigation, can't detect cursed energy. · Upgrade · Reaction: grant adv or dis to a roll by a creature in your fog · At 6th: spend up to 2× CE modifier when creating fog (3× at 11th)."},{"level":3,"title":"Kitsune Creation","rules":"Action · 2 CE each · Summon a fox shikigami for 24 hrs (dismiss free) · Command all foxes as a bonus action; they act on your turn · Max = PB; you always know when one dies · Slain foxes burst into fog."},{"level":6,"title":"Living Fog","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Transform yourself or one fox into a misty cloud for up to 1 hr (concentration) · Fly 30 ft only; enter/occupy other creatures' spaces; occupy a creature's space: force a Con save or CE-mod d8s cold as they choke on fog · +3 CE: also invisible for the duration. · Mist form traits · Resistance to nonmagical damage; adv on Str/Dex/Con saves · Pass through holes and cracks (liquids count as solid); can't fall, hover even when stunned/incapacitated · Can't manipulate, drop, or use carried objects."},{"level":11,"title":"Inari","rules":"Full-turn action · 8 CE · Summon Inari in an unoccupied space within 10 ft for 1 min (uses your PB) · Command Inari and fox shikigami as an action on your turn · Inari counts as one of your fox shikigami (except for Living Fog). · Action · 10 CE · 60-ft cone of exploding fog: Con save or (2× CE mod)d10 + 6d10 cold, half on success · Cursed spirits: ignores cold resistance, dis on the save (auto-fail at Maximum Output)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Heaven and Earth","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Expansive fog field: all creatures but you are completely blinded and suffer Cursed Fog effects · Initiative 20: all creatures take 5d10 cold (you are immune)."}],"e286":[{"level":1,"title":"Guided Control","rules":"Bonus action · Spend CE up to CE modifier · Imbue a held tool for 1 hr per CE spent: +2 to attack rolls (or +1 AC if armor/defensive); damage die rises 1 tier (D4→D6→D8→D10→2d6→2d8), +1 more tier at 6th and 11th."},{"level":3,"title":"Floating Tool","rules":"Upgrade · +2 CE when imbuing: create a Floating Tool · Action: command it to hover up to 35 ft and make a melee attack with your CE modifier (normal weapon damage, or 1d4 if improvised) · One at a time; falls if more than 120 ft from you. · Floating Tool stats · AC = your CE save DC; HP = 5× PB + 10 per grade above 4th (if a cursed tool) · Destroyed at 0 HP (a cursed tool only loses Floating Tool) · Bonus action · 2 CE: reapply Floating Tool to a touched cursed tool."},{"level":6,"title":"Wind Scythe","rules":"Action · 3 CE (+1 CE to originate from a Floating Tool within 60 ft) · 10-ft wide, 60-ft long line from a held imbued tool: Str save or 3d10 bludgeoning + pushed 10 ft, half on success (6d10 + pushed 20 ft + prone at 11th). · Upgrades · Floating Tool: costs 1 CE; command moves 40 ft; ride one for a 60-ft fly speed; two active at once, both commanded with one action · Combat Tool: +1 attack/damage per CE spent on the imbuement · Reaction: an imbued tool shields you — +AC until your next turn or reduce triggering damage by size (Tiny +1/1d4, Small +2/2d4, Medium +3/2d6, Large +4/2d8, Huge +5/2d10), adding the tool's own bonuses."},{"level":11,"title":"Tool Mastery","rules":"Upgrades · Floating: command two Floating Tools as a bonus action, or one as a free action; adv on Dex saves while riding · Combat: improvement AC +1 more, damage reduction +1 die; one extra reaction per round usable only for Combat Tool Improvement. · Reaction · When you or a creature you can see attacks with your imbued tool: grant that attack roll advantage. · Action · 8 CE · A cursed tool becomes a sentient Tsukumogami for 1 hr (always under Floating Tool; doesn't count against your limit; one at a time) · It takes an action on your turn (Attack for one weapon attack only, Dash, Disengage, Hide, Use an Object) · Wind Scythe or Combat Tool reaction through it: +3d10, or +3 of the size-based reduction die."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Tsukumogami Spirit World","rules":"Domain (18th level) · All weapon attacks by other creatures are guaranteed misses · Initiative 20: choose an imbued tool to gain Floating Tool benefits, then all Floating Tools move 60 ft and attack a creature in range — or all creatures suffer Wind Scythe · Control up to CE-modifier Floating Tools (min 2) inside."}],"e287":[{"level":1,"title":"Hunger of the Accursed","rules":"Reaction (when you reduce a cursed spirit, shikigami, or cursed corpse to 0 HP) · 3 CE · Devour its corpse: gain one of its features (action, movement, resistance, immunity, sense, AC, ability score, other statistic) for 1 hr — no legendary actions, CE, or Domains; action cost/DC/damage set with GM sign-off · +3 CE per extra ability; up to CE-modifier abilities per corpse. · Passive · Stolen abilities reshape your body to fit (e.g. wings for flight); you count as the creature type of your most-stolen source · Max stolen abilities = CE modifier at once."},{"level":3,"title":"Regurgitation","rules":"Bonus action · 4 CE · Recall any ability you have ever devoured and use it for 1 hr."},{"level":6,"title":"Digestion","rules":"Upgrades · Hunger and Regurgitation cost −1 CE (min 1; another −1 at 11th) · Once per turn, enhance a stolen ability: Efficiency (base CE cost −1, min 1); Output (spend-cap + CE mod); Speed (movement +5 ft per CE, up to CE mod); Reinforcement (1 CE: +PB AC vs a hit, possibly causing a miss); Instinct (1 CE: action cost −1 step). · Upgrade · Abilities active from up to CE-modifier creatures at once; stolen abilities last 24 hrs · Can't use different innate techniques at once."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Body of the Devourer","rules":"Action · Spend CE = 2× the devoured's CR or level (min 1) · Transform into a creature you have devoured: stats replaced by its statblock, keeping your alignment, personality, mental scores, CE, and HP · Gain temp HP = the devoured's HP (technique ends if depleted; limited to its anatomy; techniques need hand signs + chanting) · Lasts level + CE modifier minutes."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Tomb of the Devoured","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Initiative 20: regurgitate a creature you devoured into an unoccupied space within 5 ft — friendly, acts right after your turn, attacks all enemies in the domain (sentient ones are barely-sentient husks); vanishes when the domain ends."}],"e288":[{"level":1,"title":"Teleport","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Mark a person, location, or object you can touch · Max 2× CE modifier marks (3× at 11th); marks last 12 hrs (1 week at 6th); remove at will. · Action · 2 CE · While not being viewed (no line of sight to you): you + willing creatures within 5 ft (also unviewed) teleport up to 500 ft to a mark of your choice."},{"level":3,"title":"Improved Teleport","rules":"Upgrades · Teleport range: (CE mod + PB + level) × 100 ft · Reaction (to an attack or saving throw): teleport to dodge — needs a way to vanish from view; resolves before the triggering attack's hit is determined."},{"level":6,"title":"Mastered Teleport","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Cast Teleport to any mark, exact arrival, any distance · Can teleport others without going yourself · Unwilling creature within 5 ft: CE save or teleported to one of your marks."},{"level":11,"title":"Improved Marking","rules":"Upgrade · Mark as a free action; max marks = 3× CE modifier."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Crossroads of Instance","rules":"Domain (18th level) · All space inside counts as your mark · Initiative 20: teleport up to 2× CE modifier creatures anywhere in the domain (seen or not) · Reaction: teleport a creature. · Action · Two willing creatures within 15 ft swap souls for 1 hr (dismiss at will, no action): all game statistics swapped except mental stats and non-physical feats; they lose their innate technique and gain the other's, plus the other's CE, HP, racial features, weapon proficiencies · Feat prerequisites from borrowed feats: ignore one each (except race, technique, feat, breakthrough, class requirements) · A creature can be swapped twice per month · If one dies while swapped, the other dies when the duration ends."}],"e289":[{"level":1,"title":"One Man Army","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Create a clone within 5 ft for 8 hrs: indistinguishable; 1/4 your HP max (rounded up), your AC; has all your class features and cursed techniques (not innate technique features); its CE spends come from your pool. · Clone rules · Clones act on your turn: one attack each (even with Extra Attack); you can replace your attacks with attacks from a clone's space · No items · Max = PB at once; a dead clone reduces your cap by 1 for 1 min."},{"level":3,"title":"Twice the Fun","rules":"Upgrade · Action: create multiple clones at once (3 CE each) · Melee attacks vs a creature with a clone within 5 ft of it: advantage."},{"level":6,"title":"Three is a Crowd","rules":"Upgrade · Clones make as many attacks as you; 1/2 your HP · A clone reduced to 0 HP: you regain 1 CE."},{"level":11,"title":"Four is a Party","rules":"Upgrade · Clones have your full HP · Bonus action · 1 CE: swap bodies with a clone (trade HP; it becomes your body) · Reduced to 0 HP or killed with a clone active: transfer into a clone with its current HP. · Upgrade · Your clones can each create one clone per turn by spending your CE (counts against your limit)."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Divide and Conquer","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Once per turn: create one clone as a bonus action for no CE (your clones don't get this) · Unlimited clones inside; clones' attacks are guaranteed hits · Initiative 20: one more clone appears · Domain-created clones vanish when the domain ends."}],"e290":[{"level":1,"title":"Divine Dogs","rules":"Action · 1 CE per dog · Summon up to 2 Divine Dogs within 10 ft for 1 hr (or until 0 HP, or dismissed as a bonus action in line of sight) · Reaction (seeing a shikigami hit 0 HP): unsummon it instead — can't summon it again until a long rest. · Passive · Shikigami take no actions on their own: bonus action to command (action for a longer, specific order) · Control up to half your level (rounded up) at once."},{"level":3,"title":"Trial","rules":"Action · Summon an untamed shikigami within 30 ft for free: it goes berserk (attacks nearest creature) · Defeat it alone (your shikigami don't count) to 0 HP to unlock it for normal summoning · Any creature within 50 ft counts as participating in the ritual. · Summoning costs · Gama 1 · Nue 2 · Great Serpent 4 · Rabbit Escape 6 · Mourn Tiger 7 · Max Elephant 8 · Round Deer 9 · Piercing Ox 10 · Divine General Mahoraga 20 · At 0 HP during a multi-participant trial: no death saves until all participants are unconscious."},{"level":6,"title":"Shadow Manipulation","rules":"Passive · Shadow Storage: store objects in your shadow for free (they count toward carrying capacity); 1 CE to interact with or remove one. · Bonus action · 2 CE · Trap a creature in your shadow: Dex (Acrobatics) vs your CE save DC (dis in complete darkness or a veil; auto-fail in your domain) · Failed: trapped in your shadow (counts toward carrying capacity); can hold breath for Con-mod minutes (min 1); Str or Dex save at end of turns to escape, appearing prone in an unoccupied space within 5 ft."},{"level":11,"title":"Well's Unknown Abyss","rules":"Action · Combine two living shikigami into one altered form (base's body + the other's alteration) · Spend half the base's CE cost per altered shikigami, up to PB at once (each costs CE) · Half the base's HP; reduce size by 1 to reduce CE cost by 1 · At 0 HP: doesn't affect the source shikigami, ineligible for Totality · No unaltered shikigami while altered ones are out · CR 4+ base or graft: max two at a time. · Alteration grafts · Divine Dogs: Pack Tactics · Gama: Standing Leap · Great Serpent: +15 HP, Constrict attack · Nue: 80-ft fly speed · Round Deer: Antler attack · Piercing Ox: Relentless Charge · Mourn Tiger: Mourning Roar · Max Elephant: +50 HP."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Chimera Shadow Garden","rules":"Domain (18th level) · Huge shadow barrier · Hostiles ending their turn inside: Dex (Acrobatics) or restrained and sink (Str (Athletics) at start of turns to escape); difficult terrain for creatures of your choice; you have Freedom of Movement · Bonus action: spend CE up to CE modifier to create that many clones of yourself (all your features/stats, no weapons or HP, no CE; HP = your CE mod; shadow puddle at 0); reaction when hit: swap places with a clone, it takes the hit · Summoning a shikigami: spend its cost to summon a perfect copy too (up to CE-mod copies per turn; not Mahoraga) · Your normal shikigami cost nothing inside."}],"e291":[{"level":1,"title":"Polarize & Push/Pull","rules":"Polarize (bonus action · 1 CE): magnetize one creature or metal object you can see within 60 ft to end of your next turn · Attract/Repel (action · 1 CE): move one polarized target within 60 ft up to 20 ft straight toward or away from you (unwilling: Str save negates); collision: both Dex save or prone; pulled into metal: restrained until it uses an action to pass a Str check vs your Technique DC."},{"level":3,"title":"Magnetic Flight & Scrap Barrage","rules":"Passive · Fly speed = your walking speed. · Action · 1 CE · Ranged technique attack, 60 ft: 2d8 + CE modifier piercing."},{"level":6,"title":"Turn the Blade & Crush","rules":"Reaction (a creature attacks you with a metal weapon or projectile) · 1 CE · Attacker Str save vs your Technique DC: fail = the attack misses (metal torn aside) · Projectile: immediately redirect — ranged technique attack vs a creature of your choice within 60 ft, dealing the projectile's normal damage on a hit. · Bonus action · 2 CE · One polarized creature wearing metal armor or carrying a metal object: Str save or restrained to end of its next turn + 2d8 bludgeoning, half damage on success."},{"level":11,"title":"Polarity Field & Railgun","rules":"Action · 3 CE · Focus, 1 min · 15-ft emanation centered on you: attacks with metal weapons/projectiles vs creatures inside at disadvantage; polarized creatures inside at dis on saves vs your Attract, Repel, and Crush. · Passive · Once per turn, when you use Attract on a polarized metal object (not a creature): accelerate it instead — ranged technique attack vs a creature within 120 ft: 4d8 piercing on a hit."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: The Master's Field","rules":"Full-turn action · 20 CE · 60-ft radius enclosed domain centered on you, up to 1 min, Technique Focus · Initiative 20: each hostile wearing/carrying metal: Str save or pulled 20 ft toward the center and restrained (pinned on the monopole) to the next initiative 20 + disarmed (weapons orbit the center) until it leaves or the domain ends; success: pulled 10 ft, not restrained · Counterplay: drop your metal, or break the user's Focus."},{"level":20,"title":"Electromagnetic Apex","rules":"Passive · Metal sense: 1 mile · Blackout Pulse (action · 5 CE, once per long rest): 60-ft burst within 120 ft — constructs Con save or stunned 1 round then shut down 1 min; nonmagical tech stops working 1 min (attended: bearer's save)."}],"e292":[{"level":1,"title":"Rubber Body","rules":"Passive · Resistance to bludgeoning · Melee reach 15 ft (unarmed strikes and grapples); use CE modifier instead of Strength on grapple checks."},{"level":3,"title":"Wrap & Hold","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Grapple a creature within reach: success = restrained (escape DC = your technique DC), and you gain 1 Stretch."},{"level":6,"title":"Kinetic Soak","rules":"Passive · Bludgeoning damage taken: reduced by your PB after resistance · Impacts that land feed your Stretch (see Wrap & Hold)."},{"level":9,"title":"Contortionist","rules":"Passive · Squeeze through 1-inch openings; flatten to half an inch thick · Bonus action: escape a grapple or mundane restraints · Adv on checks to slip bonds, manacles, or an unchosen grapple."},{"level":11,"title":"Malleable Arsenal","rules":"Bonus action · 1 CE · Shape limbs for 1 min (one): mallet fists (unarmed 2d8 bludgeoning, 20-ft reach); whip-limbs (30-ft reach; creatures hit can't take reactions to start of your next turn); parachute (no falling damage; glide 20 ft horizontal per 5 ft descended)."},{"level":13,"title":"Living Shield","rules":"Reaction (an ally within 15 ft is hit) · 2 CE · Envelop them: resistance to the triggering damage and +2 AC to start of your next turn."},{"level":15,"title":"Soak & Rebound","rules":"Passive · Once per turn: after taking bludgeoning damage, your next unarmed strike before end of your next turn deals extra bludgeoning = damage actually taken after resistance/reduction (max your level)."},{"level":18,"title":"Colossus Coil","rules":"Action · 4 CE · Grapple up to four creatures within reach at once: Str save vs your technique DC or restrained · A restrained creature takes 3d8 bludgeoning at the start of each of its turns while held."},{"level":20,"title":"Apex Plasticity","rules":"Passive · Elastic reach 30 ft (35 ft at Stretch 5) · Immune to bludgeoning · Colossus Coil holds up to six · Stretch never falls below 3."}],"e293":[{"level":1,"title":"Bedrock Body","rules":"Passive (always on) · Bedrock reduction applies to damage you take · Unarmed strikes: 1d8 bludgeoning · Count as Large for carrying, lifting, pushing, dragging, breaking."},{"level":3,"title":"Ripped-Up Arsenal","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Tear a lamppost, girder, or paving slab from the terrain: improvised weapon, 10-ft reach, 2d8 + Str bludgeoning, 1 min · OR hurl rubble as a ranged attack (60 ft): 2d8 + Str bludgeoning on a hit."},{"level":6,"title":"Bull Rush","rules":"Passive · When you Dash: move through hostile creatures' spaces · Each creature whose space you enter: Str save or 2d8 + Str bludgeoning + prone, half on success."},{"level":9,"title":"Stonewall","rules":"Reaction (an ally within 10 ft is hit) · Interpose: you become the target (move up to 10 ft as part of the reaction); your Bedrock reduction applies."},{"level":11,"title":"Groundbreak Stomp","rules":"Action · 4 CE · 20-ft radius centered on you becomes difficult terrain (rubble) for 1 min · Creatures in the radius: Dex save or prone · No damage."},{"level":13,"title":"Shake It Off","rules":"Bonus action · End one of grappled, restrained, or poisoned on yourself."},{"level":15,"title":"Unbreakable Line","rules":"Bonus action · 3 CE · Hostiles within 30 ft that can hear you: Wis save or dis on attacks vs creatures other than you to end of your next turn · Allies within 30 ft: temp HP = 2× PB."},{"level":18,"title":"Living Avalanche","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Peak output for 1 min: Bedrock reduction doubles, immune to forced movement, melee attackers take bludgeoning = your PB."},{"level":20,"title":"Foundation Stone","rules":"Passive · Bedrock reduction now applies to all damage except psychic · Count as Gargantuan for carrying, lifting, breaking · Allies within 20 ft share your adv on saves and checks vs forced movement."}],"e480":[{"level":1,"title":"Harmony","rules":"Action · 3 CE: cast Locate Creature with no components, 1 mile range (5 miles at 11th, 30 miles at 18th) · or 2 CE: cast Speak with Animals or Tongues (6th: Tongues reaches additional creatures in range equal to your CE modifier)."},{"level":3,"title":"Chaos","rules":"Action · 2 CE: cast Chaos Bolt (auto 3rd level at 6th, 5th at 11th, 8th at 18th) · or 2 CE: roll d100 on the Chaos Table and apply the effect (X = your CE modifier)."},{"level":6,"title":"Chaos Amplification","rules":"After using Chaos · 1 CE: increase the effect's duration or damage dice by your CE modifier (1-round or 1-minute durations double instead) · Chaos Bolt: spend up to PB CE to upcast one spell level per CE (maximum 9th level)."},{"level":11,"title":"Balance","rules":"When you use Chaos · No extra CE · Choose Order (control a random element of the effect) or Equilibrium (up to CE modifier creatures immune) · Usable PB times per long rest."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion","rules":"Domain Expansion · Full turn · 20 CE · At initiative 20, choose one Chaos Table effect of 90 or below as your guaranteed hit against creatures of your choice · Inside, every use of Chaos becomes the guaranteed hit across the whole domain."},{"level":20,"title":"No further feature stated","rules":"The source grants no additional feature at 20th level; the Domain, Chaos Amplification, and the Reversal remain the pinnacle expressions of the technique."}],"e481":[{"level":1,"title":"Light Constructs","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Conjure a bar of light in a free hand for 1 minute: simple melee weapon with finesse/light/thrown (20/60), 2d8 radiant damage, CE modifier to attack and damage rolls."},{"level":3,"title":"Rain of Light","rules":"Action · 3 CE · 15-ft cone or 10-ft radius around you: Dex save vs. 3d10 radiant (5d10 at 6th, 8d10 at 11th, 10d10 at 18th), restrained on a failed save (repeat save at end of turn ends)."},{"level":3,"title":"████ of Dawn","rules":"Action · 2 CE · Dispel magical darkness within 30 ft; hostiles within 30 ft make a Con save vs. 2d10 + CE modifier radiant (3d10 at 6th, 5d10 at 11th, 8d10 at 18th), blinded until end of turn on fail (half, not blinded on success)."},{"level":6,"title":"Hyperspeed","rules":"Passive · No CE · Resistance to radiant damage."},{"level":6,"title":"Light Beam","rules":"When you attack with your Light Construct · 1 CE: make the attack at advantage and launch the bar as a ranged spell attack vs. a creature within 60 ft · On a melee hit with the construct, teleport 10 ft to an unoccupied space you can see."},{"level":6,"title":"Laser Light Techniques","rules":"When you use a Light Technique · Spend up to your CE modifier in CE · +1 additional damage die per CE spent (2 dice per CE at 11th, 3 dice per CE at 18th)."},{"level":11,"title":"Maximum: Light Speed","rules":"Action · 8 CE · Instantly travel a 5-ft-wide, 120-ft line (200 ft at 18th, 300 ft at 20th): creatures in the line make a Con save vs. 18d10 radiant and are knocked prone (half, not prone on success) · For each creature, object, or structure passed through, Con save vs. your CE save DC or take 20 bludgeoning."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: Reverse Transcendence","rules":"Full turn · 20 CE · 150-ft radius · At initiative 20, all creatures in the domain take 6d12 radiant · Inside: movement speed doubles and all movement is unreactable teleportation; as an action, teleport anywhere and deal 4d12 radiant to one creature within 5 ft of your start or end point."}],"e482":[{"level":0,"title":"Stone-Cut Body","rules":"Passive · No CE · Unarmed strikes deal 1d8 slashing or bludgeoning (chosen per strike) · Double damage vs. objects and structures; cursed techniques deal maximum damage to them."},{"level":0,"title":"Stone Cutting Strike","rules":"When you attack with an unarmed strike or melee weapon · 2 CE · On a hit, +10 damage of the attack's base damage type (15 at 6th)."},{"level":0,"title":"Swift Fury","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Make two unarmed strikes or melee weapon attacks."}],"e483":[{"level":0,"title":"Cursed Lotus","rules":"Bonus action · 2 CE · Lotus blooms on your body for 1 minute; the next time you take damage it detonates: creatures of your choice within 10 ft make a Dex save vs. your technique DC (8 + PB + CE modifier), taking 4d4 slashing (half on success) · One lotus at a time."}],"e484":[{"level":0,"title":"Residual Catch","rules":"Reaction (when hit by a cursed technique, innate technique, or cursed strike) · No CE · Reduce the damage by 2× PB (3× PB at 6th); add your PB to your next damage roll before the end of your next turn."}],"e508":[{"level":1,"title":"Reaper's Sickles","rules":"The tools of the trade. He does not conjure them from nothing, he is simply never without them, which amounts to the same thing. Light, finesse, and a habit of joining into something longer when the harvest demands it. As an action for 1 CE, you manifest a pair of sickles spun from cursed energy into your hands. Each sickle is a melee weapon with the light and finesse properties, dealing 1d6 slashing damage on a hit."},{"level":1,"title":"Death's Mark","rules":"One mark. One debt. One direction on the compass that never lies, the debt of a single soul, outstanding. He can only ever hold one such entry in his ledger, and he does not close books early. \"I am Death, and I come for you.\" As a bonus action, you mark one creature you can see within 120 feet as your due. You always know the marked creature's direction and distance from you, and it has disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks contested by your Wisdom (Perception)."},{"level":3,"title":"The Whistle","rules":"You hear him before you see him. The whistle is not a flourish; it is the announcement of proceedings. The frightened are already half-collected; the already-frightened are charged interest in psychic coin. As an action for 2 CE, you whistle, a thin, merry tune that freezes the blood. Each creature of your choice within 60 feet that can hear you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC or become frightened of you for 1 minute. A frightened creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. You hear him before you see him."},{"level":6,"title":"\"Why Did You Run?\"","rules":"The question is rhetorical. When the marked runs, he is already there, ahead of it, cutting off the escape before the running has properly begun. Running from Death is merely walking to him at pace. When your marked target moves, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed toward it; this movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},{"level":11,"title":"Wounds That Do Not Close","rules":"Death's cuts are double-entry: what they take, they keep. Healing arrives halved, or not at all, unless the healer pays extra to settle the wound cleanly. Even reverse cursed technique must balance this ledger. The cuts of Death's sickles refuse to mend. When you damage a creature with your sickles, it can't regain hit points until the end of your next turn, and any magical healing, including reverse cursed technique, restores only half its rolled amount unless the healer spends 2 additional CE to close the wound cleanly."},{"level":14,"title":"The Circle Closes","rules":"In the final duel Death slams his sickles into the earth and the world narrows to a ring of black-red flame — no audience, no escape, no interruption. Action · 5 CE. You raise a 30-foot-radius ring of flame centered on yourself, 10 feet high, lasting 1 minute (no concentration required). The flames do not block sight. When a creature other than you tries to cross the ring's edge, it takes 4d10 fire damage and its movement ends — it does not cross. Your marked target cannot cross at all; the flames deny it utterly, and the duel is joined. You may dismiss the ring as a free action."},{"level":18,"title":"Domain Expansion: The Last Whistle","rules":"The whistle, perfected into law. Three counters and the heart stops arguing; courage, one struck blow, unwinds the count. Note what it never needs: a sure-hit. The rules are the weapon. The full accounting. Darkness, a forest road, a white moon, and the whistle looping endlessly, never louder, never closer, until it is. Here his rules are the terrain, and the terrain is already his. Rules domain. Darkness, a forest road under a white moon, and the whistle looping endlessly. Never louder. Never closer. Until it is. While the domain stands, its rules bind every creature inside except you. See Pinnacle below."},{"level":20,"title":"The Inevitable","rules":"Once per long rest, he may simply declare. The killing blow is not an attack, it is a sentence read aloud. The Constitution save is the last appeal; the necrotic damage, the costs of the trial. Once per long rest, when you hit your marked target with a sickle attack, you can declare the blow a killing one. The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your CE save DC or drop to 0 hit points. On a success it takes 8d10 necrotic damage instead. Death collects."}],"e509":[{"level":1,"title":"Face the Shards","rules":"The technique's founding posture. She does not dodge, does not harden, does not endure, she angles the pieces of every reflection she couldn't stand to see, and lets the attacker meet itself. Shards of a broken mirror hang in the air around you, the pieces of every reflection you couldn't stand to see. When you can see a ranged attack or a damaging cursed-energy effect targeting you, you may spend your reaction and 1 CE: the shards catch it and throw it back. You take no damage; the attacker suffers its own effect, the same attack roll is made against the attacker's AC, or the attacker makes its own saving throw against its own save DC. In the instant of return, the attacker sees the worst part of themselves in the glass."},{"level":3,"title":"Look Away","rules":"Not every blow deserves an answer. Some things she survives by not looking, the effect falls between the shards and vanishes, harming no one, rebounding nowhere. Restraint, aimed. When you could reflect, you may instead avert the mirror: spend 1 CE as part of the same reaction and the effect falls into the cracks between the shards and vanishes, harming no one, rebounding nowhere. Some things you survive by not looking."},{"level":6,"title":"Crueler Reflection","rules":"What comes back comes back crueler. The mirror shows the attacker the worst part of itself, magnified, and the wound follows the sight. The glass never flatters; doubled dice never lie. What comes back comes back crueler, the mirror shows the attacker the worst part of themselves, magnified, and the wound follows the sight. When you reflect an effect, you may spend 1 additional CE: the reflected damage dice are doubled, as though the attack had critically hit. If the reflected effect has no damage dice, the additional CE has no effect (invented). The glass never flatters."},{"level":11,"title":"Someone Worth Shielding","rules":"Angling the shards for someone else is easier than angling them for herself, the discovery of a lifetime. An ally within thirty feet inherits her reflection, and area effects rebound to their point of origin. The mirror widens, and you learn something: angling the shards for someone else is easier than angling them for yourself. When an ally within 30 feet is targeted by a reflectable effect, you may spend your reaction and 1 CE to reflect it as though it had targeted you. You can also turn back area and line effects: the effect rebounds onto its point of origin, and the originator makes its own save, or catches its own blast."},{"level":18,"title":"Kept Wounds","rules":"Every cut, every slight, every laugh behind her back, kept. The ledger of hurts is her true inventory: pain, saved up and spent all at once, shown back to the creditor in a single opening. Every cut, every slight, every laugh behind your back, kept. When you take damage from any source (even a physical blow that shattered your mirror), you may note the amount in a ledger of hurts (no action required). The ledger holds at most 5 × your character level; unreleased hurts fade when you finish a long rest."},{"level":20,"title":"Unflinching","rules":"Once per long rest, one minute: the Flinch is suspended. She may reflect even melee physical strikes, and reflection costs no CE, only the reaction. Look at her now. Once per long rest, as a bonus action: for 1 minute, you stop flinching. The Flinch is suspended, you may reflect melee physical strikes too, and reflection costs no CE (it still costs your reaction). Look at me now."}],"e510":[{"level":1,"title":"Chain Jail","rules":"The core statute. The middle chain lashes sixty feet to grapple and Zetsu-lock the designated, no CE spent, no technique features answered. And beneath it, the Binding Vow of the Designated: mis-aim the jail, and you die without a save. Canon keeps its promises. The core of the technique. As a bonus action, conjure the five chains from the fingers of one hand, they persist until dismissed, count as conjured cursed objects, and are invisible to creatures that cannot perceive cursed energy. As an action, lash the middle-finger chain at a creature within 60 feet: make a melee attack using your CE ability (the chain strikes at reach). On a hit, the target is grappled and Zetsu-locked: it cannot spend or regain CE, and all of its innate-technique features go quiet while bound. Escape: as an action, Athletics or Acrobatics against your CE save DC; the chain itself can be attacked (AC 15, hit points equal to 5 × your level)."},{"level":3,"title":"Judgment Chain","rules":"The pinky carries the gavel. A stake driven into the heart, a single rule dictated, break it and the heart is crushed, no save. The judge was judged first: the same stake rests in her own heart from the moment she took the technique. As an action, spend 3 CE and drive the pinky chain's stake into a creature within 5 feet (melee attack using your CE ability). On a hit, the stake lodges in the target's heart and you dictate a single rule, one sentence, phrased as a prohibition or demand the target is capable of obeying. If the target breaks the rule, the stake crushes its heart: it dies, no saving throw. The stake remains until you dismiss it or the target dies, and you always know whether the rule stands or has fallen."},{"level":6,"title":"Emperor Time","rules":"Scarlet eyes, full power. Every chain at its strongest, two chains wielded at once, and the meter running: one hour of life per round, the lifespan ledger marked, the hair whitening shade by shade. Every second of godhood, paid in years. As a bonus action, your eyes turn scarlet. While Emperor Time burns, every chain works at full power: the Dowsing Chain cannot be fooled by any mundane or magical deception; the Holy Chain heals 3d6 per CE and can reattach a severed limb with a 5-CE touch; Chain Jail's escape DC increases by 2; and you may wield two chains at once, resolving two different chain actions in a single turn (paying each cost)."},{"level":11,"title":"Twin Fetters","rules":"The chains learn to hunt in pairs, a second designated member lashed with the same attack, reach doubled, and three chains at once under Emperor Time. The vow has long arms. Your chains learn to hunt in pairs. When you hit with Chain Jail, you may spend 2 CE to lash a second member of the designated group within 30 feet of the first, resolve the same attack roll against it. Chain Jail's reach extends to 120 feet, and the chain can now grapple Huge or smaller creatures."},{"level":18,"title":"The Oathbound Arsenal","rules":"Years of feeding the vow have made it heavy. Escape DCs climb, the chain's flesh doubles, the Dowsing Chain tracks any designated member ever met regardless of distance. The vow compounds like interest. Years of feeding the vow have made it heavy. Against the designated group, your chains are merciless: Chain Jail's escape DC increases by an additional 2 (stacks with Emperor Time), the chain's hit points double, and the Dowsing Chain can track any designated member you have ever met regardless of distance (same plane)."},{"level":20,"title":"Post-Mortem Protocol","rules":"Nen does not always stop at death, especially Nen bound by vow. Conscious a minute past zero, Emperor Time burning free, advantage on every chain, and if she falls, the chains carry out her last command for a day. The strongest Nen is written after death. Nen does not always stop at death, especially Nen bound by vow. The first time you drop to 0 hit points, you do not fall: you remain conscious for 1 minute, Emperor Time burns with no lifespan cost, and your chain attacks are made with advantage. If you die while the protocol runs, your chains persist for 24 hours, carrying out the last command you gave them."}],"e511":[{"level":1,"title":"Bandit's Secret","rules":"The founding rite. A black book, a bloody palm print, no limit of pages, and four conditions that must all be met within the hour. The victim loses the stolen feature while the page holds it: theft, not borrowing. As a bonus action, conjure a black book bearing a bloody palm print, it persists until dismissed and weighs nothing. The book grows a new page for every theft, canon sets no limit on how many stolen abilities it can hold. Theft is a rite with four conditions, all within 1 hour: (1) you witness the victim use one Innate Technique feature with your own eyes; (2) you ask the victim a question about that feature aloud, and the victim answers aloud, any answer counts, even a refusal; silence does not; (3) you press the book's palm print against the victim's flesh (an action; against an unwilling creature this requires a melee attack using your CE ability); (4) all three within the same hour. Complete the rite and the feature is inscribed: you may use it as though it were your own, spending your CE, using your CE save DC, provided your character level is at least the feature's level. The victim loses the stolen feature while your page holds it: theft, not borrowing."},{"level":3,"title":"Double Face: The Bookmark and the Catalogue","rules":"A blood-red ribbon marks one page for readiness, invokable while the book lies open elsewhere, and the Catalogue reads the spine: every page's exact text, and whether each owner still breathes. Every thief keeps accounts. A blood-red ribbon now marks one page, Chrollo's Double Face. Your bookmarked ability can be invoked while the book is held open to a different page (you still invoke one stolen ability per round, paying each cost normally). As a bonus action, you may move the bookmark to a different page."},{"level":6,"title":"Two Pages Open","rules":"In the Hisoka fight the troupe leader turned two pages at once, and so can you. One extra CE per ability each round buys a second miracle in the same breath. Why read one miracle when you can read two? In the Hisoka fight, the troupe leader turned two pages at once, and so can you. While the book is open in your dominant hand, you may invoke your bookmarked ability in the same round as an open-book ability (paying each cost normally, using each action type normally). The book drinks deep: each round you invoke two stolen abilities, you spend 1 additional CE per ability. Why read one miracle when you can read two?"},{"level":11,"title":"Due Diligence","rules":"A thief studies the mark before the mark knows he's studied. One minute of observation names every Innate Technique feature the creature holds, the question is sharper when you know the answer's shape. A thief studies the mark before the mark knows he's studied. As an action, observe a creature for 1 minute (it need not be aware): you learn the names of every Innate Technique feature it possesses. This does not satisfy the rite's witnessing, you must still see a feature used, but you will know exactly what to watch for. The question is sharper when you know the answer's shape."},{"level":18,"title":"The Question Compels","rules":"Politeness, with teeth. The rite's question now compels a truthful, complete answer on a failed Wisdom save, the book leans in to listen. Manners, enforced. Your politeness has grown teeth. When you ask the rite's question, the victim must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your CE save DC or be compelled to answer truthfully and completely, the book leans in to listen. A victim that succeeds answers or refuses as it pleases, and a creature that succeeds is immune to this compulsion for 24 hours. Manners, enforced."},{"level":20,"title":"The Open Shelf","rules":"The book hovers at the shoulder, turning its own pages; every stolen ability counts as bookmarked, and the dominant hand is finally free. The library lends to allies, but never gives. The book no longer needs your hands at all, it hovers open at your shoulder, turning its own pages, and every stolen ability is treated as bookmarked: invoke any of them with the book merely present. Your dominant hand is finally free."}],"e512":[{"level":1,"title":"Pain Packer","rules":"The founding bargain. One CE conjures the heat-proof armor; every wound after reductions is banked; two CE vents it in a fifteen-foot dawn. Hurt him and he thanks you, it's an investment. As an action, spend 1 CE to conjure heat-proof armor around yourself; it lasts until you dismiss it or finish a long rest. While armored: you are immune to fire damage, and you bank Pain, note every point of damage you take (after reductions). The bank holds up to 5 × your character level. As an action, spend 2 CE to vent the bank in a 15-foot-radius burst centered on you: each creature there makes a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC, taking 1d8 fire damage per 10 Pain banked (rounded down, minimum 1d8) on a failure, half on a success. The bank empties to 0. Hurt him and he thanks you. It's an investment."},{"level":3,"title":"Heat Sense","rules":"Pain radiates. For an action, no CE, he senses how much damage anything within thirty feet has taken since its last rest. He can smell what the fight cost them. Pain radiates. As an action (no CE cost), you can sense how much damage any creature within 30 feet has taken since its last rest, a number, not the source. Your armor smolders constantly, shedding dim light in a 10-foot radius. You can smell what the fight cost them."},{"level":6,"title":"Backdraft","rules":"Touch the stove, get the stove. A melee attacker earns a reaction-vent of banked pain, up to thirty points returned as fire. The armor answers rudeness with weather. When a creature hits you with a melee attack, use your reaction and spend 1 CE to vent up to 30 banked Pain outward: the attacker takes 1d6 fire damage per 10 Pain vented (Dexterity save vs. your CE save DC for half). The bank decreases by the vented amount. Touch the stove, get the stove."},{"level":11,"title":"Slow Burn","rules":"Instead of a burst, the bank becomes a sustained aura, a minute of burning air, no concentration, draining twenty pain a turn. Stand still and let the room decide. Instead of a burst, release the bank as a sustained aura, 1 minute, no concentration: at the start of each of your turns, each hostile creature within 10 feet of you takes 1d6 fire damage per 20 Pain remaining in the bank (minimum 1d6; no save, the air itself burns), and the bank drains by 20. The aura ends when the bank drops below 20, and the bank cannot go below 0 (invented). Stand still and let the room decide. Area denial, worn like weather."},{"level":18,"title":"Deep Bank","rules":"Capacity doubled to ten times level, venting demoted to a bonus action, and the armor seals fully, not even his own dawn blinds him. He has stopped bothering to flinch at his own sun. The bank's capacity becomes 10 × your character level, and venting the bank (burst or Slow Burn) becomes a bonus action instead of an action. The armor seals fully, you can't be blinded by bright light, including your own dawn. He has stopped bothering to flinch at his own sun."},{"level":20,"title":"Solar Core","rules":"The pain echoes. The first damage each round while armored is banked twice. Every cut pays double into the dawn. The pain echoes. The first time each round you take damage while armored, add it to the bank twice. Every cut pays double into the dawn. There is no longer a difference between being hurt and charging up."}],"e513":[{"level":1,"title":"The Mansion Door","rules":"The founding deed. Two CE and a palm on a surface: a five-foot doorway into a furnished thirty-foot hall in no dimension anyone can name, who may pass, decided at the hanging. One door at a time, until the estate grows. As an action, spend 2 CE and press your palm to a surface: conjure a 5-foot doorway that opens into your mansion, a furnished, lit, 30-foot-cube hall that exists in no dimension anyone can name. When you hang the door, you designate who may pass; all others meet a wall. The door lasts until you dismiss it or finish a long rest. You can maintain one door at a time."},{"level":3,"title":"Scream","rules":"The window closes. A hand-sized portal snaps shut within thirty feet; a failed Dexterity save files the target into the holding room, whose door is locked by will alone. Whatever it touched is filed away. As an action, spend 3 CE: conjure a hand-sized portal that snaps shut on a creature within 30 feet. The target makes a Dexterity saving throw against your CE save DC, on a failure, it is teleported into your mansion's holding room, whose door is locked by your will alone. On a success, nothing happens. An unwilling creature can attempt to break the holding room's door from inside (thieves' tools or a Strength check against your CE save DC). The window closes. Whatever it touched is filed away."},{"level":6,"title":"More Rooms","rules":"The mansion grows with every long rest taken inside it, vault, war room, bathhouse, cell. Square footage is a state of mind, and the state of mind is expanding. The mansion grows. Whenever you finish a long rest inside it, you may add one room, a vault, a war room, a bathhouse, a cell, guest quarters. Long rests taken inside the mansion cannot be interrupted by anything outside it, and divination and scrying cannot find creatures inside, the mansion isn't in this dimension. Square footage is a state of mind."},{"level":11,"title":"Paired Doors","rules":"Two doors, three hundred feet apart, one step between them. Distance is a rumor the keyholder doesn't repeat. You can maintain two doors at once. Step through one and out the other, so long as both are within 300 feet of each other. Hanging a second door costs an action and 2 CE as normal. Distance is a rumor the keyholder doesn't repeat."},{"level":18,"title":"Keyholder's Step","rules":"A bonus action, one CE: step into any door and out of any other within five hundred feet, or out of the mansion itself, willing hand-holders in tow. The house has hallways; they just aren't all in the same world. As a bonus action, spend 1 CE: step into any of your doors and exit from any other door you can perceive within 500 feet, or step out of the mansion itself through any of your doors. You can bring willing creatures holding your hand. The house has hallways. They just aren't all in the same world."},{"level":20,"title":"The Estate, Perfected","rules":"Twelve rooms, each with a declared property; doors hung on thin air; and Scream perfected, closed on the empty air around a creature, holding it outside reality for a minute. There are worse places than the mansion. One of them is nowhere. The mansion becomes a true estate, up to twelve rooms, each with a declared property you name when it is built: a sealed vault immune to divination and teleportation, a sickroom, a training hall, guest quarters that lock from the inside. You may hang a door on thin air, no surface required."}],"e514":[{"level":1,"title":"Spin the Clown","rules":"The curtain rises. Two CE, a leering clown over the shoulder, one d9: and whatever it deals is what you fight with, used before it can be dismissed. The clown doesn't care what you wanted. It only cares that you play. As an action, spend 2 CE: a leering clown manifests over your shoulder and spins, roll a d9 and conjure that weapon. Conjured weapons use your CE ability modifier for attack and damage rolls."},{"level":3,"title":"Second Spin","rules":"Once per long rest: roll twice, but take the second result. The clown gives mulligans, not choices. You asked for luck. Luck answered. Once per long rest, when you spin, you may roll twice, but you must take the second result. The clown gives mulligans, not choices. You asked for luck. Luck answered."},{"level":6,"title":"Encore","rules":"When a used weapon is dismissed, the show must go on, a bonus-action spin, same two CE. The clown hates dead air. Once per long rest, when a weapon is dismissed after use, you may spin again as a bonus action (spending 2 CE as normal). The show must go on. The clown hates dead air."},{"level":11,"title":"Double Feature","rules":"Spin once, roll twice, conjure both, two props, one stage, no intermission. Both must be used before the next spin; a doubled number earns a third laugh and a third roll. Once per long rest, spin once and roll twice, conjure both weapons. Both must be used before you can spin again; if you roll the same number twice, the clown laughs and you spin that one roll a third time. Two props, one stage, no intermission."},{"level":18,"title":"The Clown's Contract","rules":"Before spinning, offer the clown a binding vow, your reaction, or 2d6 psychic as its cut, and roll twice, taking the result that better fits a kind you name. You still don't choose. But the clown listens a little, when it's paid. Before spinning, you may offer the clown a binding vow, name a price (forfeit your reaction until the start of your next turn, or take 2d6 psychic damage as the clown takes its cut). If you pay it, roll twice and take the result whose weapon better fits a kind you name, melee, ranged, or defensive. You still don't choose. But the clown listens a little, when it's paid. Every deal with the clown is binding. That's the point of a clown."},{"level":20,"title":"The Number You Never Rolled","rules":"The hidden number, dealt without a spin, at the moment of death: half your maximum hit points, the Survivor conjured, double damage dice against the one who brought you down. The clown was saving it. The hidden number, the one that only comes when you truly don't want to die. Once per long rest, when you are reduced to 0 hit points (or would die outright), the clown's grin changes and it deals you the hidden number without a spin: you immediately regain half your maximum hit points, and conjure the Survivor, a plain, perfect blade (one-handed, 2d8 slashing, invented); The Survivor uses your CE ability modifier; it deals double damage dice to the creature that brought you down, which the clown marks with a laughing skull only you can see. It cannot be dismissed until that creature falls or you finish a short rest. You never rolled a 9. A 9 rolled you."}],"e515":[{"level":1,"title":"Cursed Illusion","rules":"Cursed Illusion: The founding curse. For two CE, a face warps, and with it, a mind. Confusion, disadvantage, broken concentration: the witness, not the body, is the target. As an action for 2 CE, curse a creature within 60 feet. The target makes a Charisma saving throw against your CE save DC. On a failure, the next person they see has a distorted face. The first time the cursed creature sees the distortion, it makes an Intelligence saving throw; on a failure it is confused and has disadvantage on attack rolls and on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma checks until the end of its next turn. The cursed creature repeats the Charisma save at the end of each of its turns, ending the curse on a success. · Cursed tracking: A failed Charisma save is also a thread. Four hundred feet of general location, held until the curse breaks, she always knows where the lie found purchase. A creature that fails the Charisma save can be tracked: while cursed, you know its general location up to 400 feet away, and it keeps seeing the distorted face until it succeeds on the save or leaves your tracking range. At 6th level, you may target a number of creatures up to your CE modifier with one action, spending 2 CE for each; a creature that fails its save also has disadvantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws and loses concentration on any technique or feature it is concentrating on."},{"level":3,"title":"Self Distortion","rules":"Phase Fist: A false weapon drawn beside the true one, miss and the real strike lands doubled, hit and it lands with advantage. The lie frames the truth; the truth does the cutting. As part of making a melee attack, spend 3 CE to create a duplicate of your weapon. Make a melee cursed-energy attack roll at disadvantage, then make your normal attack against the same target. If the phase attack misses, the real attack deals double the damage dice on a hit; if the phase attack hits, the real attack is instead made at advantage. · Blurring: Her body becomes a smear on the world's retina. Sight-dependent attackers swing at disadvantage, and what cannot see her cannot aim at her. As an action for 3 CE, your body becomes blurred, shifting and wavering to all who can see you for a number of rounds equal to your CE modifier. A creature that can see you has disadvantage on attack rolls against you. An attacker is immune to this effect if it does not rely on sight (such as blindsight) or can see through illusions (such as truesight). · Distorting Disguise: Self, revised. For hours equal to her CE modifier, she is whoever the witness agrees she is, until touch, or a careful eye, calls the bluff. For 3 CE, make yourself, including clothing, armor, weapons, and other belongings, look different for a number of hours equal to your CE modifier. The changes fail to hold up to physical inspection: objects pass through added features, and touch reveals the truth. To discern the disguise, a creature uses its action to inspect your appearance and must succeed on an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your CE save DC."},{"level":6,"title":"Object Distortion","rules":"Object Distortion: Objects, likewise, can lie, opacity, luster, value, even presence itself. A Medium object's invisibility costs three CE; a creature that runs into it learns the truth the hard way. As an action, choose an object within range of your Cursed Illusion that you can see and distort its appearance, opacity, luster, visible texture, or apparent value. A creature can discern the illusion with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your CE save DC. You may spend an additional 3 CE to make the object invisible. A creature that runs into a Medium or larger invisible object takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage and loses its reaction. Cost depends on size: Tiny 1 CE, Small 2 CE, Medium 3 CE, Large 4 CE, Huge 6 CE, Gargantuan 10 CE."},{"level":11,"title":"Illusive Terrain","rules":"Illusive Terrain: The battlefield, rewritten. One hundred fifty feet of difficult ground, false walls, severed lines of sight, terrain that charges double movement for the privilege of walking on nothing. As an action for 10 CE, manipulate the terrain around you in a 150-foot radius. Rough Ground: the terrain appears difficult to traverse, a creature moving through the area spends twice as much movement per 5 feet of travel. Obstructing Illusion: as an action, create a false structure or wall within range; creatures convinced it is real cannot target you with features that require line of sight. A creature can see through the illusion with an Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Perception) check against your CE save DC, a Sorcerer makes the check with its CE modifier in place of the normal ability modifier. A creature with truesight or similar automatically succeeds."}],"e516":[{"level":1,"title":"Synovia Manipulation","rules":"Synovia Manipulation: the founding liquefaction. As an action for 4 CE, force a creature within 30 ft that has bones to make a Constitution save vs your CE save DC. Failure: 4d12 necrotic and weakened — it takes an additional 5 damage from any source until the end of your next turn. Success: half damage, not weakened. No effect on boneless creatures (constructs, oozes, cursed corpses)."},{"level":3,"title":"Devour the Marrow","rules":"Devour the Marrow: when you hit a creature within 5 ft with an unarmed strike or melee weapon attack, spend 3 CE to force a Constitution save on the hit. Failed save: cursed mites burrow into one limb of your choice (chosen before the save). Deal the Limb Damage Table's required damage to that limb and the mites devour its marrow: Broken Limb until the target finishes a long rest."},{"level":6,"title":"Bone Broth","rules":"Bone Broth: as an action for 10 CE, force every creature with bones within 30 ft of you to make a Constitution save vs your CE save DC. Failures suffer the base effects of Synovia Manipulation (4d12 necrotic, weakened until the end of your next turn); successes take half damage and are not weakened."},{"level":11,"title":"Softened Frame","rules":"Softened Frame: the weakness deepens. While a creature is weakened by your technique, it has disadvantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws, and the additional damage it takes from any source becomes twice your proficiency bonus instead of 5."},{"level":18,"title":"Marrow Brood","rules":"Marrow Brood: the mites join the liquefaction. A creature that fails its save against Devour the Marrow is also weakened as if by Synovia Manipulation, no extra action required. When you use Synovia Manipulation you may target one additional creature within range for 2 CE per extra target; each makes its own save."},{"level":20,"title":"Total Liquefaction","rules":"Total Liquefaction: once per long rest, when a creature fails its save against your Synovia Manipulation or Bone Broth, its skeleton collapses entirely — it falls prone and is restrained as its bones turn to slurry. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the Constitution save, ending the effect on a success as its bones re-harden."}],"e518":[{"level":1,"title":"Shadow of the Wyrm","rules":"Shadow of the Wyrm: gain darkvision 120 ft. Nonmagical lights within 20 ft of you are snuffed (no action). Fly 40 ft (shadow wings). Devour the Fallen: reaction, when a creature within 30 ft drops to 0 HP, devour its shadow — regain CE equal to your proficiency bonus. Bane of Light: radiant damage ignores your resistances and suppresses any regeneration until the end of your next turn."},{"level":3,"title":"Breath of the End","rules":"Breath of the End: action, 4 CE. Exhale a 30-ft cone of living darkness. Dex save vs CE DC: 3d8 necrotic (4d8 at L6, 5d8 at L11, 6d8 at L18); failure also fills the cone's area with magical darkness for 1 minute. Success: half damage, no darkness."},{"level":6,"title":"Seed of Corruption","rules":"Seed of Corruption: when you damage a creature, spend 1 CE to plant a Blight Seed (no extra action). Max proficiency-bonus seeds active; a creature hosts one seed at a time. Bonus action: detonate any number of seeds within 60 ft — each host takes 2d6 necrotic (Con save vs CE DC for half); detonated seeds are destroyed."},{"level":11,"title":"Rise, Stone Army","rules":"Rise, Stone Army: action, 8 CE. Animate up to 2 stone warriors (3 at L18) from earth/stone within 60 ft. Each: Medium construct, HP 5×your level, AC 14, slam +6 (1d8+3 bludgeoning). They obey you; one bonus action commands all of them. Last 1 hour or until destroyed."},{"level":14,"title":"Dragon Ascendant","rules":"Dragon Ascendant: you become Huge; fly 80 ft; Breath of the End cone becomes 60 ft. Frightful Gloom: enemies starting their turn within 30 ft of you make a Wis save vs CE DC or are frightened until the end of your next turn."},{"level":18,"title":"Eclipse Eternal","rules":"Eclipse Eternal: action, 12 CE. For 1 minute you are the night: 120-ft radius magical darkness centered on you, moving with you. Enemies starting their turn inside take 2d8 necrotic. You regenerate 10 HP at the start of each of your turns while in dim light or darkness."},{"level":20,"title":"The Overlord Unbound","rules":"The Overlord Unbound: your necrotic damage ignores resistance (immunity becomes half damage). Devour the Fallen also ends one magical darkness or magical light effect of your choice within 30 ft."}],"e519":[{"level":1,"title":"Four Heads, One Heart","rules":"Four Heads, One Heart: four draconic heads — Flame, Spark, Frost, Stone. Action: one head breathes a 15-ft cone, Dex save vs CE DC — Flame 1d8 fire, Spark 1d8 lightning, Frost 1d8 cold, Stone 1d8 bludgeoning (+1d8 at L6/11/18). The heads share one HP pool: you are one creature. Darkvision 60 ft."},{"level":3,"title":"Wings of the Quartet","rules":"Wings of the Quartet: fly 60 ft; carry one willing creature of your size or smaller (2 at L11, 4 at L18)."},{"level":6,"title":"Twin Exhalation","rules":"Twin Exhalation: your breathe action fires two heads instead of one — two 15-ft cones, which may differ in element and direction. Resolve each cone separately."},{"level":11,"title":"Fourfold Exhalation","rules":"Fourfold Exhalation: all four heads breathe as a single action — four 15-ft cones, each in its head's direction. Resolve each cone separately."},{"level":14,"title":"Stormheart Retaliation","rules":"Stormheart Retaliation: reaction, 2 CE, when a creature damages you — one head of your choice breathes at it (15-ft cone, resolved as your level 1 breath)."},{"level":18,"title":"Dragon's Oath","rules":"Dragon's Oath: reaction, when an ally within 30 ft is hit by an attack — interpose yourself; you take the hit instead and the attack resolves against you."},{"level":20,"title":"Elemental Cataclysm","rules":"Elemental Cataclysm: once per long rest, all four heads exhale as one — 90-ft cone. Dex save vs CE DC: 8d8 total (2d8 fire + 2d8 lightning + 2d8 cold + 2d8 bludgeoning), half on success; failure also knocks the target prone."}]};